hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9188","(9183) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Rabīʿ — al-Shāfiʿī — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Qāsim al-Azraqī — from his father: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) rode his mount while in the state of iḥrām, and it began to prance, advancing one leg and withdrawing the other. Al-Rabīʿ said: I think he said — ʿUmar said: \It is as though its rider is a branch in a wind"," or a drunken drinker.\"" Then he said: \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Shāfiʿī 1688]"""
"9189","(9184) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Ḥimṣī — Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah — from his father — from al-Zuhrī, who said: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Rabīʿah informed me that al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyyāsh informed him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās informed him: While he was travelling with ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) on the road to Makkah during his caliphate, and the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār were with him, ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) recited a line of poetry. A man from the people of ʿIrāq — and there was no other Iraqi with him besides him — said: \Let someone other than you recite it"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) felt shy because of that and urged his mount until it broke away from the caravan. [Ḥasan. Tārīkh"," al-Bukhārī 2/273]"""
"9190","(9185) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān — Abū al-Azhar — Yūnus ibn Muḥammad — Fulayḥ — Ḍamrah ibn Saʿīd — Qays ibn Abī Ḥudhayfah — from Khawwāt ibn Jubayr, who said: We went out as pilgrims with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: We travelled in a caravan in which were Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with them both). The people said: \Sing for us"," O Khawwāt!\"" So he sang for them. They said: \""Sing for us from the poetry of Ḍirrār.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Leave Abū ʿAbd Allāh to sing from the 'daughters of his heart","' meaning his own poetry.\"" He said: I continued to sing for them until when it was the pre-dawn hour"," ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Raise your voice"," O Khawwāt"," for we have reached the time of saḥar.\"" Abū ʿUbaydah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Come to a man who I hope is no worse than ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" He said: I moved aside with Abū ʿUbaydah"," and we continued in that manner until we prayed Fajr. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Istīʿāb li-Ibn Fīhi al-Birr 1/135. Tārīkh Ibn ʿAsākir 25/483]"""
"9191","(9186) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār — Abū Muʿāwiyah — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad — from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): She was asked about the himyān (leather waist belt) for the muḥrim (one in the state of iḥrām), and she said: \There is no harm in it"," so that he may secure his provisions thereby.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 15448]"""
"9192","(9187) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Barzaʿī — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd — al-Haytham ibn Jamīl — Sharīk — from Abū Isḥāq — from ʬAṭāʾ and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The muḥrim has been granted concession regarding the ring and the himyān (leather waist belt).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Dāraquṭnī 2/233]"""
"9193","(9188) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — Muḥriz ibn ʿAwn — Sharīk — from Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī — from ʬAṭāʾ, and perhaps he mentioned it from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \There is no harm in the himyān (leather waist belt) and the ring for the muḥrim.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. See the one before it]"""
"9194","(9189) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb — Abū Dāwūd — Shuʿbah — from Abū Isḥāq — from al-Barāʾ, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made peace with the polytheists of Quraysh, he wrote a treaty between them: \This is what Muḥammad"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," has made peace upon.\"" They said: \""If we had known that you were the Messenger of Allah"," we would not have fought you.\"" He said to ʿAlī: \""Erase it.\"" But he refused"," so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) erased it with his own hand and wrote: \""This is what Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh has made peace upon.\"" And they stipulated that they would stay for three days and would not enter Makkah with weapons except for the sword in its sheath.\n\nShuʿbah said: I asked Abū Isḥāq: \""What is 'the sword in its sheath'?\"" He said: \""The sword with its scabbard or with what is in it.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2551. Muslim 1783]"""
"9195","(9190) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — Muḥammad ibn Salamah — from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥīm — Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah — Yaḥyā ibn al-Ḥuṣayn — from Umm al-Ḥuṣayn, who related to him: She said: \I performed Ḥajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage"," and I saw Usāmah and Bilāl (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," one of them holding the halter of his she-camel and the other raising his garment to shield him from the heat"," until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 298. Abū Dāwūd 1834]"""
"9196","(9191) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — al-Shāfiʿī — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Rabīʿah, who said: \I accompanied ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) during the Ḥajj"," and I did not see him seeking the shade of a tent until he returned.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And I think he said in his ḥadīth or in another ḥadīth: 'He would dismount beneath a tree and seek shade with a leather mat or a garment and the like.'\"" [Ḥasan. Al-Shāfiʿī 1682]"""
"9197","(9192) Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to me, saying: Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a man upon his camel, who was in the state of ihram, seeking shade between himself and the sun. He said to him: \Expose yourself to the sun for the sake of the One for whom you have entered ihram.\"" [Sahih. Ibn Abi Shaybah 14253]"""
"9198","(9193) Abu Tahir and Abu Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Warqa' narrated from 'Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, that 'Ata' narrated to him: He saw 'Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah place a stick upon the middle of his mount and spread a cloth over it to seek shade from the sun while he was in the state of ihram. Then Ibn 'Umar met him and forbade him from doing so."
"9199","(9194) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us, Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri narrated to us in Makkah, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn 'Abdullah al-Madani narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated from 'Asim ibn 'Umar from 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no one in the state of ihram who exposes himself to the sun until it sets"," except that the sun sets carrying away his sins"," until he returns as his mother bore him.\""\n\nThis chain of narration is weak"," and what precedes it is mawquf. The hadith of Umm al-Husayn is a hadith sahih. And with Allah lies success. [Munkar. Ibn Majah 2925. Ahmad 3/373]"""
"9200","(9195) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Qazzaz al-'Abd al-Salih narrated to us in Baghdad, Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas: A man was standing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) upon his she-camel at 'Arafah when it threw him — or he said, it caused him to fall — and he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Wash him with water and lotus leaves"," and shroud him in two garments\"" — or he said"," \""in his two garments\"" — \""and do not apply perfume to him"," and do not cover his head"," for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection saying the talbiyah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Rabi' from Hammad. [Sahih. Bukhari and Muslim 1206]"""
"9201","(9196) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, having heard 'Amr from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on a journey when a man fell from his camel, broke his neck, and died while he was in the state of ihram. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Wash him with water and lotus leaves"," and bury him in his two garments"," and do not cover his head"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will raise him while he is saying the talbiyah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Sufyan. [Sahih. Muslim 1206]"""
"9202","(9197) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us, Hajib ibn Ahmad al-Tusi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Munib narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar, and he mentioned the hadith with its meaning. He added: Ibn 'Uyaynah said, and Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah added to us: Sa'id ibn Jubayr added in it that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \And do not bring any perfume near him.\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 1742. Muslim 1206]"""
"9203","(9198) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us, al-Rabi' narrated to us, al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Shihab: A son of 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) died while in the state of ihram, and he did not cover his head and did not bring any perfume near him. [Da'if]"
"9204","(9199) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated from Ayyub from Nafi': Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would not approach Makkah except that he would spend the night at Dhi Tuwa until morning, then he would perform ghusl and enter Makkah during the daytime. He attributed this practice to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), saying that he used to do so.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Rabi', and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from Ayyub. [Sahih. Bukhari 1680. Muslim 1259]"
"9205","(9200) Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Adib narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hatim and Ya'qub narrated to us, saying: Isma'il, meaning Ibn 'Ulayyah, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated from Nafi', saying: When Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reached the nearest part of the Sacred Precinct, he would cease the talbiyah, then spend the night at Dhi Tuwa, then lead us in the Fajr prayer and perform ghusl. He would narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to do that.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih. Bukhari 1498. Ahmad 2/14]"
"9206","(9201) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Malik narrated from Nafi': 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, when he drew near to Makkah, would spend the night at Dhi Tuwa between the two rises until morning, then enter through the upper pass of Makkah. He would not enter Makkah when going out for Hajj or 'Umrah until he had performed ghusl before entering at Dhi Tuwa, and he would instruct those with him to perform ghusl before entering.\n\nAnd we have narrations regarding ghusl from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib and 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Sahih. Malik 705]"
"9207","(9202) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān al-Nasawī, Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ — the companion of al-Bukhārī — informed me, saying: Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bazzāz narrated to us — al-Ḥasan gave his lineage — Abū Usāmah narrated to us. And al-Qāsim narrated to us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered during the Year of the Conquest from Kadāʾ, from the upper part of Makkah, and he exited for ʿUmrah from Kudā. Hishām said: \My father used to enter from both of them.\"" And he said: \""My father would most often enter from Kudā"," and it was the closer of the two to his dwelling.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Qāsim. And they said: \""And he entered for ʿUmrah from Kudā.\"" And ʿUrwah used to enter from both of them"," and most often he would enter from Kudā"," and it was the closer of the two to his dwelling.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Maḥmūd"," from Abū Usāmah"," and he said in its text: \""And he entered during the Year of the Conquest from Kadāʾ and exited from Kudā from the upper part of Makkah.\"" And Muslim narrated it from Abū Kurayb"," and he said in its text: \""He entered during the Year of the Conquest from Kadāʾ from the upper part of Makkah","\"" without mentioning ʿUmrah"," and he mentioned the statement of Hishām. Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī said: \""The ḥadīth scholars rarely pronounce these two names correctly; it is Kadāʾ and Kudā"," and they are two mountain passes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1503. Muslim 1258]"""
"9208","(9203) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Aṣamm and Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Qabbānī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Prophet (ﷺ) came to Makkah, he entered from its upper part and exited from its lower part.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1258. Bukhārī 1502]"
"9209","(9204) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, and Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to enter Makkah from the upper pass (al-thaniyyah al-ʿulyā) and exit from the lower pass (al-thaniyyah al-suflā).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1500. Muslim 1257]"
"9210","(9205) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad and Ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us from Yaḥyā, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to enter Makkah from Kadāʾ, from the pass of al-Baṭḥāʾ, and exit from the lower pass.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and he said: \From Kadāʾ"," from the upper pass which is at al-Baṭḥāʾ.\"" And Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān"," without mentioning Kadāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous one.]"""
"9211","(9206) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Zayd ibn Hārūn narrated to us in Makkah; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Qāḍī Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us in Aṣbahān; Masʿadah ibn Saʿd al-Aṭṭār narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us; Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to enter from the upper pass and exit from the lower one.\n\nThe wording of both is the same. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous one.]"
"9212","(9207) As for the daytime, it is due to what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh; Nāfiʿ informed me, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spent the night at Dhī Ṭuwā until he entered the morning, then he entered Makkah. And Ibn ʿUmar used to do that. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others, from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān.\n\nAs for the night, it has preceded in the narration of Muḥarrish al-Kaʿbī, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) set out from al-Jiʿrānah at night"," performing ʿUmrah"," and entered Makkah at night and completed his ʿUmrah.\"""""
"9213","(9208) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah, Qays, and Salām — all of them — narrated to us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Khālid ibn ʿArʿarah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When the House was demolished after Jurhum"," Quraysh rebuilt it. When they intended to place the Black Stone"," they disputed over who should place it. They agreed that the first person to enter through this gate should place it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered through the Gate of Banī Shaybah. He ordered a cloth to be brought"," placed the Black Stone in its centre"," and ordered each clan to take hold of an edge of the cloth and lift it. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took it and placed it.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ṭayālisī 113. Ḥākim 1/629]"""
"9214","(9209) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Mandah narrated to us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated to us; Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated to us; Ibn ʿAbbās informed us that when the Prophet (ﷺ) arrived during the era of Quraysh, the Prophet (ﷺ) entered Makkah through this great gate, while Quraysh had seated themselves near the Stone.\n\nIt has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar, marfūʿ, regarding his entering through the Gate of Banī Shaybah and his exiting through the Gate of the Perfumers (al-Ḥannāṭīn), but its chain is not preserved.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \The muḥrim may enter from wherever he wishes.\"" He said: \""And the Prophet (ﷺ) entered through the Gate of Banī Shaybah and exited through the Gate of Banī Makhzūm towards al-Ṣafā.\"" This is a good mursal narration. [Ḥasan. Ibn Khuzaymah 2770]"""
"9215","(9210) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I was told from Miqsam"," the mawlā of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: 'The hands are raised in prayer"," and upon seeing the House"," and at al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and in the evening at ʿArafah"," and at Jamratayn"," and over the deceased.'\""\n\nThus it is in our hearing"," and in the extended version: \""And at Jamratayn.\""\n\nAnd with its meaning"," Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," from Miqsam"," and it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," for Ibn Jurayj did not hear it from Miqsam.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated it from al-Ḥakam"," from Miqsam"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar — once mawqūf upon both of them"," and once marfūʿ to the Prophet (ﷺ) — without mentioning the deceased.\n\nAnd this Ibn Abī Laylā is not strong in ḥadīth. [Munkar. Shāfiʿī 586]"""
"9216","(9211) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd, al-Ṭayālisī, narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to me; Abū Qazʿah al-Bāhilī — and his name is Suwayd ibn Ḥujayr — narrated to us from Muhājir al-Makkī, who said: \I said to Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh: 'Should a man raise his hands when he sees the Kaʿbah?' He said: 'I did not think anyone would do this except the Jews. We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — would we have done that?'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 1870. Nasāʾī 2895. Dārimī 1920]"""
"9217","(9212) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn informed us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to them — Shuʿbah said: I heard Abū Qazʿah narrating, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: \We performed Ḥajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and we used to do it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The first narration"," despite its being mursal"," is more well-known among the people of knowledge than the ḥadīth of Muhājir. It has supporting narrations"," even though they are mursal"," and the ruling in such cases is the view of the one who considers it reliable and affirms it. [Weak. See the preceding.]"""
"9218","(9213) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, that the Prophet ﷺ, when he saw the House (the Kaʿbah), would raise his hands and say: \O Allah"," increase this House in honour"," magnificence"," veneration"," and reverence; and increase those who honour and venerate it among those who perform Ḥajj or ʿUmrah to it"," in honour"," veneration"," magnificence"," and righteousness.\""\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nIt has a supporting mursal narration from Sufyān al-Thawrī"," from Abū Saʿīd al-Shāmī"," from Makhūl"," who said: The Prophet ﷺ"," when he entered Makkah and saw the House"," would raise his hands"," say the takbīr"," and say: \""O Allah"," You are Peace"," and from You comes peace; so keep us alive"," our Lord"," with peace. O Allah"," increase this House in honour"," magnificence"," veneration"," and reverence; and increase those who perform Ḥajj or ʿUmrah to it"," in veneration"," honour"," magnificence"," and righteousness.\""\n\n[Munkar. al-Shāfiʿī 585]"""
"9219","(9214) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Darābjardī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Saʿīd al-Shāmī narrated to me, and he mentioned it. [Munkar. Ibn Abī Shaybah 15756]"
"9220","(9215) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʾAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Saʿīd (ibn al-Musayyib), when he performed Ḥajj and saw the Kaʿbah, would say: \O Allah"," You are Peace"," and from You comes peace; keep us alive"," our Lord"," with peace.\"" [Ḥasan. Ibn Abī Shaybah 15757]"""
"9221","(9216) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭarīf, on the authority of Ḥumayd ibn Yaʿqūb, who heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: I heard from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) a word which no one else among the people has heard besides me. I heard him say when he saw the House: \O Allah"," You are Peace"," and from You comes peace; so keep us alive"," our Lord"," with peace.\""\n\nAl-ʿAbbās said: I asked Yaḥyā"," \""Who is this Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭarīf?\"" He said: \""A Yamāmī.\"" I said: \""And who is this Ḥumayd ibn Yaʿqūb?\"" He said: \""Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated from him.\"" [Ḥasan. Tārīkh Ibn Maʿīn 2173]"""
"9222","(9217) Abū ʿAmr al-Razjāhī informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Hasanjānī narrated to us, Abū al-Ṭāhir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ḥasan — that is, Ibn Sufyān — informed me, Ḥarmalah narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us, Yūnus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, on the authority of Sālim, on the authority of his father: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he arrived in Makkah, touch the Black Stone (al-Rukn al-Aswad) at the beginning of his ṭawāf, and he would walk briskly (yakhubbu) in three circuits out of the seven.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aṣbagh, from Ibn Wahb, and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1566. Muslim 1261]"
"9223","(9218) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah al-Qaysī — and he was an excellent man — narrated to us, Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl narrated to us, on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṣāmit, on the authority of Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was between the Kaʿbah and its covering when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered. He began with the Black Stone and touched it, then performed ṭawāf of the House seven times, and prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqām (of Ibrāhīm).\n\nMuslim narrated it in the story of the Islām of Abū Dharr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2473]"
"9224","(9219) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal al-Māsarjasī informed us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baṣrī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʾAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Ibrāhīm, on the authority of ʿĀbis ibn Rabīʿah, on the authority of ʿUmar: that he came to the Black Stone, kissed it, and said: \Indeed"," I know that you are a stone; you neither benefit nor harm. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you"," I would not have kissed you.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī.\n\nIn the narration of Yaʿlā: I saw ʿUmar face the Black Stone and then say: \""By Allah"," indeed I know that you are a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you"," I would not have kissed you.\"" Then he advanced and kissed it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abū Muʿāwiyah"," from al-Aʿmash. It was also narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis"," and Aslam"," the freedman of ʿUmar"," from ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1520. Muslim 1270]"""
"9225","(9220) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb — Tamtām — narrated to us, Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to kiss the Black Stone and say: \Indeed"," I know that you are a stone; you neither harm nor benefit. However"," I saw Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ showing keen devotion to you.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī. In the narration of Abū Ḥudhayfah"," the words \""you neither harm nor benefit\"" are not present. And he narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he kissed the Black Stone and said: \""Indeed"," I kiss you"," and indeed I know that you are a stone.\"" Then he mentioned the narration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\nWakīʿ also narrated it from al-Thawrī"," and he said in the ḥadīth: I saw ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) kiss the Black Stone and embrace it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1271. And see the preceding.]"""
"9226","(9221) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed me, al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us, Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, on the authority of Abū Jaʿfar — that is, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn — on the authority of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: We entered Makkah at the time of forenoon. The Prophet ﷺ came to the gate of the Mosque, made his mount kneel, then entered the Mosque. He began with the Black Stone and touched it, and his eyes overflowed with tears. Then he performed ramal in three circuits and walked in four, until he finished. When he had finished, he kissed the Black Stone, placed his hands upon it, and wiped his face with them. [Munkar. al-Ḥākim 1/625]"
"9227","(9222) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Hammad narrated from al-Zubayr ibn 'Arabi, who said: A man asked Ibn 'Umar regarding the touching (istilam) of the Black Stone. He said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch it and kiss it.\"" The man said: \""What do you think if I am crushed [by the crowd] — what do you think if I am overpowered?\"" He replied: \""Leave that 'what do you think' in Yemen! I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching it and kissing it.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from Musaddad. [Sahih. Bukhari 1533. Tirmidhi 761]"""
"9228","(9223) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ja'far ibn 'Uthman al-Qurashi, from the people of Makkah, said: \I saw Muhammad ibn 'Abbad ibn Ja'far kiss the Black Stone and prostrate upon it"," and then say: 'I saw your maternal uncle Ibn 'Abbas kissing it and prostrate upon it.'\""\n\nAnd Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi in Marw narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Abu 'asim al-Nabil narrated to us: Ja'far ibn 'Abd Allah said: \""I saw Muhammad ibn 'Abbad ibn Ja'far kiss the Black Stone and prostrate upon it"," and then say: 'I saw your maternal uncle Ibn 'Abbas kissing it and prostrate upon it.'\""\n\nAnd Ibn 'Abd Allah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I saw 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," kiss it and prostrate upon it"," and then say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing this"," so I did it.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Abu 'asim. And in the narration of al-Tayalisi"," 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," then said: \""Had I not seen the Prophet ﷺ kiss it"," I would not have kissed it.\"" And this Ja'far is Ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman — al-Tayalisi attributed him to his grandfather. [Munkar. Tayalisi 28. Darimi 1865]"""
"9229","(9224) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Sa'id narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Abu Ja'far, who said: \I saw Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," on the Day of Tarwiyah with his head uncovered. He kissed the Corner [i.e."," the Black Stone]"," then prostrated upon it"," then kissed it"," then prostrated upon it three times.\"" [Sahih. Shafi'i 591]"""
"9230","(9225) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabrani narrated to us: Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yamani narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Husayn from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \I saw the Prophet ﷺ prostrate upon the Black Stone.\"" Sulayman said: \""No one narrated it from Sufyan except Ibn Yamani.\"" And Ibn Abi Husayn is 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn. [Munkar. Hakim 1/646. Darqutni 2/289]"""
"9231","(9226) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abay Shahbah narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Nafi', who said: \I saw Ibn 'Umar touch the Black Stone with his hand"," then kiss his hand"," and say: 'I have not ceased doing this since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it.'\"" Narrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Sahih. Muslim 1268]"""
"9232","(9227) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ata', who said: \I saw Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"," Abu Hurayrah"," Abu Sa'id al-Khudri"," and Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them — when they touched the Black Stone"," they would kiss their hands.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: \""I said to Ata': 'And Ibn 'Abbas?' He said: 'And Ibn 'Abbas — I think"," frequently.'\"" [Sahih. Ibn Abi Shaybah 14555]"""
"9233","(9228) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated from al-Zuhri from Musafi' al-Hajabi from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Corner (Rukn) and the Maqam are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Allah has extinguished their light; had He not done so"," they would illuminate everything between the East and the West.\"" [Munkar. Ibn Khuzaymah 2731. Hakim 1/636]"""
"9234","(9229) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: al-Asfati, meaning al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Shabib narrated to us: my father narrated from Yunus from al-Zuhri, who said: Musafi' al-Hajabi narrated to me that he heard 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," the Corner and the Maqam are from the rubies of Paradise. Were it not for the sins of the children of Adam that have touched them"," they would illuminate everything between the East and the West. And no afflicted or sick person touches them but is healed.\"" [Munkar. Fath al-Bari 3/462]"""
"9235","(9230) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ata' from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, who attributed it [to the Prophet ﷺ], saying: \Were it not for the impurities of the pre-Islamic era (Jahiliyyah) that touched it"," no afflicted person would touch it but be healed. And there is nothing upon the earth from Paradise other than it.\"" [Sahih]"""
"9236","(9231) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Warraq narrated to us: Shad ibn Fayyad, Abu 'Ubaydah, narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"9237","(9232) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Allah shall raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection; it shall have two eyes by which it sees and a tongue by which it speaks"," and it shall bear witness against whoever touched it with rightful intent.\"" This was likewise narrated by a group from Ḥammād"," and likewise by a group from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān"," and some of them said in the hadith: \""in favour of whoever touched him with rightful intent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Tirmidhī 961. Ibn Mājah 2944]"""
"9238","(9233) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā both said: Yaḥyā — that is, Ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh informed us, Nāfiʿ informed me from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I have not ceased touching these two corners — the Yamānī corner and the Black Stone — since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching them"," neither in hardship nor in ease.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1529]"""
"9239","(9234) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr informed us, Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Sulaymān al-Rāzī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch the Yamānī corner and the Black Stone — I think he said — in every circuit"," and he did not touch the other two corners.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 2947. Aḥmad 2/115]"""
"9240","(9235) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAbbās al-Zawzanī narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām al-Riyāḥī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, ʿUmar ibn Qays narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched the Black Stone and kissed it, and he touched the Yamānī corner and kissed his hand. ʿUmar ibn Qays al-Makkī is weak. A report has been narrated regarding its kissing, the like of which is not established. [Very Weak. Tārīkh Dimashq 40/367]"
"9241","(9236) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Firās informed us in Makkah, Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad al-Jumaḥī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm Abū Ismāʿīl al-Muʾaddib narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched the Yamānī corner"," he would kiss it and place his right cheek upon it.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz is alone in narrating it"," and he is weak. The narrations from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding kissing the Black Stone and prostrating upon it — unless by \""the Yamānī corner\"" he meant the Black Stone"," for it is also called by that name"," in which case it would be in agreement with others. [Weak]"""
"9242","(9237) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, al-Layth informed us. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch anything of the House except the two Yamānī corners.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1529. Muslim 1267]"""
"9243","(9238) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl both said: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbdullāh, who mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not touch except the Black Stone and the Yamānī corner. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 127]"
"9244","(9239) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from ʿUbayd ibn Jurayj, that he said to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar: \I see you do not touch any of the corners except the two Yamānī ones.\"" So ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""As for the corners"," I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch anything except the two Yamānī ones.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5513. Muslim 1187]"""
"9245","(9240) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Abū al-Ṭāhir informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Qatādah ibn Dīʿāmah narrated to him that Abā al-Ṭufayl narrated to him that he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās say: \I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch anything other than the two Yamānī corners.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1269]"""
"9246","(9241) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us from Qatādah from Abī al-Ṭufayl, who said: \Muʿāwiyah performed Hajj and did not come to any corner of the House without touching it. So Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only used to touch the Yamānī corner and the Black Stone.' So Muʿāwiyah said: 'None of its corners is to be forsaken.'\"" ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith followed him up from Qatādah"," without the episode of Muʿāwiyah"," and from that angle Muslim narrated it. And Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās and Muʿāwiyah"," and he added: \""And Ibn al-Zubayr used to touch all of them.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""No one abandoned touching them both as a migration from the House of Allah; rather"," he touched what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touched and refrained from what he refrained from.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 4/94. Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 16036]"""
"9247","(9242) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulaymān ibn ʿAtīq, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Bābayh, from some of the children of Yaʿlā, from Yaʿlā, who said:\n\nI performed ṭawāf with ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and when we reached the two western corners, I said: \Will you not perform istislām (touching/kissing)?\"" I positioned myself between him and the wall. He said: \""Did you not perform ṭawāf with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" I said: \""Yes"," indeed.\"" He said: \""Did you see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing istislām of them?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then you have in the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) an excellent example — proceed on your behalf.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) said: \""As for the ʿillah (legal rationale) regarding these two corners"," we hold that the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrāhīm"," so they are like the rest of the House.\""\n\n[Weak. Aḥmad 1/45. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 8945]\n\n---"""
"9248","(9243) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān informed us of the authenticity of that: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq informed ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Did you not see that your people"," when they built the Kaʿbah"," fell short of the foundations of Ibrāhīm?\"" She said: I said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," why do you not restore it to the foundations of Ibrāhīm?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Were it not for the fact that your people had only recently left disbelief"," I would have done so.\""\n\nʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""If ʿĀʾishah heard this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," then I do not think the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) abandoned performing istislām of the two corners adjacent to the Ḥajar (al-Aswad) except because the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrāhīm.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 15. Muslim 1333]\n\n---"""
"9249","(9244) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Bakr ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us, and Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Surayj asked him: Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, the orphan of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, that a man from the people of Iraq said to him:\n\n\Ask ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr about a man who enters iḥrām for Ḥajj — when he performs ṭawāf of the House"," does he exit iḥrām or not? If he tells you he does not exit iḥrām"," then tell him: indeed a man says that (i.e."," that he does exit iḥrām).\""\n\nHe (Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān) said: \""So I asked him"," and he said: 'One who enters iḥrām for Ḥajj does not exit iḥrām except by completing the Ḥajj.' I said: 'But a man used to say that.' He said: 'Evil is what he said.'\""\n\nHe said: \""Then the man confronted me and asked me"," so I narrated to him. He said: 'Then tell him: indeed a man reports that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did that — and what is the matter with Asmāʾ and al-Zubayr"," for they did that?'\""\n\nHe said: \""So I came and mentioned that to him (ʿUrwah)"," and he said: 'Who is this?' I said: 'I do not know.' He said: 'Then why does he not come to me and ask me? I think he is an Iraqi.' I said: 'I do not know.' He said: 'Then he has lied. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Ḥajj"," and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed me that the first thing he began with when he arrived in Makkah was that he performed wuḍūʾ"," then performed ṭawāf of the House. Then Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Ḥajj"," and the first thing he began with was ṭawāf of the House"," and there was nothing else. Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) likewise. Then ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Ḥajj"," and I saw that the first thing he began with was ṭawāf of the House"," and there was nothing else. Then Muʿāwiyah and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar. Then I performed Ḥajj with my father"," al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām"," and the first thing he began with was ṭawāf of the House"," and there was nothing else. Then I saw the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār doing that"," and there was nothing else. Then the last of those I saw doing that was Ibn ʿUmar"," and he did not break it with an ʿUmrah. And this Ibn ʿUmar is among them — why do they not ask him? And none of those who have passed away — they would not begin with anything when they placed their feet (in Makkah) before ṭawāf of the House"," and then they would not exit iḥrām. And I saw my mother and my maternal aunt: when they arrived"," they would not begin with anything before the House — they would perform ṭawāf of it"," and then they would not exit iḥrām. And my mother informed me that she"," her sister"," al-Zubayr"," and so-and-so and so-and-so came with an ʿUmrah only. When they touched the Rukn"," they exited iḥrām. And he has lied in what he mentioned of that.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ in its entirety from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī"," thus. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Aṣbagh"," from Ibn Wahb"," in abridged form"," without the story of the man. And from Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā"," from Ibn Wahb"," in its entirety"," and he said in place of his words \""and there was nothing else\"" (lam yakun ghayruhu): \""and there was no ʿUmrah\"" (lam takun ʿumrah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 135]\n\n---"""
"9250","(9245) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me, and he said:\n\nIbn ʿAbbās used to say: \No one — neither a ḥājj nor other than a ḥājj — performs ṭawāf of the House except that he exits iḥrām.\""\n\nI said to ʿAṭāʾ: \""From where does he say that?\"" He said: \""From the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: 'Then its place of sacrifice is at the Ancient House' (al-Ḥajj 22:33).\""\n\nI said: \""That is after al-Maʿraf (the standing at ʿArafah).\"" He said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: 'After al-Maʿraf and before it.' And he used to derive that from the command of the Prophet (ﷺ) to his Companions when he commanded them to exit iḥrām during the Farewell Pilgrimage (Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""We have narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and then from Abū Dharr"," that which indicates that their conversion of the Ḥajj into an ʿUmrah was specific to the caravan (raḥl) of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and that others — if they perform Ḥajj or perform qirān (combined Ḥajj and ʿUmrah) and then perform the ṭawāf of arrival (ṭawāf al-qudūm) — do not exit iḥrām until the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)"," at which point they exit iḥrām by that which constitutes the dissolution (taḥallul). And Allah knows best.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1245]\n\n---"""
"9251","(9246) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated — and Muḥammad informed us, he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us a ḥadīth, and the wording is from both of them — they said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbthar, Abū Zubayd, narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Wabarah, who said:\n\nI was sitting with Ibn ʿUmar when a man came to him and said: \Is it permissible for me to perform ṭawāf of the House before I come to the standing place (al-Mawqif)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""But Ibn ʿAbbās says: 'Do not perform ṭawāf of the House until you come to the standing place.'\""\n\nIbn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Ḥajj and performed ṭawāf of the House before he came to the standing place. So is the statement of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more deserving of being followed"," or the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās — if you are truthful?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1233]\n\n---"""
"9252","(9247) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Nawfal, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that she said:\n\n\I complained to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that I was ill.\"" He said: \""Perform ṭawāf from behind the people while you are mounted.\"" She said: \""So I performed ṭawāf"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at that time praying beside the House"," reciting: 'By the Mount"," and a Book inscribed' (al-Ṭūr 52:1–2).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1552. Muslim 1276]\n\n---"""
"9253","(9248) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to me. He said: ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī said to me: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to me. He said: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me — when Ibn Hishām prevented the women from performing ṭawāf with the men — he said:\n\n\How does you prevent them"," when the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ṭawāf?\"" I said: \""Was that after the ḥijāb or before?\"" He said: \""By my life"," I indeed encountered them after the ḥijāb.\"" I said: \""How could they mix with the men?\"" He said: \""They did not mix. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to perform ṭawāf separated from the men"," not mixing with them. A woman said: 'Come"," let us perform istislām"," O Umm al-Muʾminīn.' She said: 'Go away from me","' and she refused. So they went out disguised at night and performed ṭawāf with the men. However"," when they entered the House"," they would stand until the women entered and the men were brought out. And I used to come to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," along with ʿUbayd"," while she was residing in the interior of Thabīr. I said: 'What was her ḥijāb?' He said: 'She was in a Turkish tent that had a curtain"," and there was nothing between us and her besides that. And I saw upon her a rose-colored garment (dirʿ).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ thus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1538. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 9018]\n\n---"""
"9254","(9249) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Anbārī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abī al-Ṭufayl, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ):\n\n\Performed iḍṭibāʿ (exposing the right shoulder)"," then performed istislām"," then said 'Allāhu Akbar","' then performed ramal (brisk walking) in three circuits. And when they reached the Rukn al-Yamānī and were hidden from Quraysh"," they would walk"," and then they would appear to them and perform ramal. Quraysh would say: 'They are like gazelles.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""So it became a sunnah.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 1889. Ibn Mājah 2953]\n\n---"""
"9255","(9250) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Ḥamdān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Ismāʿīl, meaning Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated to me, from Nāfiʿ, who said:\n\nIbn ʿUmar would enter Makkah in the forenoon (ḍuḥā), come to the House, perform istislām of the Ḥajar (al-Aswad), and say: \Bismillāhi wa Allāhu Akbar (In the name of Allah"," and Allah is the Greatest).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Musnad Aḥmad 2/14]\n\n---"""
"9256","(9251) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Masʿūdī narrated to us, from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, that:\n\n\When he passed by the Ḥajar al-Aswad and saw crowding upon it"," he would face it"," say 'Allāhu Akbar","' and say: 'O Allah"," in affirmation of Your Book and in accordance with the sunnah of Your Prophet (ﷺ).'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ṭayālisī 178. Ibn Abī Shaybah 15797]"""
"9257","(9252) And it was narrated from another chain from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that when he touched the Black Stone (istalama al-Hajar), he would say: \O Allah"," [I do this] out of faith in You"," belief in Your Book"," and adherence to the Sunnah of Your Prophet (peace be upon him).\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah"," who was informed by Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sarraj"," who was informed by Mutayyin"," who was informed by Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari"," who was informed by Sharik"," from Abu Ishaq. He said: And Mutayyin narrated to us"," Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us"," Hafs ibn Ghayath narrated to us"," from Abu al-Umais"," from Abu Ishaq"," from al-Harith"," from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"," to that effect. [Weak. See its predecessor.]"""
"9258","(9253) Abu al-Rudhbari informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Dassah informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Ya'la, from Ya'la, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) performed Tawaf wrapped in a green cloak (mudtabi'an bi-burdin akhdar).\""\n\nAnd Waki' narrated it similarly from al-Thawri. [Weak. Abu Dawud 1883. Ibn Abi Shaybah 18996.]"""
"9259","(9254) And Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabari informed us, Ibn Abi Maryam informed us, al-Firyabi informed us. And Sulayman informed us, Hafs ibn 'Umar informed us, Qabisah informed us. They both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Abd al-Hamid, from Ibn Ya'la, from his father, who said: \I saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) performing Tawaf around the House wrapped (mudtabi'an).\""\n\nAbu 'Isa said: I asked him"," meaning al-Bukhari"," \""Who is this 'Abd al-Hamid?\"" He said: \""He is Ibn Jubayr ibn Shaybah"," and Ibn Ya'la is Ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah.\"" [Sahih in other chains. Tirmidhi 859.]"""
"9260","(9255) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'faranai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his Companions wrapped themselves (idtaba'u) and performed Raml for three circuits and walked four.\"" [Hasan.]"""
"9261","(9256) And Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us, Isma'il al-Qadi informed us, Hajjaj ibn Minhal and Sulayman ibn Harb informed us. They both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his Companions performed 'Umrah from al-Ji'ranah. They performed Raml around the House, wrapped themselves (idtaba'u), and placed their cloaks under their armpits and on their shoulders. This is the wording of Sulayman's narration. [Hasan. Abu Dawud 1884.]"
"9262","(9257) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Dassah informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Abu Salamah Musa ibn Isma'il informed us, Hammad narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \They performed Raml around the House and placed their cloaks under their armpits"," then cast them upon their left shoulders.\"" [Hasan. See its predecessor.]"""
"9263","(9258) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Why should there be Raml now and the uncovering of the shoulders"," when Allah has granted Islam victory and expelled disbelief and its people? Despite that"," we will not abandon anything that we used to do with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 1887. Ibn Majah 2952.]"""
"9264","(9259) And Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us, Bishr ibn Musa informed us, Khallad — meaning Ibn Yahya — informed us, 'Abd al-'Aziz — meaning Ibn Abi Rawwad — narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) would not leave these two corners in every circuit that he passed by them — the Black Corner (al-Aswad) and the Yemeni Corner (al-Yamani) — touching them (yastalimuhuma), and he would not touch the two corners that are near the Stone. [Hasan. Ahmad 2/18.]"
"9265","(9260) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid informed us, 'Atiyyah ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Ubayr ibn 'Umayr al-Laythi, from his father, who said: I said to Ibn 'Umar: \Why is it that I see you crowding around these two corners"," when I have not seen anyone else among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) crowding around them other than you?\"" He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Wiping them (mashuhuma) erases sins.'\"" [Sahih. Tirmidhi 909. Ahmad 2/3.]"""
"9266","(9261) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzhali informed us — dictating in the Mosque of Raja' ibn Mu'adh — 'Abd Allah informed us, Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \O 'Umar"," you are a strong man. Do not harm the weak when you wish to touch the Black Stone (istilam al-Hajar). If it is clear for you"," then touch it (fa-stalimhu); otherwise"," face it and say Takbir.\"" [Weak. Ahmad 3/29.]"""
"9267","(9262) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʢbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abū Yaʿfūr, from a shaykh of Khuzāʿah, who said: Al-Ḥajjāj had appointed him as his deputy over Makkah. He said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was a strong man and he would jostle at the Corner (al-Rukn). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \O ʿUmar"," do not jostle at the Corner"," for you thereby harm the weak. If you find space"," then touch it (istalimhu); otherwise"," face it and say the takbīr and move on.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah"," from Abū Yaʿfūr"," from al-Khuzāʿī. Sufyān said: He was ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith"," whom al-Ḥajjāj had appointed over it upon his departure from it"," and he corroborates the narration of Ibn al-Musayyab. [Weak. Aḥmad 1/28. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 890]"""
"9268","(9263) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \How did you do"," O Abū Muḥammad?\"" He said: \""I touched it (the Black Stone) and I left it.\"" He said: \""You did correctly.\"" This is a mursal hadith.\n\n(T) Likewise"," Mālik narrated it from Hishām. (Q) Al-Shāfiʿī said: I think the Prophet (ﷺ) said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \""You did correctly.\"" He described for him that he touched it when there was no crowding and left it when there was crowding. [Weak. Ibn Ḥibbān 3823]"""
"9269","(9264) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: If you find crowding at the Corner, then move on and do not stand (waiting). [Good. Shāfiʿī 594]"
"9270","(9265) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us, Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Sājī, the jurist of Baṣrah, informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ḥisāb informed us, Muʿāwiyah al-Ḍāll narrated to me, Qays ibn Saʿd narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: You have only been commanded to perform ṭawāf; if it is made easy for you, then touch the Stone (istalimū). [Good. Ṭabarānī, al-Kabīr 11348]"
"9271","(9266) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah, Abū al-Walīd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Ḥajjāj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: When you come level with it (the Corner), then say the takbīr, make supplication, and send blessings upon Muḥammad, the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Weak. Ibn Abī Shaybah 13153]"
"9272","(9267) Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd and Rūḥ said: ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I never saw him (Ibn ʿUmar) jostle at the Black Stone at all. Indeed, I once saw him jostle until his nose became swollen and blood flowed from his nostrils. [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 8903]"
"9273","(9268) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Ḥusayn, from Manbūdh ibn Abī Sulaymān, from his mother, who said: She was with ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), when a freedwoman of hers entered upon her and said: \O Mother of the Believers"," I performed seven circuits of the House and touched the Corner only two or three times.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: \""May Allah not reward you! May Allah not reward you! Did you push against the men? Why did you not say the takbīr and pass by?\"" (T) It has also been narrated from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say to them (the women): \""When you find a gap among the people"," then touch it; otherwise"," say the takbīr and move on.\"" [Weak. Shāfiʿī 595]"""
"9274","(9269) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he would perform ramal in the first three circuits and walk in the four, and he would mention that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to do that. I said to Nāfiʿ: Did he walk between the two Corners? He said: He only walked because it was easier for him to touch the Stone (istilām). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 2/13. Dārimī 1838]"
"9275","(9270) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Yūnus and Surayj said: Fulayḥ narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) ran (saʿā) three circuits. Surayj said: three rounds (ashwāṭ), then walked four, in both the Ḥajj and the ʿUmrah. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān.\n\n(T) Al-Bukhārī said: Al-Layth followed him (in narrating it). He said: Kathīr ibn Farqad narrated to me, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1537. Muslim 1261]"
"9276","(9271) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us, al-Layth informed us, Kathīr ibn Farqad narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to hasten (yakhubbu) in his ṭawāf when he arrived for ḥajj or ʿumrah, three circuits, and walk four. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"
"9277","(9271) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us. And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: al-Jurayri narrated from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas, \Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ramal and that it is a sunnah.\"" He said"," \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said"," \""What is the truth and what is the lie in what they say?\"" He said"," \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived while the polytheists were upon Qa'qi'aqan"," and the people of Makkah were a people of envy"," so they began to say among themselves that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were weak. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) therefore said: 'Show them what you dislike.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ramal to show the polytheists his strength and the strength of his Companions"," and it is not a sunnah.\"" He said: I said"," \""Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rode between al-Safah and al-Marwah and that it is a sunnah.\"" He said"," \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said"," \""What is the truth and what is the lie?\"" He said"," \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Makkah and the people of Makkah were a people of envy"," so they came out"," even the women among them"," to look at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the people would not be driven away from him.\"" Yazid said"," meaning: they would not push them away from him. \""So he rode"," though walking was dearer to him.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Abu 'Abd Allah.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. [Sahih. Muslim 1264. Ahmad 1/233]"""
"9278","(9273) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq and Abu Muslim said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us from Ayyub.\n\nAnd Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu al-Rabi' informed us: Hammad informed us: Ayyub from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his Companions arrived, and they had been weakened by the fever of Yathrib. The polytheists said, \A people are coming to you who have been weakened by the fever.\"" So they sat down in the area adjoining al-Hijr. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded them to perform ramal for the three circuits and to walk between the two Corners. He said: And nothing prevented him from commanding them to perform ramal for all the circuits except compassion toward them. Abu Muslim did not mention \""the fever of Yathrib.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 1525. Muslim 1366]"""
"9279","(9274) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani informed us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab said: Abu al-Rabi' informed us. And Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu al-Rabi' informed us: Hammad from Ayyub from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his Companions came to Makkah, and they had been weakened by the fever of Yathrib. The polytheists said, \Tomorrow a people will come to you who have been weakened by the fever and have suffered greatly from it.\"" So they sat down in the area adjoining al-Hijr. The Prophet (ﷺ) commanded them to perform ramal for three circuits and to walk between the two Corners"," so that the polytheists might see their vigor. The polytheists then said"," \""These are the ones you claimed had been weakened by the fever! These are more vigorous than such-and-such.\"" Ibn 'Abbas said: And he did not command them to perform ramal for all the circuits except out of compassion toward them.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani. [Sahih. See the preceding.]"""
"9280","(9275) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — dictation — my father and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad said: Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi informed us: Sufyan from 'Amr from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed sa'i between the House and al-Safah and al-Marwah only to show the polytheists his strength.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and others. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 1566. Muslim 1226]"
"9281","(9276) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydus informed us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini informed us: from Sufyan from 'Amr from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed sa'i between the House and al-Safah and al-Marwah only to show the polytheists his strength.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari from 'Ali. [Sahih. See the preceding.]"
"9282","(9277) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam informed us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed me: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me from his father that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Corner (al-Hajar): \By Allah"," I most certainly know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit. But I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kiss you"," and so I kiss you.\"" So he kissed it and said: \""We have no need for ramal. We only performed it to show the polytheists"," and Allah has destroyed them.\"" Then he said: \""Something the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did — we do not like to abandon it.\"" Then he performed ramal.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari in al-Sahih from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam.\n\n(T) And it was narrated to us from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," Abu Bakr"," 'Umar"," and 'Uthman"," may Allah be pleased with them"," and the caliphs after them"," performed ramal for three circuits and walked for four. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 1520. Muslim 1270]"""
"9283","(9278) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban informed us: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us from 'Ubayd Allah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ramal from the Stone to the Stone three times, and walked four times.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban. [Sahih. Muslim 1262]"
"9284","(9279) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Abu Kamil informed us: Sulaym ibn Akhdar informed us: 'Ubayd Allah from Nafi' that Ibn 'Umar performed ramal from the Stone to the Stone, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had done that. It was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from Abu Kamil. [Sahih. See the preceding.]"
"9285","(9280) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Asam — dictation — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan al-'Amiri informed us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us: Malik ibn Anas informed us. And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Baghawi said: al-Qa'ni narrated from what he read to Malik.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abd Allah informed us: Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya said: I read to Malik ibn Anas: Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed me from his father from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform ramal from the Black Stone until he returned to it, three circuits.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Sahih from al-Qa'ni and Yahya ibn Yahya. In the narration of Zayd ibn al-Hubab, it is said: \He performed ramal from the Stone to the Stone three times"," and walked four times.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1263. Malik 810]"""
"9286","(9281) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asam informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Masruq from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, who said: He saw him begin by kissing the Stone, then take it to his right, and perform ramal for three circuits and walk for four, then come to al-Maqam and pray two rak'ahs behind it. [Sahih. al-Shafi'i 589]"
"9287","(9282) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed the first ṭawāf around the House, would walk briskly (raml) for three circuits and walk normally for four. And Ibn ʿUmar used to do the same. And he would run in the bottom of the valley (al-masīl) when performing saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I said to Nāfiʿ: \Would ʿAbdullāh walk when he reached the Yamānī Corner?\"" He said: \""No"," unless he was crowded at the corner"," for he would not leave it until he had touched it (istalama).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from ʿUbaydullāh"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr from ʿUbaydullāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1562. Muslim 1261]"""
"9288","(9283) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: I heard Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrating. And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl al-Khuzāʿī informed me, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us, saying: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed ṭawāf during Ḥajj and ʿUmrah upon his first arrival, would walk briskly (saʿā) for three circuits around the House, then walk normally for four, then pray two prostrations (rakʿatayn), then perform ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\n\nThe wording is that of Ibn ʿAbbād. And in the narration of Shujaʿ: \He would"," when performing ṭawāf during Ḥajj and ʿUmrah upon his first arrival"," walk briskly for three circuits around the House and walk normally for four\"" — he did not mention what came after that.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ from Mūsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1547. Muslim 1261]"""
"9289","(9284) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from his original copy narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤabd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ did not perform ramal in the seven circuits during which he made the ifāḍah (ṭawāf al-ifāḍah). ʿAṭāʾ said: \There is no ramal in it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 2001. Ibn Mājah 3060]"""
"9290","(9285) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated to us from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, when he entered iḥrām from Makkah, would not perform ṭawāf around the House nor between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah until he returned from Minā. And he would not walk briskly (saʿā) when performing ṭawāf around the House if he had entered iḥrām from Makkah.\n\n(Sh) al-Shāfiʿī said in al-Qadīm regarding his statement \he would not saʿā","\"" meaning \""he would not perform ramal.\"" He said: \""And whoever enters iḥrām from Makkah"," or performs ṭawāf before Minā"," then performs ṭawāf on the Day of Naḥr"," he does not perform ramal. Ramal is only for one whose ṭawāf is at the beginning.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 814]"""
"9291","(9286) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: \There is no saʿī (brisk walking) for women around the House"," nor between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\""\n\nal-Shāfiʿī also narrated it from ʿĀʾishah and from ʿAṭāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Shāfiʿī 611. al-Dāraquṭnī 2/295]"""
"9292","(9287) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Zurārah narrated to us, saying: Sharīk narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \O company of women"," there is no ramal upon you"," but in us there is an example (uswah).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah 9069]"""
"9293","(9288) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ narrated, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said: \I love that whenever one passes by it — meaning the Black Stone — he should say takbīr"," and that during his raml he should say: 'O Allah"," make it an accepted Ḥajj"," a forgiven sin"," and a thanked-for saʿī.' And during the remaining four circuits he should say: 'O Allah"," forgive"," have mercy"," and pardon what You know"," for You are the Most Mighty"," the Most Generous. O Allah"," grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter"," and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 2/322]"""
"9294","(9289) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: al-Ṣaghānī and ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, saying: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated to me from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf on his camel"," and whenever he came to the Corner"," he would point to it and say takbīr.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 153]"""
"9295","(9290) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh from his original copy of hearing narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Dārabjirdī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿĀṣim and ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rāwād narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd, from his father, that he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib say: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say between the two Corners: 'Our Lord"," give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter"," and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 1892. Aḥmad 3/411]"""
"9296","(9291) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from Abī ʿUbayd, saying: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us from ʿĀṣim, from Ḥabīb ibn Ṣuhbān, that he saw ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ṭawāf around the House while saying: \Our Lord"," give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter"," and protect us from the punishment of the Fire\"" — he had no regular supplication other than this. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah 29341]"""
"9297","(9292) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, al-Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The ṭawāf (circumambulation) of the House (i.e."," the Kaʿbah) is a prayer (ṣalāh)"," except that speech has been permitted therein. So whoever is able to speak only in goodness"," let him do so.\""\n\n(Tirmidhī) And similarly"," Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd"," Mūsā ibn Aʿyan"," and others narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib"," raised to the Prophet (marfūʿ). And Ḥammād ibn Salamah and Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib"," as a stopped narration (mawqūf).\n\nAnd similarly"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāwūs narrated it from Ṭāwūs"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," as a stopped narration (mawqūf).\n\n[Denounced (Munkar). Tirmidhī 960. Dārimī 1847]"""
"9298","(9293) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār in Baghdād informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The ṭawāf is a prayer (ṣalāh)"," so reduce speech therein.\""\n\n(Tirmidhī) And similarly"," Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah narrated it from Ṭāwūs.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 12811. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 9789]"""
"9299","(9294) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated from Ḥanẓalah, from Ṭāwūs, that he heard him say: \I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: 'Reduce speech during the ṭawāf"," for indeed you are in a prayer (ṣalāh).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 2923]"""
"9300","(9295) And Abū Bakr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \I performed ṭawāf behind Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — and I did not hear either of them speaking until he had completed his ṭawāf.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Shāfiʿī 599]"""
"9301","(9296) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Firās in Makkah informed us, Abū Ḥafṣ al-Jumaḥī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, al-Qaʿnabī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Jumaḥī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ḥabbān, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \Whoever circumambulates this House (i.e."," the Kaʿbah) seven times and does not speak therein except with takbīr (saying 'Allāhu Akbar') or tahlīl (saying 'Lā ilāha illallāh')"," it will be equivalent to freeing a slave.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Shuʿab al-Īmān 4088]"""
"9302","(9297) The Shaykh said: Perhaps he intended what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʀāṣim, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ drank water during the ṭawāf. This is gharīb (uncommon) with this wording.\n\nAnd the well-known narration from ʀāṣim al-Aḥwal is:\n\n[Denounced (Munkar)]"
"9303","(9298) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us, Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʀāṣim, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Zamzam and requested water"," so I brought him a bucket of Zamzam water"," and he drank while standing.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muthannā"," from Wahb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1556. Muslim 2027]"""
"9304","(9299) And he (Muslim) extracted it from the ḥadīth of Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh, from Shuʿbah, from ʀāṣim, who heard al-Shaʿbī, who heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water from Zamzam to drink"," and he drank while standing"," and he requested the water while he was near the House.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me"," Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us"," al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us"," ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh informed us"," my father informed us"," Shuʿbah narrated it.\n\nMuslim narrated it from ʿUbaydullāh. And Hushaym narrated it from ʀāṣim and Mughīrah"," from al-Shaʿbī"," in an abbreviated form: \""He drank from Zamzam while standing.\""\n\nAnd similarly"," al-Thawrī"," Ibn ʿUyaynah"," Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah"," Abū ʿAwānah"," and others narrated it from ʀāṣim.\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī and Marwān. And some of them said in the ḥadīth: \""I gave him water to drink (saqaytu)","\"" and there is in the narration of none of them any mention of ṭawāf. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2027]"""
"9305","(9300) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Saʿīd Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah informed us, Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿUrwah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Ḥajj"," and ʀāʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — informed me that the first thing he began with when he arrived in Makkah was that he performed wuḍūʾ (ablution) and then circumambulated the House (i.e."," the Kaʿbah).\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb"," as has preceded.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1536. Muslim 1230]"""
"9306","(9301) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Mālik narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʀāʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — that she said: \I arrived in Makkah while I was menstruating"," so I did not circumambulate the House or perform saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: 'Do what the pilgrim does"," except that you do not circumambulate the House until you become pure (ṭāhir).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf"," and both (Bukhārī and Muslim) extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim"," and in it: \""except that you do not circumambulate the House until you bathe (perform ghusl).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 299. Muslim 1211]"""
"9307","(92302) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā informed us; Sufyān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father.\n\nʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, seeing nothing but [the intention of] Ḥajj. When we were at Sarf or near it, I experienced menstruation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was weeping, and he said: \What is the matter with you? Have you entered the state of menstruation (nufis)?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," this is a matter that Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Ādam. Perform all that the pilgrim performs"," except that you do not perform ṭawāf around the House until you have taken a ritual bath (ghusl).\""\n\nWhen we were at Minā"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives.\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAmr. In the narration of Abū ʿAbdillāh"," it is stated: from al-Qāsim"," from ʿĀ'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and she did not mention her words \""I experienced menstruation\"" nor her words \""When we were at Minā\""; rather she said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī and others"," from Ibn ʿUyaynah"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 290. Muslim 1211]"""
"9308","(9303) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad ibn Daʿlaj informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣā'igh informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd informed us; al-Nufaylī informed us; Mūsā ibn Aʿyan informed us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿAlī — meaning Ibn al-Madīnī — informed us; Jarīr informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us; al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān informed us. All of them [narrated] from ʿAṭā' ibn al-Sā'ib, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās. Sufyān said in his narration, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ: \Indeed"," ṭawāf around the House is like prayer"," except that you speak during it. So whoever speaks"," let him not speak except with good [words].\"" And likewise in the narration of Jarīr. Mūsā ibn Aʿyan said in his narration"," from the Prophet ﷺ: \""Ṭawāf around the House is prayer"," but Allah has permitted speech (al-minṭaq) therein. So whoever speaks"," let him not speak except with good [words].\"" And with the same meaning in the narration of al-Fuḍayl.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"9309","(9304) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us by dictation; Abū al-Walīd Ḥassān ibn Muḥammad informed us; ʿImrān ibn Mūsā informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir informed us; Maʿn informed us; Mūsā ibn Aʿyan, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Ṭawāf around the House is prayer"," but Allah has permitted speech (al-nuṭq) therein. So whoever speaks"," let him not speak except with good [words].\"" ʿAṭā' and Layth ibn Abī Sulaym raised it [to the Prophet]"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāwūs and Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah stopped it [as a statement of Ibn ʿAbbās] in the authentic narration.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"9310","(9305) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ibn Abī Qumāsh informed us; al-Ḥārith ibn Manṣūr, from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Ṭawāf is from the prayer"," so reduce speech during it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 9789]"""
"9311","(9306) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Yazīd informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿImrān informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Ṭawāf around the House is prayer…\"" and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd al-Bāghandī narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿImrān"," raised [to the Prophet]"," but he did nothing [of significance]"," for Ibn Jurayj and Abū ʿAwwānah narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah"," stopped [as a statement of Ibn ʿAbbās].\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""
"9312","(9307) And al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim narrated it from Ṭāwūs, from one of those who met the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Ṭawāf around the House is prayer.\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿArūbah informed us; Salamah ibn Shabīb informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj"," from al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim… and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd likewise ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar and Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad said it from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Munkar. Nasā'ī 2922. Aḥmad 3/414]"""
"9313","(9308) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqri' al-Mihrajānī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us; Fulayḥ, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us; al-Layth, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me that Abū Hurayrah informed him that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, sent him during the Ḥajj that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded him to lead before the Farewell Pilgrimage, on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr), among a group, to announce to the people: \No polytheist shall perform Ḥajj after this year"," and no one shall perform ṭawāf around the House while naked.\"" And in the narration of al-Muqri': \""And let no one perform ṭawāf around the House while naked.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ and from Ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Yūnus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 362. Muslim 1347]"""
"9314","(9309) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Shuʿbah, from Salamah ibn Kuḥayl, who said: I heard Muslim al-Baṭīn narrate from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A woman used to perform ṭawāf around the House while naked, and she would say:\n\nToday some of it or all of it appears,\nAnd whatever of it appears, I do not permit it.\n\nThen the verse was revealed: \O children of Ādam"," take your adornment at every mosque.\"" (Qur'an 7:31)\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 3028. Nasā'ī 2956]"""
"9315","(9310) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in al-Mustadrak; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us; Shuʿbah, from Salamah ibn Kuḥayl, who said: I heard Muslim al-Baṭīn narrate from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman used to perform ṭawāf around the House during the Jāhiliyyah while naked, with a rag over her private parts, and she would say:\n\nToday some of it or all of it appears,\nAnd whatever of it appears, I do not permit it.\n\nThen this verse was revealed: \Say: Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah?\"" (Qur'an 7:32)\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9316","(9311) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik, from Abī al-Zubayr al-Makkī, that Abū Māʿiz ʿAbdullāh ibn Sufyān informed him that he was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar when a woman came to him seeking a fatwā. She said: \I came intending to perform ṭawāf around the House"," but when I reached the door of the mosque"," the blood flowed"," so I returned. When that ceased"," I came again"," but when I reached the door of the mosque"," the blood flowed"," so I returned. When that ceased"," I came again"," but when I reached the door of the mosque"," the blood flowed.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""That is but a kick from the Shayṭān. Take a ritual bath (ightasili)"," then wrap a cloth around yourself (istathfirī bi-thawb)"," then perform ṭawāf.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Mālik 827]"""
"9317","(9312) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi informed us; Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi informed us; Abu 'Asim informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed us; Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me that Tawus informed him: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by, while he was performing Tawaf around the Ka'bah, a man who was leading another man with a ring in his nose. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cut it with his hand and then commanded him to lead him by his hand. He (the narrator) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) also passed by a man who was performing Tawaf, having been tied — meaning to another person — with a strap or a cord or something other than that. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cut it and said: \Lead him by your hand.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me collectively of this"," that Tawus informed him that Ibn 'Abbas said that from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu 'Asim"," abridged"," mentioning the first incident but not the second. [Sahih. Bukhari 1541]"""
"9318","(9313) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Yahya ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam informed us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed me, saying: I read before Malik.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id informed us; al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik ibn Anas, from what was read to him, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abdillah, that 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Have you not seen your people when they built the Ka'bah — they fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim?\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," why do you not restore it upon the foundations of Ibrahim?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Were it not for the fact that your people were recently in a state of disbelief"," I would have done so.\"" 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar said: \""If 'A'ishah heard this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," I do not think the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) left the two corners adjacent to the Hijr except because the House was not completed upon the foundations of Ibrahim.\"" The wording is that of al-Qa'nabi's hadith. Al-Bukhari narrated it from al-Qa'nabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 1506. Muslim 1333]"""
"9319","(9314) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Makhlad ibn Khalid informed us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, that he was informed of the statement of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Hijr is part of the House. Ibn 'Umar said: \By Allah"," I strongly think that if 'A'ishah heard this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," I think the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not leave the two corners (i.e."," their Istilam) except because they are not upon the foundations of the House"," and the people did not perform Tawaf behind the Hijr except for that reason.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 1857]"""
"9320","(9315) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim said: Musaddad informed us; Abu al-Ahwas informed us; al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym narrated, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the wall (al-jidr) — is it part of the House?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" I said: \""Why did they not incorporate it into the House?\"" He said: \""Your people fell short in expenditure.\"" I said: \""What is the matter with its door being elevated?\"" He said: \""Your people did so in order to admit whom they wished and to bar whom they wished. Were it not that your people were recently in a state of Jahiliyyah"," I would have feared that their hearts would reject it. I would have considered incorporating the wall into the House and lowering its door to the ground.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Sa'id ibn Mansur from Abu al-Ahwas. [Sahih. Bukhari 1507. Muslim 1333]"""
"9321","(9316) Abu 'Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan al-Naysaburi informed us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, dictating; Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah and al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl informed us — al-Husayn said: \informed us","\"" and Ibrahim said: \""informed us\"" — 'Abdillah ibn Bakr informed us; Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah narrated"," from Abu Qaza'ah"," that 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan"," while he was performing Tawaf of the House"," said: \""May Allah destroy Ibn al-Zubayr"," for he lies upon the Mother of the Believers"," claiming that he heard her say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Were it not for the fact that your people were recently in a state of disbelief"," I would have demolished the House until I added to it from the Hijr"," for your people fell short in the building.'\"" Al-Harith ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Rabi'ah said: \""Do not say this"," O Commander of the Faithful"," for I heard the Mother of the Believers narrate this.\"" He said: \""Had I heard this before I demolished it"," I would have left it upon the building of Ibn al-Zubayr.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from 'Abdillah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""I heard a number of the scholars of Quraysh mention that approximately six cubits were left out of the Ka'bah in the Hijr.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1333]"""
"9322","(9317) The Shaykh said: Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me of the authenticity of that; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; 'Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed me; my father informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us; Salim ibn Hayyan narrated, from Sa'id ibn Mina', who said: I heard 'Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr say: \My maternal aunt — meaning 'A'ishah — informed me"," saying: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'O 'A'ishah"," were it not that your people were recently in a state of shirk"," I would have demolished the Ka'bah"," lowered it to the ground"," made for it two doors — an eastern door and a western door — and added to it six cubits from the Hijr"," for Quraysh fell short when they built the Ka'bah.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi. In the narration of 'Ata' from Ibn al-Zubayr from 'A'ishah: \""five cubits.\"" And in the narration of 'Abdillah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr from al-Harith ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Rabi'ah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \""approximately seven cubits.\"" And the six is the more well-known. [Sahih. Muslim 1333]"""
"9323","(9318) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abdillah ibn Ishaq al-Baghawi al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us; Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi informed us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Jarir ibn Hazim informed us; Yazid ibn Roman narrated, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: \Were it not that your people were recently in a state of Jahiliyyah"," I would have commanded the House to be demolished"," and I would have incorporated into it what was taken out of it"," lowered it to the ground"," and made for it two doors — an eastern door and a western door — for they were unable to build it"," and I would have raised it to the building of Ibrahim.\"" He said: \""That is what prompted Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it.\"" Yazid ibn Roman said: \""I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr when he demolished it and incorporated the Hijr into it. I had seen the building of Ibrahim (peace be upon him) — its stones were like the humps of camels"," fitted tightly together\"" — or he said: \""interlocking.\"" Jarir said: \""I asked him: 'Where is its place?' He said: 'I will show you now.' He took me into the Hijr and pointed to a place and said: 'Here it is.'\"" Jarir said: \""I estimated from the Hijr six cubits or thereabouts.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Bayan ibn 'Amr from Yazid ibn Harun.\n\nAnd al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun from Jarir from Yazid ibn Roman from 'Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr. 'A'ishah said: \""He informed us of it.\"" Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abdillah ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi in Marw informed us; al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah informed us"," and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim from his father"," and it is as though Yazid ibn Roman heard it from both 'Abdillah and 'Urwah. [Sahih. Bukhari 1509]"""
"9324","(9319) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Bishr ibn Musa informed us; al-Humaydi informed us; Sufyan narrated, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \The Hijr is part of the House"," because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Tawaf of the House from behind it.\"" Allah"," the Most High"," said: \""And let them perform Tawaf of the Ancient House.\"" [Hasan. Ibn Khuzaymah 2740. al-Hakim 1/360]"""
"9325","(9320) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us, among the last narrators, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Anas ibn 'Iyad narrated, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): that when he performed Tawaf during Hajj and 'Umrah, upon his first arrival, he would walk briskly (raml) three circuits around the House and walk four, then he would perform two prostrations (i.e., two rak'ahs of prayer), then he would perform Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir from Anas ibn 'Iyad, and Muslim narrated it from another route from Musa. [Sahih. Bukhari 1537. Muslim 1261]"
"9326","(9321) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Ayyub informed us; Abu Hatim al-Razi informed us; Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan informed us; Ma'qil informed us.\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Saydalani informed us; Salamah ibn Shabib informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan informed us; Ma'qil — meaning Ibn 'Ubaydillah al-Jazari — narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Istijmar (cleaning with stones) is with an odd number"," the stoning of the Jimar is with an odd number"," the Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah is with an odd number"," and the Tawaf is with an odd number. When any one of you performs Istijmar"," let him do so with an odd number.\""\n\nTheir wording is the same. Al-Rudhbari added in his narration: \""And al-Taw means al-Witr (odd number).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Salamah ibn Shabib. [Sahih. Muslim 1300]"""
"9327","(9322) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, al-Ḥaḍramī and Aḥmad ibn Shuʿayb al-Nasāʾī both said: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Wāṣil narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — that is, al-Shaybānī — informed us, Aḥmad ibn Sahl ibn Baḥr informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Sufyān narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) arrived in Makkah, he came to the Black Stone and touched it (istalama), then moved to his right and performed ramal (brisk walking) for three circuits and walked normally for four.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"
"9328","(9323) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Rūḥ — meaning Ibn ʿUbāda — informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed me: that he heard his father narrate that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrate from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: \When the Prophet (peace be upon him) completed his ṭawāf"," he went to the Maqām and said: {And take the Maqām of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer} [al-Baqarah: 125]. Then he prayed two rakʿahs.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"9329","(9324) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAmr al-Muqrīʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father, who said: We entered upon Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and he mentioned the ḥadīth regarding the ḥajj of the Prophet (peace be upon him). He said: \Until we came to the House with him; he touched the Corner (Rukn) and performed ramal for three circuits and walked for four. Then he advanced toward the Maqām of Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) and recited: {And take the Maqām of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer} [al-Baqarah: 125]. He placed the Maqām between himself and the House.\"" He said: \""And my father used to say — and I do not know him as mentioning it except from the Prophet (peace be upon him) — that he used to recite in the two rakʿahs {Qul huwa Allāhu Aḥad} [al-Ikhlāṣ] and {Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn} [al-Kāfirūn]. Then he returned to the House and touched the Corner.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218. Ibn Abī Shaybah 14999]"""
"9330","(9325) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, al-Qaʿnabī informed us, Mālik narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) performed ṭawāf of the House, performing ramal from the Black Stone for three circuits, then he prayed two rakʿahs in which he recited {Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn} [al-Kāfirūn] and {Qul huwa Allāhu Aḥad} [al-Ikhlāṣ]. Thus I found it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9331","(9326) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī in Ṭūs informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us, Ādam informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed us, he said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) arrived and performed ṭawāf of the House seven times"," then prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqām"," then went out to al-Ṣafā.\"" He said: \""Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {Indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example} [al-Aḥzāb: 21].\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from ʿAmr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1547]"""
"9332","(9327) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī informed him: that he performed ṭawāf of the Kaʿbah with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) after the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ). When ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) completed his ṭawāf, he looked but did not see the sun (had not yet risen), so he rode until he halted at Dhī Ṭuwwā and prayed two rakʿahs.\n\nAnd with his chain of narration, he said: Mālik narrated from Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī, who said: \I saw ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ṭawāf of the House after the afternoon prayer (ṣalāt al-ʿaṣr)"," then entering his chamber"," and I do not know what he did (there).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain: that he prayed them after the ʿAṣr prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 820]"""
"9333","(9328) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Ḥāsib informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he performed ṭawāf after the ʿAṣr prayer and prayed two rakʿahs.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, Ibn al-Zubayr, and Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with them all): that they prayed them — Ibn ʿUmar after the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ) and those others after the afternoon prayer (ṣalāt al-ʿaṣr). [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 9500]"
"9334","(9329) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us by dictation, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Firās al-Mālikī in Makkah informed us, Mūsā ibn Hārūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād informed us, Sufyān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bābāh, from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, tracing it back to the Prophet (peace be upon him), that he said: \O Banū ʿAbd Manāf"," do not prevent anyone from performing ṭawāf of this House and praying at any hour he wishes"," whether by night or by day.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9335","(9330) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mūsāwī in Makkah informed us, Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Ḥanẓalī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us, Sufyān narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out to al-Ṣafā, he returned to the Black Stone and touched it (istalama).\n\nAnd this has already been mentioned in the established ḥadīth from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl, from Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9336","(9331) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ṣafwān, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) conquered Makkah"," I said: 'I shall put on my garments — my house was on the road — and I shall see what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) does.' So I set out and saw that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had emerged from the Kaʿbah"," and he and his Companions had touched (istalama) the House from the Door to the Ḥaṭīm"," and they had placed their cheeks upon the House"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was in their midst.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 1898. Aḥmad 3/431]"""
"9337","(9332) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father, who said: I was performing ṭawāf with my father, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, and I saw a group of people clinging to the House (the Kaʿbah). I said to him: \Come"," let us cling to the House along with these people.\"" He said: \""I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Shayṭān.\"" When he finished his ṭawāf"," he clung to the area between the Door and the Ḥijr. He said: \""By Allah"," this is the place where I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cling.\""\n\nThus he said"," \""with my father","\"" whereas in reality it was his grandfather"," for he is Shuʿayb ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. And I do not know whether Ibn Jurayj heard it from ʿAmr or not. The ḥadīth is well-known through al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd 1899. Ibn Mājah 2922]"""
"9338","(9333) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us: al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father, who said: I performed ṭawāf with ʿAbdullāh. When we came behind the Kaʿbah, I said to him: \Will you not seek refuge?\"" He said: \""I seek refuge in Allah from the Fire.\"" Then he proceeded until he touched the Black Stone. He stood between the Corner (al-Rukn) and the Door"," placed his chest"," his face"," his two arms"," and his two palms"," and spread them out widely. Then he said: \""Thus did I see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do it.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it from Musaddad"," and Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Muthannā in an abridged form. [Weak. See the preceding.]"""
"9339","(9334) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Sulamī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he exited the mosque intending to go to al-Ṣafā, say: \We begin with that which Allah began with.\"" So he began with al-Ṣafā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 829]"""
"9340","(9335) And with his chain of narration: Mālik narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he stood upon al-Ṣafā, said the takbīr three times and said: \Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamd"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr.\"" He did this three times and made duʿāʾ"," and he did the same upon al-Marwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9341","(9336) And with his chain of narration: Mālik narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he descended from al-Ṣafā, walked until his feet reached the bottom of the valley, then he ran (saʿy) until he emerged from it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9342","(9337) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us from his father, who said: We visited Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, and he mentioned the ḥadīth regarding the ḥajj of the Prophet (ﷺ). He said: Then he went out through the door towards al-Ṣafā. When he drew near to al-Ṣafā, he recited: \Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.\"" (He said:) \""I begin with that which Allah began with.\"" So he began with al-Ṣafā. He ascended upon it until he saw the House. He magnified Allah (said takbīr)"," declared His oneness (tahlīl)"," and said: \""Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamd"," yuḥyī wa yumīt"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr. Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu"," anjaza waʿdah"," wa naṣara ʿabdah"," wa hazama al-aḥzāba waḥdah.\"" Then he made duʿāʾ between that and said the same three times. Then he descended towards al-Marwah until his feet reached the bottom of the valley"," and he ran (ramal) in the bottom of the valley. When he ascended"," he walked until he reached al-Marwah. He did at al-Marwah as he had done at al-Ṣafā"," until the last ṭawāf was at al-Marwah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," without his words: \""yuḥyī wa yumīt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"9343","(9338) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: Thābit al-Bunānī narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ from Abū Hurayrah, in the story of the Conquest of Makkah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered. He began with the Black Stone and touched it (istalamahu), then performed ṣalāh behind the Maqām two rakʿahs, then proceeded until he reached al-Ṣafā. He ascended upon it until he saw the House, and he praised Allah and made duʿāʾ to Him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"
"9344","(9339) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿImrān ibn Mūsā said: Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, except that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came forward until he approached the Black Stone and touched it (istalamahu), and performed ṭawāf of the House. When he finished his ṭawāf, he went to al-Ṣafā and ascended upon it until he looked at the House. He raised his hands and praised Allah and made duʿāʾ as he wished to make duʿāʾ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9345","(9340) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hāniʾ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he performed ṭawāf of the House—the first ṭawāf—he walked briskly (ramal) three circuits and walked four. And he would run (saʿy) in the bottom of the masīl when performing ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I said to Nāfiʿ: \Would ʿAbdullāh walk when he reached the Yamānī Corner?\"" He said: \""No"," unless there was crowding at the Corner"," for he would not leave it until he touched it (istalamahu).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Maymūn from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1563. Muslim 1261]"""
"9346","(9341) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us: My father narrated to me: ʿUbaydullāh narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he did not mention the statement of Nāfiʿ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9347","(9342) And it was narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that he said: \The saʿy is from the house of Banī ʿAbbād to the alley of Banī Abī Ḥusayn.\"" Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār al-Naysābūrī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us — Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us — Sufyān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see the preceding hadith]"""
"9348","(9343) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us — Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us — Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from ʿĀmir from Wahb ibn al-Ajdʿ that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) in Makkah, while he was addressing the people, saying: \When any one of you comes as a pilgrim"," let him perform ṭawāf around the House seven times"," let him pray two rakʿahs at the Maqām"," then let him begin at al-Ṣafā"," facing the House"," and say seven takbīrs"," between every two takbīrs uttering ḥamd and thanāʾ to Allah"," sending ṣalawāt upon the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and supplicating for himself. And let him do the same at al-Marwah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf; Ibn Abī Shaybah 29638]"""
"9349","(9344) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar: that when he performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, he would begin at al-Ṣafā, ascending it until the House became visible to him. He would say three takbīrs and recite: \Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamd"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr\"" (There is no deity except Allah"," alone"," without partner. To Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs all praise"," and He is over all things competent). He would do this seven times"," making twenty-one takbīrs and seven tahlīls. Then he would supplicate between those"," asking Allah. Then he would descend until"," when he was in the bottom of the wādī"," he would hasten until he emerged from it"," then walk until he came to al-Marwah"," ascend it"," and do the same as he had done at al-Ṣafā — he would do this seven times until he completed his saʿy. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9350","(9345) And through his isnād, he said: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, while he was at al-Ṣafā, supplicating and saying: \Allāhumma"," innaka qulta idʿūnī astajib lakum"," wa innaka lā tukhuliful-mīʿād"," wa innī asʾaluka kamā hadaytanī ilāl-islāmi allā tanziʿahu minnī ḥattā tatawaffānī wa anā muslim\"" (O Allah"," You said: 'Call upon Me"," I will answer you","' and You do not break the promise. I ask You"," just as You have guided me to Islam"," not to take it away from me until You cause me to die while I am a Muslim). [Ṣaḥīḥ; Mālik 831]"""
"9351","(9346) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Bazmahrānī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me — my father narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he would say at al-Ṣafā: \Allāhumm-ʿiṣmīnā bi-dīni wa ṭāʿatika wa ṭāʿati rasūlika wa jannibnā ḥudūdak. Allāhumm-ijʿalnā nuḥibbuka wa nuḥibbu malāʾikataka wa anbiyāʾaka wa rusulaka wa nuḥibbu ʿibādaṣ-ṣāliḥīn. Allāhumm-ḥabbibnā ilayka wa ilā malāʾikatika wa ilā anbiyāʾika wa rusulika wa ilā ʿibādikaṣ-ṣāliḥīn. Allāhumm-yassirnā lil-yusrā wa jannibnāl-ʿusrā waghfir lanā fīl-ākhirati wal-ūlā wajʿalnā min aʾimmatil-muttaqīn\"" (O Allah"," protect us through Your religion"," Your obedience"," and the obedience of Your Messenger"," and keep us away from Your boundaries. O Allah"," make us love You"," Your angels"," Your prophets"," Your messengers"," and Your righteous servants. O Allah"," make us beloved to You"," to Your angels"," to Your prophets"," to Your messengers"," and to Your righteous servants. O Allah"," make ease accessible to us"," keep difficulty away from us"," forgive us in the Hereafter and in this world"," and make us among the leaders of the God-fearing). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9352","(9347) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naṣrābādhī narrated to us — Abū Zurʿah al-Rāzī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd ibn Rāshid al-Dimashqī, Abū Bakr, narrated — Ṣadaqah narrated from Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Nāfiʿ: \Was there any statement that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar would adhere to?\"" He said: \""Do not ask about that"," for it is not obligatory.\"" But I refused to leave him until he informed me. He said: \""He would stand for so long that"," were it not for our sense of modesty before him"," we would have sat. He would say three takbīrs"," then recite: 'Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamd"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr.' Then he would supplicate at length"," raising and lowering his voice"," to the point that he would ask Him to settle his debt in what he had asked for. Then he would say three takbīrs and recite: 'Lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamd"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr.' Then he would supplicate at length likewise"," until he did this seven times. He would say this at al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah during every ḥajj and ʿumrah he performed.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9353","(9348) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us — Abū Zurʿah narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us — Ṣadaqah narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Sālim from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), the same as that. [Ḍaʿīf; see the preceding hadith]"
"9354","(9349) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdad informed us — Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us — Shādhān informed us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Abī al-Aswad from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he would say at al-Ṣafā: \Allāhumm-aḥyinī ʿalā sunnati nabiyyika (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) wa tawaffanī ʿalā millatihi wa aʿidh min muḍillāti al-fitan\"" (O Allah"," keep me alive upon the sunnah of Your Prophet (peace be upon him)"," cause me to die upon his religion"," and protect me from the misguiding trials). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9355","(9350) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us — al-Muḥāribī narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim from Abī Maʿshar from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad, who both said: ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, stood upon the rock face at al-Ṣafā, and a man said to him: \Is it here"," O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" He said: \""By the One besides Whom there is no deity"," this is the station upon which Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"9356","(9351) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah al-Bashīrī informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us — Abū Khalīfah narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr from Abī Wāʾil from Masrūq, who said: I came to offer salām to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and accompanied ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd until he entered upon the ṭawāf. He performed three circuits ramal (briskly) and four walking. Then he prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqām. Then he returned to the Black Stone and kissed it. Then he went out to al-Ṣafā and stood upon the side that is at al-Ṣafā, and he recited the talbiyah. I said: \I have been forbidden from the talbiyah.\"" He said: \""But I command you with it. The talbiyah was a supplication to which Ibrāhīm responded.\"" When he descended into the valley"," he performed saʿy and said: \""Allāhumm-ighfir warḥam wa anta al-aʿazzu al-akram\"" (O Allah"," forgive and have mercy"," and You are the Most Mighty"," the Most Generous). This is the most authentic of the narrations regarding that from Ibn Masʿūd. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Ibn Abī Shaybah 15570"," 15571]"""
"9357","(9352) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAmr, meaning ibn Khālid al-Ḥarrānī, narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar saying between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah: \My Lord"," forgive me and have mercy"," for You are the Most Mighty"," the Most Generous.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9358","(9353) Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from his father, who said: The one who saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that he would stand in a pool at the lower part of al-Ṣafā and would not ascend upon it. [Ḍaʿīf — al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 2/323]"
"9359","(9354) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḷī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we pronounced the talbiyah for Ḥajj. We arrived in Makkah on the fourth of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to perform ṭawāf of the House and to perform saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and to make it an ʿUmrah, and to exit the state of iḥrām — except for the one who had the sacrificial animal with him. None of us had a sacrificial animal except the Prophet ﷺ and Ṭalḥah. Then ʿAḷī came from Yemen and he had a sacrificial animal with him. He said: \I have entered iḥrām for that for which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered iḥrām.\"" We said: We are departing for Minā"," and one of us is dripping with semen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""If I had known beforehand what I came to know later"," I would not have brought the sacrificial animal"," and had I not had the sacrificial animal with me"," I would have exited the state of iḥrām.\"" He said: Surāqah met him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," is this for us specifically"," or is it forever?\"" He said: \""No"," rather it is forever.\"" ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," had arrived in Makkah while she was menstruating. The Prophet ﷺ commanded her to perform all the rites of Ḥajj except that she should not perform ṭawāf of the House and should not pray until she became pure. When they descended to al-Baṭḥāʾ"," ʿĀʾishah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will you depart having performed Ḥajj and ʿUmrah while I depart having performed only Ḥajj?\"" The Prophet ﷺ commanded Ibn Abī Bakr to accompany her to al-Tanʿīm"," so she performed an ʿUmrah in Dhū al-Ḥijjah after the days of Ḥajj.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmar"," from Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 6803]"""
"9360","(9355) Abū ʿAḷī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir, and he mentioned the hadith. In it, from the Prophet ﷺ, at his statement: \Enter iḥrām for Ḥajj"," then perform Ḥajj"," and do what the pilgrims do"," except that you shall not perform ṭawāf of the House and you shall not pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9361","(9356) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madinah, who used to say: Any woman who performs ṭawāf of the House and then sets out to perform ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and then menstruates — let her perform the ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah while she is menstruating. And likewise, the one who has a minor ritual impurity after performing ṭawāf of the House and before performing saʿī. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"9362","(9357) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated, reciting to Mālik, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, who said: I said to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her — and I was at that time young in age: \What is your view regarding the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Ḥajj to the House or performs ʿUmrah"," there is no blame upon him for walking between them' — I do not think there is any blame upon anyone for not walking between them.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""Not at all! If it were as you say"," it would have been: 'There is no blame upon him for not walking between them.' Rather"," this verse was revealed concerning the Anṣār. They used to pronounce the talbiyah for Manāt"," and Manāt was near Qudayd. They used to feel reluctant to walk between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. When Islam came"," they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"," so Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah' — the verse.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik. Al-Bukhārī said: Abū Muʿāwiyah added from Hishām: \""Allah does not complete the Ḥajj of any person nor his ʿUmrah if he does not perform ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 1561"," Muslim 1277]"""
"9363","(9358) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us orally; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Hannād ibn al-Sarī narrated to us. Isḥāq said: \informed us","\"" and Hannād said: \""narrated to us\"" — Abū Muʿāwiyah"," from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. He said: I said: \""I think that if a person were to leave out al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," it would not harm him.\"" She said: \""Why?\"" I said: \""Because Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," says: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Ḥajj to the House or performs ʿUmrah"," there is no blame upon him for walking between them.'\"" She said: \""O son of my sister"," if it were as you say"," it would have been: 'There is no blame upon him for not walking between them.' Allah does not complete the Ḥajj of any person nor his ʿUmrah if he does not perform ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Do you know regarding what this was revealed? The Anṣār used to pronounce the talbiyah in the Jāhiliyyah for an idol on the shore of the sea. Then they would come and walk between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and shave their heads. When Islam came"," they disliked walking between them because of what they used to do between them in the Jāhiliyyah. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Ḥajj to the House or performs ʿUmrah"," there is no blame upon him for walking between them"," and whoever volunteers good — then indeed"," Allah is Appreciating and Knowing.'\"" So the people returned and performed ṭawāf.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. Abū Muʿāwiyah said from Hishām: \""Indeed"," the verse was revealed concerning those who used to perform ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah in the Jāhiliyyah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — see the one before it]\n\nAbū Usāmah narrated from Hishām"," similar to the narration of Mālik"," that it was revealed concerning those who did not walk between them. It is possible that both are correct."""
"9364","(9359) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḷī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and I said to her: 'What is your view regarding the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: \""Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Ḥajj to the House or performs ʿUmrah"," there is no blame upon him for walking between them\""?'\"" I said to ʿĿʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her: \""By Allah"," there is no blame upon anyone for not performing ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\"" ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""How evil is what you have said"," O son of my sister! If this verse were as you interpret it"," it would have been: 'There is no blame upon him for not walking between them.' Rather"," it was revealed concerning the fact that the Anṣār"," before they accepted Islam"," used to pronounce the talbiyah for Manāt al-Ṭāghiyah"," which they used to worship near al-Mushallal. And whoever pronounced the talbiyah for her used to feel reluctant to walk between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. When they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"," Allah revealed: 'Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah' — the verse.\"" ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established the practice of ṭawāf between them"," so it is not for anyone to abandon the ṭawāf between them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Mālik 832]"""
"9365","(9360) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; Ḥujayn ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, and he mentioned the hadith similarly. And he added: He said: \I informed Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām of what ʿUrwah narrated to me from that"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. So Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: 'Indeed"," this is knowledge and a matter that I had not heard. And indeed"," I heard men among the people of knowledge saying: Indeed"," the people — except those whom ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," mentioned"," those who used to pronounce the talbiyah for Manāt — they all used to perform ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. So they said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we used to perform ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and indeed Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," mentioned the ṭawāf of the House and did not mention the ṭawāf of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Is there any blame upon us"," O Messenger of Allah"," for walking between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah?\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Ḥajj to the House or performs ʿUmrah"," there is no blame upon him for walking between them.\""'\"" Abū Bakr said: \""I understand that this verse was revealed concerning both groups — both those who used to feel reluctant in the Jāhiliyyah to walk between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and those who used to walk between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah in the Jāhiliyyah along with the ṭawāf of the House when He mentioned it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. He also narrated it from the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah"," from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī"," likewise. And al-Bukhārī narrated it from the hadith of Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah"," from al-Zuhrī"," likewise. The narration of al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah agrees with the narration of Mālik and others from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father. And his narration from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān agrees with the narration of Abū Muʿāwiyah from Hishām. Then Abū Bakr carried it upon both matters together"," that the verse was revealed concerning both groups together. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 1561"," Muslim 1277]"""
"9366","(9361) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḷī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah were among the rites of the Jāhiliyyah. When Islam came, we refrained from them. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \Indeed"," al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī. And Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Abū Muʿāwiyah"," from ʿĀṣim"," with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 1565"," Muslim 1278]"""
"9367","(9362) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: that a man asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): \May a man have intercourse with his wife before performing saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah?\"" He said: \""As for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," he performed ṭawāf of the House"," then prayed two rakʿahs"," then performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," then he recited: {Indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example}.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1546. Muslim 1234]"""
"9368","(9363) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: Surayj, ʿAmr al-Nāqid, Ibn ʿAbbād, Ibn al-Muqriʾ, and Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr from Jābir: \We asked him about a man who performed ṭawāf of the House but did not perform saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah during an ʿUmrah — may he go to his wife?\"" He said: \""No.\"" And they asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) about it"," and Ibn ʿUmar said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived and performed ṭawāf of the House seven times"," prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqām"," and performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah seven times. And indeed"," in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Yaʿlā 5634]"""
"9369","(9364) Abū ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū Bakr narrated to us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr, who said: \We asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who came for ʿUmrah and performed ṭawāf of the House but did not perform saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah — may he go to his wife?\"" Ibn ʿUmar said… and he mentioned it with wording similar to their ḥadīth from Sufyān. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh and others from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1563. Muslim 1234]"""
"9370","(9365) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us: Maʿrūf ibn Mushkān narrated to us: Manṣūr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from his mother Ṣafiyyah, who informed me from among the women of Banī ʿAbd al-Dār who had met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). They said: \We entered the house of Ibn Abī Ḥusayn and peered through a broken door"," and we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) hastening in the saʿy until"," when he reached the alley of Banī Fulān — a place he named within the masʿā — he turned to the people and said: 'O people"," perform saʿy"," for saʿy has been made obligatory upon you.'\"" [Ḥasan. al-Dāraquṭnī 2/255]"""
"9371","(9366) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us among the last narrations, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Muʾammal al-ʿĀbidī narrated to us from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥayṣin from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah, who said: \The daughter of Abī Tijrāh"," one of the women of Banī ʿAbd al-Dār"," informed me"," saying: 'I entered the house of Āl Abī Ḥusayn with women from Quraysh"," looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was performing saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I saw him performing saʿy"," and his waist-wrapper was spinning around due to the intensity of his saʿy"," to the point that I would say: I can see his knees. And I heard him saying: \""Perform saʿy"," for Allah has made saʿy obligatory upon you.\""'\"" Yūnus ibn Muḥammad and Muʿādh ibn Hānīʾ narrated it from Ibn al-Muʾammal"," except that they said ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥayṣin and said it from Ḥabībah bint Abī Tijrāh. Al-Wāqidī claimed"," from ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-ʿUmarī"," from Manṣūr ibn Ṣafiyyah"," from his mother"," from Burrah bint Abī Tijrāh. And it was said: from Ṣafiyyah from Tamlik"," as though she heard it from both of them. For she reported in the first narration that she took it from women. [Ḍaʿīf. al-Ḥākim 4/79]"""
"9372","(9367) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Mandah narrated to us: Yūsuf al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Mihrān narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from al-Mughīrah ibn Ḥakīm from Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah from Tamlik, who said: \I looked at the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while I was in my room between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and he was saying: 'O people"," indeed Allah has made saʿy obligatory upon you"," so perform saʿy.'\"" Mihrān ibn Abī ʿAmr is the only one who narrated it from al-Thawrī. [Ḍaʿīf. al-Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 529]"""
"9373","(9368) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: Budayl ibn Mayṣarah narrated to us from al-Mughīrah ibn Ḥakīm from Ṣafiyyah bint Shaybah from Umm Walad of Shaybah, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from a window"," performing saʿy in the bottom of the masʿā between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and he was saying: 'The valley — or al-Baṭḥāʾ — is not to be crossed except with vigor (shaddan).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Nasāʾī 2980. Ibn Mājah 2987]"""
"9374","(9369) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who used to say: \No one performs Ḥajj"," whether from near or far"," without performing saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. And women do not become lawful for men until they have performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9375","(9370) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Yūsuf ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated to us from Kathīr ibn Kathīr ibn al-Muṭṭalib ibn Abī Wadaʿah — and Ayyūb, one of them adding over his companion — from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \The first time women wore the waist-wrapper (mintaq) was on account of Umm Ismāʿīl. She wore a waist-wrapper to conceal her traces from Sārah. Then Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) came with her and her son Ismāhīl (peace be upon him)"," while she was nursing him"," until he placed her near the House. At that time there was no one in Makkah"," and there was no water there. He placed them there and placed with them a leather bag containing dates and a water-skin containing water. Then Ibrāhīm turned to depart"," and Umm Ismāʿīl followed him"," saying: 'O Ibrāhīm"," where are you going"," leaving us in this valley where there is no companion and nothing?' She said this three times"," and he did not turn back. So she said to him: 'Did Allah command you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' She said: 'Then He will not forsake us.' Then she returned"," and Ibrāhīm departed until"," when he was near the House where they could not see him"," he turned his face toward the House"," raised his hands"," and made these supplications"," saying: {My Lord"," I have settled some of my offspring in a barren valley near Your Sacred House}… until He reached: {that they may give thanks}. Umm Ismāʿīl continued to nurse Ismāʿīl and drink from that water. When what was in the water-skin was exhausted"," she became thirsty"," and her son became thirsty"," and hunger afflicted him. She began to look at him as he writhed — or he said: as he rolled about. She set out"," averse to looking at him"," and found al-Ṣafā to be the nearest mountain on the earth adjacent to her. She stood upon it"," then faced the valley to see if she could see anyone"," but she saw no one. She descended from al-Ṣafā until"," when she reached the valley"," she raised the edge of her garment and ran with the exertion of a person striving intensely"," until she crossed the valley. Then she came to al-Marwah and stood upon it to see if she could see anyone"," but she saw no one. She did this seven times.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""For this reason the people perform saʿy between them.\"" When she looked out over al-Marwah"," she heard a sound. She said: 'Hush!' — addressing herself. Then she listened again and heard it. She said: 'You have heard — if you have any relief (help) with you.' And there she was"," at the angel at the site of Zamzam"," scratching with his heel — or he said: with his wing — until the water appeared. She began to dam it up and scoop water into her water-skin from it"," while it was bubbling up as much as she scooped. Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'May Allah have mercy on Umm Ismāʿīl — had she left Zamzam alone' — or he said: 'Had she not scooped from the water — Zamzam would have been a flowing spring.' She drank and nursed her child. The angel said to her: 'Do not fear being forsaken"," for here is the House of Allah. This boy and his father will build it. Indeed"," Allah does not forsake its people.' And he mentioned the ḥadīth at length. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 3184. Aḥmad 1/347]"""
"9376","(9371) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī narrated to us in Kūfah: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Kathīr ibn Jumhān: that a man said to Ibn ʿUmar regarding the saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah: \I see you walking while the people are running.\"" He said: \""If I walk"," then I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) walk. And if I run"," then I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) run. And I am an old man.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1904. al-Tirmidhī 864]"""
"9377","(9372) Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me. And Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us; Ahmad ibn Sahl and Muhammad ibn Ismā'īl said: Abū al-Ṭāhir narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from 'Ubaydullāh ibn 'Abdillāh ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbās: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf during the Farewell Pilgrimage upon a camel, touching the Corner (al-Rukn) with a hooked staff. The wording of both their narrations is the same.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ahmad ibn Ṣāliḥ, and by Muslim from Abū al-Ṭāhir.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1530. Muslim 1272]"
"9378","(9373) Abū 'Amr, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillāh al-Adīb, informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī informed me; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Karīm narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Shāhin narrated to us; Khālid narrated, from Khālid, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbās: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf around the House (al-Bayt) upon a camel. Whenever he came to the Corner, he would gesture toward it with something in his hand and say the takbīr.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Shāhin. Yazīd ibn Zuraī' narrated it from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhā' and added therein: \Then he would kiss it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1551]"""
"9379","(9374) Hilāl ibn Muhammad al-Ḥaffār informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn 'Ayyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Abū al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraī' narrated it with the same meaning and with his addition. Then Yazīd said: \He would kiss that thing which was in his hand.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9380","(9375) Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbās: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah while he was complaining of illness. He performed ṭawāf around the House upon his mount. Whenever he came to the Corner, he touched it with a hooked staff that he had with him. When he finished, i.e., his ṭawāf, he made his camel kneel and prayed two rak'ahs.\n\n'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; Abū 'Imrān narrated to us; al-'Abbās al-Narsī and 'Abd al-A'lā said: Khālid narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from 'Ikrimah, and he mentioned it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it from Musaddad, from Khālid ibn 'Abdillāh. Thus said Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, and this is an addition unique to him, and Allah knows best.\n\nJābir ibn 'Abdillāh al-Anṣārī and Ibn 'Abbās explained in another narration from him, and also 'Ā'ishah bint al-Ṣiddīq, the meaning.\n\n[Ḍa'īf. Abū Dāwūd 1881. Aḥmad 1/304]"
"9381","(9376) As for the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh: Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-'Abbās, Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb, informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me.\n\nAnd Abū 'Abdillāh informed us, saying: Abū 'Amr ibn Abī Ja'far informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; 'Alī ibn Mushir narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf around the House during the Farewell Pilgrimage upon his mount, touching the Corner with his hooked staff, so that the people could see him, and so that he could be prominent, and so that they could ask him, for the people had crowded around him. The wording is that of Abū Bakr.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1273]"
"9382","(9377) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū 'Abdillāh, Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb, narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Hārūn ibn 'Abdillāh narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf during the Farewell Pilgrimage upon his mount around the House, and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, so that the people could see him, and so that he could be prominent, and so that they could ask him, for the people had crowded around him.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abd ibn Ḥumayd, from Muhammad ibn Bakr.\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of Ibn 'Abbās:\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1273]"
"9383","(9378) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Bakr ibn 'Abdillāh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us. He said: And Muhammad ibn Abī Ja'far al-Faqīh informed me; 'Imrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us. They said: Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; al-Jurarī narrated, from Abū al-Ṭufayl, who said: I said to Ibn 'Abbās: \What do you say about this ramal (brisk walking) around the House for three circuits and walking for four — is it a Sunnah? For your people claim that it is a Sunnah.\"" He said: \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said: \""What do you mean by 'they have spoken the truth and they have lied'?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah and the polytheists said: 'Indeed Muḥammad and his Companions are too weak to perform ṭawāf around the House.' And they used to envy him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to perform ramal for three circuits and to walk for four.\"" I said: \""Tell me about the ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah while mounted — is it a Sunnah? For your people claim that it is a Sunnah.\"" He said: \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said: \""What do you mean by 'they have spoken the truth and they have lied'?\""\n\nHe said: \""The people crowded around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," saying: 'This is Muḥammad","' until even the young women came out of the houses. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have the people pushed away from in front of him. So when they became too many"," he rode (his mount)"," and walking and sa'ī are more meritorious.\"" The wording is that of 'Imrān.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil al-Jaḥdarī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1264]"""
"9384","(9379) Abū al-Ḥasan, 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdan, informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, from Abū 'Āṣim al-Ghanawī, from Abū al-Ṭufayl, who said: I said to Ibn 'Abbās: \Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah upon his camel"," and that this is a Sunnah.\"" He said: \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said: \""What do you mean by 'they have spoken the truth and they have lied'?\"" He said: \""They have spoken the truth — he did perform ṭawāf upon his camel — and they have lied — it is not a Sunnah. The people were not kept away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," nor were they turned aside. So he performed ṭawāf upon his camel so that they could hear his speech and see his station"," and so that their hands could not reach him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9385","(9380) As for the ḥadīth of 'Ā'ishah: Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us by dictation, and Abū Bakr, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzzakkī narrated to us verbatim. They said: Abū 'Abdillāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us; al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Shu'ayb ibn Isḥāq narrated, from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from his father 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ performed ṭawāf around the Ka'bah during the Farewell Pilgrimage upon a camel, touching the Corner, disliking that the people should be pushed away from him.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1274]"
"9386","(9381) Abū Bakr, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakkī informed us. They said: Abū Ja'far, Muhammad ibn 'Alī ibn Duḥaym, narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah informed us; he said: 'Ubaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Ma'rūf, i.e., ibn Kharrabūdh, narrated, from Abū al-Ṭufayl, who said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ performing ṭawāf around the House upon a camel, touching the Black Stone with his hooked staff.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1275. Abū Dāwūd 1879]"
"9387","(9382) It was narrated by Abu 'Asim from Ma'ruf, and he added in it: \Then he would kiss it"," then go out to al-Safa and al-Marwa"," and perform Tawaf seven times on his mount.\"" It was narrated to us by Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari"," who was informed by Muhammad ibn Bakr"," who was informed by Abu Dawud"," who was informed by Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," who was informed by Abu 'Asim"," and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of al-Tayalisi from Ma'ruf"," without mention of the camel"," and he also did not mention this addition which was uniquely narrated by Ibn Rafi' from Abu 'Asim.\n\nIt was also narrated by Harun ibn 'Abdullah from Abu 'Asim without this addition. [See the one before it]"""
"9388","(9383) It was narrated by Yazid ibn Mulayk, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: \I saw the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage performing Tawaf of the House on his mount"," touching the Corner with his crooked staff.\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr"," who was informed by Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm"," who was informed by Yahya ibn Abi Talib"," who was informed by Yazid ibn Abi Hakim"," who was informed by my grandfather Yazid ibn Mulayk"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""As for his seven circuits upon his arrival"," they were performed on foot"," because Jabir"," whose narration is reported regarding it"," states that he performed Raml for three circuits and walked for four. It is not possible that Jabir would narrate the Prophet's Tawaf as both walking and riding within a single set of seven circuits. And he preserved the knowledge that the seven circuits in which he rode were during his Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice.\"" And he mentioned the mursal hadith which: [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"""
"9389","(9384) It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — who was informed by Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm, who was informed by al-Rabi', who was informed by al-Shafi'i, who was informed by Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn Tawus, from his father: \That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his Companions to hasten with the Ifadah (Tawaf al-Ifadah)"," and he performed the Ifadah with his wives at night"," on his mount"," touching the Corner with his crooked staff — I think he said — and kissing the tip of the staff.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""As for what has been narrated from him that he performed Tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwa while mounted"," he intended thereby"," and Allah knows best"," his Sa'i after the Tawaf of Arrival. As for after the Tawaf of Ifadah"," it has not been preserved from him that he performed Tawaf between them.\"" [Da'if. Ahmad 3/413. Tirmidhi 903. Nasa'i 30611]"""
"9390","(9385) It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, who both said: It was narrated to us by Abu Ja'far — Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym — who was informed by Ahmad ibn Hazim, who was informed by 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa and Ja'far ibn 'Awn, who both said: It was narrated to us by Ayman ibn Nabil, from Qudamah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ammar, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwa on a camel — no striking"," no driving"," and no 'ilayka ilayka.'\"" Thus they both said. And it was narrated by a group from Ayman"," and they said in the hadith: \""He stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice.\"" And it is possible that both are correct. [Da'if. Tirmidhi 903]"""
"9391","(9386) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — who was informed by Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar, who was informed by Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Ibn Ishaq, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Thawr, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt secure in Makkah in the year of the Conquest"," he performed Tawaf on his mount"," touching the Black Stone with a crooked staff in his hand. Then he entered the Ka'bah and found in it a bird made of wood"," so he broke it. Then he stood with it at the door of the Ka'bah"," and I was looking"," and he threw it.\"" [Hasan. Ibn Majah 2947]"""
"9392","(9387) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, who was informed by Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam, who was informed by Yahya ibn Yahya, who said: I recited to Malik. And it was narrated to us by Abu 'Abdullah, who was informed by Abu al-Hasan — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus — who was informed by 'Uthman ibn Sa'id, who was informed by al-Qa'nabi, from what he recited to Malik, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: \I complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I was ill"," and he said: 'Perform Tawaf from behind the people while you are mounted.'\"" She said: \""So I performed Tawaf while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying beside the House"," reciting: {By the Mount"," and a Book inscribed} [al-Tur: 1-2].\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from al-Qa'nabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 1552. Muslim 1276]"""
"9393","(9388) It was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Abu 'Amr al-Muqri' and Abu Bakr al-Warraq, who both said: It was narrated to us by al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, who was informed by Hisham ibn 'Ammar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, who both said: It was narrated to us by Hatim ibn Isma'il, who was informed by Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: \We visited Jabir ibn 'Abdullah"," and he mentioned the hadith regarding the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'When it was the end of the Tawaf at al-Marwa"," he said: \""Had I known beforehand what I have come to know now"," I would not have brought the Hadi (sacrifice)"," and I would have made it an 'Umrah. So whoever among you does not have a Hadi with him"," let him exit the state of Ihram and make it an 'Umrah.'\"" So all the people exited the state of Ihram and shortened their hair"," except the Prophet ﷺ and those who had a Hadi with them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Sahih]"""
"9394","(9389) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' — who was informed by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who was informed by Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi, who was informed by Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, who was informed by Fudayl ibn Sulayman, who was informed by Musa ibn 'Uqbah, who was informed by Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out and arrived in Makkah"," and he mentioned the hadith. He said: 'And he commanded his Companions to perform Tawaf of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwa"," then to shorten their hair and exit the state of Ihram. And that was for those who did not have a Badanah (sacrifice) which had been garlanded. And whoever had his wife with her"," she was lawful for him"," and so were perfume and garments.'\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 1644]"""
"9395","(9390) And it was narrated to us by Abu 'Amr al-Adib, who was informed by Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili, who was informed by Yusuf al-Qadi — with some doubt in it — who was informed by Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration, except that he said in its text: \The Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah and commanded his Companions to perform Tawaf of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwa"," then to exit the state of Ihram and shave or shorten their hair.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr"," in one of the two places with the first wording"," and in the other place with the second wording. [Sahih. See the one before it]"""
"9396","(9391) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, who was informed by Abu al-Husayn — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mati al-Kufi — in Baghdad, who was informed by Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Ghurazah, who was informed by Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd, who was informed by Isma'il, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he performed 'Umrah. He performed Tawaf and we performed Tawaf with him. He prayed and we prayed with him. He performed Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwa"," and we shielded him from the people of Makkah"," so that nothing would harm him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr"," from Ya'la. [Sahih. Bukhari 3953. Ibn Majah 2990]"""
"9397","(9392) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Tamim ibn al-Muntasir informed us; Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us; Sharik reported from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: We performed 'Umrah with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He performed Tawaf of the House seven times, then prayed two rak'ahs at the Maqam. Then he came to al-Safa and al-Marwa and performed Sa'i between them seven times. Then he shaved his head."
"9398","(9393) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Ibn Jurayj reported from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas that Mu'awiya informed him, saying: I trimmed the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with a pair of scissors at al-Marwa.\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in their Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj with this meaning, though it does not mention 'Umrah. [Sahih. Bukhari 1643. Muslim 1246]"
"9399","(9394) Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Tabarani informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Tusi informed us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'ig informed us; Rawh informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; al-Hasan ibn Muslim reported from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas from Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him), saying: We trimmed the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) during his 'Umrah at al-Marwa with a pair of scissors.\n\nAnd likewise Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi reported from Rawh ibn 'Ubada. [Sahih. See the preceding hadith.]"
"9400","(9395) Abu al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih informed us; Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi reported from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar from Nafi': that Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to slaughter at Makkah near al-Marwa and to slaughter at Mina near the place of sacrifice. [Da'if]"
"9401","(9396) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Malik ibn Anas and others informed us that Nafi' informed them. And Abu 'Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan al-Naysaburi informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr and Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, saying: I read to Malik from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \O Allah"," have mercy upon those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""And upon those who trim their hair"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""O Allah"," have mercy upon those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""And upon those who trim their hair"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""And upon those who trim their hair.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 1640. Muslim 1301]"""
"9402","(9397) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us; Ibn Milhan informed us; Yahya informed me; al-Layth reported.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutayba informed us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; al-Layth reported from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) shaved his head, and a group of his Companions shaved their heads, and some of them trimmed their hair. Ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \May Allah have mercy upon those who shave their heads","\"" once or twice"," then he said: \""And upon those who trim their hair.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and they both narrated it from the hadith of 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar"," and in the fourth instance he said: \""And upon those who trim their hair.\"" [Sahih. See the preceding hadith.]\n\nAbu Hurayra also narrated something similar to it in one of the two narrations from him"," and in one narration he said in the third instance: \""And upon those who trim their hair.\"""""
"9403","(9398) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani informed us; Yunus ibn Habib informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Shu'ba reported from Yahya ibn Husayn from his grandmother: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) supplicated for those who shave their heads three times and for those who trim their hair once.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Dawud, and he added: \In the Farewell Pilgrimage.\"" The Sheikh said: His grandmother was Umm Husayn al-Ahmasiyya. [Sahih. Muslim 1303. Tayalisi 1655]"""
"9404","(9399) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan reported from Ibn Abi Husayn from Abu 'Ali al-Azdi, who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) say to the one shaving his head: \Reach to the bone.\"" [Hasan. Shafi'i 938]"""
"9405","(9400) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath reported from Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to Mina, then came to the Jamra and stoned it. Then he came to his dwelling in Mina and sacrificed. Then he said to the barber: \Take","\"" and he pointed to his right side"," then to his left side"," and he began to give it to the people.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Ibn 'Awn from Muhammad ibn Sirin. [Sahih. Bukhari 169. Muslim 1305]"""
"9406","(9401) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sulayman reported from 'Amr ibn Dinar, who said: A barber informed me that he trimmed the hair of Ibn 'Abbas, and he said: \Begin with the right side.\"" [Da'if. Shafi'i 1697]"""
"9407","(9402) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Bahlul narrated to us; Mu'ammal ibn Ihhab narrated to us; Yahya al-Jariyy narrated from Abd al-Aziz from Ubayd Allah from Nafi' from Ibn Umar regarding the bald man: he should pass the razor over his head.\n\nAnd this was narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar al-Umari from Nafi' from Ibn Umar as a mawquf (stopped) narration.\n\n[Weak. Al-Daraqutni 2/256]"
"9408","(9403) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quq narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us from Nafi': that Ibn Umar, when he shaved his head during Hajj or Umrah, would trim his beard and his moustache.\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Nafi', adding therein: \and his nails.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj said: I said to Ata': \""What do you think if he does not do any of that?\"" He said: \""Allah only said: {Some having your heads shaved"," and some having your hair trimmed} [al-Fath: 27].\""\n\n[Sahih. Malik 889]"""
"9409","(9404) Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us; Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr, i.e., ibn Shaybah, informed me from Safiyyah bint Shaybah ibn Uthman from Umm Uthman bint Abi Sufyan that Ibn Abbas said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: {\There is no shaving (halq) upon women; upon women is only trimming (taqsir).\""}\n\n[Sahih. Abu Dawud 1985]"""
"9410","(9405) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ataki informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Ibn Jurayj said: \It reached me from Safiyyah bint Shaybah ibn Uthman","\"" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Sahih. Abu Dawud 1984]"""
"9411","(9406) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quq narrated to us; al-Sariyy ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated from Ibn Ata' from Safiyyah bint Shaybah from Umm Uthman from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: {\There is no shaving (halq) upon women; upon women is only trimming (taqsir).\""} Ibn Ata' is Ya'qub ibn Ata'.\n\n[Sahih. Al-Daraqutni 2/271]"""
"9412","(9407) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; Abu Yunus Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Hafari narrated to us; Huraym narrated from Layth from Nafi' from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the woman in ihram: she should take from her hair the extent of a fingertip.\n\nAnd it is narrated from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \We used to perform Hajj and Umrah"," and we would not exceed trimming the extent of a finger.\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from Ata' that he said: \""She should take from the abundance of her hair.\""\n\n[Weak. Al-Daraqutni 2/271]"""
"9413","(9408) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari, Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran, and Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukri all said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Umar ibn Dharr from Mujahid who said: \Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) would perform talbiyah during Umrah until he touched the Black Stone"," then he would stop.\""\n\nHe said: \""And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would perform talbiyah during Umrah until he saw the houses of Makkah"," whereupon he would leave the talbiyah and turn to takbir and dhikr until he touched the Black Stone.\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"9414","(9409) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us; Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us; Abd al-Malik, i.e., ibn Abi Sulayman, said: \Ata' was asked: 'When does the one performing Umrah stop the talbiyah?' He said: 'Ibn Umar said: When he enters the Haram. And Ibn Abbas said: Until he touches the Black Stone.' I said: 'O Abu Muhammad"," which of the two is more beloved to you?' He said: 'The statement of Ibn Abbas.'\""\n\n[Sahih]"""
"9415","(9410) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both said: Abu al-Abbas al-Asamm informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Muslim ibn Khalid and Sa'id ibn Salim informed us from Ibn Jurayj from Ata' from Ibn Abbas who said: \The one performing Umrah continues the talbiyah until he begins the Tawaf"," whether touching (the Black Stone) or not.\""\n\nAnd similarly Ibn Jurayj and Hammam narrated it from Ata' from Ibn Abbas as a mawquf (stopped) narration. And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated it from Ata' and raised it (to the Prophet).\n\n[Sahih. Al-Shafi'i 1695]"""
"9416","(9411) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quq narrated to us; al-Abbas al-Dawri narrated to us; Shadhan narrated to us; Zuhayr and al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated from Ibn Abi Layla from Ata' from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): that he would perform talbiyah during Umrah until he touched the Black Stone, and during Hajj until he stoned the Jamrah.\n\n[Munkar. Abu Dawud 1817. Al-Tirmidhi 919]"
"9417","(9412) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us; Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabī' reported; al-Shāfi'ī said: Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from 'Aṭā' from Ibn 'Abbās that the Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah during 'Umrah until he touched the Corner (al-Rukn). However, we are cautious about his narration because we found the ḥuffāẓ of the Makkans stopping it at Ibn 'Abbās (i.e., making it a mawqūf report). Al-Shaykh said: Raising it to the Prophet ﷺ is an error, for this Ibn Abī Laylā was prone to frequent error, especially when narrating from 'Aṭā', in which case he made many mistakes. The scholars of transmission declared him weak, despite his high standing in jurisprudence.\n\nIt has also been narrated from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from 'Aṭā' as a marfū' report, and its chain is even weaker than what we have mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9418","(9413) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Ḥafṣ, who is ibn Ghiyāth, narrated from Ḥajjāj from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet ﷺ performed three 'Umrahs, and in each of them he did not discontinue the talbiyah until he touched the Black Stone.\n\nIt has also been said: from Ḥajjāj from 'Aṭā' from Ibn 'Abbās as a marfū' report. But Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭā' is not used as a proof.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Abū Bakrah as a marfū' report: that he went out with him during one of his 'Umrahs and he did not discontinue the talbiyah until he touched the Black Stone, but its chain is weak. [Weak. Aḥmad 2/180. Ibn Abī Shaybah 14003]"
"9419","(9414) Abū Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn 'Adī informed us; Muḥammad ibn 'Abdah informed us; 'Amr ibn Mālik informed us; 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Uthmān informed us; Baḥr ibn Marrār ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah narrated from his grandfather 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah from his father: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for one of his 'Umrahs and I went out with him, and he did not discontinue the talbiyah until he touched the Black Stone. This chain is not strong, and Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"9420","(9415) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; 'Abbās al-Asfaṭī informed us; Ismā'īl informed us; Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from 'Urwah from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we entered into iḥrām for 'Umrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him"," let him enter into iḥrām for Ḥajj along with the 'Umrah"," and let him not exit from iḥrām until he exits from both of them together.\"" She said: I arrived (in Makkah) while I was menstruating"," so I did not perform ṭawāf of the House nor of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: \""Undo your head (hair) and comb it"," and enter into iḥrām for Ḥajj"," and leave the 'Umrah.\"" She said: I did so. When we had completed the Ḥajj"," he sent me with 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr to al-Tan'īm"," and I performed 'Umrah. He said: \""This is in place of your 'Umrah.\"" She said: Those who had entered into iḥrām for 'Umrah performed ṭawāf of the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," then exited from iḥrām"," then performed another ṭawāf after returning from Minā for their Ḥajj. As for those who had combined Ḥajj and 'Umrah"," they performed only one ṭawāf.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4134. Muslim 1281]"""
"9421","(9416) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs informed us; 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī informed us; al-Qa'nabī, in what he read to Mālik; and Abū 'Abd Allāh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik, and he mentioned the hadith similarly.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qa'nabī, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nAl-Shāfi'ī and Ibn Bukayr narrated it from Mālik likewise, and they added: \As for those who entered into iḥrām for Ḥajj or combined Ḥajj and 'Umrah"," they performed only one ṭawāf.\""\n\nAs for the hadith of al-Shāfi'ī"," it is in the narration of al-Muzanī from him. As for the hadith of Ibn Bukayr… [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9422","(9417) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik narrated, and he mentioned it. 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, intended by her statement about them that they performed only one ṭawāf—the sa'ī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah—and this is also clear in the narration of Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"
"9423","(9418) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us; they said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhāb ibn 'Aṭā' informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh that he said: The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions did not perform ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah except one ṭawāf—their first ṭawāf.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān and Muḥammad ibn Bakr from Ibn Jurayj.\n\nThis is because the Prophet ﷺ, as far as we know, was performing ifrād (Ḥajj only), and some of his Companions were performing qirān (combined Ḥajj and 'Umrah), so they sufficed with one sa'ī. As for 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she was a qārinah (one who combined Ḥajj and 'Umrah) by incorporating the Ḥajj upon the 'Umrah, and she did not perform ṭawāf of the House nor of al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah before 'Arafah. She performed ṭawāf after that of the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1215. Abū Dāwūd 1895]"
"9424","(9419) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad 'Abd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; they said: Abū Muḥammad 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī informed us in Makkah; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah informed us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfi' narrated from 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she menstruated at Sarif and became pure at 'Arafah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \One ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah will suffice you for your Ḥajj and your 'Umrah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥulwānī from Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb from Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfi'. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1211]"""
"9425","(9420) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us; al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from 'Aṭā' that the Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ā'ishah: \Your ṭawāf of the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah will suffice you for your Ḥajj and your 'Umrah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfi'ī 512]"""
"9426","(9421) With its chain, he said: al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from 'Aṭā' from 'Ā'ishah from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. Al-Shāfi'ī said: And sometimes Sufyān said, from 'Aṭā' from 'Ā'ishah, and sometimes he said, from 'Aṭā' that the Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ā'ishah. Al-Shaykh said: Ibn Abī 'Umar narrated it from Sufyān as a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfi'ī 513. Abū Dāwūd 1897]"
"9427","(9422) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani', Ibrahim ibn 'Ismat ibn Ibrahim, and Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: al-Sari ibn Khuzayma narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated to us: Ibn Tawus narrated from his father, from 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her), that she entered into ihram for 'Umra. She arrived without having performed Tawaf of the House, and then she menstruated. She performed all the rites, having entered into ihram for Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to you: \Your Tawaf shall suffice you for both your Hajj and your 'Umra.\"" But she refused"," so he sent her with 'Abd al-Rahman to al-Tan'im"," and she performed 'Umra after the Hajj.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Bahz ibn Asad from Wuhaib. [Sahih. Muslim 1218]"""
"9428","(9423) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq informed us: Harun ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us. And Abu 'Abdullah informed us, and Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed me: Abu 'Aruba informed us: al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered upon 'A'isha while she was weeping. He said: \What is the matter with you that you are weeping?\"" She said: \""I weep because the people have exited the state of ihram and I have not exited"," and they have performed Tawaf of the House and I have not performed Tawaf"," and this Hajj has now arrived.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," this is a matter that Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Adam. Perform ghusl and enter into ihram for Hajj"," then perform Hajj.\"" She said: \""So I did that. When I became pure"," he said: 'Perform Tawaf of the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa"," then you have exited from your Hajj and your 'Umra.'\"" She said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I find in my heart regarding my 'Umra that I did not perform Tawaf until I had performed Hajj.\"" He said: \""Take her"," O 'Abd al-Rahman"," and have her perform 'Umra from al-Tan'im.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim and 'Abd ibn Humayd from Muhammad ibn Bakr. [Sahih. Muslim 1211]"""
"9429","(9424) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, dictating from the original of his book: Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to me: My father narrated to me from Matar al-Warraq, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her), during the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), entered into ihram for 'Umra. When she was at Sarif, she menstruated, and this distressed her greatly. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \You are among the daughters of Adam; what befalls them befalls you.\"" When she arrived at al-Batha'"," the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded her"," and she entered into ihram for Hajj. When she completed her rites and came to al-Hasba'"," she wished to perform 'Umra. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: \""You have indeed completed your Hajj and your 'Umra.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was an easygoing man; when she desired something"," he would accommodate her in it. Matar said: Abu al-Zubayr said: 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her)"," when she performed Hajj"," would do as she had done.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn 'Abd al-Wahid. [Sahih. Muslim 1213]"""
"9430","(9425) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abdullah informed me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us: My father narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah narrated from Nafi', who said: Ibn 'Umar intended to perform Hajj when al-Hajjaj descended upon Ibn al-Zubayr. His two sons, Salim and 'Abdullah, spoke to him and said: \It will not harm you if you do not perform Hajj this year. We fear that there will be fighting among the people"," and you will be prevented from reaching the House.\"" He said: \""If I am prevented from reaching the House"," then I will do as we did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when the disbelievers of Quraysh prevented him from the House — he shaved his head and returned. And I bear witness to you that I have obligated upon myself an 'Umra.\"" Then he went out to the tree and entered into ihram for 'Umra. When he ascended the heights of al-Bayda'"," he said: \""Their command is but one. If I am prevented from the 'Umra"," I am prevented from the Hajj.\"" He said: \""Bear witness that I have obligated upon myself a Hajj along with my 'Umra.\"" He had no sacrificial animal with him at that time. He proceeded until he reached Qudayd"," where he purchased a sacrificial animal. He garlanded it"," marked it"," and drove it along with him. When he entered Makkah"," he performed one Tawaf for both — of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwa. He used to say: \""Whoever combines Hajj and 'Umra"," one Tawaf suffices him"," and he does not exit the state of ihram until he exits from both of them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr. [Sahih. Muslim 1230]"""
"9431","(9426) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Adhan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us: al-'Abbas al-Asfati narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Hamza narrated to us: al-Darawardi narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa and Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Madani informed us, saying: al-Darawardi narrated from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever combines Hajj and 'Umra performs one Tawaf for both and one Sa'i for both.\"" They added in their narration: \""And he does not exit the state of ihram until he exits from both of them.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us in the hadith of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The 'Umra has been incorporated into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\"" It is said regarding its meaning: it has been incorporated into the components of the acts of Hajj"," so the two have become unified in practice. Thus"," the Qarin (one performing Hajj and 'Umra together) does not perform more than one Tawaf for both"," and likewise the Sa'i"," just as he does not enter into ihram for them except with one ihram.\n\nAnd al-Shafi'i narrated in al-Qadim from a man — whom I think to be Ibrahim ibn Muhammad — from Ja'far ibn Muhammad"," from his father"," from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said regarding the Qarin: \""He performs two Tawafs and one Sa'i.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: \""This is in accordance with our position — meaning"," he performs Tawaf when he arrives"," of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwa"," then he performs Tawaf of the House for the Tawaf of Visitation (Ziyara).\"" Some people have said: \""Upon him are two Tawafs and two Sa'is","\"" and they cited in support of this a weak narration from 'Ali and Ja'far"," who narrated from 'Ali our position. And it has been narrated to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Shaykh said: \""The most authentic narration regarding the two Tawafs from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) is what...\""\n\n[Munkar. al-Tahawi in Sharh al-Ma'ani 2/197]"""
"9432","(9427) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id informed us: Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us: Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us: Mansur narrated from Ibrahim, from Malik ibn al-Harith — or Mansur narrated from Malik ibn al-Harith — from Abu Nasr, who said: I met 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) while I had entered into ihram for Hajj and he had entered into ihram for Hajj and 'Umra. I said: \Am I able to do as you have done?\"" He said: \""That would be possible had you begun with the 'Umra.\"" I said: \""How should I do it if I wish to do that?\"" He said: \""Take a vessel of water and pour it over yourself"," then enter into ihram for both of them together. Then perform two Tawafs for them and two Sa'is for them"," and nothing forbidden shall be permissible for you before the Day of Sacrifice.\"" Mansur said: \""I mentioned that to Mujahid"," and he said: 'We used to give fatwa only with one Tawaf. But now"," we shall not do so.'\"" This is how it was narrated from Fudayl from Mansur.\n\nAnd al-Thawri narrated from Mansur"," but he did not mention the Sa'i in it. Likewise Shu'ba and Ibn 'Uyayna. And Abu Nasr is unknown. If this narration is authentic"," it is possible that what is meant by it is the Tawaf of Arrival (Qudum) and the Tawaf of Visitation (Ziyara)"," and that he intended one Sa'i"," as narrated by al-Thawri and his companions"," in which case it would not contradict the narration of Ja'far. And it has been narrated through weak chains from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"," both as a mawquf and marfu' narration"," which I have mentioned in al-Khilafiyat. The basis of that rests upon al-Hasan ibn 'Umarah and Hafs ibn Abi Dawud"," and 'Isa ibn 'Abdullah and Hammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — all of them are weak"," and nothing that they narrated from that constitutes a proof. And with Allah lies success.\n\n[Hasan li-ghayrihi. al-Daraqutni 2/265]"""
"9433","(9428) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Muzzi informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Malik informed me.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Isa al-Hayri informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Ali and Musa ibn Muhammad informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us. I read to Malik, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from 'Urwa, from 'A'isha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. Among us were those who entered into ihram for 'Umra"," among us were those who entered into ihram for Hajj and 'Umra"," and among us were those who entered into ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered into ihram for Hajj. As for those who entered into ihram for 'Umra"," they exited the state of ihram. As for those who entered into ihram for Hajj or combined Hajj and 'Umra"," they did not exit the state of ihram until the Day of Sacrifice.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Yahya ibn Yahya. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from al-Qa'bi and others from Malik. And in the hadiths that preceded it in the chapter before this"," there is evidence for this. [Sahih]"""
"9434","(9429) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Hammam narrated from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever performs Tawaf of the House seven times"," counting them"," for each step a good deed shall be recorded for him"," a sin shall be erased from him"," a degree shall be raised for him"," and it shall be equivalent to the freeing of a slave.\""\n\n[Sahih. al-Tayalisi 1900]"""
"9435","(9430) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us: Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Bazmahrani informed us: Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn 'Abdullah informed me: My father informed me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman informed me: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr al-Laythi, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever performs seven circuits and prays two rak'ats"," it shall be as if he has freed a slave.\"" He did not mention his father in its chain of narration"," and there is disagreement regarding it from 'Ata' — some of them mentioned it from him and some of them did not mention it.\n\n[Sahih. See the one before it]"""
"9436","(9431) Abu Nasr ibn Qatada and Abu Bakr al-Farisi informed us, saying: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Hushaym informed us: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr that he heard his father say to Ibn 'Umar: \Why is it that I see you touching only these two corners and not touching any others?\"" He said: \""If I do so"," then indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Indeed"," touching them both erases sins.'\"" He said: \""And I heard him say: 'Whoever performs a complete Tawaf of seven circuits and prays two rak'ats"," for him shall be the equivalent of freeing a slave. And whoever raises a foot and places another"," Allah shall record for him thereby a good deed"," erase from him thereby a sin"," and raise for him thereby a degree.'\"" This indicates that both the father and the son heard it together.\n\n[Sahih li-ghayrihi. See the one before it"," and this wording is of Ahmad 2/3 and Abu Ya'la 5688]"""
"9437","(9432) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us orally, and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us by recitation; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Najīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Bābāh, who said: I heard Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \Let me not find"," O Banū ʿAbd Manāf"," that you have prevented anyone from performing ṭawāf around this House at any hour of night or day.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9438","(9433) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Maʿmarī and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Tammār both said: Hudbah narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us from Qatādah from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ṭawāf seven times, then performed ṭawāf seven times, because he wished the people to see his strength.\n\nIn the narration of al-Maʿmarī: \He performed ṭawāf seven times and performed ṭawāf seven times"," because he wished that the people see"," or that he show the people"," his strength.\"" Others have said regarding this text: \""He performed ṭawāf seven times and performed saʿy seven times.\"" It has also been said that what is meant thereby is seven circuits around the House and seven circuits between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," in which case it would not fall under this chapter. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 1/255. Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 21827]"""
"9439","(9434) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Firās informed us in Makkah; Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Janāb narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Abī al-Janūb from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ṭawāf around the House three complete sets of seven circuits, then he came to the Maqām and prayed behind it six rakʿahs, making salām after every two rakʿahs, turning right and left. Abū Hurayrah said: He intended thereby to teach us.\n\nAl-Ṣaghānī Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq contradicted him in his isnād from Aḥmad ibn Janāb. [Munkar. Ḍuʿafāʾ al-ʿUqaylī 3/66]"
"9440","(9435) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd al-Ṣayrafī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Janāb narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Abī al-Janūb from al-Zuhrī from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh from his father, who said: I performed ṭawāf with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb around the House, and when we completed one set, we entered upon the second, so we said to him: We have completed [the ṭawāf]. He said: I did not make an error, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) combine [two sets], and I love to combine.\n\nThis is not strong. al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and ʿĀʿishah permitted this, while Ibn ʿUmar disliked it. [Munkar. See the preceding]"
"9441","(9436) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Julūdī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū Qurrah narrated to us from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), when it was before the Day of Tarwiyah, would address the people and inform them of their rites. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ḥākim 1/632]"
"9442","(9437) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Ṭabarī narrated to us; Abū Ḥummah narrated to us; Abū Qurrah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym informed me from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) returned [from his journey], he sent Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) for the Hajj, and we set out with him until, when we were at al-ʿAraj, the iqāmah for Fajr was called. When he stood to say the takbīr, he heard the grunting of a she-camel behind him, so he stopped the takbīr and said: \This is the grunting of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," al-Jadʿāʾ. It seems the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has decided to perform Hajj"," and perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) is upon it.\"" And there was ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) upon it. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""As a commander or as a messenger?\"" He said: \""Rather as a messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has sent me with Barāʾah to recite to the people at the stations of Hajj.\"" We arrived in Makkah"," and when it was the day before Tarwiyah"," Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and addressed the people"," informing them of their rites. When he finished"," ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and recited Barāʾah to the people until he completed it. Then we departed with him until"," when it was the Day of ʿArafah"," Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and addressed the people"," informing them of their rites. When he finished"," ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and recited Barāʾah to the people until he completed it. Then came the Day of Naḥr"," and we departed. When Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) returned"," he addressed the people"," informing them of their departure"," their sacrifice"," and their rites. When he finished"," ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and recited Barāʾah to the people until he completed it. When it was the Day of the First Nafar"," Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and addressed the people"," teaching them how to depart and how to perform the stoning"," and he taught them their rites. When he finished"," ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and recited Barāʾah to the people until he completed it.\n\nIsḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm similarly narrated it from Abū Qurrah Mūsā ibn Ṭāriq; Ibn Khuthaym is alone in narrating it in this manner. [Ḍaʿīf. Nasāʾī 2993. Dārimī 1915]"""
"9443","(9438) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Muqrīʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq both informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us from his father, who said: We visited Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him), and he mentioned the hadīth regarding the Hajj of the Prophet (peace be upon him). He said: Then all the people exited iḥām and cut their hair, except the Prophet (peace be upon him) and those who had sacrificial animals with them. When it was the Day of Tarwiyah and they turned towards Minā, they entered iḥām for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mounted and prayed at Minā the Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, ʿIshāʾ, and Fajr. Then he remained a little while until the sun rose. He commanded that a tent of hair be pitched for him at Namirah. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) proceeded, and Quraysh did not doubt except that he would stop at al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām, as Quraysh used to do in the Jāhiliyyah. But the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed on until he reached ʿArafah, and he found the tent had been pitched for him at Namirah, so he dismounted there.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"
"9444","(9439) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī both said: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, who said: I asked Anas ibn Mālik. I said: \Inform me of something you understood from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): where did he pray Ẓuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah?\"" He said: \""At Minā.\"" I said: \""Where did he pray ʿAṣr on the Day of Nafar?\"" He said: \""At al-Abṭaḥ.\"" Then he said: \""Do as your commanders do.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad from Isḥāq"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1570. Muslim 1309]"""
"9445","(9440) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to pray Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, ʿIshāʾ, and Fajr at Minā, then he would proceed from Minā to ʿArafah when the sun rose. The wording is that of Ibn Bukayr, and the hadīth of al-Shāfiʿī is abridged, mentioning only the proceeding. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 897]"
"9446","(9441) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abī Sulaymān, narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās from al-Faḍl, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) departed from ʿArafāt, and Usāmah was riding behind him. The she-camel swayed with him while he was standing at ʿArafāt before he departed, and he was raising his hands, not letting them go beyond his head. When he departed, he continued in his manner until he reached Jamʿ [Muzdalifah]. Then he departed from Jamʿ, and al-Faḍl was riding behind him. Al-Faḍl said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) continued saying the talbiyah until he came to the Jamrah.\n\nMuslim extracted it from the hadīth of Yazīd ibn Hārūn from ʿAbd al-Malik, and he did not mention al-Faḍl at the beginning but only mentioned him at the end. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both extracted it from the hadīth of Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1601. Muslim 1286]"
"9447","(9442) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed me — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us — al-Qa'nbi recited to Malik, and Abu 'Abd Allah informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Isa narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi and Musa ibn Muhammad al-Dhuhli said — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I read before Malik, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, that he asked Anas ibn Malik, while they were both proceeding from Mina to 'Arafah: \How did you used to behave on this day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He replied: \""The one among us who pronounced the talbiyah would do so"," and it was not objected to; and the one who pronounced the takbir would do so"," and it was not objected to.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik"," and narrated by Muslim from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 1576. Muslim 1285]"""
"9448","(9443) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me — my father narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr said; and Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed me — Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Muthanna narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, from his father, who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Mina to 'Arafah — some of us pronouncing the talbiyah and some of us pronouncing the takbir.\""\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Muthanna. [Sahih. Muslim 2284]"""
"9449","(9444) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Husayn narrated from Kathir ibn Mudrik al-Ashja'i, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that 'Abd Allah, i.e., ibn Mas'ud, pronounced the talbiyah when he departed from Jam' (al-Muzdalifah). It was said: \This is a Bedouin!\"" So 'Abd Allah said: \""I heard the one upon whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed reciting at this place: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk.'\""\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Surayj ibn Yunus. [Sahih. Muslim 1283]"""
"9450","(9445) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us — Sa'dan — and Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who mentioned it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, that his father went to Ibn al-Zubayr on the day of 'Arafah and said: \What prevented you from pronouncing the talbiyah? I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," pronouncing the talbiyah in this very place.\"" So Ibn al-Zubayr pronounced the talbiyah. [Da'if]"""
"9451","(9446) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Shayban al-Ramli narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \I heard 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," pronouncing the talbiyah at al-Muzdalifah"," so I said to him: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," what is the occasion of the ihram?' He replied: 'Have we not already completed our rites?'\"" [Hasan]"""
"9452","(9447) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Nasa'i narrated to us — Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Salih narrated from Ma'ysarah ibn Habib al-Nahdi, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'd ibn Jubayr, who said: \We were with Ibn 'Abbas at 'Arafah"," and he said: 'O Sa'd"," why do I not hear the people pronouncing the talbiyah?' I replied: 'They fear Mu'awiyah.' So Ibn 'Abbas emerged from his tent and said: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk"," even if the nose of Mu'awiyah be covered in dust. O Allah"," curse them"," for they have abandoned the Sunnah out of hatred for 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him.'\"" [Hasan. Nasa'i 2006. Ibn Khuzaymah 2830]"""
"9453","(9448) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas, i.e., al-Asamm, narrated to us — Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Asad narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from 'Ubayd Allah, i.e., ibn Abi Yazid, who heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: \Continue pronouncing the talbiyah until you reach your sacred precinct"," when you have stoned the jamrah.\"" [Hasan]"""
"9454","(9449) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us — Abu al-Jamahir narrated to us — 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Ibrahim ibn 'Uqbah, from Kurayb, the mawla of Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Ibn 'Abbas sent me with Maymunah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," on the day of 'Arafah. I followed her haudaj and I continued to hear her pronouncing the talbiyah until she stoned Jamrat al-'Aqabah"," after which she pronounced the takbir.\"" And we have also received a narration concerning this from al-Husayn ibn 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with them both. [Hasan]"""
"9455","(9450) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us — Muhadir narrated to us — Hisham.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Quraysh and those who followed their religion used to halt at al-Muzdalifah"," and they were called the Hums"," while the rest of the Arabs used to halt at 'Arafah. When Islam came"," Allah commanded His Prophet ﷺ to come to 'Arafah and halt there"," then to depart from it. That is the statement of Allah: {Then depart from where the people depart.} The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah. Narrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from 'Ali from Abu Mu'awiyah"," and narrated by Muslim from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 4248. Muslim 1219]"""
"9456","(9451) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us — Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razaq informed us — al-Thawri narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Quraysh said: 'We are the inhabitants of the House; we shall not go beyond the Sacred Precinct.' So Allah"," Glorified and Exalted is He"," revealed: {Then depart from where the people depart.}\"" [Sahih. See the preceding hadith.]"""
"9457","(9452) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb al-Bajalī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from his father, who said:\n\n\I lost a camel of mine and went out searching for it on the day of ʿArafah. I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) standing at ʿArafah"," so I said: 'By Allah"," this man is from the Ḥums — what is the matter with him?'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Sufyān.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1581. Muslim 1220]"""
"9458","(9453) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū Aḥmad ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me; Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us. Abū Bakr said: ʿImrān narrated to us; ʿUthmān narrated to us; both said: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, and he mentioned the hadith similarly, except that he said: \This is from the Ḥums — what is the matter with him that he has come out of the Ḥaram?\"" Sufyān said"," meaning Quraysh"," who were called the Ḥums"," and Quraysh used not to go beyond the Ḥaram"," saying: 'We are the people of Allah; we do not go out of the Ḥaram.' Thus the rest of the people would stand at ʿArafah"," and that is the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Then depart from where the people depart} [al-Baqarah: 199]. Sufyān said: \""Al-Aḥmas means one who is strict in his religion.\"" Al-Ismāʿīlī said: The hadith of Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah ends at his words 'from the Ḥums — what is the matter with him?' here.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9459","(9454) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us; both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father, who said:\n\n\We entered upon Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him) and he mentioned the hadith regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet (ﷺ) and his descent at Namirah. He said: 'Until when the sun passed its zenith"," he ordered al-Qaṣwāʾ"," so it was saddled for him"," and he rode until he reached the bottom of the valley. He addressed the people and mentioned the hadith of his sermon as has preceded in this hadith"," where we have cited it with its full context in this book. Then Bilāl gave the adhān"," then he pronounced the iqāmah and prayed Ẓuhr. Then he pronounced the iqāmah and prayed ʿAṣr"," and he did not pray anything between them.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n[Munkar 121]"""
"9460","(9455) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and others narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, regarding the Ḥajj of Islam, who said:\n\n\The Prophet (ﷺ) departed for the standing place at ʿArafah and addressed the people with the first sermon. Then Bilāl gave the adhān. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) began the second sermon. When he finished the sermon and Bilāl had finished the adhān"," Bilāl pronounced the iqāmah and he prayed Ẓuhr. Then he pronounced the iqāmah and prayed ʿAṣr.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā is alone in this detailed narration. And in the hadith of Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl there is evidence that he delivered a sermon and then Bilāl gave the adhān"," except that there is no mention in it of the Prophet (ﷺ) beginning the second sermon. And Allah knows best.\n[Munkar 121]"""
"9461","(9456) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us; Abū ʿImrān Ibrāhīm ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us; al-Ramādī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr and Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated that al-Layth narrated to both of them, saying: ʿUqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Sālim informed me that al-Ḥajjāj asked Ibn ʿUmar: 'How should one act at the standing place on the day of ʿArafah?' Sālim said: 'If you wish to follow the Sunnah, then hasten the prayer on the day of ʿArafah.' Ibn ʿUmar said: 'He has spoken the truth. They used to combine Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr on the day of ʿArafah in accordance with the Sunnah.' Ibn Shihāb said: 'I asked Sālim: Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do that?' Sālim said: 'Do they follow anything other than his Sunnah?'\\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it"," saying: \""And al-Layth narrated.\"" And it has been narrated from Nāfiʿ that Ibn ʿUmar used to combine the two when he missed the prayer with the imām on the day of ʿArafah. And from Ibn Jurayj from ʬāʾ: 'If he wishes"," he may combine"," and if he wishes"," he may separate.'\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 3009]"""
"9462","(9457) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us; both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rode until he reached the standing place. He turned the belly of his she-camel al-Qaṣwāʾ toward the rocks"," placed the path of the pedestrians before him"," and faced the Qiblah. He remained standing until the sun set.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"9463","(9458) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\I have stood here at ʿArafah"," and all of ʿArafah is a standing place. I have stood here at Jamʿ [al-Muzdalifah]"," and all of Jamʿ is a standing place. I have offered the sacrifice here at Minā"," and all of Minā is a place of sacrifice. So offer your sacrifices at your encampments.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth from his father.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1288]"""
"9464","(9459) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us; Ibn Jurayj said: And Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\All of ʿArafah is a standing place"," and keep clear of ʿUranah. All of al-Muzdalifah is a standing place"," and keep clear of Muḥassir.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih]"""
"9465","(9460) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd informed us; both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʬāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\n\Keep clear of ʿUranāt and keep clear of Muḥassir.\"" He said: \""And ʿUranāt is part of ʿArafāt.\"" ʬāʾ said: \""And Baṭn ʿUranah is the one in which the Mubyān is.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from ʬāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: 'It used to be said…' And it has been narrated from Abū Maʿbad from Ibn ʿAbbās"," raised to the Prophet (ﷺ).\n[Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Ibn Khuzaymah 2817. Ḥākim 1/633]"""
"9466","(9461) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us in Marw; Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ziyād ibn Saʿd, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Abū Maʿbad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Keep clear of Baṭn ʿUranah and keep clear of Muḥassir.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Ibn Khuzaymah 2816. Ḥākim 1/633]"""
"9467","(9462) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿAlī informed us, Sufyān informed us — from Ziyād ibn Saʿd, if Allah wills; Sufyān expressed doubt — and he mentioned it, except that he said: \Raise yourselves above the valley of Muḥassir"," and keep to pebbles the size of those flung by the fingers.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ by other than this chain; see the preceding hadith.]"""
"9468","(9463) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Sufyān informed us — from ʿAmr, meaning Ibn Dīnār — who heard ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣafwān narrate from Yazīd ibn Shaybān, who said: \We were standing at ʿArafah in a place far from the place of standing"," keeping away from it. Then Ibn Mirbaʿ al-Anṣārī came to us and said: 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you. He says: \""Be at your places of these rites"," for you are upon an inheritance from the legacy of Ibrāhīh"," peace be upon him.\""'\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 1919. Tirmidhī 883.]"""
"9469","(9464) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Shaybān informed us, Sufyān informed us, and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said \from\"" twice"," and he said: \""Ibn Mirbaʿ al-Anṣārī came to us at ʿArafah while we were in a place of the standing that ʿAmr — meaning the Imam — kept away from. Then he mentioned it.\"" [Ḥasan; see the preceding.]"""
"9470","(9465) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us, ʿAbdullāh informed us — from Mālik. And Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik informed us — from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān wrote to al-Ḥajjāj ibn Yūsuf: 'Do not oppose ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar in the matter of the Ḥajj.' When the day of ʿArafah came"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar came to him when the sun had passed its zenith"," and he called out near his canopy"," 'Depart!' So al-Ḥajjāj came out to him in a dyed wrap and said: 'At this hour?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Wait for me until I pour water over myself.' He entered and performed ghusl"," then came out and walked between me and my father. I said to him: 'If you wish to follow the Sunnah today"," then shorten the khutbah and hasten the Ṣalāh.' He kept looking at ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar so that he might hear that from him. So ʿAbdullāh said: 'He has spoken the truth.'\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn Bukayr.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī and others"," and he said: \""And hasten the standing.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh that the Prophet's ﷺ arrival at the place of standing was after the sun had passed its zenith. And in Jābir's narration he said: \""So that you may learn your rites of Ḥajj.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1577.]"""
"9471","(9466) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us, Sufyān informed me, Abū al-Zubayr informed me — from Jābir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed"," and upon him was calmness"," and he commanded them with calmness"," and he said: 'Let my Ummah learn its rites of Ḥajj"," for I do not know — perhaps I shall not meet them after this year of theirs.'\"" Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj from Abī al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1297. Abū Dāwūd 1970.]"""
"9472","(9467) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation and recitation, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us by dictation, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us — from Sufyān ibn Saʿīd al-Thawrī — from Bukayr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿmur al-Dīlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The Ḥajj is ʿArafāt"," the Ḥajj is ʿArafāt. Whoever attains the night of Jamʿ before the dawn rises has attained it. The days of Minā are three days. Whoever hastens in two days"," there is no sin upon him"," and whoever delays"," there is no sin upon him.'\"" Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: \""I said to Sufyān al-Thawrī: 'There is no ḥadīth in al-Kūfah more noble or more excellent than this.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Tirmidhī 2975. Dārimī 1887. Ibn Ḥibbān 3892.]"""
"9473","(9468) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Zakariyyā — meaning Ibn Abī Zāʾidah — informed us from ʿĀmir, who said: ʿUrwah ibn Muḍarris ibn Aws ibn Ḥārithah ibn Lām narrated to me that he performed Ḥajj during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He found the people at Jamʿ, so he set out for ʿArafāt by night, departed from there, then returned to Jamʿ. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have exhausted myself and worn out my mount. Do I have a Ḥajj?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever prays with us the morning Ṣalāh and stands with us until we depart"," and has come to ʿArafāt before that"," by night or by day"," his Ḥajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 3041. Ibn Mājah 3016.]"""
"9474","(9469) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ informed us in Baghdād, Muḥammad ibn Mālik al-Shaʿīrī Abū Bakr informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿUbaydah ibn Ḥumayd informed us, ʿUrwā — meaning Abā Farwah — informed us from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿUrwah ibn Muḍarris, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have come from the mountain of Ṭayyʾ. I have worn out my mount and exhausted myself. Do I have a Ḥajj?' He said: 'Whoever stands with us at ʿArafah"," his Ḥajj is complete.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; see the preceding.]"""
"9475","(9470) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bushrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us, al-Thawrī and Mālik informed us — from Abī al-Naḍr.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī informed us — from Mālik ibn Anas, from what was recited to him — from Abī al-Naḍr, the mawlā of ʿUmar ibn ʿUbaydullāh, from ʿUmayr, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Umm al-Faḍl bint al-Ḥārith, that some people differed in her presence on the day of ʿArafah concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some of them said: \He is fasting","\"" and some of them said: \""He is not fasting.\"" So she sent to him a vessel of milk while he was standing on his camel at ʿArafah"," and he drank it. The wording is from the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī. And in the narration of Rūḥ it says: \""They disputed","\"" and he said: \""He drank while he was at ʿArafah"," addressing the people.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1578. Muslim 1123.]"""
"9476","(9471) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū Usāmah al-Kalbī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ḥawshab ibn ʿAqīl informed us, Mahdī al-Hajarī informed us, ʿIkrimah informed us — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited fasting on the day of ʿArafah at ʿArafah.\""\n\nThus said al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd"," but the preserved narration from ʿIkrimah is from Abī Hurayrah. [Munkar.]"""
"9477","(9472) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: they said, Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hawshab ibn 'Aqil narrated to us: from Mahdi al-Hajari, from 'Ikrimah, who said: We were in the presence of Abu Hurayrah, and he narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he forbade fasting on the Day of 'Arafah at 'Arafah.\n\nLikewise, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi reported it from Hawshab, and in the hadith of Umm al-Fadal there is sufficiency."
"9478","(9473) Abu Nasr 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Najayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated to us: from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, the mawla of Ibn 'Ayyash, from Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Kariz, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The best of supplications is the supplication on the Day of 'Arafah"," and the best of what I and the Prophets before me have said is: *La ilaha illAllahu wahdahu la sharika lahu* (There is no god but Allah"," alone"," without partner).\""\n\nThis is a *mursal* hadith. It has also been reported from Malik through another chain with a connected (*mawsul*) narration"," but its connection is weak."""
"9479","(9474) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: 'Abd al-Majid ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: from Husayn ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hashimi, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ making supplication at 'Arafah, raising his hands toward his chest like a beggar asking for food."
"9480","(9475) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Asbahani, Abu al-Shaykh, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us: from his brother, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Ubaydah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talid, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most frequent supplication of mine and of the Prophets before me at 'Arafah is: *La ilaha illAllahu wahdahu la sharika lahu"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd"," wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir* (There is no god but Allah"," alone"," without partner; to Him belongs sovereignty"," and to Him belongs praise; and He is over all things competent). O Allah"," place light in my heart"," light in my hearing"," and light in my sight. O Allah"," expand my breast for me and ease my affair for me. I seek refuge in You from the whisperings of the chest"," the disarray of affairs"," and the trial of the grave. O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the evil of what enters the night"," the evil of what enters the day"," the evil of what the winds carry"," and the evil of the calamities of time.\""\n\nMusa ibn 'Ubaydah is the sole narrator of this hadith"," and he is weak (*da'if*)"," and his brother 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," did not meet him.\n\nAnd it has been reported to us from Abu Shu'bah that he said: I kept watch over Ibn 'Umar while he was at 'Arafah to hear what he was supplicating. He did not add to saying: *La ilaha illAllahu wahdahu la sharika lahu"," lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd"," wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir*."""
"9481","(9476) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Faddal al-Qattan informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us. And Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Faddal al-Qattan also informed us: Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us: Musa ibn Harun ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, saying: I saw al-Hasan al-Basri on the Day of 'Arafah after the 'Asr prayer; he sat and made supplication and mentioned Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, and the people gathered around him.\n\nIn the narration of Muslim: I saw al-Hasan come out on the Day of 'Arafah from the *maqsurah* after the 'Asr prayer, and he sat, and he was recognized."
"9482","(9477) Abu al-Fath, the Sharif, informed us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us: Shu'bah said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about the gathering of people in the mosques on the Day of 'Arafah, and they both said: It is an innovation (*muhdath*). And from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: It is an innovation.\n\nAnd from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: The first one to do that was Ibn 'Abbas."
"9483","(9478) Abu Mansur Dhufur ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Husayni, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — by dictation — in Kufah: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mati narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharazah narrated to us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us: from Abu al-'Umayth, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: \O Commander of the Faithful"," a verse in your Book which you recite — if it had been revealed upon us"," the assembly of the Jews"," we would have taken that day as a festival.\"" He said: \""Which verse?\"" He said: *{Al-yawma akmaltu lakum dinakum wa atmantu 'alaykum ni'mati wa radaytu lakum al-islaman dinan}* (This day I have perfected for you your religion"," completed My favor upon you"," and approved for you Islam as your religion). 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""We know that day and the place in which it was revealed. It was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Arafat on a Friday.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari reported it in the *Sahih* from al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah"," and Muslim reported it from 'Abd ibn Humayd"," both from Ja'far ibn 'Awn."""
"9484","(9479) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us: Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us: from his father, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: A Jew said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: \If this verse had been revealed upon us"," the assembly of the Jews — *{Al-yawma akmaltu lakum dinakum wa atmantu 'alaykum ni'mati wa radaytu lakum al-islaman dinan}* — we would have known the day in which it was revealed"," and we would have taken that day as a festival.\"" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I know the place in which it was revealed"," the day"," and the hour. It was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were at 'Arafah"," on the evening of a Friday.\""\n\nMuslim reported it in the *Sahih* from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others"," from 'Abd Allah ibn Idris."""
"9485","(9480) Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Munqidh al-Khulani narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhrah ibn Bukayr narrated to us: from his father, who said: I heard Yusuf ibn Yusuf narrating from Sa'id al-Musayyib, from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no day on which Allah frees more servants from the Fire than the Day of 'Arafah. Indeed"," He draws near"," then boasts of them to the angels"," saying: 'What did these people want?'\""\n\nMuslim reported it in the *Sahih* from Harun ibn Sa'id and others"," from Ibn Wahb."""
"9486","(9481) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Asbahani informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Qattan narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi 'Isa al-Hilali narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to me: a son of Kinanah ibn al-'Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami narrated to me: from his father, from his grandfather, 'Abbas ibn Mirdas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated on the evening of 'Arafah for his *ummah* with forgiveness and mercy, and he prolonged the supplication. Then Allah, the Most High, revealed to him: \I have done it"," except for the injustice of some of them toward others. As for their sins between Me and them"," I have forgiven them.\"" He said: \""O Lord"," You are able to reward this wronged one with better than his wrong"," and to forgive this wrongdoer.\"" He was not answered that evening. When it was the morning of Muzdalifah"," he repeated the supplication"," and Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," answered him: \""I have forgiven them.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled"," and one of his Companions said to him: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you have smiled at a time in which you do not usually smile.\"" He said: \""I smiled at the enemy of Allah"," Iblis. When he learned that Allah had answered me regarding my *ummah*"," he fell supplicating destruction and ruin"," and began casting dust upon his head.\"""""
"9487","(9482) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed me, both saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us from his father, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \He (peace and blessings be upon him) remained standing until the sun had set and the yellow light had faded somewhat"," when the disc had disappeared. He seated Usāmah ibn Zayd behind him"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out"," having drawn tight the reins of al-Qaṣwāʾ so that her head was almost touching the front of his saddle"," and he was saying with his right hand: 'Calmness"," calmness!' Whenever he came to a mountain pass"," he would loosen the reins slightly for her until she ascended"," until he reached al-Muzdalifah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9488","(9483) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us; ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned around at ʿArafah during the departure while the people were rushing"," and he said: 'Calmness"," O people"," for righteousness is not in hastening.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam"," from Ibrāhīm ibn Suwayd"," from ʿAmr"," with a more complete chain than this. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1587]"""
"9489","(9484) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated from al-Aʿmash, from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from ʿArafah in a state of calmness"," with Usāmah as his companion riding behind him"," and he said: 'O people"," observe calmness"," for righteousness is not in urging on the horses and camels.' He said: 'I did not see her raising her feet in a galloping manner until he reached Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1930. Ṭayālisī 2702]"""
"9490","(9485) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us; Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qays ibn Saʿd, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from ʿArafah and I was riding behind him. He kept pulling back his mount so that the tips of her ears were almost touching the front of the saddle"," and he was saying: 'O people"," observe calmness and solemnity"," for righteousness is not in hastening the camels.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 5/107. Nasāʾī 3018]"""
"9491","(9486) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, who said: \Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked — while I was sitting — 'How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) travel during the Farewell Pilgrimage when he set out?' He said: 'He would travel at a moderate pace (al-ʿanaq)"," and when he found an open space"," he would urge his mount forward (naṣṣ).'\""\n\nHishām said: \""Al-Naṣṣ (urging forward) is faster than al-ʿanaq (moderate pace).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it through various routes from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1583. Muslim 1286]"""
"9492","(9487) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū ʿAbdillāh Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ṣūfī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed me; Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah narrated from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from ʿArafāt. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the left mountain pass before al-Muzdalifah"," he dismounted and urinated. Then he came"," and I poured water for him"," and he performed a light ablution. I said: 'The prayer"," O Messenger of Allah!' He said: 'The prayer is ahead of you.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) rode until he reached al-Muzdalifah and prayed. Then al-Faḍl rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the morning of Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah).\"" Kurayb said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās informed me from al-Faḍl that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued saying the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Ismāʿīl"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and others. Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated it from Kurayb and said: \""The mountain pass through which the commanders enter.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1086. Muslim 1280]"""
"9493","(9488) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī informed us verbally, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar ibn Fāris Abū Muḥammad informed us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, from Usāmah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When he reached the mountain pass through which the commanders enter"," he entered it and called for water and performed ablution. I said: 'The prayer!' He said: 'The prayer is ahead of you.' When he reached al-Muzdalifah"," he called the Iqāmah and prayed Maghrib. The last of the people had not yet arrived when he called the Iqāmah and prayed ʿIshāʾ.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9494","(9489) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Bazmahrānī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \I asked Usāmah ibn Zayd: 'What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do when he departed from ʿArafah?' He said: 'He departed from ʿArafah until"," when he was near the mountain pass"," he turned toward it and dismounted and urinated. I brought him water and he performed a light ablution. I said: 'Shall you not pray?' He said: 'The prayer is ahead of you.' Then he rode until he reached Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah) and dismounted and performed his ablution for the prayer. Then he prayed the Maghrib prayer — three rakʿahs — and then he prayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer — two rakʿahs — and there was no supererogatory prayer between them.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9495","(9490) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn Hārūn ibn Ibrāhīm al-Naḥwī narrated to us in Baghdād; Isḥāq ibn Ṣadaqah narrated to us; Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Sulaymān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me; ʿAdiyy ibn Thābit informed me; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī informed me; Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed Maghrib and the last ʿIshāʾ at al-Muzdalifah during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Khālid ibn Makhlad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1590. Muslim 1287]"""
"9496","(9491) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me; ʿAdiyy ibn Thābit informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī narrated to him; Abū ʿAbdillāh informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated from what he read to Mālik, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAdiyy ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī, that Abū Ayyūb (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him: \He prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at al-Muzdalifah together.\"" The narration of Sulaymān did not include the word \""together\"" (jamīʿan).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9497","(9492) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, and Mālik informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh informed me, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ prayers at Muzdalifah together.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 703. Mālik 898]"
"9498","(9493) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Mālik ibn Anas and Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ prayers at Muzdalifah together. Ibn Abī Dhiʾb said in the hadith: \The adhān was not called for either of them separately; only an iqāmah was made for each"," and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer between them or after either of them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," and he said in the hadith: \""He combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah)"," with an iqāmah for each of them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1589]"""
"9499","(9494) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, Abū Khaythamah narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ combined the two prayers at Muzdalifah, and he performed each of them with an iqāmah, and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer before either of them or after them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9500","(9495) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥammāmī al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī al-Khaṭabī narrated to us, Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ prayers and called the iqāmah for each one. The difference of the narrators regarding it from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿUmar has already been mentioned in the Book of Prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9501","(9496) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Birtī narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, and Sufyān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, my father narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, and Sufyān narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ prayers at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah). It was said to him: \What is this prayer"," O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" He said: \""I performed both of them — the Maghrib as three rakʿahs and the ʿIshāʾ as two rakʿahs — with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place"," with a single iqāmah.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1288]"""
"9502","(9497) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \Until he came to al-Muzdalifah"," and he prayed there the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with one adhān and two iqāmahs"," and he did not pray anything between them.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"9503","(9498) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Zurʿah ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Dimashqī narrated to us, Aḥmad — meaning Ibn Khālid al-Wahbī — narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: \I went out with Ibn Masʿūd to Makkah"," and he continued reciting the talbiyah. A Bedouin heard him on the evening of ʿArafah and said: 'Who is this one reciting the talbiyah in this place?' I heard Ibn Masʿūd reciting the talbiyah"," saying: 'Labbayka"," number of the particles of dust"," labbayka — I have not heard him say this before or after.' Then we came to Jamʿ (Muzdalifah)"," and he led us in the two prayers"," each prayer separately with an adhān and an iqāmah"," and the evening meal was between them. Then he prayed the Fajr prayer when the dawn rose"," and he said: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""These two prayers are shifted from their times in this place\"" — meaning the Maghrib and the Fajr — \""and the people do not arrive at Jamʿ until they have performed the ʿIshāʾ.\""' He prayed the Fajr at this hour"," then he stood until it became bright"," and he said: 'If the Commander of the Faithful' — meaning ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him — 'were to depart now"," he would have followed the Sunnah.' I do not know whether he said that before ʿUthmān's departure or after ʿUthmān's departure. Then he did not stop the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rajāʾ from Isrāʾīl. Imām Aḥmad said: \""I did not confirm from them his statement 'they are shifted from their times.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1599. \""They are shifted from their times.\""]\n\nWe have narrated in the Book of Prayer from al-Aswad from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he did the same."""
"9504","(9499) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿUrbah al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Bajalī narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, and Abū Isḥāq narrated to us. He said: \I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd say: 'ʿAbdullāh performed Ḥajj' — and he mentioned the hadith — he said: 'We came to al-Muzdalifah at the time of the adhān for the ʿIshāʾ or close to that"," and he ordered a man"," so he called the adhān and the iqāmah. Then he prayed the Maghrib"," and after it he prayed two rakʿahs. Then he called for his evening meal. Then he ordered' — Zuhayr doubted — 'so he called the adhān and the iqāmah. Then he prayed the ʿIshāʾ as two rakʿahs.' And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Khālid from Zuhayr"," and Zuhayr attributed the wording of \""al-taḥwīl\"" (the shifting) to ʿAbdullāh.\n\nWe have narrated in the Book of Prayer from al-Aswad from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he did the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1591]"""
"9505","(9500) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, and Mālik ibn Anas informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, and al-Qaʿnabī narrated from what he read to Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, that he heard him say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ʿArafah"," and when he was in the valley"," he stopped and urinated"," then he performed wuḍūʾ but did not perform it thoroughly. I said to him: 'The prayer!' He said: 'The prayer is ahead of you.' So he mounted"," and when he came to al-Muzdalifah"," he stopped and performed wuḍūʾ thoroughly. Then the iqāmah for the prayer was called"," and he prayed the Maghrib. Then every person made his camel kneel at his place. Then the iqāmah for the ʿIshāʾ was called"," and he prayed it"," and he did not pray anything between them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 139. Muslim 1280]"""
"9506","(9501) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, and Kurayb informed me that he asked Usāmah ibn Zayd. He said: \Tell me"," how did you do or what you did on the evening when you were the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He said: \""We came to the valley where the people make their camels kneel for the overnight stop"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his she-camel kneel. Then he urinated\"" — Zuhayr said: \""he poured water\"" — \""then he called for wuḍūʾ and performed a wuḍūʾ that was not very thorough. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," the prayer!' He said: 'The prayer is ahead of you.' He said: 'So he mounted until we came to al-Muzdalifah"," and he called the iqāmah for the Maghrib. Then the people made their camels kneel at their places"," and they did not untie their loads until the iqāmah for the ʿIshāʾ was called"," and he prayed. Then the people untied their loads.' He said: 'I said: How did you do when morning came?' He said: \""Al-Faḍl was his riding companion"," and I went on foot among the vanguard of Quraysh.\"" Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Yaḥyā ibn Ādam from Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1280]"""
"9507","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'quob al-Hafiz narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It is the Sunnah of Hajj that the Imam lead the Dhuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, 'Isha', and Subh prayers at Mina, then proceed to 'Arafah and rest wherever he finds space. When the sun passes its zenith, he should deliver the sermon to the people, then pray Dhuhr and 'Asr combined. He should then stand at 'Arafat until the sun sets, then depart and pray at Muzdalifah or wherever Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, decrees. He should then stand at Jam' (Muzdalifah) until the sky becomes bright, then set out before the sun rises. When he pelts the largest Jamrah, everything that had been forbidden to him becomes permissible except women and perfume, until he visits the House (the Ka'bah)."
"9508","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi narrated to me that 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah narrated to him that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdillah narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \All of 'Arafah is a standing place"," and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place"," and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice"," and all the paths of Makkah are a road and a place of sacrifice.\"""""
"9509","Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyabi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated. And Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Asadi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Zayd ibn 'Ali, from his father, from 'Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stood at 'Arafah and said: \This is 'Arafah"," and it is the standing place"," and all of 'Arafah is a standing place.\"" Then he departed from 'Arafah when the sun had set"," with Usamah seated behind him"," and he was proceeding at his measured pace while the people rushed to the right and left. He did not turn toward them"," saying: \""O people"," observe tranquility.\"" He continued until he reached Jam' (Muzdalifah)"," where he prayed the two prayers combined. When morning came"," he went to Quzah and stood upon it"," saying: \""This is Quzah"," and it is the standing place"," and all of Jam' is a standing place.\"" And he said"," referring to Mina: \""This is the place of sacrifice"," and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Muqri'. The hadith of Ibn 'Abdan ends at his words \""he prayed the two prayers","\"" and it states: \""He urged on his camel\"" instead of \""he was proceeding at his measured pace.\"" The remainder carries the same meaning."""
"9510","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated from Shu'bah, from Abi Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I asked 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr while he was standing at 'Arafah about al-Mash'ar al-Haram. He remained silent until he departed and the feet of the mounts scraped against those mountains. Then he said: \This is al-Mash'ar al-Haram.\"" Thus said 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr"," and it is also said 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar."""
"9511","Abu 'Abdillah and Abu Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; Ibrahim narrated to us; Abu Hudhayfah narrated from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about al-Mash'ar al-Haram, and he said: \It is what lies between the two mountains of Jam' (Muzdalifah).\"" And it has been narrated from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah that he said: \""I think that the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," alighted on the night of Jam' at the places where the Imams now alight on the night of Jam'.\"""""
"9512","Abu 'Abdillah and Abu Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; Ibrahim narrated to us; 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated from Hushaym; al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he said regarding the verse: \Remember Allah at al-Mash'ar al-Haram\"" — he said: \""It is the mountain and what surrounds it.\"""""
"9513","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Sufyan narrated that he heard 'Ubaydillah ibn Abi Yazid say: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," sent ahead on the night of Muzdalifah from among the weak of his family.\"" In the narration of al-Shafi'i: \""I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," sent ahead from the weak of his family from Muzdalifah to Mina.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn 'Abdillah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Sufyan. And 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated it from 'Ata'"," from Ibn 'Abbas"," similarly."""
"9514","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to me; 'Ata' narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, sent me from Jam' (Muzdalifah) at the time of sahar (pre-dawn) with the belongings of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. I said to 'Ata': Did you hear Ibn 'Abbas say, \The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," sent me at night?\"" He said: \""No"," only at sahar.\"" I said: And Ibn 'Abbas said"," \""We pelted the Jamrah before dawn"," and where did he pray Fajr?\"" He said: \""No"," only at sahar.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd ibn Humayd from Muhammad ibn Bakr"," except that at the words \""at night\"" he said: \""at a long night","\"" and he said: \""No"," only at sahar.\"""""
"9515","Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," hastened me with the belongings from Jam' (Muzdalifah) at night.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb."""
"9516","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim all narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to me; Yunus ibn Yazid narrated from Ibn Shihab that Salim ibn 'Abdillah narrated to him that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to send ahead the weak of his family, and they would stand at al-Mash'ar al-Haram at Muzdalifah during the night, remembering Allah as much as they wished. Then they would set out before the Imam stood and before he departed. Some of them would arrive at Mina by the time of the Fajr prayer, and some would arrive after that. When they arrived, they would pelt the Jamrah. And Ibn 'Umar used to say: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," granted a concession for those people.\"""""
"9517","(9512) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed me — 'Ali ibn Hamshadh, the upright, narrated to me — Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us. And 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us — Ibn Milhan informed us — they both said: Ibn Bukayr narrated to me — al-Layth informed me — Yunus informed me. Ibn Shihab said: Salim said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar used to set out [early], and he mentioned the hadith in its like, identically.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr, and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Tahir and Harmalah from Ibn Wahb.\n\n[Authentic. See above.]"
"9518","(9513) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed me — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi narrated to us — al-Qa'nabi informed us — Aflah ibn Humayd informed us — from al-Qasim — from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: Sawdah sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-Muzdalifah to set out before him and before the crush of the people. She was a heavy, slow woman — al-Qasim said: \Heavy"," slow.\"" He said: \""So he gave her permission"," and she departed before the people's departure"," and he held us back until morning came. Then we departed with his departure. Had I sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah had sought permission"," and had departed with his permission before the people"," that would have been dearer to me than any joy.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym from Aflah"," and Muslim narrated it from al-Qa'nabi.\n\n[Authentic. Bukhari 1597. Muslim 1290.]"""
"9519","(9514) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid, the Qur'an reciter, both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us — from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Qasim — from his father — from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \I wished I had sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Sawdah had sought permission"," so that I could have prayed the Fajr prayer at Mina and stoned the jamrah before the people arrived.\"" They said to 'A'ishah: \""And did Sawdah seek permission?\"" She said: \""Yes. She was a heavy"," slow woman"," and he gave her permission.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Sahih from the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah"," and both [al-Bukhari and Muslim] extracted it in abridged form from the hadith of al-Thawri from 'Abd al-Rahman.\n\n[Authentic. Bukhari 1596.]"""
"9520","(9515) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us orally — Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us — from 'Amr ibn Dinar — from Salim ibn Shawwal — from Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \We used to set out at night from Jam' [Muzdalifah] to Mina during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others"," from Sufyan.\n\n[Authentic. Muslim 1292. Ahmad 6/426.]"""
"9521","(9516) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us — Abu 'Asim narrated to us — from Ibn Jurayj — from 'Ata' — from Ibn Shawwal — from Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her: \The Prophet ﷺ ordered some of his wives to set out from Jam' [Muzdalifah] at night.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Authentic. Muslim 1292.]"""
"9522","(9517) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed me — Abu 'Amr, the Qur'an reciter, and Abu Bakr, the warraq, both said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us — Hisham ibn 'Ammar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah both said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us — from his father — from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \He came to al-Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and 'Isha' with one adhan and two iqamahs"," and he did not pray anything between them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down until Fajr rose. He prayed Fajr when the morning became clear to him"," with an adhan and an iqamah. Then he mounted al-Qaswa' until he reached al-Mash'ar al-Haram"," and he stood upon it. He praised Allah"," magnified Him"," and declared His oneness"," and he did not cease standing until it became very light [at dawn]. Then he set out before the sun rose"," and he made al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas ride behind him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah.\n\n[Muslim.]"""
"9523","(9518) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, informed me — Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us — al-Sari (meaning ibn Khuzaymah) narrated to us — 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us — my father narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated to me — 'Umarah narrated to me — from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: 'Abd Allah said: \I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray a prayer outside its prescribed time"," except for two prayers: he combined Maghrib and 'Isha' at Jam' [Muzdalifah]"," and he prayed Fajr before its prescribed time.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Umar ibn Hafs"," and Muslim extracted it from two other routes from al-A'mash.\n\n[Authentic. Bukhari 1598. Muslim 1289.]"""
"9524","(9519) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — from Abu Ishaq — he said: I heard 'Amr ibn Maymun saying: \'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," I witnessed him at Jam' [Muzdalifah] after he had prayed Fajr. He stood and said: 'Indeed"," the polytheists used not to set out until the sun rose"," and they would say: \""Shine"," Thabir!\"" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ opposed them"," and set out before the sun rose.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Hajjaj ibn Minhal"," from Shu'bah.\n\n[Authentic. Bukhari 1600. Abu Dawud 1938.]"""
"9525","(9520) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi, the Hafiz, informed us orally from his memory — Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammay, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us — Ma'mar informed us. He said: Ayyub said to me while we were here: \Take us to the tent of Ja'far ibn Muhammad"," for it has reached me that he has ordered the people not to set out from Jam' [Muzdalifah] until the sun rises.\"" Ma'mar said: \""So I went with Ayyub until we came to his tent"," and lo"," there were people from the 'Alawis with him"," and he was conversing with them. When Ayyub caught his eye"," he stood and came out of his tent until he embraced Ayyub"," then took him by the hand and turned him toward another tent.\"" Ma'mar said: \""He disliked to have him sit with them.\"" He said: \""Then he called for a dish of dates and began placing them in Ayyub's hand"," and then said: 'Go to these people with a dish"," for if we send to them"," they will abandon us"," and if we do not"," they will speak ill of us.'\"" Ayyub said to him: \""What is this that has reached me about you?\"" He said: \""And what has reached you about me?\"" He said: \""It has reached me that you have ordered the people not to set out from Jam' until the sun rises.\"" He said: \""Glory be to Allah! This is contrary to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My father narrated to me from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah that the Prophet ﷺ set out from Jam' before the sun rose. But the people attribute lies to us and narrate from us what we do not say"," and they claim that we possess knowledge that the people do not have. By Allah"," some people possess knowledge that we do not have. But we have a right and a kinship.\"" He continued mentioning their right and their kinship until I saw tears flowing from Ayyub's eyes.\n\n[Authentic.]"""
"9526","(9521) Abu 'Abd Allah, the Hafiz, narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us — Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-'Ayshi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us — from Ibn Jurayj — from Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah — from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us at 'Arafah. He praised Allah and glorified Him"," then said: 'To proceed: the people of polytheism and idols used to set out from here at sunset"," when the sun would be upon the tops of the mountains like the turbans of men upon their heads — our practice being contrary to theirs. And they used to set out from al-Mash'ar al-Haram at sunrise"," when the sun would be upon the tops of the mountains like the turbans of men upon their heads — our practice being contrary to theirs.'\""\n\n'Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," from Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people on the Day of 'Arafah and said: \""This is the Day of the Greater Hajj.\"" Then he mentioned the remainder of the hadith with its meaning"," in a mursal form.\n\n[Authentic otherwise. Al-Hakim 2/304. Al-Tabrani al-Kabir 28.]"""
"9527","(9522) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yarbūʿ, from Jubayr ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, who said: I saw Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) standing upon Quzah, saying: \O people"," depart! O people"," depart!\"" Then he set off"," and I was looking at his thigh"," which had become exposed due to his prodding his camel with his crook."""
"9528","(9523) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father, from Jābir, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When he reached Muḥassir"," he urged on his mount a little.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah."""
"9529","(9524) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Abū Nuʿaym said — and Ḥafṣ informed us: Qabīṣah said — and Yūsuf al-Qāḍī and Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā said: Ibn Kathīr informed us — all of them said: Sufyān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed"," and upon him was tranquility"," and he commanded the people to observe tranquility. He hastened in the valley of Muḥassir and commanded them to pelt the jamarāt with pebbles the size of date-stones"," and he said: 'Learn from me your rites of Ḥajj"," for perhaps I shall not see you after this year of mine.'\"""""
"9530","(9525) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Asadī informed us: Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith, from Zayd ibn ʿAlī, from his father, from ʿUbaydillāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from Jamʿ until he reached Muḥassir, whereupon he urged on his she-camel until he crossed the valley. Then he halted, then he took al-Faḍl as his riding companion, then he came to the Jamrah and pelted it."
"9531","(9526) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me: Abū Bakr, who is Ibn Abī Uways, narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that Abū Maʿbad, the freedman of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, informed him that he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-ʿAbbās narrating from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \On the day of ʿArafah"," al-Faḍl was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and the people were numerous around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When the people became very numerous"," I said: 'Al-Faḍl will inform me of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did.' Al-Faḍl said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set forth"," and the people set forth with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) kept holding the reins of his camel and calling out to the people: \""Upon you is tranquility.\"" When he reached al-Muzdalifah"," he dismounted and prayed Maghrib and the last ʿIshāʾ together. When Fajr rose"," he prayed Ṣubḥ. Then he stood at al-Muzdalifah near the Mashʿar al-Ḥarām. Then he set forth"," and the people set forth with him"," holding the head of his camel"," saying: \""O people"," upon you is tranquility.\"" When he reached Muḥassir"," he hastened somewhat and said: \""Take to pebbles the size of date-stones.\""' Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways similarly narrated it from his brother."""
"9532","(9527) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Sulmān the jurist in Baghdād and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān said: Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Muʿādh ibn al-Mustahill, known as Darrān, in Ḥalab informed us: al-Qaʿnabī informed me: My father, Maslamah ibn Qaʿnab, informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to hasten and say:\n\n\Towards you it runs"," anxious and distressed","\nIts people opposing the religion of the Christians"," their religion.\""\n\nAnd Ibn al-Zubayr used to hasten with the utmost hastening"," having taken it from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," meaning the hastening in the valley of Muḥassir."""
"9533","(9528) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to urge on his mount in the belly of Muḥassir the distance of a stone's throw."
"9534","(9529) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from ʿAlqamah, from his mother, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that when she departed on the morning of al-Muzdalifah and came to the belly of Muḥassir, she said to me: \Urge on the beast and raise it up.\"" She said: \""So I urged it on one day and the beast fell upon her"," and upon her was the howdah. Then I urged it on a second time"," and Allah raised it up"," and it did not harm her at all.\"" She used to raise her beast until it crossed the belly of Muḥassir and entered the belly of Minā. Something similar has been narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd and Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them)."""
"9535","(9530) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Kathīr ibn Shinzīr, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The origin of hastening was from the Bedouins. They used to stand on the flanks of the people"," having hung up crooks and staffs. When they departed"," they rattled them and caused the people to rush ahead. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and the ears of his she-camel were touching its saddle-pad"," while he was saying: 'O people"," upon you is tranquility.'\"""""
"9536","(9531) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Wahb ibn Bayān informed us: ʿAbīdah informed us: Sulaymān al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from ʿArafah\"" — and he mentioned the hadith up to his words: \""until he reached Jamʿ.\"" He said: \""Then he took al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās as his riding companion and said: 'O people"," righteousness is not in hastening horses and camels; rather"," upon you is tranquility.' I did not see her raising her forelegs until she reached Minā.\"""""
"9537","(9532) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz reported to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir reported to us; ʿAffān reported to us; Hammām reported to us; Qatādah reported to me; ʿAzrah reported to me that al-Shaʿbī narrated to him — and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf both said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā reported to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ reported to us; Hammām reported from Qatādah, from ʿAzrah, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: Usāmah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that he departed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ʿArafah, and his mount did not raise its forelegs from a walking pace until he reached Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah). And al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that he was the one riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Jamʿ, and his mount did not raise its forelegs from a walking pace until he stoned the Jamrah. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Muqriʾ. In the narration of ʿAffān: Usāmah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the evening of ʿArafah, and when he departed… And in the second ḥadīth he said: Indeed al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās narrated to him.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ṭāwūs al-Yamānī from the Prophet ﷺ similarly, and he used to disapprove of hastening (al-iḍāʿah) the mount.\n\nAnd from ʿAṭāʾ who said: It is these people who innovated the rushing, intending to escape the dust. And the hastening of the mount in the Valley of Muḥassir has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ, and then from a group of the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them.\n\nAnd the ruling in such a matter is the position of the one who affirms it over the position of the one who denies it. And with Allah lies success. [Aḥmad 1/213; Abū Yaʿlā 6721]"
"9538","(9533) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb reported to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad reported to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Muʾaddib reported to us; Layth ibn Saʿd reported to us — and Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī reported to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ismāʿīlī reported to us; ʿĪsā ibn Ḥammād reported to us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd reported to us; Abū al-Zubayr narrated to me from Abū Maʿbad, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, from al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās, who was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: On the evening of ʿArafah and the morning of Jamʿ, when the people set forth, (the Prophet ﷺ said): \Upon you is tranquility (al-sakīnah).\"" And he was restraining his she-camel until"," when he entered Muḥassir — which is part of Minā — he said: \""Take up pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf)"," with which the Jamrah is stoned.\"" And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ"," from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1282]"""
"9539","(9534) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār reported to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī reported to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq reported to us; Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān reported to us; ʿAwf reported from Ziyād ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say — al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the morning of the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr): \Come"," pick up pebbles for me.\"" So I picked up for him pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf)"," and I placed them in his hand. He said: \""With the likes of these"," with the likes of these. And beware of excess (al-ghuluw)"," for indeed it was excess in religion that destroyed those who came before you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 3057; Ibn Mājah 3029; Aḥmad 1/215]"""
"9540","(9535) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq reported to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī reported to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr reported to us; Sufyān reported to me; Abū al-Zubayr reported from Jābir that the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to stone with pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1299]"
"9541","(9536) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī reported to us; Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh reported to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr reported to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: I saw the Prophet ﷺ stoning the Jamrah with pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim and others, from Muḥammad ibn Bakr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9542","(9537) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb reported to us; Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā reported to us; Sufyān reported from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from a man of his people, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ teaching the people their rites, and he said: \Stone the Jamrah with pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1957; Nasāʾī 2996]"""
"9543","(9538) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh reported to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān reported to me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak reported to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith reported to us; Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj reported from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿādh al-Taymī, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us while we were in Minā. He said: \Our ears were opened"," so that we could hear what he was saying even while we were in our dwellings.\"" He then began teaching us our rites until he reached the matter of the Jimār (stoning pillars)"," and he said: \""With pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\"" And he placed one index finger upon the other. And he commanded the Muhājirūn to camp in front of the mosque"," and he commanded the Anṣār"," and they camped behind the mosque. Then the people camped thereafter. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9544","(9539) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb reported to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī reported to us; Muʿādh ibn Hānīʾ al-Sukkarī reported to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān reported to me; Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād reported from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Aḥwaṣ, from his mother Umm Jundub, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoning the Jamrah from the bottom of the valley, with a man behind him shielding him from the stones, and he was saying: \O people"," let not some of you kill others. And when you stone the Jamrah"," stone with pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 1966; Aḥmad 1/604]"""
"9545","(9540) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb reported to us; Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā reported to us; Sufyān reported from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Aḥwaṣ al-Azdī, from his mother, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the bottom of the valley, stoning the Jamrah, and he was saying: \O people"," let not some of you kill others. And when you stone the Jamrah"," stone with pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. See the preceding.]"""
"9546","(9541) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd reported to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Narsī reported to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn reported to us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh reported from Abū Yazīd, the freedman of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith, meaning from Umm Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O people"," do not kill yourselves at the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah"," and upon you is (to use) pebbles the size of date-stones (ḥaṣā al-khadhf).\"" Al-Ḥajjāj said: And ʿAṭāʾ said: \""Pebbles the size of date-stones are like the tip of a finger.\"" Our shaykh did not mention Umm Jundub by name"," and she is Umm Jundub. Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ said this from Yazīd ibn Hārūn.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: I asked al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth"," and he said: Her name is Umm Jundub. I said: Then the ḥadīth of al-Ḥajjāj? He said: I think al-Ḥajjāj took it from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād"," and I believe it is the ḥadīth of Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr from his mother.\n\n[Bāṭil. Aḥmad 6/376]"""
"9547","(9542) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Kūfī informed us that Abū Ghassān informed us that Mūsā ibn Muḥammad al-Anṣārī narrated on the authority of Jamīl ibn Zayd, who said: I saw Ibn ʿUmar pelting the jamarāt with pebbles the size of sheep droppings.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to collect the pebbles from Muzdalifah, disliking descending (to Minā beforehand).\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: From whichever place he takes them, they suffice him, except that I disapprove of his taking them from the mosque, lest the pebbles of the mosque be removed from it; and from the refuse dump, due to its impurity; and from the jamrah itself, because they are pebbles of unaccepted (rites).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And we have narrated in the Book of Ṣalāh from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, marfūʿ: that the pebbles appeal against the one who takes them out of the mosque. [Weak]"
"9548","(9543) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṭabarānī informed us there that Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed us by dictation that Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Qurashī informed us that Azhar ibn Saʿd al-Sammān informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated on the authority of Abū al-Ṭufayl, who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the pebbles that are thrown at the jamarāt since the establishment of Islam. He said: \Whatever of them was accepted was raised"," and whatever was not accepted was left. Were it not for that"," the space between the two mountains would have been filled.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī"," from Ibn Khuthaym"," from Abū al-Ṭufayl"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""An angel is appointed over them; whatever of them is accepted is raised"," and whatever is not accepted is left.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān"," who said: Sulaymān al-ʿAbsī narrated to me"," from Ibn Abī Nuʿm"," who said: I asked Abū Saʿīd about pelting the jamarāt. He said to me: \""Whatever of them is accepted is raised. Were it not for that"," it would be taller than Thabīr.\"" [Weak]"""
"9549","(9544) Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me with these two traditions that Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us that Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us that Sufyān narrated them both.\n\nAnd he mentioned the ḥadīth of Sufyān, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to collect the pebbles from Muzdalifah, disliking descending (to Minā beforehand). And the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī has been narrated marfūʿ through another weak chain. [Good]"
"9550","(9545) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated on the authority of his father, from Jābir, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Then he took the middle road"," which leads you out to the Jamrah al-Kubrā"," until he reached the jamrah near the mosque. He pelted it with seven pebbles"," pronouncing takbīr with each pebble"," like the pebbles of khadhf (sling-stones)"," casting from the bottom of the valley. Then he turned towards the place of sacrifice.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Authentic — Muslim]"""
"9551","(9546) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Musaddad informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us that al-Aʿmash narrated — and Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us that Minjāb ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿAlī ibn Mushhir informed us — from al-Aʿmash, who said: I heard al-Ḥajjāj ibn Yūsuf saying while he was delivering the sermon from the minbar: \Arrange the Qurʾān as Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," arranged it: the sūrah in which al-Baqarah is mentioned"," the sūrah in which al-Nisāʾ is mentioned"," and the sūrah in which Āl ʿImrān is mentioned.\"" He (al-Aʿmash) said: \""I met Ibrāhīm and informed him of his statement"," whereupon he cursed him. Then he said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd narrated to me that he was with ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd when they came to the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah. He entered the valley"," faced it"," and pelted it from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles"," pronouncing takbīr with each pebble. I said: 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," the people are pelting it from above.' He said: 'By the One besides whom there is no deity"," this is the station of the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Minjāb ibn al-Ḥārith. [Authentic — Bukhārī 163"," Muslim 1296]"""
"9552","(9547) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us that Shuʿbah narrated — and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Abū ʿUmar informed us — that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: \When we reached the Jamrah al-Kubrā"," he placed the House on his left and Minā on his right"," and he pelted the jamrah with seven pebbles"," saying: 'Thus did the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh. In the narration of al-Rūdhabārī"," he said: \""I performed Ḥajj with ʿAbdullāh. When he came to Minā"," he placed Minā on his right and the House on his left"," and he pelted the jamrah with seven pebbles"," saying: 'This is the station of the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar (Abū ʿUmar)"," and Muslim narrated it from two other chains from Shuʿbah. [Authentic — Bukhārī 1661"," Muslim 1296]"""
"9553","(9548) Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Armawī informed us that Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that Ibn Idrīs narrated from Layth, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from his father, who said: \I departed with ʿAbdullāh from Muzdalifah"," and he continued reciting the talbiyah until he pelted the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah. He entered the valley and then said: 'O my nephew"," hand me seven stones.' So he pelted it with seven pebbles"," pronouncing takbīr with each pebble. When he finished"," he said: 'O Allah"," make it an accepted Ḥajj"," a forgiven sin"," and a thanked-for deed.' Then he said: 'Thus did I see the one upon whom Sūrat al-Baqarah was revealed do.'\"" [Denounced — Ibn Abī Shaybah 14016]"""
"9554","(9549) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us that Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥukaym ibn al-Azhar al-Madanī informed me that Zayd Abū Usāmah narrated, who said: \I saw Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh"," meaning Ibn ʿUmar"," enter the valley"," then pelt the jamrah with seven pebbles"," pronouncing takbīr with each pebble: 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. O Allah"," make it an accepted Ḥajj"," a forgiven sin"," and a thanked-for deed.' So I asked him about what he had done. He said: 'My father informed me that the Prophet ﷺ used to pelt the jamrah in this place and say"," each time he threw a pebble"," the same as what I have said.'\""\n\nʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥukaym is weak"," and Allah knows best. [Denounced]"""
"9555","(9550) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram ibn Ḥassān al-Bazzāz informed us that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, who said: \I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ pelting the jamarāt while mounted on his riding camel.'\"" [Authentic — Muslim 1297"," Nasāʾī 3062]"""
"9556","(9551) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us that Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn al-Mubārak al-Mustamlī informed us that Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī informed us that my father informed me that Yazīd ibn Sinān narrated from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from his father Abī Saʿīd, who said: \We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," these stones that are thrown at the jamarāt are carried away"," and it is assumed that they are being depleted.' He said: 'Whatever of them is accepted is raised. Were it not for that"," you would see them like mountains.'\"" Yazīd ibn Sinān is not strong in ḥadīth"," and it has also been narrated through another weak chain from Ibn ʿUmar as marfūʿ. [Weak — Ḥākim 1/650]"""
"9557","(9552) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj narrated to me that Abū al-Zubayr narrated to me, saying: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: I saw the Prophet ﷺ pelting the jamrah on his mount on the Day of Sacrifice, saying: \Take your rites from me"," for I do not know—perhaps I shall not perform Ḥajj after this Ḥajj of mine.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""
"9558","(9553) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us that Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan narrated to us from Maʿqil, from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from Yaḥyā ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from his grandmother Umm al-Ḥuṣayn, saying: I heard her say: I performed Ḥajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I saw him when he pelted the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah and departed while he was on his mount, and with him were Bilāl and Usāmah. One of them was leading his mount, and the other was raising his garment over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to shield him from the sun.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1298.]"
"9559","(9554) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdād informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us that ʿAbīdah ibn Ḥumayd narrated to me that Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Aḥwaṣ, from his mother, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah riding, and behind him a man shielding him from the pelting of the people. He said: \O people"," let not some of you kill others. And whoever pelts the jamrah"," let him pelt it with pebbles the size of those used for khadhf (slinging).\"" She said: And I saw a stone between his fingers. She said: Then he pelted"," and the people pelted"," and then he departed. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9560","(9555) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Mahdī narrated to me that my grandfather ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to me from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, who narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Aḥwaṣ, from his mother, who said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ pelting the jamrah from the bottom of the valley while he was riding, saying the takbīr with every pebble, and a man behind him was shielding him. I asked about the man, and they said: al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās. The people crowded together, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \O people"," let not some of you kill others. And when you pellet the jamrah"," pelt it with pebbles the size of those used for khadhf (slinging).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9561","(9556) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us that al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us that Ayman ibn Nābil narrated to us. And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation, and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us by reciting to both of them, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn, Abū Nuʿaym, and Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us from Ayman ibn Nābil, who said: I heard Qudāmah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmmār al-Kilābī say: I saw the Prophet ﷺ pelting the jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice on a reddish-brown she-camel, with no driving, no striking, and no \Move aside! Move aside!\"" [Ḥasan. Ṭayālisī 1338. Aḥmad 3/413.]"""
"9562","(9557) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Ḥasan ibn Mūsā al-Ashyab narrated to us that al-ʿUmarī narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pelt the Jamrah al-ʿAqabah while riding, saying the takbīr with every pebble. And from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: During these days—meaning the Days of Tashrīq—he would come to them on foot, both going and returning, and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to do that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1969. Aḥmad 2/138.]"
"9563","(9558) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdād narrated to us that Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us that al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to come to the jamarāt during the three days after the Day of Sacrifice on foot, both going and returning, and he informed them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"
"9564","(9559) And likewise Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated it, and he mentioned it. And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar narrated it from his father and his uncle, but he did not mention his statement regarding the three days, and in the narration of al-Ashyab there is also no explicit mention of the three days. Al-Shāfiʿī said: It is as though, when he pelted on the Day of Sacrifice while riding—due to the continuity of his riding from Muzdalifah—he would also pelt on the Day of Departure while riding, due to the continuity of his riding upon departure. The Shaykh said: And this is the statement of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"
"9565","(9560) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us from Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, who said: ʿAṭāʾ said: The pelting of the jamarāt is done riding for two days and walking for two days. The Shaykh said: If the ḥadīth of al-ʿUmarī is authentic, then it is more deserving of being followed. And success is through Allah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 13749.]"
"9566","(9561) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from his father that when the people pelted the jamarāt, they would walk both going and returning, and the first one to ride was Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 916.]"
"9567","(9562) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that he used to dislike riding toward any of the jamarāt except out of necessity. Thus I found it in my book, though a man has dropped from its isnād between Ibrāhīm and ʿAṭāʾ, and the narration of Ibn ʿUyaynah is more authentic. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9568","(9563) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Lahīʿah and Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stone the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah on the first day in the morning"," and it is a single one; as for after that"," then after the sun's decline.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1299]"""
"9569","(9564) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: al-Thawrī narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Ḥasan al-ʿUranī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought us forward on the night of al-Muzdalifah — the young lads of Banī ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib — and he began striking our thighs with his hand"," saying: 'O my little sons"," do not stone until the sun rises.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1940. al-Nasāʾī 3064]"""
"9570","(9565) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Bazmahrānī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: My father narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Manṣūr, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Ḥasan al-ʿUranī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to us — the young lads of Banī ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib — and place us upon our donkeys and strike our thighs"," then say: 'Do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises"," and I do not think anyone would stone it until the sun rises.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9571","(9566) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib both said: Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī informed us: Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. al-Tirmidhī 893]"""
"9572","(9567) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Saqqāʾ al-Mihrajānī and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ al-Mihrajānī both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān informed us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed us: Kurayb informed me, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ used to command his women and their young children on the morning of Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah) to set out with the first light of dawn in the darkness and not to stone the jamrah until they were in the morning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Sharḥ al-Maʿānī 2/216]"
"9573","(9568) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAbd Allāh, the freed slave of Asmāʾ, narrated to me, from Asmāʾ, that she alighted on the night of Jamʿ at the dwelling of al-Muzdalifah. She stood and prayed, then she said: \O my dear son"," has the moon set?\"" I said: \""No.\"" She prayed for a while"," then said: \""O my dear son"," has the moon set?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Then depart.\"" So we departed and proceeded until she stoned the jamrah. Then she returned and prayed the morning prayer in her dwelling. I said to her: \""O my dear mother"," I think we have set out in the darkness.\"" She said: \""No"," O my dear son. Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave permission to the womenfolk (al-ẓuʿun).\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 15959]"""
"9574","(9569) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj: ʿAbd Allāh, the freed slave of Asmāʾ, informed me. He said: Asmāʾ said while she was at al-Muzdalifah: \Has the moon set?\"" I said: \""No.\"" She prayed for a while"," then said: \""O my dear son"," has the moon set?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Mount with me.\"" So we departed until she stoned the jamrah. Then she prayed in her dwelling. I said to her: \""O my dear mother"," we have indeed set out in the darkness.\"" She said: \""No. Indeed"," the Prophet ﷺ gave permission to the womenfolk (al-ẓuʿun).\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr. Likewise"," ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1291]"""
"9575","(9570) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khallād al-Bāhilī informed us: Yaḥyā narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me, who said: An informant informed me, from Asmāʾ (may Allah be pleased with her), that she stoned the jamrah. I said: \We stoned the jamrah at night.\"" She said: \""We used to do this in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1943]"""
"9576","(9571) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd al-Mālikī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to me: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Umm Salamah on the night of sacrifice"," and she stoned the jamrah before dawn"," then she departed and performed the ṭawāf al-ifāḍah. That was the day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be at her place.\"" [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd 1942. al-Ḥākim 1/641]"""
"9577","(9572) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūzdbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us — and he mentioned it similarly. [Munkar. See its predecessor.]"
"9578","(9573) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us from Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAṭṭār and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawurdī, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Umm Salamah on the Day of Sacrifice and commanded her to hasten the departure from Muzdalifah so that she would come to Makkah and pray the Fajr prayer there"," and it was her day"," so he liked that she accompany him.\""\n\nHe said: And al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us"," saying: Someone I trust from the people of the East informed me"," from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah"," from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," something similar to that.\n\nThus he narrated it in the dictation (imlāʾ)"," and he narrated it in al-Mukhtaṣar al-Kabīr with both chains of narration together"," except that he said: \""…so that she would stone the Jamrah and arrive for the Fajr prayer in Makkah"," and it was her day"," so he liked that she accompany him or arrive with him.\"" And he said in the second chain of narration: \""Al-Thiqah informed me"," from Hishām.\"" Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated it to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. It is as though al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) took it from Abū Muʿāwiya al-Ḍarīr"," and Abū Muʿāwiya narrated it with a connected chain. [Munkar. al-Shāfiʿī 1701]"""
"9579","(9574) Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī narrated it to us; Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Muʿāwiya narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abī Salamah, from Umm Salamah: \That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to perform the Fajr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice in Makkah.\"" [Munkar. Aḥmad 6/391]"""
"9580","(9575) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr al-Muqriʾ and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jābir, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ — and he mentioned the stoning of Jamrat al-ʿAqabah. He said: \Then he turned to the place of sacrifice and sacrificed sixty-three camels"," and he gave ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) the remainder"," and he sacrificed what remained and included him in his sacrificial offering. Then he commanded that a piece be taken from each camel"," and it was placed in a pot and cooked"," and both of them ate from its meat and drank from its broth.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""
"9581","(9576) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar used to say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaved his head during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," from Nāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1639. Muslim 1304]"""
"9582","(9577) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shaved his head"," and a group of his Companions shaved their heads"," and some of them shortened their hair.\"" Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May Allah have mercy upon those who shave their heads.' Once or twice"," and then he said: 'And upon those who shorten their hair.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," and al-Bukhārī mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1640. 1301]"""
"9583","(9578) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿAliyy al-Saqqāʾ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ al-Mihrajāniyyān both informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us; Sufyān informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to me, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \May Allah have mercy upon those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and upon those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""May Allah have mercy upon those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and upon those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""May Allah have mercy upon those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and upon those who shorten their hair?\"" He said on the fourth occasion: \""And upon those who shorten their hair.\""\n\nThey (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) both narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1640. Muslim 1301]"""
"9584","(9579) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; ʿUmārah narrated to us, from Abū Zurʿah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O Allah"," forgive those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""O Allah"," forgive those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""O Allah"," forgive those who shave their heads.\"" They said: \""And those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""And those who shorten their hair.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAyyāsh ibn al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," all of them from Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1641. Muslim 1302]"""
"9585","(9580) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us. And ʿAlī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us. He said: I heard Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrating from Ibn Sīrīn, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned the Jamrah"," sacrificed his offering"," and shaved his head"," he gave the barber the right side of his head"," and he shaved it. Then he called Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī and gave it to him. Then he gave him the left side and said: 'Shave it.' So he shaved it and he gave it to Abū Ṭalḥah"," and said: 'Distribute it among the people.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1305]"""
"9586","(9581) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed us. Nāfiʿ said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \Ḥafṣah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," informed me that the Prophet ﷺ commanded his wives to exit the state of iḥrām during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage.\"" Ḥafṣah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to him: \""What prevents you from exiting the state of iḥrām?\"" He said: \""I have matted my head and garlanded my sacrificial animal"," so I will not exit the state of iḥrām until I have sacrificed my offering.\""\n\nThey (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) both narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Nāfiʿ. And we have narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he shaved his head during the Farewell Pilgrimage. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1610. Muslim 1229]"""
"9587","(9582) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb said: Nāfiʿ said that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever braids his head for iḥrām"," let him shave it. Do not resemble talbīd.\"" This is the authentic narration from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"9588","(9583) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Mālik al-Māliniyy informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us; Ibn Salm informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Abī Fudayk informed me; ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ informed me from his father, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever applies talbīd to his head for iḥrām"," then shaving becomes obligatory upon him.\"" This ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ is not strong (in ḥadīth). The authentic version is that it is from the statement of ʿUmar and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both). Sālim also narrated it from his father"," from ʿUmar. [Munkar]"""
"9589","(9584) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb informed me from al-Zuhrī; Sālim informed me that ʿAbdullāh used to say: \I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'Whoever braids"," let him shave. Do not resemble talbīd.'\"" He said: And ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with his head matted (mulabbidan).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5570]"""
"9590","(9585) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed me, and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"
"9591","(9586) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever ties up (his hair)"," or braids it"," or applies talbīd"," then shaving becomes obligatory upon him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9592","(9587) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ ibn al-Ḥammāmiyy (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us in Baghdād; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us; Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us; Sufyān informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Whoever applies talbīd"," or braids"," or ties up (his hair)"," let him shave.\"" This is the authentic version from ʿAbdullāh"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," as his own statement"," and from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," as his own statement. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9593","(9588) ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-ʿUmariyy narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Whoever applies talbīd to his head"," let him shave"," for shaving has become obligatory upon him.\"" Abū Saʿd al-Ṣūfī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Madāʾinī informed us; Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā informed me; ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ informed me from ʿĀṣim"," and he mentioned it. ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar is weak"," and this narration is not established as marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet). [Munkar. Ibn ʿAdiyy 5/229]"""
"9594","(9589) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us in Bukhārā; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us; Sufyān informed us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Whoever applies talbīd"," or braids"," or ties"," or twists"," or knots (his hair)"," then he is upon what he intended thereby.\"" He said: And Ibn ʿUmar said: \""He must shave"," without doubt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 14506]"""
"9595","(9590) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bashrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb informed me; Nāfiʿ informed me that Ibn ʿUmar said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed the people at ʿArafah and informed them about the rites of Ḥajj. He said in what he said: 'When it is morning"," if Allah the Most High wills"," and you have departed from Jamʿ (Muzdalifah)"," then whoever pelts the Jamrah al-Quṣwā"," which is near al-ʿAqabah"," with seven pebbles"," then turns away and sacrifices a hady if he has one"," then shaves or shortens (his hair)"," that which was forbidden to him regarding the matters of Ḥajj becomes permissible for him"," except perfume and women. So no one should touch perfume or women until he has performed ṭawāf of the House (the Kaʿbah).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 922]"""
"9596","(9591) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'When you have pelted the Jamrah with seven pebbles"," and sacrificed"," and shaved"," then everything becomes permissible for you except women and perfume.'\"" Sālim said: And ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Everything becomes permissible for him except women.\"" She said: And ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\"" — meaning for his ḥill (coming out of iḥrām). [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9597","Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas al-Ammam narrated to us: al-Rabi' narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Salim, who said: 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: \I used to apply perfume to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his state of ihram and for his state of hal (exit from ihram).\"" Salim said: \""And the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more deserving of being followed.\"""""
"9598","Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahawayh al-'Askari narrated to us: Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Susi narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Aflah ibn Humayd narrated from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from 'A'isha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram when he entered the state of ihram"," and for his hal before he performed Tawaf around the House.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from al-Qa'nabi"," and both al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it from the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father"," and it has already been mentioned earlier in this book."""
"9599","'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran narrated to us in Baghdad: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated from Ibn Jurayj: 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Urwah informed me that he heard 'Urwah and al-Qasim narrating from 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my hands using dharira (a type of perfume) during the Farewell Pilgrimage"," for the state of hal and for ihram.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhari and Muslim reported it in their Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj."""
"9600","Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to me. And Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim, the son of the daughter of Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated to us: my grandfather narrated to us. They both said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur, meaning Ibn Zadhan, narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated from his father from 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I used to apply perfume to the Prophet ﷺ for his ihram before he entered the state of ihram"," and on the Day of Sacrifice before he performed Tawaf around the House"," using a perfume containing musk.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Mani' and Ya'qub al-Dawraqi."""
"9601","Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzak narrated to us: al-Thawri narrated to us. And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Hasan al-'Urni from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \When you have stoned the Jamrah"," you have become halal (permitted) from everything that was forbidden upon you"," except women"," until you perform Tawaf around the House.\"" A man said: \""What about perfume"," O Abu al-Abbas?\"" He said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ anointing his head with musk. Is that perfume or not?\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Wahb."""
"9602","Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran narrated to us in Baghdad: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us: Malik ibn Yahya narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm from 'Amrah from 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \When you have stoned (the Jamrah) and shaved (your heads)"," perfume"," garments"," and everything have become permissible for you"," except women.\"""""
"9603","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, and he added in it: \And when you have slaughtered (the sacrifice)"," then everything — perfume and garments — has become permissible for you"," except women.\"" Abu al-Hasan ibn al-Saqqa' and Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us"," saying: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated it"," and he said: \""From the Prophet ﷺ.\"" This is among the confusions of al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah. The hadith from 'Amrah from 'A'isha"," may Allah be pleased with her"," from the Prophet ﷺ is only as the rest of the people narrated it from 'A'isha"," may Allah be pleased with her."""
"9604","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated it to us: Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to me: 'Abd Allah ibn Shirawayh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated from al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn 'Uthman, from Abu al-Rijal from his mother from 'A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ihram when he entered the state of ihram"," and for his hal before he performed Tawaf al-Ifadah"," using the finest perfume I could find.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'. The mother of Abu al-Rijal is 'Amrah. This wording has also been narrated in the hadith of Umm Salamah along with another ruling"," which I do not know any of the jurists to have held."""
"9605","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated it to us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-'Ataridi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Ishaq: Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah narrated to me from his mother, and his mother was Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: \The night in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me was the evening of the Day of Sacrifice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me when Wahb ibn Zam'ah and a man from the family of Abi Umayyah entered upon me"," both wearing shirts. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Have you performed Tawaf al-Ifadah?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Then remove your shirts.' So they removed them. Wahb said: 'Why"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'This is a day on which permission has been granted to you: when you have stoned the Jamrah and sacrificed your hady (offering)"," if you have one"," you have become permissible from everything that was forbidden upon you"," except women"," until you perform Tawaf around the House. If you reach the evening without having performed Tawaf"," you return to the state of ihram as you were the first time"," until you perform Tawaf around the House.'\"""""
"9606","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu al-Muthanna al-'Anbari narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah narrated from his father and from his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, both narrating to him from Umm Salamah, who said: \My night — that is"," the evening of the Day of Sacrifice — on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to me arrived. He came to me"," and Wahb ibn Zam'ah entered upon me along with a man from the family of Abi Umayyah"," both wearing shirts. The Prophet ﷺ said to Wahb: 'Have you performed Tawaf al-Ifadah"," O Abu 'Abd Allah?' He said: 'No"," by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Remove your shirt.' So he removed it from his head"," and his companion removed his shirt from his head. They said: 'Why"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'This is a day on which permission has been granted to you: when you have stoned the Jamrah"," you become permissible from everything that was forbidden upon you"," except women. If you reach the evening before performing Tawaf around this House"," you return to the state of ihram as you were before stoning the Jamrah"," until you perform Tawaf.'\""\n\nAbu 'Ubaydah said: \""And Umm Qays bint Mihsan"," who was their neighbor"," narrated to me"," saying: \""'Ukkashah ibn Mihsan went out from me among a group of Banu Asad"," wearing shirts on the evening of the Day of Sacrifice. They returned to me at nightfall with their shirts in their hands"," carrying them. I said: 'O 'Ukkashah"," what is the matter? You went out wearing shirts and returned carrying them in your hands!' He said: 'It is well"," O Umm Qays. This was a day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted us permission: when we stoned the Jamrah"," we became permissible from everything that was forbidden upon us"," except women"," until we perform Tawaf around the House. When we reached the evening without having performed Tawaf"," we placed our shirts over our hands.'\""\n\nAbu Dawud narrated it similarly in his Kitab al-Sunan from Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Ma'in with the first chain of narration"," without the second chain from Umm Qays"," and he also did not mention the slaughtering (of the sacrifice)."""
"9607","(9602) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from al-Faḍl — may Allah be pleased with him — that the Prophet ﷺ continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim.\n\nAnd in the established ḥadīth from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that the Prophet ﷺ came to the Jamrah which is by the tree and pelted it with seven pebbles, pronouncing Takbīr with each pebble. And likewise in the established ḥadīth from Ibn Masʿūd from the Prophet ﷺ: he pronounced Takbīr with each pebble. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1601]"
"9608","(9603) And the Imam Abū ʿUthmān — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us: Abū Ṭāhir ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from ʿĀmir ibn Shaqīq, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: I watched the Prophet ﷺ and he continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah with the first pebble. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Ibn Khuzaymah 2886]"
"9609","(9604) And the Imam Abū ʿUthmān informed us: Abū Ṭāhir informed us: my grandfather narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father, from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from al-Faḍl — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: I departed with the Prophet ﷺ from ʿArafāt, and he continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah, pronouncing Takbīr with each pebble. Then he discontinued the Talbiyah with the last pebble.\n\nThe Shaykh said: His pronouncing Takbīr with each pebble indicates that he discontinued the Talbiyah with the first pebble, as we have narrated in the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. And his statement \he continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah\"" means until he began the stoning of the Jamrah. As for the additional wording in the narration of al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās"," it is unusual (gharībah); Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah reported it and selected it"," but it is not found in the well-known narrations from Ibn ʿAbbās from al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Nasāʾī 3079. Bazzār 2142]"""
"9610","(9605) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Bakrah Bakkār ibn Qutaybah al-Qāḍī in Egypt narrated to us: Ṣafwān ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Dhubāb narrated from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sakhrat, who said: I went out with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd from Minā to ʿArafah. ʿAbd Allāh was a dark-skinned man with two braids, wearing the garment of the desert dwellers, and he was reciting the Talbiyah. A mob of the common people gathered around him and said: \O Bedouin! This is not a day of Talbiyah; rather it is a day of Takbīr.\"" At that point he turned to me and said: \""Are the people ignorant"," or have they forgotten? By the One Who sent Muḥammad ﷺ with truth"," I departed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Minā to ʿArafah"," and he did not abandon the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah"," except that he would mix it with Takbīr or Tahlīl.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated the meaning of this in an abridged form in the established ḥadīth from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. [Ḥasan. Ibn Khuzaymah 2806. Ḥākim 1/632]"""
"9611","(9606) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Abān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me from ʿIkrimah, who said: I departed with al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī — peace be upon them both — and I continued to hear him reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah. When he cast the pebble, he fell silent. I said: \What is this?\"" He said: \""I saw my father ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — may Allah the Most High be pleased with him — reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah"," and he informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that.\"" [Ḥasan. Aḥmad 1/114. Abū Yaʿlā 321. Ibn Abī Shaybah 13987]"""
"9612","(9607) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Maḥmūd al-Marwazī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Ibn Dāwūd narrated from Abū ʿUthmān al-Makkī, from ʿAṭāʾ, that ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — recited the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah. And we have narrated this from a group of the Companions, the mention of which has already passed. [Ḥasan]"
"9613","(9608) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿādh, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Prophet ﷺ addressed the people at Minā and assigned them their places. He said: \Let the Muhājirūn camp here\"" — and he pointed to the right of the Qiblah — \""and the Anṣār here\"" — and he pointed to the left of the Qiblah — \""and then let the people camp around them.\"" This is how I found it in my book: \""from a man.\""\n\nAnd Abū Dāwūd narrated it from Musaddad"," from ʿAbd al-Wārith"," from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj"," from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿādh al-Taymī"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us while we were at Minā"," and our hearing was so sharp that we could hear what he was saying while we were in our camps. He proceeded to teach them their rites until he reached the matter of the Jimār. He placed his two index fingers together and said: 'With pebbles of khadhf (small pebbles).' Then he commanded the Muhājirūn to camp in front of the mosque"," and he commanded the Anṣār to camp behind the mosque. Then the people camped thereafter.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad informed us: ʿAbd al-Wārith informed us"," and he mentioned it. And this is the correct version. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿādh was a Companion"," and it is claimed that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī did not meet him"," and that his narration from him is mursal. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd we have narrated from Ṭāwūs and others that the Prophet ﷺ camped to the left of the prayer place of the Imām at Minā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1951. Aḥmad 4/161]"""
"9614","(9609) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī in Kūfah narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Zuhrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥik, from his mother Maysakah, from ʿĀʾishah — may Allah be pleased with her — who said: It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," shall we not build for you a structure at Minā to shade you?\"" He said: \""No. Minā is the camping place of the one who arrives first.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3019]"""
"9615","(9610) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah al-Dīlī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿImrān al-Anṣārī, from his father, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar — may Allah the Most High be pleased with him — came to me while I was camped beneath a tree (sarḥah) on the road to Makkah. He said: \What made you camp beneath this tree?\"" I said: \""I wanted its shade.\"" He said: \""Is there anything other than that?\"" I said: \""I wanted its shade.\"" He said: \""Is there anything other than that?\"" I said: \""No"," nothing other than that made me camp here.\"" Then ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""When you are between the two mountains (al-Akhsabayn) of Minā\"" — and he gestured with his hand toward the east — \""there is a valley there called al-Surrar"," in which there is a tree beneath which seventy Prophets rested.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Nasāʾī 1995. Tirmidhī 881]"""
"9616","(9611) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbadah narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Ibn Shihāb say: ʿĪsā ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ, while he was delivering a sermon on the Day of Naḥr, a man stood up and said: \I used to think"," O Messenger of Allah"," that such-and-such was before such-and-such.\"" Then another stood up and said: \""I used to think"," O Messenger of Allah"," that such-and-such was before such-and-such.\"" Regarding all three"," the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Do it"," and there is no harm.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1650. Muslim 1306]"""
"9617","(9612) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and he mentioned it with its meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from Muḥammad ibn Bakr, and he (al-Bukhārī) also reported it from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī from Ibn Jurayj. And Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān followed him in mentioning the khuṭbah in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see its predecessor]"
"9618","(9613) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī narrated to us in Makkah: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us: Abū Jābir narrated to us: Hishām ibn al-Ghāz narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood at the jamarāt on the Day of Naḥr during the Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ and said: \What day is this?\"" They said: \""The Day of Naḥr.\"" He said: \""What land is this?\"" They said: \""The Sacred Land.\"" He said: \""What month is this?\"" They said: \""The Sacred Month.\"" He said: \""This is the Day of the Greater Ḥajj. Indeed"," your blood"," your wealth"," and your honours are sacred to you"," like the sanctity of this land on this day.\"" Then he said: \""Have I conveyed?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then began saying: \""O Allah"," bear witness.\"" Then he bade farewell to the people"," and they said: \""This is the Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said in al-Ṣaḥīḥ: And Hishām ibn al-Ghāz mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Abū Dāwūd 1945; Ibn Mājah 3058]"""
"9619","(9614) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad both said: Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us: Qurrat ibn Khālid narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah narrated to me from his father, and a man who was better than ʿAbd al-Raḥmān in my estimation—Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—from Abū Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us on the Day of Naḥr and said: \What day is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not the Day of Naḥr?\"" We said: \""Indeed"," yes.\"" He said: \""What month is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not Dhū al-Ḥijjah?\"" We said: \""Indeed"," yes.\"" He said: \""What land is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not al-Balad (the City)?\"" We said: \""Indeed"," yes.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," your blood is sacred"," like the sanctity of this day of yours"," in this month of yours"," in this land of yours. O Allah"," have I conveyed?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Let the one present among you convey to the absent"," for often the one to whom it is conveyed is more mindful than the hearer. Beware! Do not return after me as disbelievers"," striking the necks of one another.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 1654; Muslim 1679]"""
"9620","(9615) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muʾakkī informed us: al-Qāḍī Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us: Qurrat ibn Khālid narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah narrated to me, and a man who was better in my estimation than ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—from Abū Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us on the Day of Naḥr and said: \Do not return after me as disbelievers"," striking the necks of one another.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Musnadī from Abū ʿĀmir"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Jabalah and others from Abū ʿĀmir. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see its predecessor]"""
"9621","(9616) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Ḥujayn ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: ʿIkrimat ibn ʿAmmār narrated from al-Hirmās ibn Ziyād, who said: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) while I was a boy; my father had mounted me behind him, addressing the people at Minā on the Day of al-Aḍḥā on his she-camel.\n\n[Ḥasan; Ibn Khuzaymah 2953; Aḥmad 5/7]"
"9622","(9617) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muʾammal ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: al-Walīd narrated to us: Ibn Jābir narrated to us: Sulaym ibn ʿĀmir al-Kilāʿī narrated to us and said: I heard Abā Umāmah say: I heard the khutbah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Minā on the Day of Naḥr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; Abū Dāwūd 1955; al-Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 8668]"
"9623","(9618) Abū ʿAlī informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Marwān narrated from Hilāl ibn ʿĀmir al-Muzanī: Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr al-Muzanī narrated to me and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressing the people at Minā when the forenoon had advanced, on a grey mule, and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was relaying his words, and the people were standing and sitting.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; see the forthcoming takhrij]"
"9624","(9619) Al-Bukhārī said in the book of al-Tārīkh: Abū Jaʿfar narrated to me: Marwān narrated to us: Hilāl ibn ʿĀmir al-Muzanī narrated to us and said: I heard Rāfiʿ ibn ʿAmr al-Muzanī say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of Naḥr during the Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ, delivering a khutbah on a grey mule.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Fārisī informed it to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Abū Dāwūd 1956; Aḥmad 3/477]"
"9625","(9620) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated in the section of the last narrators, and they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us and said: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muʾakkī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd, Mālik, and others informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed them from ʿĪsā ibn Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh, who was informed by ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood for the people during the Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ while they were asking him. A man came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I did not realize"," so I sacrificed before I performed the rami.\"" He said: \""Perform the rami"," and there is no harm.\"" Another said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I did not realize"," so I shaved my head before I slaughtered.\"" He said: \""Slaughter"," and there is no harm.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not asked that day about anything that was done prematurely or delayed except that he said: 'Do it"," and there is no harm.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb"," and the ḥadīth of al-Shāfiʿī and Yaḥyā is similar to it"," except that they both said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood during the Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ at Minā for the people while they were asking him","\"" and they both presented the question of shaving before the question of sacrificing"," and they did not say \""my head.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," all of them from Mālik. And Muslim also narrated it from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb from Yūnus ibn Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 83; Muslim 1306]"""
"9626","(9621) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: al-Zuhrī narrated to us and said: I heard ʿĪsā ibn Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I slaughtered before I performed the rami.\"" He said: \""Perform the rami"," and there is no harm.\"" Another said: \""I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" He said: \""Slaughter"," and there is no harm.\"" Abū Bakr said: Then I heard Sufyān being asked about this ḥadīth"," and Bulbul said to him: \""This is what I have preserved from al-Zuhrī"," O Abū Muḥammad.\"" He said: \""Yes"," as though you heard it"," except that he used to lengthen it"," and this is what I have preserved from him.\"" He said: \""And I heard Bulbul say to Sufyān: 'Indeed"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī said: You said to him"," \""I did not preserve it.\""' Sufyān said: \""Ibn Mahdī spoke the truth; I did not preserve it in its entirety"," but as for this"," I have memorized it precisely.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim 1306]\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān"," without the story of Bulbul. And he narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī"," and he referred its text to the narration of Ibn ʿUyaynah"," apart from what he excepted. And in the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq there is an additional point not found in the narration of Ibn ʿUyaynah."""
"9627","(9622) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Ashbahani informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Qattan narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar ibn Rashid informed us — from al-Zuhri — from Ibn Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah — from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) upon his she-camel, when a man came to him and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I used to think that shaving preceded the stoning"," so I shaved before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" Then another man came and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I used to think that shaving preceded the slaughtering"," so I slaughtered before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Slaughter now"," and there is no harm.\"" He said: \""He was not asked about anything that a man had done prematurely or delayed"," except that he said: 'Do it"," and there is no harm.'\""\n\nAnd similarly did Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrate it from 'Abd al-Razzaq.\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah also narrated it from al-Zuhri with an additional wording. [Sahih. Al-Daraqutni 2/251. Al-Bazzar 2418]"""
"9628","(9623) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Halim ibn Muhammad ibn Halim ibn Ibrahim al-Sa'igh in Marw narrated to us — Abu al-Muwajjih informed us — 'Abdan informed us — 'Abd Allah informed us — Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah informed us — from al-Zuhri — from 'Isa ibn Talhah — from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), when a man came to him on the Day of Sacrifice while he was standing at the Jamrah, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I shaved before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" Then another came and said: \""I slaughtered before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" Then another came and said: \""I proceeded to the House before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" He said: \""I did not see him being asked about anything on that day except that he said: 'Do it"," and there is no harm.'\"" Muslim extracted it in his Sahih in this manner from the hadith of 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak. [Sahih. Muslim 1306. Ahmad 2/210. Al-Daraqutni 2/251]"""
"9629","(9624) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdus narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Wuhayb narrated to us — from Ibn Tawus — from his father — from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about the slaughtering, the shaving, the stoning, and about doing things prematurely or delaying them, and he said: \There is no harm.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Bahz from Wuhayb. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari 1647. Muslim 1307]"""
"9630","(9625) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us — al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us — al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — Abu Salamah Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us — Ayyub narrated to us — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and it was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I slaughtered before I stoned.\"" He gestured with his hand and said: \""There is no harm.\"" Then a man said: \""I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" He gestured with his hand and said: \""There is no harm.\"" He said: \""He was not asked that day about anything concerning premature or delayed actions except that he gestured with his hand and said: 'There is no harm.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari 1647]"""
"9631","(9626) Abu al-Hasan al-'Alawi informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Bazmahrani narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us — from Khalid al-Hadha' — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: \I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" He said: \""There is no harm.\""\n\nThen another said: \""I stoned after nightfall.\"" He said: \""There is no harm.\"" He said: \""I did not know of him being asked about anything that day except that he said: 'There is no harm.'\"" And he did not command any expiation (kaffarah) for anything.\n\nThis is a sound (sahih) chain of narration. [Sahih]"""
"9632","(9627) Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Razjahi informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us — Abu Ya'la narrated to me — Abu Kaythamah narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — Mansur informed us — from 'Ata' — from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about one who shaved before he slaughtered, and about similar matters, and he said: \There is no harm"," there is no harm.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Hawshab from Hushaym. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari 1634]"""
"9633","(9628) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Baghawi in Baghdad narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us — from 'Abd al-'Aziz, who is ibn Rufay' — from 'Ata' — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: \I slaughtered before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" Another said: \""I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" He said: \""Slaughter now"," and there is no harm.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash"," and he added in its text: \""I visited before I stoned.\"" He said: \""There is no harm.\"" [Sahih. Al-Bukhari 1635]"""
"9634","(9629) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Umar narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us — and he mentioned it with his addition, except that he differed in the remainder, and he said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I shaved before I stoned.\"" He said: \""Stone now"," and there is no harm.\"" And he did not mention his statement: \""I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" [See above]"""
"9635","(9630) And Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us — Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us — from 'Ata' — from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stoned and then sat down for the people, when a man came to him and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I shaved before I slaughtered.\"" He said: \""There is no harm.\"" Then another came and said: \""I shaved before I stoned.\"" He said: \""There is no harm.\"" He said: \""He was not asked about anything except that he said: 'There is no harm.'\"" [Sahih. Ibn Majah 3053. Ahmad 3/326]"""
"9636","(9631) And Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from 'Abbad ibn Mansur and Qays ibn Sa'd — from 'Ata' — from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked about a man who stoned before he shaved, and who shaved before he stoned, and who slaughtered before he shaved, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Do it"," and there is no harm.\""\n\nAnd Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — al-Qasim narrated to me — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us — and al-Bukhari alluded to the narration of Hammad. [Sahih. See above]"""
"9637","Muqatil narrated that they asked Anas ibn Malik about people who shaved their heads before slaughtering (their sacrificial animal). He said: \You have contravened the Sunnah"," but there is no penalty upon you.\"" [Da'if]"""
"9638","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever advances something from his rites or delays it"," there is upon him no (sin).\"" [Sahih. Ahmad 1/216]"""
"9639","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the ifadah (return from Arafat) on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed Dhuhr at Mina. Nafi said: \And Ibn Umar used to perform the ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice"," then return and pray Dhuhr at Mina"," and he would mention that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did so.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1308]"""
"9640","(a) Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated regarding the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the ifadah to the House and prayed Dhuhr in Makkah.\"" [Sahih. Muslim]\n\n(b) Imam Abu Dawud narrated in his Marasil"," through his chain"," from Ibn Shahab al-Zuhri that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had stoned the Jamrah"," he returned to the place of sacrifice and slaughtered"," then shaved his head"," then departed immediately from that place.\n\n(c) Imam al-Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the Tawaf al-Ziyarah until night. [Sahih. Muslim]"""
"9641","A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the ziyarah (Tawaf al-Ziyarah) on the Day of Sacrifice until night. [Da'if. Ahmad 1/309. Abu Dawud 2000. Abu Ya'la 2700]"
"9642","(a) A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the Tawaf on the Day of Sacrifice until night. [Da'if. See what preceded.]\n\n(b) In the hadith of Abu Salamah, we have narrated that A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \We performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and we performed the ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice.\""\n\n(c) In another narration"," A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the ifadah at the end of his day"," when he had prayed Dhuhr"," then returned to Mina.\"" [Da'if. See what preceded.]"""
"9643","A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave permission to his Companions, so they visited the House (i.e., performed Tawaf al-Ziyarah) on the Day of Sacrifice during the midday, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the visit at night with his wives. [Da'if]"
"9644","Tawus narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Tawaf of the Day of Sacrifice at night. [Da'if]"
"9645","(a) Mis'ar also narrated from Jabir, from Mujahid, a similar narration.\n\n(b) Urwah ibn al-Zubayr inclined toward this view, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Tawaf at night upon his she-camel. However, the most authentic of these narrations are the hadith of Nafi from Ibn Umar, the hadith of Jabir, and the hadith of Abu Salamah from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"9646","Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \As for Ibrahim (peace be upon him)"," he came to his place in Mina and spent the night there until morning"," and when the sun's edge rose"," he came to his place in Arafat and stood there until the sun set"," then he departed and came to his place in Muzdalifah and spent the night there. When the time of the hastened prayer arrived"," he stood (in prayer)"," and when the time of the traveler's prayer arrived"," he departed. And that is the millah of your father Ibrahim (peace be upon him)"," and your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has been commanded to follow him.\"" [Sahih. Ibn Khuzaymah 2803. Ibn Abi Shaybah 14548]"""
"9647","(9642) And Abū al-Ḥasan informed us — al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Yūsuf narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who mentioned the hadith similarly, then he paused at the ṣalāh of al-ṣabāḥ (the morning prayer). Then Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: \Follow the religion of Ibrāhīm"," the upright"," and he was not of the polytheists.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9648","(9643) And Abū al-ḥasan al-Muqri' informed us — al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Yūsuf narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to me — Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: Jibrīl, peace be upon him, brought Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him, to Minā, and he prayed there the ẓuhr, ʿaṣr, maghrib, ʿishā', and ṣubḥ prayers. Then he set out from Minā to ʿArafāt and prayed there the two prayers. Then he stood until the sun set. Then he brought him to al-Muzdalifah, where he descended and spent the night. Then he prayed there — meaning the ṣubḥ — in the most hurried manner in which any Muslim prays. Then he stood there in the most delayed manner in which any Muslim prays. Then he proceeded to Minā and performed the ramy (stoning), slaughtered, and shaved his head. Then Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed to Muḥammad ﷺ: \Follow the religion of Ibrāhīm"," the upright"," and he was not of the polytheists.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; Ibn Khuzaymah 2804]"""
"9649","(9644) And Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqri' informed us — al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Yūsuf narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Thawr narrated from Maʿmar, who said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated to me with its chain of narration, similarly. Then he shaved his head, then brought him to the House, and Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, said to His Prophet ﷺ: \Then We revealed to you: Follow the religion of Ibrāhīm"," the upright"," and he was not of the polytheists.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; see the preceding]"""
"9650","(9645) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, who mentioned it with its chain of narration and its meaning, raised (marfūʿ) to the Prophet ﷺ. He added: Then he came to the House and performed ṭawāf around it, then returned to Minā and stayed there those days. Then Allah, the Most High, revealed to Muḥammad ﷺ: \Follow the religion of Ibrāhīm"," the upright.\"" And the mawqūf (stopped) version is more correct. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9651","(9646) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us — Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Ziyād, who said: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad saying: ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The ṭawāf around the House"," the saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," and the ramy of the jamār were only established for the remembrance of Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic.\"" This is the wording of Sufyān's hadith. Abū Qutaybah narrated it from Sufyān but did not raise it. Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from ʿUbaydullāh but did not raise it"," and he said: \""I heard him raise it"," but I was reluctant to do so.\"" ʿAbdullah ibn Dāwūd and Abū ʿĀṣim narrated it from ʿUbaydullāh and they raised it. Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated it from al-Qāsim from ʿĀ'ishah but did not raise it. Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated it from ʿAṭā' from ʿĀ'ishah but did not raise it. [Ḍaʿīf; Abū Dāwūd 1888]"""
"9652","(9647) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm, meaning Ibn Milḥān, narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said — and he mentioned the hadith, in which he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he arrived in Makkah, performed ṭawāf. He first touched the Corner (al-Rukn), before anything else. Then he walked briskly (khabba) for three circuits out of the seven, and walked normally for four circuits. Then, when he had completed his ṭawāf at the House, he prayed two rakʿahs near the Maqām. Then he gave the salām and departed. He came to al-Ṣafā and performed ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah for seven circuits. Then he did not make permissible anything that had been forbidden to him until he had completed his ḥajj and sacrificed his hady on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr). Then he returned and performed ṭawāf around the House, then made permissible everything that had been forbidden to him. And whoever among the people had offered a hady and brought it did the same as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, and Muslim reported it through another chain from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 1606, Muslim 1227]"
"9653","(9648) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā narrated to us — al-Layth narrated to me — Jaʿfar, meaning Ibn Rabīʿah, narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: We performed ḥajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We returned (afḍnā) on the Day of Sacrifice, and Ṣafiyyah began to menstruate. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to do with her what a man does with his wife. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," she is menstruating.\"" He said: \""Has she detained us?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," she has already returned (afāḍat) on the Day of Sacrifice.\"" He said: \""Then send her forth.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 1646]"""
"9654","(9649) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — both said: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Jarīr narrated from al-Shaybānī from Ziyād ibn ʿIlāqah from Usāmah ibn Sharīk, who said: I went out with the Prophet ﷺ performing ḥajj. The people would come to him — one saying: \O Messenger of Allah"," I performed saʿy before performing ṭawāf","\"" or \""I delayed something\"" or \""I brought something forward.\"" And he would say to them: \""No harm"," no harm — except upon a man who defames the honour of a Muslim man unjustly"," for he is the one in jeopardy and perished.\"" The shaykh said: The wording \""I performed saʿy before performing ṭawāf\"" is gharīb; Jarīr is alone in transmitting it from al-Shaybānī. If it is preserved"," it is as though he asked about a man who performed saʿy after the ṭawāf of arrival (ṭawāf al-qudūm) before the ṭawāf of ifāḍah"," and he said: \""No harm.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Abū Dāwūd 2014"," Ibn Khuzaymah 2774]"""
"9655","(9650) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffā' informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashīr narrated to us — Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us — Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the fuqahā' whose word is authoritative among the people of Madīnah, who used to say: Whoever forgets to perform the ṭawāf of ifāḍah until he returns to his homeland, he becomes ḥarām (in a state of iḥrām) at the moment he remembers, until he returns to the House and performs ṭawāf around it. And if he has intercourse with women, he must sacrifice a badanah (a cow or camel). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"9656","(9651) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed him — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — al-Maʿmarī narrated to us — Ibn ʿArʿarah narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn Hishām handed us a book and said: \I heard it from my father"," but he did not read it to me.\"" In it was from Qatādah from Abū Ḥassān from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to visit the House every night as long as he was in Minā. He (Muʿādh) said: \""I have not seen anyone who kept pace with him in this.\"" The shaykh said: And al-Thawrī narrated in al-Jāmiʿ from Ibn Ṭāwūs from Ṭāwūs that the Prophet ﷺ used to perform ifāḍah every night — meaning the nights of Minā. [Ḍaʿīf; al-Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 12904]"""
"9657","(9652) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Amr al-Muqri' and Abu Bakr al-Warraq informed us, they both said — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Hisham ibn 'Ammar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said — Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated from his father, from Jabir, regarding the account of the Hajj of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proceeded to the House and prayed the noon prayer (Dhuhr) in Makkah. Then he came to Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib"," who were drawing water from Zamzam"," and he said: 'Draw water"," O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib! Were it not that the people would overtake you in providing water"," I would have drawn water with you.' They handed him a bucket"," and he drank from it.\"" [Sahih. Reported by Muslim in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah.]"""
"9658","(9653) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Karim narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us — Khalid narrated from Khalid, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to those providing water and asked for a drink. Al-'Abbas said: \O Fadl"," go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a drink from her.\"" He said: \""Give me a drink.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," they put their hands into it.\"" He said: \""Give me a drink.\"" So he drank from it. Then he came to Zamzam"," where they were drawing water and working at it"," and he said: \""Keep working"," for you are engaged in righteous work.\"" Then he said: \""Were it not that you would be overtaken"," I would come down and place the rope upon this\"" — meaning his shoulder — and he pointed to his shoulder. [Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Shahin.]"""
"9659","(9654) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani, Abu al-Walid al-Faqih, and Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah informed us, they said — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us — Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us — Humayd narrated from Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani, who said: \I was sitting with Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," when a Bedouin came to him and said: 'Why do I see your paternal cousins serving milk and honey while you serve nabidh? Is it out of need or miserliness?' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'All praise is due to Allah — we have no need and no miserliness. The Prophet ﷺ came upon his mount"," with Usamah behind him"," and asked for a drink. We brought him a vessel of nabidh"," and he drank from it and gave the remainder to Usamah"," and he said: \""You have done well and acted beautifully. Do thus"," for we do not wish to change what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded.\""'\"" [Sahih. Reported by Muslim in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Minhal.]"""
"9660","(9655) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us — Hajib ibn Ahmad narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Munib narrated to us — al-Fazari narrated — (and) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — Harun ibn Yusuf — Abu Ahmad ibn Ziyad narrated to us — Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us — Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated from 'Asim, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water from Zamzam to drink"," and he drank while standing.\"" 'Asim said: \""'Ikrimah swore that on that day he was only upon a camel.\"" In the narration of 'Abd al-Rahim"," it is said: \""'Ikrimah said: 'By Allah"," he was only upon a she-camel.'\"" [Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from Muhammad from Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari.]"""
"9661","(9656) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me — a companion of Ibn 'Abbas said: \Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to me: 'From where have you come?' I said: 'I have drunk from Zamzam.' He said: 'Have you drunk as it should be drunk?' I said: 'How should I drink?' He said: 'When you drink"," face the qiblah"," then mention the name of Allah"," then breathe three times"," and fill your belly from it. When you have finished"," then praise Allah"," for the Prophet ﷺ said: \""A sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not fill their bellies from Zamzam.\""'\"" [Sahih.]"""
"9662","(9657) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Ya'qub al-Thaqafi narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated from 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: \A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said to him: 'From where have you come?' He said: 'I have drunk from Zamzam","' and he mentioned something similar to it.\"" Al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinan also narrated it from 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Mulaykah. [See the preceding hadith.]"""
"9663","(9658) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan al-Sayrafi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadal narrated to us — Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, who said: \A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and mentioned something similar to it.\"" [Sahih. See the preceding hadith.]"""
"9664","(9659) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Raja' and 'Imran ibn Musa narrated to us, they both said — Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us — Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us — Humayd ibn Hilal narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, who said: Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said — and he mentioned the hadith in full regarding the account of his Islam, until he said: \Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came"," along with his companion"," and he touched the Black Stone"," then performed Tawaf of the House with his companion"," then prayed. When he had completed his prayer"," Abu Dharr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'I came to him"," and I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam"," and he said: \""And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.\""' He mentioned the hadith and said: 'He asked: \""How long have you been here?\"" I said: \""I have been here for thirty nights and days.\"" He said: \""Then who has been feeding you?\"" I said: \""I had no food except the water of Zamzam"," and I grew so fat that the folds of my belly began to crack"," and I found no trace of hunger upon my liver.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Verily"," it is blessed; it is food that nourishes and a cure for illness.\""'\"" [Sahih. Reported by Muslim in his Sahih from Haddab ibn Khalid.]"""
"9665","(9660) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — al-Baghandi and Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, they both said — Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'mal narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The water of Zamzam is for whatever purpose it is drunk for.\"" ['Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'mal is alone in reporting it. Da'if. Ibn Majah 3062. Ahmad 3/357.]"""
"9666","(9661) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed on the last of his days after he had prayed the noon prayer (Dhuhr)"," then returned and stayed in Mina during the days of al-Tashriq. He would stone the jamrah when the sun had declined"," pelting each jamrah with seven pebbles"," saying the takbir with each pebble. He would stand at the first and the second jamrah"," prolonging his standing and supplicating"," then he would stone the third and not stand at it.\"" [Da'if. Abu Dawud 1974. Ahmad 6/90.]"""
"9667","(9662) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, saying: Yūnus informed us, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stone the jamrah adjacent to the mosque of Masjid Minā, he would pelt it with seven pebbles, pronouncing takbīr each time he cast a pebble. Then he would move forward in front of it and stand facing the House (the Kaʿbah), raising his hands and supplicating, and he would prolong the standing. Then he would come to the second jamrah and pelt it with seven pebbles, pronouncing takbīr each time he cast a pebble. He would then descend to the left, towards the side of the valley, and stand facing the qiblah, raising his hands and supplicating. Then he would come to the jamrah near al-ʿAqabah and pelt it with seven pebbles, pronouncing takbīr each time he cast a pebble. Then he would depart and not stand by it.\n\nAl-Zuhrī said: I heard Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrating a similar hadith from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: And Ibn ʿUmar used to do it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ, saying: And Muḥammad—it is said that he is ibn Yaḥyā—narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1666. Nasāʾī 3083.]"
"9668","(9663) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Muʾadhdhin informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us, saying: Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, saying: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us, on the authority of Yūnus ibn Yazīd, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, that Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed him that ʿAbd Allāh used to stone the nearest jamrah (al-jamrah al-dunyā) with seven pebbles, pronouncing takbīr after each pebble. Then he would move forward until he reached level ground and stand facing the qiblah for a long while, supplicating and raising his hands. Then he would stone the middle jamrah likewise. He would then take the left side and descend to level ground, and stand facing the qiblah for a long while, supplicating and raising his hands. Then he would stone the jamrah of al-ʿAqabah from the bottom of the valley, and he would not stand by it. He said: \Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," on the authority of his brother Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1665.]"""
"9669","(9664) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, saying: Misʿar narrated to us, on the authority of Waraṭah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar, \When should I stone the jamār?\"" He said: \""When your imām stones"," stone.\"" He said: I repeated the question to him"," and he said: \""We used to watch carefully"," and when the sun passed the meridian (zawālat al-shams)"," we would stone.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Abī Nuʿaym.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1659. Abū Dāwūd 1972.]"""
"9670","(9665) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī by recitation, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, on the authority of Abū al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned the jamrah on the first day at mid-morning (ḍuḥā), and he did not stone after that until the sun had passed the meridian.\n\nMuslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1299.]"
"9671","(9666) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik informed us, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \One should not stone the jamār during the three days until the sun has passed the meridian.\""\n\nAnd on the authority of Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to stand at the first two jamrahs for a prolonged standing"," and he would pronounce takbīr to Allah"," glorify Him"," praise Him"," and supplicate to Allah. He would not stand at the jamrah of al-ʿAqabah.\n\nAnd on the authority of Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to pronounce takbīr when stoning the jamār each time he cast a pebble.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 918.]"""
"9672","(9667) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us, saying: al-Muḥāribī narrated to us, on the authority of Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, on the authority of Waraṭah, who said: Ibn ʿUmar stood after stoning the jamrah to its left for as long as one could recite Sūrat al-Baqarah if one wished.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abī Mijlaz regarding the estimation of Ibn ʿUmar's standing: he said: \It was approximately the length of the recitation of Sūrat Yūsuf.\"" And from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he would stand for the length of the recitation of a sūrah of the hundreds (al-miʾīn). And it has been narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ: that the Prophet ﷺ would be at an elevated position at the two jamrahs when he stoned them.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn Masʿūd"," in a marfūʿ narration"," regarding the stoning of the jamrah of al-ʿAqabah from the bottom of the valley.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he said: \""Do not stone the jamrah until the day has declined (yamīl al-nahār).\"""""
"9673","(9668) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥinnāʾī narrated to us, saying: Shaybān narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated to us, on the authority of Abī Mijlaz, that a man asked Ibn ʿUmar and said: \I stoned the jamrah but I do not know whether I stoned six or seven.\"" He said: \""Go to that man\""—meaning ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. So he went and asked him"," and ʿAlī said: \""If that had happened to me in my prayer"," I would repeat the prayer.\"" So he came back and informed Ibn ʿUmar of that"," and he said: \""He spoke the truth\"" or \""He did well.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It is as though he intended—and Allah knows best—that the doubtful act should be repeated"," just as the doubtful act in stoning should be repeated. And there has already been discussed in the book of Prayer the hadith of Abī Saʿīd and others from the Prophet ﷺ regarding proceeding upon certainty (al-bināʾ ʿalā al-yaqīn). And with Allah lies success.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"9674","(9669) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, saying: al-Firyābī narrated to us, saying: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abī Najīḥ, who said: Ṭāwūs was asked about a man who omitted a pebble. He said: \He should feed a morsel.\"" He said: I mentioned that to Mujāhid"," and he said: \""Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān did not hear the statement of Saʿd.\"" Saʿd ibn Mālik said: \""We returned during the Ḥajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and among us were those who said: 'I stoned six","' and those who said: 'I stoned seven","' and none of us found fault with another.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Nasāʾī 3077. Aḥmad 1/168. Mujāhid did not hear from Saʿd.]"""
"9675","(9670) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Bazmahrānī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, on the authority of Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, on the authority of ʿIkrimah, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \I shaved before I sacrificed.\"" He said: \""No harm.\"" Another said: \""I stoned after evening (afternoon) had set in.\"" He said: \""No harm.\"" I did not know that he was asked about anything on that day except that he said: \""No harm.\"" And he did not command anything by way of expiation (kaffārah).\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it from the hadith of Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ and others"," on the authority of Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 84"," except for the final sentence; discussion on that final sentence has already passed in hadith no. 9626.]"""
"9676","(9671) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated to us, on the authority of Abū Bakr ibn Nāfiʿ, the mawlā of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the daughter of a brother of Ṣafiyyah ibn Abī ʿUbayd, the wife of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar: that she experienced menstruation (nufisat) in al-Muzdalifah, so she and Ṣafiyyah fell behind until they reached Minā after the sun had set on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr). ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar commanded them both to stone the jamrah upon their arrival, and he did not consider any expiation (kaffārah) to be incumbent upon them."
"9677","(9672) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: Whoever forgets the days of stoning the jamarat, or [he said] delays stoning the jamarat until night, let him not stone until the sun sets the following day.\n\nAnd al-Thawri reported it from a man from Nafi', who said: Ibn 'Umar said: If you forget stoning the jamra on the Day of Sacrifice until night, then stone it at night. But if it is the following day and you forget the jamarat until night, do not stone them until it is the following day at the time of the sun's decline, then stone the first one, then the first one. [Sahih]"
"9678","(9673) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Malik ibn Anas informed me. And Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, that Abu al-Baddah ibn 'Asim ibn 'Adi informed him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted the shepherds of the camels permission to spend the night and stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then stone the following day or the day after, for two days, then stone on the Day of Departure. And in the narration of Ibn Wahb: Abu al-Baddah informed him that his father 'Asim ibn 'Adi informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted permission, and he mentioned something similar to that. [Sahih. Malik 919. Abu Dawud 1975. Al-Tirmidhi 954]"
"9679","(9674) Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Isma'il ibn al-Khalil informed us: Ibn Abi Zaida informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from 'Asim ibn 'Adi, that the Prophet ﷺ granted the shepherds permission to alternate, so that they would stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then leave one day and one night, then stone the following day. [Sahih. See the preceding]"
"9680","(9675) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr and Muhammad, from their father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn 'Adi, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ granted the shepherds permission to stone one day and leave one day — thus said Ibn 'Uyayna. And thus said Ruh ibn al-Qasim from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, as though they attributed Abu al-Baddah to his grandfather, and his father was 'Asim ibn 'Adi. [Sahih. See the preceding]"
"9681","(9676) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted the shepherds of the camels permission to stone the jamarat at night. [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Malik 920]"
"9682","(9677) Abu Bakr and Abu Zakariyya informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: Muhammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: 'Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The shepherd stones at night and tends the flocks by day. [Da'if. 'Umar ibn Qays is matruk (abandoned)]"
"9683","(9678) With this isnad: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it. [Da'if. It is mursal]"
"9684","(9679) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet ﷺ granted the shepherds permission to stone at night. [Da'if. Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji is known for many errors]"
"9685","(9680) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from two men of Banu Bakr, who said: We saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon between the middle days of al-Tashriq, and we were near his mount, and this was the sermon of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which he delivered in Mina. [Sahih. Abu Dawud 1952]"
"9686","(9681) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah — (h) — and Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qatada al-Nu'mani informed us: Abu 'Amr Isma'il ibn Nujayd al-Sulami informed us: Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn al-Basri narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hisn al-Ghannawi, who narrated to me: Sarra' bint Nabhan, who was a mistress of a household in the pre-Islamic era, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \Do you know what day this is?\"" — and it was the day they called Yawm al-Ru'us — they said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""This is the middle day of al-Tashriq. Do you know what land this is?\"" They said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""This is the Sacred Monument (al-Mash'ar al-Haram).\"" Then he said: \""I do not know"," perhaps I shall not meet you after this. Beware! Your blood"," your wealth"," and your honour are sacred to you like the sacredness of this day of yours"," in this land of yours"," until you meet your Lord and He asks you about your deeds. Beware! Let those who are near inform those who are far. Beware! Have I conveyed?\"" When we arrived in Madinah"," he did not remain long before he passed away ﷺ.\n\nAnd Muhammad ibn Bashshar reported it from Abu 'Asim with this isnad"," and he said: She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on Yawm al-Ru'us. [Da'if. Abu Dawud 1953. Ibn Khuzaymah 2973. Al-Tabarani al-Kabir 777. Al-Tabarani al-Awsat 2430. Rabi'ah is majhul al-hal]"""
"9687","(9682) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq ibn Yazīd al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah al-Rabadhī informed me; Ṣadaqah ibn Yasār informed me from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: This Sūrah — *\When the victory of Allah and the conquest come\""* (Idhā jāʾa naṣru Allāhi wa al-fatḥ) — was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the middle of the Days of Tashrīq"," and he understood that it was the [sign of] farewell. He ordered his she-camel al-Qaṣwāʾ to be saddled"," so it was saddled for him. He mounted it and stopped at al-ʿAqabah. The people gathered"," and he said: \""O people…\"" — and he mentioned the hadith regarding his sermon. [Weak. ʿAbd ibn Ḥamīd in al-Muntakhab: 858. Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah al-Rabadhī is weak.]"""
"9688","(9683) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us; Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿmur al-Dīlī, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) standing at ʿArafāt. A group of people from the people of Najd came to him and asked him about the Ḥajj. He said: \The Ḥajj is [the standing on] the Day of ʿArafah. Whoever catches it before the dawn prayer has caught the Ḥajj. The Days of Minā are three days — the Days of Tashrīq. Whoever hastens [to depart] within two days"," there is no sin upon him"," and whoever delays"," there is no sin upon him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 1949. Al-Tirmidhī 889. Al-Nasāʾī 3016.]"""
"9689","(9684) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Ḥibbān ibn Hilāl narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Qudāmah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ruʾāsī narrated to us; al-Ḍaḥḥāk narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Exalted: *\Whoever hastens within two days"," there is no sin upon him"," and whoever delays"," there is no sin upon him\""* — he said: Whoever hastens within two days will be forgiven"," and whoever delays until [the end of] three days will be forgiven. [Weak. Qudāmah is unknown in status"," and al-Ḍaḥḥāk did not meet Ibn ʿAbbās.]"""
"9690","(9685) He said: And Ḥibbān ibn Hilāl narrated to us from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from ʿAlī ibn Zayd, from al-Ḥasan, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding [the verse]: *\Whoever hastens within two days"," there is no sin upon him\""* — he said: He will return having been forgiven — or he said: He will be forgiven. [Weak. Al-Ṭabarānī in his Tafsīr 2/314. It contains ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān"," who is weak.]"""
"9691","(9686) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: Whoever is overtaken by sunset while he is in Minā during the middle of the Days of Tashrīq, let him not depart until he has stoned the jamarāt the following day. Al-Thawrī narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said — and he mentioned its meaning. That was also narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, in a marfūʿ (elevated) narration, but its elevation is weak. It is the view of al-Ḥasan, Jābir ibn Zayd, and al-Nakhaʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 915.]"
"9692","(9687) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ṭalḥah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When the day begins from the Day of the Final Departure (al-Nafr al-Ākhir), then the stoning (ramy) and the departure (al-ṣadr) become permissible. Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAmr al-Makkī is very weak. [Very weak. It contains Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAmr, who is severely weak.]"
"9693","(9688) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās said: Whoever forgets or omits anything from his rites (nusuk), let him shed blood [i.e., offer a sacrifice]. Mālik said: \I do not know whether he said 'omits' or 'forgets.'\"" The Sheikh said: And al-Thawrī narrated it from Ayyūb: \""Whoever omits or forgets anything from his rites"," let him shed blood for it\"" — as though he said both together. And it has been narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he said: Whoever forgets one jamrah or all the jamarāt until the Days of Tashrīq have passed"," a single blood offering will suffice him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 940. Ibn al-Jaʿd 1749.]"""
"9694","(9689) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Khallād al-Bāhilī narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ḥarīz — or Abū Ḥarīz — informed me. Abū Bakr said: \This [element of] doubt is from Yaḥyā.\"" He said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Farrūkh asking Ibn ʿUmar. He said: \""We buy\"" — or he said: \""We trade\"" — \""with the wealth of the people"," and one of us comes to Makkah and spends the night with the wealth.\"" He said: \""As for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," he spent the night\"" — or he said: \""He did spend the night\"" — \""in Minā and remained there during the day.\"" [Very weak. Abū Dāwūd 1958. Abū Ḥarīz is unknown.]"""
"9695","(9690) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \None of the pilgrims shall spend the nights of Minā behind [i.e."," beyond] al-ʿAqabah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 910.]"""
"9696","(9691) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Usāmah and Ibn Numayr said: ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to spend the nights of Minā in Makkah on account of his duty of providing water (siqāyah), and he granted him permission. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shayyah, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr from his father. He said: And Abū Usābah and Abū Ḍamrah — meaning Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ — and others followed him [in this narration]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 1658. Muslim 1315.]"
"9697","(9692) It was narrated by ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from ʿUbayd Allāh from Nāʿif from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib permission to spend the nights of Minā in Makkah on account of his providing water (siqāyah) to the pilgrims. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus informed us — and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Maymūn from ʿĪsā, and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"
"9698","(9693) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Anas al-Qurashī informed us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Ibn ʿAbbās, who attributed it (marfūʿan) and said: When Ibrāhīm, the Khalīl of Allah, peace be upon him, came to perform the rites (manāsik), the Shayṭān appeared to him at the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank into the earth. Then he appeared to him at the second Jamrah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank into the earth. Then he appeared to him at the third Jamrah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank into the earth. Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is the Shayṭān you are stoning, and it is the millah of your father (Ibrāhīm) that you are following. [Ṣaḥīḥ in its own right (li-ghayrihi).]"
"9699","(9694) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us; al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī al-Ghazzāl narrated to us. Both said: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us; Abū Ḥamzah narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Jibrīl, peace be upon him, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took him to show him the rites (manāsik). Thabīr split open for him, and he entered Minā. He showed him the jamarāt, then he showed him al-Muzdalifah (Jamaʿ), then he showed him ʿArafāt. Then the Shayṭān appeared before the Prophet ﷺ at the Jamrah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank. Then he appeared to him at the second Jamrah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank. Then he appeared to him at the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he sank, and then he departed.\n\nA similar narration was reported from ʿAbdān ibn ʿUthmān from Abū Ḥamzah — thus ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib was alone in narrating it in this manner. [Munkar. Ibn Khuzaymah 2967. Al-Ḥākim 1/650.]"
"9700","(9695) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us from Abū ʿĀṣim al-Ghawwī from Abī al-Ṭufayl, who said: I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, \Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ṭawāf upon a camel and that it is a sunnah.\"" He said"," \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said"," \""What is the truth and what is the lie?\"" He said"," \""They spoke the truth that he performed ṭawāf upon a camel"," but it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have the people kept away from him nor pushed aside"," so he performed ṭawāf upon the camel so that they could hear his words and their hands could not reach him.\"" I said"," \""They claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal during the ṭawāf of the House and that it is a sunnah.\"" He said"," \""They have spoken the truth and they have lied.\"" I said"," \""What is the truth and what is the lie?\"" He said"," \""They spoke the truth that he performed ramal"," but they lied in saying it is a sunnah. Quraysh said"," 'Leave Muḥammad and his companions until they die the death of the nasaf worm.' When they made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that they would come the following year and stay in Makkah for three days"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived"," and the polytheists were positioned at Quʿayqiʿān. He said to your companions"," 'Perform ramal.' And it is not a sunnah.\"" I said"," \""Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and that it is a sunnah.\"" He said"," \""They have spoken the truth. When Ibrāhīm"," peace be upon him"," was shown the rites"," the Shayṭān appeared to him at the place of saʿy"," so he raced him"," and Ibrāhīm"," peace be upon him"," outran him. Then Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," took him until he brought him to Minā and said"," 'This is the place where the people dismount.' Then he came to the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah"," and the Shayṭān appeared to him"," so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he departed. Then Jibrīl brought him to al-Muzdalifah and said"," 'This is al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām.' Then he brought him to ʿArafah and said"," 'This is ʿArafah.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said"," \""Do you know why it was called ʿArafah?\"" He said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""Because Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," said to him"," 'Have you recognized (ʿarafta)?'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said"," \""Do you know how the talbiyah was?\"" I said"," \""How was the talbiyah?\"" He said"," \""When Ibrāhīm"," peace be upon him"," was commanded to announce the ḥajj to the people"," the mountains were commanded"," so they lowered their peaks and the villages were raised up for him"," and he announced the ḥajj to the people.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in its own right (li-ghayrihi). Aḥmad 1/297. Abū Dāwūd 1885. Ṭayālisī 2697.]"""
"9701","(9696) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAmmī informed us; Ibn ʿĀʾishah informed us; Ḥammād — and he is Ibn Salamah — informed us; Abū ʿĀṣim al-Ghawwī informed us, and he mentioned the hadith similarly, except that he said: \He performed ṭawāf between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah upon a camel.\"" And he added at his statement: \""Then the Shayṭān appeared to him at the middle Jamrah"," so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he departed. Then he laid him down on the forehead"," and Ismāʿīl was wearing a white shirt"," and he said"," 'O father"," I have no garment in which you can shroud me.' So he set about removing it for him"," and a voice called out from behind him: 'O Ibrāhīm"," you have fulfilled the vision. Indeed"," thus do We reward the doers of good.' So Ibrāhīm turned and saw a large-horned"," wide-eyed white ram"," and he slaughtered it.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said"," \""We used to seek out that type of ram.\"" Then Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," took him to the furthest Jamrah"," and the Shayṭān appeared to him"," so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he departed. Then he mentioned the remainder of the hadith similarly. Ibn ʿĀʾishah said: \""The nasaf is a worm found in the nostrils of sheep.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in its own right (li-ghayrihi). See its predecessor and its chain is ṣāliḥ.]"""
"9702","(9697) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and the wording is his — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us; Abū al-Naḍr informed us. Both said: Isḥāq ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from his father Saʿīd, who said: al-Ḥajjāj came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, to visit him while I was with him, and he said to him, \How do you find yourself?\"" He said"," \""I find myself well.\"" He said"," \""Who injured your leg?\"" He said"," \""The one who ordered the carrying of weapons on a day in which carrying them is not permissible\"" — meaning al-Ḥajjāj. He said"," \""Had we known him"," we would have punished him.\"" The reason for this was that the people had departed on the night of departure (nafar)"," and a man from al-Ḥajjāj's guards was standing with his spear extended"," and he struck the top of Ibn ʿUmar's foot"," and he was treated for it until he died from it. The hadith of Abū Nuʿaym is abridged"," and this is the hadith of Abū al-Naḍr.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb from Isḥāq ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 924.]"""
"9703","(9698) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashīr al-Dahqān al-Kūfī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ informed us.\n\nAnd Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj informed us; Muṭayyin informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ṭarīf informed us. Both said: al-Muḥāribī narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Suqah from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: I was with Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, when the point of a spear struck him in the sole of his foot, and the sole of his foot became stuck in the stirrup. He dismounted and removed it, and that was at Minā. News of this reached al-Ḥajjāj, so he came to visit him and said, \If only we knew who injured you!\"" Ibn ʿUmar said"," \""You are the one who injured me.\"" He said"," \""How so?\"" He said"," \""You carried weapons on a day in which they were not to be carried"," and you brought weapons into the Ḥaram"," when weapons were not to be brought into the Ḥaram.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Sukayn Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Muḥāribī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 923.]"""
"9704","(9699) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī informed us; Salamah ibn Shabīb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan informed us; Maʿqil narrated to us from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \It is not permissible for any one of you to carry weapons in Makkah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1356.]"""
"9705","(9700) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī informed us, and he mentioned it similarly. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb."
"9706","(9701) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — among the last narrators — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah from Kurayb, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet ﷺ was returning (from a journey), and when he was at al-Rawḥāʾ, he met a group of riders. He greeted them and said, \Who are the people?\"" They said"," \""The Muslims.\"" He said"," \""And who are the people?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""The Messenger of Allah.\"" A woman raised her child to him from a howdah and said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," does this one have a ḥajj?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1336.]"""
"9707","(9702) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — he dictated — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik reported to us, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a woman who was in her howdah. It was said to her: \This is the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" She took hold of the arm of a young boy who was with her and said: \""Is there Hajj for this one?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\nAl-Rabīʿ narrated it from al-Shāfiʿī in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. It was also narrated from Abī Muṣʿab from Mālik"," and al-Zaʿfarānī narrated it in al-Qadīm from al-Shāfiʿī in a disconnected (munqaṭiʿ) chain without the mention of Ibn ʿAbbās therein. Likewise"," Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr and others narrated it from Mālik in a disconnected chain. And likewise"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated it from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah in a disconnected chain. And Abū Nuʿaym narrated it from Sufyān in a connected chain."""
"9708","(9703) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu), who said: A woman raised her son in a howdah, nursing him, on the road to Makkah, and she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," is there Hajj for this one?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\"" Or as he said.\n\n[Sound. See the preceding.]"""
"9709","(9704) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — he dictated — Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A woman raised a young boy to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \Is there Hajj for this one?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\n[Sound. See the preceding.]"""
"9710","(9705) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yazīd narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Abī ʿAbbād narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated from his father, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu), who said: While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was travelling on the road to Makkah, a woman in her howdah spoke to him. She took hold of the arm of a young boy, raised him, and said: \Is there Hajj for this one"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""For him is Hajj"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\n[Sound. See the preceding.]"""
"9711","(9706) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us — he dictated — Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Qāḍī al-Zuhrī narrated to us in Makkah, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Asbāṭ narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a woman who was in her howdah, and she had a young boy with her. She said: \O Messenger of Allah"," is there Hajj for this one?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us"," Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī informed us"," Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us"," Ibn Kathīr narrated to us"," Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah"," from Kurayb"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: A woman raised a young boy of hers from a howdah and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," is there Hajj for this one?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\n[Sound. See the preceding.]"""
"9712","(9707) He said, and Sulaymān narrated to us, Muʿādh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Ibn Mahdī narrated.\n\n[Sound.]"
"9713","(9708) He said, and Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated — all of them from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (ﷺ), similar to it, but there is no mention of the howdah in it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muthannā from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, and from Abī Kurayb from Abū Usāmah.\n\n[Sound. See the preceding.]"
"9714","(9709) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Suqah, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: A woman raised a young boy of hers to the Prophet (ﷺ) during his Hajj and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," is there Hajj for this one?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and for you is a reward.\""\n\n[Sound. Tirmidhī 924. Ibn Mājah 2910.]"""
"9715","(9710) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Fāryābī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, al-Qāsim ibn Mālik narrated from al-Juʿayd, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: al-Sāʾib said to me: \The Ṣāʿ at the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was a mudd and a third of your mudd today. Then it was increased during the time of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz.\"" Al-Sāʾib said: \""I was taken for Hajj in the caravan of the Prophet (ﷺ) while I was a young boy.\""\n\n[Sound. Bukhārī 6334.]"""
"9716","(9711) Abū ʿAmr informed us, Abū Bakr informed us, Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād al-Makkī narrated to us, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd, who said: \I was taken for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage"," and I was seven years old.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Zurārah from al-Qāsim ibn Mālik"," and from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yūnus from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl.\n\n[Sound. Bukhārī 6899.]"""
"9717","(9712) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd narrated to us; he said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās relating, he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with the weak members of the family from Muzdalifah at night"," so we prayed and stoned [the Jamrah] before the people arrived.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿmān"," from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1757"," Muslim 1293]"""
"9718","(9713) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Haddādī narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated to us from Ashʿath, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \We set out with the Prophet ﷺ"," and with us were women and children"," until we reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah"," so we pronounced the talbiyah for Ḥajj and performed the talbiyah on behalf of the children.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 6564"," Ibn Mājah 3038"," Tirmidhī 927]"""
"9719","(9714) Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mihrānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Sakhtiyānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Sarrāj narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad ibn Bukayr al-Nāqid narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us from Ayman, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \We performed Ḥajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and with us were women and young children"," so we pronounced the talbiyah on behalf of the young children and performed the stoning on their behalf.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. See the preceding]"""
"9720","(9715) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ṣaqr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Saʿdawayh narrated to us, Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Aswad narrated to us from Ashʿath, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, and he mentioned it with the same wording that Ayman ibn Nābil mentioned.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"
"9721","(9716) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, Hārūn ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us from Muṭarrif, from Abū al-Safar, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās saying: \O people"," listen to what I say to you"," and make me hear what you say"," and do not go away and say 'Ibn ʿAbbās said such-and-such.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Whoever performs ṭawāf of the House"," let him perform ṭawāf from behind the Ḥijr"," and do not say 'al-Ḥaṭīm","' for a man in the Jāhiliyyah would take an oath and cast aside his whip"," or his sandal"," or his bow. And any child whose family performs Ḥajj on his behalf"," his Ḥajj has been fulfilled for him so long as he remains a minor; but when he reaches puberty"," another Ḥajj is incumbent upon him. And any slave whose family performs Ḥajj on his behalf"," his Ḥajj has been fulfilled for him so long as he remains a slave; but when he is freed"," another Ḥajj is incumbent upon him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"," from Sufyān"," except that he did not narrate the hadith in its entirety.\n\nAnd we have narrated previously the hadith of Abū Ẓabyān from Ibn ʿAbbās"," both Mawqūf and Marfūʿ"," regarding the Ḥajj of the child and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3635]"""
"9722","(9717) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʬAṭāʾ, that a young man from Quraysh killed a pigeon from the pigeons of Makkah, so Ibn ʿAbbāh — may Allah be pleased with him — ordered that a sheep be given as ransom on his behalf.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Shāfiʿī 1689]"
"9723","(9718) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in the year twenty-five and three hundred, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered on the day of the Conquest of Makkah upon the she-camel of Usāmah ibn Zayd"," until he made it kneel at the courtyard of the Kaʿbah. Then he called ʿUthmān ibn Ṭalḥah for the key; he brought it and opened it. The Prophet ﷺ entered"," along with Usāmah"," Bilāl"," and ʿUthmān ibn Ṭalḥah"," and they closed the door upon themselves for a long time"," then they opened it. ʿAbd Allāh said: I hastened ahead of the people and found Bilāl at the door"," so I asked: 'Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?' He said: 'Between the two front pillars.' And I forgot to ask him how many he prayed.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1329]"""
"9724","(9719) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I read to Mālik ibn Anas. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us — in what he read to Mālik — from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Kaʿbah, he and Usāmah ibn Zayd, ʿUthmān ibn Ṭalḥah al-Ḥajabī, and Bilāl, and he closed it upon himself and remained inside. ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \I asked Bilāl when he came out: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do?' He said: 'He placed one pillar to his left"," two pillars to his right"," and three pillars behind him. The House at that time stood upon six pillars. Then he prayed.'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and others"," from Mālik"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," except that he said: \""Two pillars to his left.\""\n\nAnd likewise al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from Mālik in one of the two places"," and in another place he said: \""One pillar to his right and one pillar to his left.\""\n\nAnd likewise ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated it from Mālik"," and Abū Dāwūd from al-Qaʿnabī from Mālik"," and Ibn Abī Uways and Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated it from Mālik"," as we have narrated it.\n\nAnd likewise ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated it from Mālik: \""Two pillars to his right and one pillar to his left","\"" and this is the correct version.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 483"," Muslim 1329]"""
"9725","(9720) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Baghawī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṭālaqānī narrated to us in the year twenty-five and two hundred; he said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he asked Bilāl where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed — meaning inside the Kaʿbah — so Bilāl showed him where he had prayed, and he did not ask him how many he prayed. And whenever Ibn ʿUmar entered the House, he would walk straight ahead, placing the door behind his back, then walk until he was close to the wall, approximately three cubits away, then he would pray, seeking the place which Bilāl had informed him the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed in.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1522]"
"9726","(9721) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to me, al-Layth narrated to me. And Yūnus ibn Yazīd said: Nāfiʿ informed me from ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came on the Day of the Conquest from the upper part of Makkah upon his mount, with Usāmah ibn Zayd riding behind him, and with him was Bilāl, and with him was ʿUthmān ibn Ṭalḥah from the gatekeepers, until he made it kneel in the mosque. He then ordered him to bring the key of the House. He opened it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, along with Usāmah, Bilāl, and ʿUthmān, and he remained inside for a long part of the day, then he came out. The people rushed forward, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar was the first to enter. He found Bilāl standing behind the door and asked him: \Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\"" He pointed to the place in which he had prayed. ʿAbd Allāh said: \""I forgot to ask him how many prostrations he prayed.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ"," and he said: \""And al-Layth said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1522]"""
"9727","(9722) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and Abū ʿImrān al-Tustarī both said: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived—meaning Makkah—he refused to enter the House while the idols were inside it. He gave the command, and they were brought out. Then the image of Ibrāhīm and Ismāʿīl was brought out, with arrows of divination in their hands. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \May Allah destroy them! By Allah"," they certainly knew that the two of them never used these for divination at all.\"" Then he entered the House and pronounced takbīr in its corners"," but he did not pray inside it.\n\nThese are the words of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿImrān. The ḥadīth of al-Qāḍī is abridged: that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered the House and pronounced takbīr in its corners"," then descended"," and did not pray.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Maʿmar from ʿAbd al-Wārith.\n\nThe correct position is the one who said he prayed"," because he is a witness"," whereas the one who said he did not pray is not a witness. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1524]"""
"9728","(9723) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Ḥajjāj al-Aʿwar said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh assert that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade images in the House and forbade a man from making them; and that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb at the time of the Conquest, while he was in al-Baṭḥāʾ, to go to the Kaʿbah and erase every image in it. He did not enter the House until every image in it had been erased. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Ḥibbān 5844. Aḥmad 3/335. Abū Yaʿlā 2244]"
"9729","(9724) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr informed me that Bukayr narrated to him from Kurayb, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the House and found therein the image of Ibrāhīm and the image of Maryam, he said: \As for them"," they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrāhīm depicted—so what is the matter with him that he is practising divination?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3173]"""
"9730","(9725) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Ibn al-Muʾammal narrated from Ibn Muḥayṣin from ʬAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever enters the House enters into a good deed"," departs from a sin"," and leaves forgiven.\""\n\nThis is narrated solely by ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Muʾammal"," and he is not strong (in ḥadīth). [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Khuzaymah 3013. Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 1149]"""
"9731","(9726) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Mālik al-Lakhmī in Tinnīs narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah al-Tinnīsī narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad al-Makkī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh that ʿĀʾishah used to say: \How remarkable it is for a Muslim person—when he enters the Kaʿbah"," how he raises his gaze toward the ceiling! He should abandon that out of reverence for Allah and out of veneration. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the Kaʿbah and did not divert his gaze from the place of his prostration until he came out of it.\"" [Bāṭil. Ḥākim 1/652. Ibn Khuzaymah 3012]"""
"9732","(9727) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us by recitation. Both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: ʬAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). She said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," all your wives have entered the House except me.\"" He said: \""Go to your relative and let him open it for you.\"" She said: So I went to him and said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commands you to open it for me.\"" She said: So he took the keys and went with her to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," the door was never opened at night"," neither in the Jāhiliyyah nor in Islam.\"" He said to ʿĀʾishah: \""Your people"," when they built the House"," the expenditure fell short for them"," so they left part of the House within the Ḥijr. Go and pray two rakʿahs in the Ḥijr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Aḥmad 6/67. Ṭabarānī al-Awsaṭ 7098. Abū Dāwūd 2028. Tirmidhī 876]"""
"9733","(9728) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid. He said: I said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Awfā: \Did the Prophet (ﷺ) enter the House during his ʿUmrah?\"" He said: \""No.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Surayj ibn Yūnus"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Ismāʿīl."""
"9734","(9729) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī narrated to us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Ṣafirāʾ narrated—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mihrān ibn Khālid narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). She said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) left me while his eyes were content and his soul was at ease. Then he returned to me while he was distressed. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you left me in such-and-such a state.' He said: 'I entered the Kaʿbah"," and I wish I had not done so. I fear that I may have placed a burden upon my Ummah after me.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Tirmidhī 873. Ibn Mājah 3064]\n\nThe Sheikh said: This would have been during his Ḥajj"," whereas the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Awfā pertains to his ʿUmrah"," so neither of the two contradicts the other."""
"9735","(9730) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Hārūn ibn Yūsuf Abū Aḥmad narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Wāṣil ibn Ḥayyān al-Aḥdab from Abū Wāʾil Shaqīq ibn Salamah. He said: \I sat with Shaybah ibn ʿUthmān in the Masjid al-Ḥarām"," and he said to me: 'ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) sat with me in the very place where you are sitting"," and he said: \""I have resolved not to leave any gold or silver in it\""—meaning the Kaʿbah—\""except that I will distribute it.\""' Shaybah said: I said: 'You had two companions who did not do that—the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him).' ʿUmar said: 'They are the two men whose example I follow.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6847]"""
"9736","(9731) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfaraʾīnī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Madanī narrated to us: My father informed me: ʿAlqamah ibn Abī ʿAlqamah narrated from his mother. She said: \Shaybah ibn ʿUthmān al-Ḥajabī came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: 'O Mother of the Believers"," the cloth coverings of the Kaʿbah accumulate with us and become numerous"," so we resort to digging wells and deepening them"," then we bury the cloth coverings of the Kaʿbah in them"," so that no one in a state of janābah or a menstruating woman may wear them.' ʿĿʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to him: 'You have not done well"," and what you have done is indeed bad. When the cloth coverings of the Kaʿbah are removed from it"," it does no harm for a person in a state of janābah or a menstruating woman to wear them. Rather"," sell them and give their price to the poor and in the cause of Allah.'\"" She said: \""After that"," Shaybah used to send them to Yemen"," where they were sold"," and their price was given to the poor"," to the cause of Allah"," and to the wayfarer.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9737","(9732) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Ḥibbān narrated to us from Ibn al-Mubārak.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us that Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Abī Ḥafṣah, narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \They used to fast on ʿĀshūrāʾ before Ramaḍān was made obligatory"," and it was a day on which the Kaʿbah was covered.\"" She said: \""When Allah made Ramaḍān obligatory"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever wishes to fast it"," let him fast it"," and whoever wishes to leave it"," let him leave it.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1515]"""
"9738","(9733) Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us that my father informed me that al-Awzāʿī informed me that Ibn Shihāb narrated to me from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said when he intended to depart from Minā: \We shall descend tomorrow"," if Allah wills"," at Khayf Banī Kinānah"," where they swore upon disbelief.\"" He meant by that al-Muḥaṣṣab. That was because Quraysh and Banī Kinānah had sworn against Banī Hāshim and Banī al-Muṭṭalib that they would not intermarry with them and that there would be no dealings between them until they handed over the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to them.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī and Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1523. Muslim 1314]"""
"9739","(9734) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Mihrajānī informed us there that Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Madanī informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn Hammām informed me that Maʿmar narrated to me from al-Zuhrī from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn from ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān from Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," where will you encamp?' That was during his Ḥajj. He said: 'Has ʿAqīl left us any place to stay?' Then he said: 'We shall descend tomorrow at Khayf Banī Kinānah"," where the disbelievers swore.'\"" He meant by that al-Muḥaṣṣab. That was because Quraysh and Kinānah had sworn against Banī Hāshim that they would not intermarry with them"," nor trade with them"," nor give them shelter. Al-Zuhrī said: \""Al-Khayf means the valley.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Maḥmūd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Mihrān and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2893. Muslim 1351]"""
"9740","(9735) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that my father informed us that Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated to us from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ), Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to encamp at al-Abṭaḥ.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Rāzī from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. He also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he considered al-Taḥṣīb (encamping at al-Muḥaṣṣab) to be a Sunnah, and he used to pray Ẓuhr on the day of departure at al-Ḥaṣbah. Nāfiʿ said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encamped there"," and so did the Caliphs after him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1310]"""
"9741","(9736) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿd al-Bazzāz informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Khālid and Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf both said: Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah informed us that Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿUbaydullāh narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to pray there—meaning al-Muḥaṣṣab—Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr. Khālid said: \And I think he also mentioned Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.\"" He said: \""And he would rest and mention that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did that"," or used to do that.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥajjābī from Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1679]"""
"9742","(9737) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Qatādah ibn Dāʿimah narrated to him from Anas ibn Mālik that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ at al-Muḥaṣṣab, then took a short rest, then rode to the House and performed Ṭawāf around it.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Muʿālī ibn Ṭālib from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1675]"
"9743","(9738) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us orally that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \Al-Muḥaṣṣab is nothing; it is merely a place where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encamped.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madanī"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1677. Muslim 1312]"""
"9744","(9739) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us that Abū Nuʿaym informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \It was merely a place where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encamped to make his departure easier—meaning al-Abṭaḥ.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Hishām. Some of them added from Hishām: \""And it is not a Sunnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1676. Muslim 1311]"""
"9745","(9740) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only encamped at al-Muḥaṣṣab to make his departure easier"," and it is not a Sunnah. So whoever wishes may encamp there"," and whoever wishes may not.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 2008. Aḥmad 6/190. Ibn Khuzaymah 2987]"""
"9746","(9741) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that Abū ʿAlī Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣawwāf informed us that Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us that al-Ḥumaydī informed us that Sufyān informed us that Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān informed us that he heard Sulaymān ibn Yasār narrating from Abū Rāfiʿ, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not command me to encamp with those who were with me at al-Abṭaḥ; rather"," I set up his tent"," then he came and encamped there.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""ʿAmr ibn Dīnār used to narrate this ḥadīth from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān. When Ṣāliḥ came to us"," ʿAmr said: 'Go to him and ask him about this ḥadīth.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," Abū Bakr"," and Zuhayr from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1313]"""
"9747","(9742) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Aflaḥ ibn Ḥumayd informed us, from al-Qāsim, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the nights of Hajj. She mentioned the hadith and said: Until Allah decreed the completion of Hajj, and we departed from Minā and encamped at al-Muḥaṣṣab. Then he ﷺ called ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr and said: \Take your sister out of the Ḥaram"," then complete your Ṭawāf"," and then come to me here at al-Muḥaṣṣab.\"" She said: So Allah decreed the completion of the ʿUmrah"," and we completed our Ṭawāf in the depths of the night"," and came to him at al-Muḥaṣṣab. He ﷺ said: \""Have you completed?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" Then he ﷺ announced the departure to the people. He passed by the House and performed Ṭawāf of it"," then departed heading towards Madīnah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Aflaḥ ibn Ḥumayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1696. Muslim 1217]"""
"9748","(9743) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Abū Bakr, i.e., al-Ḥanafī, narrated to us: Aflaḥ narrated it, mentioning it up to where she said: Then I came to him at the time of suḥr, and he ﷺ announced the departure to his companions. He set out and passed by the House before the Ṣalāt al-Ṣubḥ and performed Ṭawāf of it when he departed, then he turned away heading towards Madīnah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1485. Abū Dāwūd 2006]"
"9749","(9744) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Sulaymān al-Aḥwal, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The people used to disperse in every direction, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \Let none of the pilgrims depart until his last act be at the House.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1668. Muslim 1328]"""
"9750","(9745) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Shīrāzī narrated to us: Saʿīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated, and he mentioned the hadith with a similar meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9751","(9746) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The people were commanded that their last act should be at the House, except that concession was granted to the menstruating woman. And in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \except that concession was granted to the menstruating woman.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"9752","(9747) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Let none of the pilgrims depart until he has performed Ṭawāf of the House"," and indeed the last of the rites is the Ṭawāf of the House.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 823]"""
"9753","(9748) And with his chain of narration, he said: Mālik narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah the Most High be pleased with him, sent back a man from Marr al-Ẓahrān who had not performed the farewell Ṭawāf of the House.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Mālik 824]"
"9754","(9749) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated, and he mentioned both hadiths together.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"9755","(9750) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik and Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Mālik narrated, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, menstruated, and that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he ﷺ said: \Will she detain us?\"" It was said: \""She has already performed the Ifāḍah Ṭawāf.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Then no.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbd Allāh.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim recorded it from the ḥadīth of Ayyūb"," Ibn ʿUyaynah"," and al-Layth"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 167. Muslim 1311]"""
"9756","(9751) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb narrated, from al-Zuḥrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān both narrated to me that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed them that Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, menstruated during the Farewell Pilgrimage at Minā after she had performed the Ifāḍah and had done Ṭawāf of the House. ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Ṣafiyyah has menstruated.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Will she detain us?\"" I said: \""Indeed"," she has already performed the Ifāḍah"," O Messenger of Allah"," and has done Ṭawāf of the House.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Then let her depart.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 9140]"""
"9757","(9752) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus ibn Yazīd and others from the people of knowledge informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," menstruated after the Farewell Pilgrimage"," after she had performed the Ifāḍah in a state of purity and had circumambulated the House. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: 'Will she hold us back?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," she has already performed the Ifāḍah while she was pure"," and then she menstruated after the Ifāḍah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then let her depart.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and others"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1211]"""
"9758","(9753) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \Ṣafiyyah menstruated after she had performed the Ifāḍah. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: 'Will she hold us back?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," she has already performed the Ifāḍah"," and then she menstruated after that.' He ﷺ said: 'Then let her depart.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Mālik 929]"""
"9759","(9754) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy, and it was said: \She has menstruated.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Perhaps she will hold us back.\"" It was said: \""She has already performed the Ifāḍah.\"" He said: \""Then no [she will not hold us back].\""\n\nMālik said: Hishām said: ʿUrwah said: ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""We used to mention that. Why would the people send their women ahead if it were of no benefit to them? Had that been the case"," there would have been more than six thousand menstruating women in Minā"," all of whom had already performed the Ifāḍah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 5805"," Muslim 1211]"""
"9760","(9755) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī al-Faqīh in Ṭūs informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī in Baṣrah informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us: Ādam informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī informed us: al-Aswad ibn Yazīd informed us, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to depart"," and he saw Ṣafiyyah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," at the door of her tent"," distressed or grieved"," because she had menstruated. He said to her: 'Aqri ḥalqi' — in the dialect of Quraysh: 'Indeed"," you will hold us back.' Then he said: 'Did you not perform the Ifāḍah on the Day of Sacrifice?' — meaning the circumambulation. She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then depart.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās"," and Muslim narrated it from two other routes from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 5805]"""
"9761","(9756) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, saying: I read to Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, from his father, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \O Messenger of Allah"," Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy has menstruated.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Perhaps she will hold us back.\"" And in the narration of ʿAbd Allāh: \""Perhaps she will hold us back. Did she not circumambulate the House with you?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then depart.\"" And in the narration of ʿAbd Allāh: \""Then you [all] depart.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 322"," Muslim 1211]"""
"9762","(9757) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Abū al-Rijāl, from his mother ʿAmrah, that she informed him that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when her women performed the Ḥajj with her and she feared that they might menstruate, she would send them forward on the Day of Sacrifice, so they would perform the Ifāḍah. If they menstruated after that, she would not wait for them to become pure; she would depart with them while they were menstruating. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Mālik 928]"
"9763","(9758) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us: Wuhayb informed us. And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā informed us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād informed us: Wuhayb informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs informed us, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Concession was granted to the menstruating woman that she may depart if she has performed the Ifāḍah.\"" Abū ʿAmr added in his ḥadīth: \""And I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: 'At first"," the matter was that she would not depart.' Then I heard him say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted them concession.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿallā ibn Asad"," from Wuhayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 323]"""
"9764","(9759) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Rūḥ informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ḥasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Ṭāwūs, who said: \I was with Ibn ʿAbbās when Zayd ibn Thābit said to him: 'Do you issue a fatwā that the menstruating woman may depart before her final act at the House?' He said: 'Yes.' Zayd said: 'Then do not issue that fatwā.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'As for me"," go and ask so-and-so woman from the Anṣār — did the Prophet ﷺ command her to do that?' Zayd ibn Thābit returned to him"," laughing"," and said: 'I see that you have spoken the truth.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1328]"""
"9765","(9760) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, and he mentioned it with its meaning. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — see the previous ḥadīth]"
"9766","(9761) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿAlī al-Saqqāʾ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ al-Isfarāʾinī both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us, from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \The people of Madīnah asked Ibn ʿAbbās about a woman who circumambulated the House on the Day of Sacrifice and then menstruated. He said: 'She may depart.' They said: 'We will not accept your opinion"," for Zayd ibn Thābit contradicts you.' He said: 'When you come to Madīnah"," then ask.' When they came to Madīnah"," they asked"," and they were informed about Ṣafiyyah. Among those they asked was Umm Sulaym"," and she informed them about Ṣafiyyah.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān"," from Ḥammād. al-Bukhārī said: And it was narrated by Khālid and Qatādah from ʿIkrimah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 1671]"""
"9767","(9762) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khālid al-Ḍaḥḥāʾ narrated from ʿIkrimah that Zayd ibn Thābit said: \She should remain until she becomes pure and her last occasion is at the House.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās then said: \""If she has performed ṭawāf on the Day of Naḥr"," then let her depart.\"" So Zayd ibn Thābit sent a message to Ibn ʿAbbās: \""I have found what you said to be exactly as you said it.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās then said: \""I know the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding women"," but I preferred to speak according to what is in the Book of Allah.\"" Then he recited this verse: *\""Then let them complete their rites"," fulfill their vows"," and perform ṭawāf around the Ancient House\""* (al-Ḥajj 22:29). She has completed her rites"," fulfilled her vow"," and performed ṭawāf around the House — so what remains? [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9768","(9763) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: \If she performs ṭawāf on the Day of Naḥr and then menstruates"," let her depart.\"" And Zayd ibn Thābit said: \""She should not depart until she becomes pure and performs ṭawāf around the House.\"" Then after that he sent a message to Ibn ʿAbbāb and mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9769","(9764) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from ʿIkrimah who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās and Zayd ibn Thābit differed concerning this matter. Zayd said: 'Her last occasion should be at the House' — meaning the ṭawāf around the House. Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'If she has performed the ifāḍah on the Day of Naḥr and then menstruates"," let her depart if she wishes.' The Anṣār said: 'We will not follow you when you oppose Zayd ibn Thābit.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'Ask your companion Umm Sulaym.' So they asked her"," and she informed them that Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy ibn Akhṭab menstruated after she had performed ṭawāf around the House on the Day of Naḥr. ʿĀʾishah said to her: 'What a loss for you! You have detained us.' They mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he commanded her to depart. Umm Sulaym reported that the same had happened to her"," and he commanded her to depart.\"" Al-Bukhārī alluded to these two narrations and extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 6/430. Ṭayālisī 1651]"""
"9770","(9765) Abū Muḥammad Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us — and Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Dāwud al-Makkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — both saying: Sufyān narrated from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pressing his face and chest against the Multazam.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Dāraquṭnī 2/289]"""
"9771","(9766) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated from Sulaymān — meaning Ibn Bilāl — from Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl from Abū al-Zubayr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās that he used to cling to the area between the Corner (Rukn) and the Door, and he used to say: \What is between the Corner and the Door is called the Multazam. No one clings to it asking Allah for anything without Him granting it to him.\"" This is mawqūf"," and the other aḥādīth concerning it have preceded. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9772","(9767) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī said: \I would love for him"," when bidding farewell to the House"," to stand at the Multazam — which is between the Corner and the Door — and say: 'O Allah"," the House is Your House"," and the servant is Your servant"," the son of Your servant"," the son of Your maidservant. You carried me upon what You have subjected to me of Your creation"," until You caused me to travel through Your lands and brought me to the point of Your blessing"," until You helped me to fulfill my rites. If You are pleased with me"," then increase Your pleasure with me; otherwise"," now"," before my home becomes distant from Your House — this is the time of my departure"," if You permit me — not seeking a replacement for You or for Your House"," and not turning away from You or from Your House. O Allah"," accompany me with well-being in my body"," protection in my religion"," and make my return good"," and grant me obedience to You for as long as You keep me alive.'\"" This is from the statement of al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," and it is good. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 2/343]"""
"9773","(9768) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Bursānī narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me: ʿUmar ibn ʿAṭāʾ — said to be ʿUmar ibn ʿAṭāʾ ibn Warāz — narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ṣarūrah in Islam.\"" Abū Dāwūd extracted it in the Book of Sunan. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 1729. Aḥmad 1/312]"""
"9774","(9769) And ʿUmar ibn Qays — who is not strong — narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited calling a Muslim a ṣarūrah. Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Ṭāhir ibn Khālid ibn Nizār narrated to us, my father narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Qays narrated it. Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah also narrated it from ʿAmr from ʿIkrimah from the Prophet ﷺ as a mursal narration. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it from ʿAmr from ʿIkrimah as his own statement, denying that it was from Ibn ʿAbbās or from the Prophet ﷺ — and Allah knows best. In the narration of Ibn ʿUyaynah and others from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah, it is stated: \A man would strike another man in the Jāhiliyyah and say: 'I am a ṣarūrah (bound one).' It would be said to him: 'Leave the ṣarūrah to his ignorance","' even if he were to throw his dung upon his own leg.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""There is no ṣarūrah in Islam.\"" In another narration: \""He would strike the man's face and then say: 'I am a ṣarūrah.' It would be said: 'Bind the face of the ṣarūrah","' even if he were to cast his excrement upon his own leg.\"" It is also narrated from Manṣūr ibn Abī Sulaym — once from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim"," once from Ibn Jubayr from his father"," once from the brother of Jubayr"," and once from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr — I think from his father — from the Prophet ﷺ: \""The ʿUmrah has been incorporated into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection — there is no ṣarūrah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9775","(9770) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās — I think he raised it — who said: \None of you should say: 'I am a ṣarūrah.'\"" Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad said: \""No one raised it from Sufyān except Muʿāwiyah.\"" [Ḥasan. Ṭabarānī al-Awsaṭ 1297. Dāraquṭnī 2/23]"""
"9776","(9771) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, al-Masʿūdī narrated from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: \None of you should say: 'I am a ṣarūrah","' for the Muslim is not a ṣarūrah. And none of you should say: 'I am a ḥājj (pilgrim)","' for the ḥājj is the one who is in iḥrām.\"" It is mursal"," and it is also mawqūf upon ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. [Ḍaʿīf. Ṭabarānī al-Kabīr 8932]"""
"9777","Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us, saying: I disapprove of the month of Muharram being called Ṣafar; rather, it should be called al-Muharram. I only disapprove of it being called Ṣafar because the people of the Jāhiliyyah used to count two months as \Ṣafar\"" — one Ṣafar and the other Muharram — and they would intercalate"," performing Hajj one year in one month and another year in a different month"," saying: \""If we erred regarding the month of the Ḥaram this year"," we will correct it in another year.\"" So Allah"," exalted be His praise"," revealed: {Indeed"," the intercalation (al-nasīʾ) is an increase in disbelief} (al-Tawbah: 37). And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," time has returned to its form on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth.\"" Thus"," no month shall be intercalated"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) named it al-Muharram. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9778","Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us — that 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us regarding that.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and the wording is his — Abū 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Ibn Abī Bakrah, from Abī Bakrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Indeed"," time has returned to its form on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months"," of which four are sacred: three consecutive months — Dhū al-Qa'dah"," Dhū al-Ḥijjah"," and al-Muharram — and Rajab of Muḍar"," which falls between Jumādā and Sha'bān.\""\n\nThen he (ﷺ) said: \""Which month is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is it not Dhū al-Ḥijjah?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Which land is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is it not al-Baldah (i.e."," Makkah)?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Which day is this?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is it not the Day of Naḥr (Sacrifice)?\"" We said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," your blood"," your wealth\"" — Muḥammad said"," and I think he also said: \""and your honours — are sacred to you"," as sacred as this day of yours"," in this land of yours"," in this month of yours. And you will meet your Lord"," and He will ask you about your deeds. So do not go astray after me"," striking one another's necks. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent"," for perhaps some of those to whom it is conveyed may retain it better than some of those who heard it.\"" Then he said: \""Have I not conveyed (the message)?\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (raḥimahu Allāh) did not narrate the full text of this ḥadīth; rather"," he narrated from Muḥammad"," from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah"," from his father"," from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Indeed"," time has returned…\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shayyah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from 'Abd al-Wahhāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3025. Muslim 1679]"""
"9779","Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abu al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs informed us; 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī informed us; 'Abd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ informed me; Mu'āwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me from 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālah, from Ibn 'Abbās, regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {Indeed, the intercalation (al-nasīʾ) is an increase in disbelief} (al-Tawbah: 37). He said: Al-nasīʾ refers to the practice of Junādat ibn 'Awf ibn Umayyah al-Kinānī, who would come to the gathering every year and was known as Abū Thumāmah. He would proclaim: \Indeed"," Abū Thumāmah is neither shown favour nor reproached. Indeed"," the first Ṣafar this year is lawful.\"" So he would declare it lawful for the people"," making Ṣafar lawful one year and sacred another"," and making al-Muharram sacred one year. That is the meaning of the words of Allah"," the Most High: {Indeed"," the intercalation is an increase in disbelief. The disbelievers are led astray; they declare it lawful one year and sacred another} — until His words: {He does not guide the disbelieving people} (al-Tawbah: 37). [Ḍa'īf. al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr 6/368]"""
"9780","Abū Bakr informed us; Abu al-Ḥusayn 'Abd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fasawī al-Dāwūdī informed us; Abū 'Alī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Lu'lu'ī informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī informed us; Abū Tābah informed us; Mu'āwiyah — meaning Ibn Salām — narrated to us from Yaḥyā, who said: Yazīd ibn Nu'aym or Zayd ibn Nu'aym — Abū Tābah was uncertain — informed me that a man from Judhām had intercourse with his wife while they were both in the state of iḥrām. The man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said to them: \Complete your rites and offer a sacrifice. Then return until you reach the place where you committed what you committed"," then separate"," and let neither of you see the other. And you must perform another Hajj. Then"," when you reach the place where you committed what you committed"," enter into iḥrām and complete your rites and offer a sacrifice.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is munqaṭi' (disconnected)"," and the narrator is Yazīd ibn Nu'aym al-Aslamī"," without doubt. Much of what is in his ḥadīth"," or most of it"," has been narrated from a group of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ḍa'īf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl"," no. 129]"""
"9781","'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Bushrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū 'Amr ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū 'Abd Allāh — meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated a report from Mujāhid regarding the words of Allah: {Indeed, the intercalation is an increase in disbelief} (al-Tawbah: 37). He said: They performed Hajj in Dhū al-Ḥijjah for two years, then performed Hajj in al-Muharram for two years. Thus, they would perform Hajj every year in every month for two years, until the Hajj of Abū Bakr (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu) coincided with the last of those two years in Dhū al-Qa'dah, one year before the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ). Then the Prophet (ﷺ) performed Hajj the following year in Dhū al-Ḥijjah. That is when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said in his sermon: \Indeed"," time has returned to its form on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth.\""\n\nAbū 'Abd Allāh said: 'Abd al-Razzāq narrated to us this ḥadīth; Ma'mar narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ"," from Mujāhid. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9782","Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us; Ādam informed us; Warqā' informed us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, who said: Al-Rafath means sexual intercourse; al-Fusūq means acts of disobedience; and \no disputing in Hajj\"" means that it is not a month that is intercalated. The time of Hajj has been made clear; there is no doubt about it. That is because they used to"," in the Jāhiliyyah"," drop al-Muharram and then say: \""Ṣafar in place of Ṣafar.\"" And they would drop the month of Rabī' al-Awwal and then say: \""The month of Rabī' in place of Rabī'.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: There is a difference of opinion regarding the Hajj of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu) before the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ) — whether it took place in Dhū al-Qa'dah or in Dhū al-Ḥijjah. Mujāhid held the view that it occurred in Dhū al-Qa'dah"," while some others held that it occurred in Dhū al-Ḥijjah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Shībah 13226]"""
"9783","Abū 'Abd Allāh said: As for al-Zuhrī, it was narrated from him that Ḥumayd ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān informed him that Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu) said: \Abū Bakr sent me during that Hajj"," among the mu'adhdhins"," on the Day of Naḥr"," to announce in Minā that no mushrik should perform Hajj after this year"," and no one should perform ṭawāf of the House naked.\""\n\nAbū 'Abd Allāh said: The ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī has a good chain of narration. However"," according to what al-Zuhrī mentioned"," the Hajj of Abū Bakr (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu) took place in Dhū al-Ḥijjah.\n\nAbū 'Abd Allāh said: Sūrat al-Barā'ah was revealed before the Hajj of Abū Bakr (raḍiya Allāh ta'ālā 'anhu)"," and in it is: {Indeed"," the intercalation is an increase in disbelief} (al-Tawbah: 37)"," and in it is: {Indeed"," the number of months with Allah is twelve months} (al-Tawbah: 36). So would it have been permissible for Abū Bakr to perform Hajj according to the practice of the Arabs"," when Allah had informed that their doing so constituted disbelief? [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 362. Muslim 1347]"""
"9784","Abū Naṣr 'Umar ibn al-'Azīz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū 'Amr Ismā'īl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-'Abdī informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik informed us: It reached him that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib, and Abū Hurayrah (raḍiya Allāh ta'ālā 'anhum) were asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife while in iḥrām for Hajj. They said: \They should continue on their course until they complete their Hajj. Then they must perform Hajj the following year and offer a sacrifice.\""\n\nAnd 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu) said: \""When they enter into iḥrām for Hajj the following year"," they should separate until they complete their Hajj.\"" [Very weak. Mentioned by Mālik 854]"""
"9785","Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — Abū al-Shaykh — informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz informed us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us; Abū 'Amr — meaning al-Awzā'ī — narrated to us from 'Aṭā': that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiya Allāh ta'ālā 'anhu) said regarding a man in iḥrām for Hajj who had intercourse with his wife — meaning while she was also in iḥrām: \They should complete their Hajj"," and they must perform Hajj the following year from the place where they entered into iḥrām"," and they should separate until they complete their Hajj.\""\n\n'Aṭā' said: \""And they must offer a badanah (a camel as sacrifice)"," whether she consented or he compelled her; they are required to offer only one badanah.\"" [Ḍa'īf. Jāmi' al-Taḥṣīl"," p. 237]"""
"9786","And in what Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — informed us; Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Yazīd ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir, who said: \I asked Mujāhid about a muḥrim who has intercourse with his wife. He said: 'This occurred during the time of 'Umar (raḍiya Allāh 'anhu).' He said: 'They should complete their Hajj — and Allah knows best regarding their Hajj — then they should return"," each one lawful for the other. Then"," the following year"," they should perform Hajj and offer a sacrifice"," and they should separate at the place where he had intercourse with her.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 13081]"""
"9787","(9782) And Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā — informed us, Abū Ṭāhir informed us, my grandfather Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Ḥumayd narrated from Abū al-Ṭufayl ʿĀmir ibn Wāthilah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife while in the state of iḥrām: \Complete your rites"," then return to your town. When the following year comes"," go out as pilgrims. When you enter iḥrām"," do not meet one another until you have completed your rites"," and offer a sacrificial animal.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr narrated it from Abū al-Ṭufayl from Ibn ʿAbbās in this story: \""Then pronounce the talbiyah from where you first pronounced it.\"" [Weak]"""
"9788","(9783) Abū ʿAbdullāh — reciting to him — and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī said: Abū ʿAbdullāh informed me, and they both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Faqīh al-Naysābūrī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr and ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb al-Mawṣilī said: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, that a man came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr asking about a muḥrim who had intercourse with a woman. He gestured toward ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and said: \Go to that one and ask him.\"" Shuʿayb said: The man did not recognize him"," so I went with him and he asked Ibn ʿUmar"," who said: \""Your ḥajj is void.\"" The man said: \""What should I do?\"" He said: \""Go out with the people and do what they do. When the next year arrives"," perform ḥajj and offer a sacrifice.\"" He returned to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and I was with him"," and informed him. He said: \""Go to Ibn ʿAbbās and ask him.\"" Shuʿayb said: I went with him to Ibn ʿAbbās and he asked him"," and he said to him what Ibn ʿUmar had said. He returned to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and I was with him"," and informed him of what Ibn ʿAbbās had said. Then he said: \""What do you say?\"" He said: \""My saying is the same as what they both said.\"" This is a sound chain of narration"," and it contains evidence for the soundness of Shuʿayb ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh's having heard directly from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. [Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Shaybah"," 1085]"""
"9789","(9784) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Bishr, who said: I heard a man from Banī ʿAbd al-Dār say: A man came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and asked him about a muḥrim who had intercourse with his wife, and he said nothing. He then came to Ibn ʿAbbās and mentioned that to him. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr said: \If anyone can inform him about it"," it is the cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Let them both complete the remainder of their rites. When the next year comes"," let them perform ḥajj. When they reach the place where they committed the act"," let them separate"," and each one of them owes a sacrificial animal\"" — or he said: \""Upon both of them is the sacrificial animal.\"" Abū Bishr said: I mentioned that to Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and he said: \""Thus did Ibn ʿAbbās used to say.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9790","(9785) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me by way of ijāzah that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed them, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Maʿmar al-Qaysī informed us, Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Bakr — informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abū al-Zubayr informed him that ʿIkramah, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, informed him: A man and his wife from Quraysh met Ibn ʿAbbās on the road to Madīnah. The man said: \I have had intercourse with my wife.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""As for your ḥajj this year"," it is void. Perform ḥajj the following year"," then pronounce the talbiyah from where you first pronounced it"," until you reach the place where you committed the act — then separate from her. Let him not see her and let her not see him until you have stoned the jamrah. And offer a she-camel"," and let her offer a she-camel.\"" [Hasan]"""
"9791","(9786) He said: And Ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If he has intercourse"," then upon each of them is a badanah (a full sacrificial camel).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9792","(9787) He said: And Ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muḥammad informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʬāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A jazūr (a mature she-camel) will suffice between the two of them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9793","(9788) He said: And Ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Khuthaym, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: \I had intercourse with my wife before performing the ṭawāf (ziyārah).\"" He said: \""If she assisted you in it"," then upon each of you is a fine"," beautiful she-camel. If she did not assist you"," then upon you is a fine"," beautiful she-camel.\""\n\n(T) And it has been narrated from Jābir ibn Zayd — Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ — that he said: \""Let them complete their ḥajj"," and upon them is ḥajj the following year. If they are of means"," let them offer a jazūr (a mature she-camel).\"" And from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī: \""They separate and do not come together until they have completed their ḥajj.\"" [Hasan]"""
"9794","(9789) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: \What do you think about a man who has intercourse with his wife while in the state of iḥrām?\"" The people said nothing to him. Saʿīd said: \""A man had intercourse with his wife while in the state of iḥrām"," and he sent to Madīnah to ask about that. Some of the people said to him: 'Let them be separated until the following year.'\"" Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib said: \""Let them proceed on their course and complete the ḥajj that they have vitiated. When they have finished"," let them return. When ḥajj comes upon them again"," upon them is ḥajj and a sacrificial animal. Let them pronounce the talbiyah from where they first pronounced it for the ḥajj that they vitiated"," and let them separate until they have completed their ḥajj.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 855]"""
"9795","(9790) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūd ibn Khurrāzādh informed us, Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sharīk narrated from Jābir, from Abū Jaʿfar, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Whoever kisses his wife while in the state of iḥrām"," let him offer a blood sacrifice (i.e."," a sacrificial animal).\"" This chain is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nAnd something to this effect has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he should complete his ḥajj. This is also the view of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," Qatādah"," and the fuqahāʾ. [Very weak]"""
"9796","(9791) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Mazzī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Mālik ibn Anas and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith —\n\n(H) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Mihrānjānī informed us thereby, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Aḥmad informed us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at al-Ḥudaybiyah: a badanah (a camel) shared by seven people"," and a cow shared by seven people.\"" In the narration of Ibn Wahb: \""In the year of al-Ḥudaybiyah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1318]"""
"9797","(9792) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh informed me from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \I have vowed a badanah (sacrificial camel)"," but I cannot find one.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"," \""Then slaughter seven sheep in its place.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj also narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī. Abū Dāwūd recorded it in al-Marāsīl because ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī did not meet Ibn ʿAbbās"," and it has also been narrated as a mawqūf (stopped) report. [Weak]"""
"9798","(9793) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: al-Sakan ibn Nāfiʿ Abū al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn narrated to us from Mujāhid from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, who said: \This verse was revealed concerning me.\"" He said: \""I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me"," 'Come near.' I drew near two or three times"," and he said"," 'Do your vermin harm you?' — I think he said"," 'Yes.'\"" He said: \""And Ayyūb narrated from Mujāhid: 'Do the vermin of your head harm you?'\"" He said: \""Then he commanded me with fasting"," or charity"," or a sacrifice — whatever was easy.\"" Ibn ʿAwn said: \""Mujāhid explained it to me"," but I forgot"," so Ayyūb informed me that he heard it from Mujāhid"," who said: 'Fasting for three days"," or charity to six poor persons"," or the sacrifice of a sheep.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1720. Muslim 1201]"""
"9799","(9794) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik ibn Anas informed me from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī from Mujāhid ibn Jabr from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, who said: \He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the state of iḥrām"," and lice afflicted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to shave his head and said"," 'Fast three days"," or feed six poor persons — two mudd for each two mudd — or sacrifice a sheep. Whichever of these you do"," it will suffice you.'\""\n\nThis is the correct version. Mālik also narrated it on another occasion from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā without mentioning Mujāhid in its isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it 938]"""
"9800","(9795) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\nAnd Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik informed us — mentioning it similarly, without mentioning Mujāhid in its isnād. In some of these recensions, al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, heard it in a group of the companions of al-Muwaṭṭāʾ, other than the recension witnessed by Ibn Wahb. Then al-Shāfiʿī became aware of it through the narration of al-Muzanī and Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam from him, and said: \Mālik erred in this ḥadīth.\"" The ḥuffāẓ preserved it from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Mujāhid from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah. The Shaykh said: \""The error occurred only in some of the recensions"," for he narrated it in some of them correctly.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Mujāhid from Ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb. And we narrated it previously from the ḥadīth of Abū Qilābah from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah"," in which he said: \""Three ṣāʿ of dates.\"" And from the ḥadīth of al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \""A farq of raisins.\"" And from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil from Kaʿb: \""For each poor person"," half a ṣāʿ of food.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it 937]"""
"9801","(9796) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us: My father informed me: My father informed me: ʿUqayl narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said — and he mentioned the ḥadīth — he said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah"," he said to the people: 'Whoever among you has brought a sacrificial animal"," nothing that was forbidden to him shall become lawful until he completes his Ḥajj. And whoever among you has not brought a sacrificial animal"," let him perform ṭawāf of the Bayt and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," let him shorten his hair and exit the state of iḥrām"," then let him enter iḥrām for Ḥajj and offer a sacrifice. Whoever cannot find a sacrificial animal"," let him fast three days during the Ḥajj and seven days when he returns to his family.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ibn Bukayr from al-Layth.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar regarding the one who misses the Ḥajj: \""If he catches the Ḥajj the following year"," let him perform Ḥajj if he is able"," and let him offer a sacrifice in his Ḥajj. If he cannot find a sacrificial animal"," let him fast on its behalf three days during the Ḥajj and seven days when he returns to his family.\""\n\nAnd similarly"," Sulaymān ibn Yasār narrated it from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāẹ"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in the story of Habbār when he missed the Ḥajj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1606. Muslim 1227]"""
"9802","(9797) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father from Jābir that the Prophet ﷺ said: \I have sacrificed my animal here in Minā"," and all of Minā is a place of sacrifice"," so sacrifice in your camps.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"9803","(9798) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me: Usāmah ibn Zayd informed me that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated to him that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Every path and passage of Makkah is a road and a place of sacrifice.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 1937]"""
"9804","(9799) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us: My grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Ḥammād informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās: A man came to him and said, \I had intercourse with my wife before performing ṭawāf of the Bayt.\"" He said"," \""Do you have anything?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," I am well-off.\"" He said"," \""Then sacrifice a fat she-camel and feed it to the poor.\"" [Ḥasan in other than this chain]"""
"9805","(9800) And Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding a man who completed all the rites except the ṭawāf of the Bayt, and then had intercourse: \Upon him is a badanah (sacrificial camel)"," and his Ḥajj is complete.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed them"," saying: Ibn Khuzaymah informed us"," saying: Salm ibn Junādah narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān and Shuʿbah from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit"," and he mentioned it."""
"9806","(9801) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: ʿAbīdah narrated to us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Musayyab narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās: \A man had intercourse with his wife before performing ṭawāf of the Bayt on the Day of Sacrifice.\"" He said"," \""Let the two of them sacrifice a jazūr (she-camel) between them"," and there is no Ḥajj upon them the following year.\"" [Ḥasan. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it 2/272]"""
"9807","(9802) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Ibn Bukayr informed us — Mālik from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dīlī from ʿIkrimah, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I do not think it except from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife before performing Ṭawāf al-Ifāḍah: he must perform ʿUmrah and offer a sacrifice. He said: And Mālik narrated to us from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that he used to say the same. Mālik said: And that is the best of what I have heard. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik, 859]"
"9808","(9803) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik from Abī al-Zubayr from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he was asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife while he was in iḥrām, at Minā, before performing Ṭawāf al-Ifāḍah, so he commanded him to slaughter a she-camel. Al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And this is the position we hold. Mālik said: Upon him is an ʿUmrah, a she-camel sacrifice, and his Ḥajj is complete. And he narrated it from Rabīʿah, abandoning the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās in favour of the opinion of Rabīʿah, and he narrated it from Thawr ibn Zayd from ʿIkrimah — he thought it was from Ibn ʿAbbās — and he is objectionable in his view regarding ʿIkrimah; he does not consider anyone to accept his ḥadīth, while he narrates with certainty from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās something contrary to it. And ʿAṭāʾ is considered trustworthy (thiqah) by him and by the people. The Shaykh said: And it has been narrated to us from the jurists of the people of Madīnah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by others, 858]"
"9809","(9804) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us — al-Ḥumaydī informed us — Sufyān informed us — ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: We asked Ibn ʿUmar about a man who performed ʿUmrah and circumambulated the House but did not perform saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah — may he have intercourse with his wife? Ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqām, and performed saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. And Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, said: \There has certainly been for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent pattern\"" (Q. 33:21). ʿAmr said: I asked Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and he said: He must not approach her until he performs saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī. Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 387]"""
"9810","(9805) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us — Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us — Shuʿbah informed us — from Abī Bishr from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that a man performed ʿUmrah and had intercourse with his wife before performing saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, after having circumambulated the House. Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about it, and he said: An expiation (fidyah) of fasting, charity, or a sacrifice (nasak). I said: Which of these is most meritorious? He said: A jazūr (she-camel) or a baqarah (cow). I said: Which of these is most meritorious? He said: A jazūr. Ayyūb differed from Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9811","(9806) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Tawbah al-Ṣūfī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Ḥātim al-Najjār al-Āmulī informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Jumaḥī informed us — Ḥammād from Ayyūb from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that a man and his wife both entered iḥrām for ʿUmrah together. She completed all her rites except the cutting of hair (taqṣīr), and he had intercourse with her before she cut her hair. Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about that, and he said: Indeed, she is excessively lustful (shabīqah). It was said to him: Indeed, she is listening, so he was shy because of that and said: \Would you not have informed me?\"" And he said to her: \""Shed blood.\"" She said: \""What?\"" He said: \""Slaughter a she-camel"," a cow"," or a sheep.\"" She said: \""Which of these is most meritorious?\"" He said: \""A she-camel — and perhaps this is more appropriate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9812","(9807) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us — Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sharayḥ informed us — Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — Shuʿbah from al-Ḥakam from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, that a man came to his wife during ʿUmrah, and she said: \I will not cut my hair.\"" So he began to cut her hair with his teeth. He said: \""Indeed"," he is excessively lustful; he shall shed blood.\"" Thus he said"," and he did not mention Ibn ʿAbbās in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 152]"""
"9813","(9808) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā informed us — Abū Ṭāhir informed us — my grandfather Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr informed us — Ismāʿīl, that is Ibn Jaʿfar, informed us — Ḥumayd, that he asked al-Ḥasan about a woman who came to perform ʿUmrah and circumambulated the House and performed saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and her husband had intercourse with her before she cut her hair. He said: Let her offer a sacrifice of a camel or a cow. Ḥumayd said: And Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh mentioned that Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about that, and he said: \Indeed"," she is excessively lustful.\"" It was said to him: \""The woman is present.\"" So he fell silent"," then said: \""Let her offer a sacrifice of a camel or a cow.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9814","(9809) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Sinān informed us — Ibn Abī ʿUmar informed us — Sufyān, that is Ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿĀʾishah, that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: \Your circumambulation of the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah is sufficient for your Ḥajj and your ʿUmrah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1897]"""
"9815","(9810) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī informed us — Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-Raqqī informed us — Qabīṣah informed us — Sufyān, that is al-Thawrī, from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿĀʾishah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \A single circumambulation after the standing at al-Maʿrifah is sufficient for your Ḥajj and your ʿUmrah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/262]"""
"9816","(9811) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us — Mūsā, that is Ismāʿīl, informed us — Wahb informed us — Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she entered iḥrām for ʿUmrah and menstruated before circumambulating the House. She performed all the remaining rites, having also entered iḥrām for Ḥajj. The Prophet ﷺ said to her on the Day of al-Nafr (Departure): \Your saʿī is sufficient for your Ḥajj and your ʿUmrah.\"" But she refused"," so he sent ʿAbd al-Raḥmān with her to al-Tanʿīm"," and she performed ʿUmrah after the Ḥajj. [Narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Wahb. Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1211]"""
"9817","(9812) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿmur saying: I was present when the Prophet ﷺ said: \The Ḥajj is ʿArafah; the Ḥajj is ʿArafāt. Whoever reaches ʿArafah before the rising of the dawn has attained the Ḥajj"," or his Ḥajj has been completed. The days of Minā are three days. Whoever hastens to depart within two days"," there is no sin upon him"," and whoever delays"," there is no sin upon him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 2985]"""
"9818","(9813) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masrah informed us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Ḥassān both said: Sufyān al-Thawrī informed us: Bukayr ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Laythī informed me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿmur al-Dīlī narrated to me, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at ʿArafāt. A group of his Companions came to him and they instructed a man, so he called out: \O Messenger of Allah"," how is the Ḥajj performed? How is the Ḥajj performed?\"" He ﷺ instructed a man"," so he called out: \""The Ḥajj is the day of ʿArafah. Whoever comes before the morning prayer from the night of Jamʿ"," his Ḥajj has been completed. The days of Minā are three. Whoever hastens within two days"," there is no sin upon him.\"" Then he ﷺ sent a man behind him"," and he proclaimed that.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9819","(9814) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us. And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj, Abū al-Zinbāʿ informed us: Ḥāmid ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Sufyān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, Zakariyyā, and Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: I heard ʿUrwah ibn Muḍarris ibn Aws ibn Ḥārithah ibn Lām saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Muzdalifah and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have come from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. By Allah"," I did not come until I exhausted myself and wore out my mount"," and I did not leave any of these mountains without stopping at it. Do I have a Ḥajj?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever witnesses this prayer with us — the Fajr prayer at al-Muzdalifah — and has already stood at ʿArafah before that"," by night or by day"," his Ḥajj has been completed and he has fulfilled his remaining rites.\"" Sufyān said: Zakariyyā added in it"," and he was the most retentive of the three regarding this ḥadīth: He said: \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have come at this hour from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ; I have exhausted my mount and wearied myself. Do I have a Ḥajj?' He said: 'Whoever witnesses this prayer with us and stands with us until he departs"," and has already stood at ʿArafah before that"," by night or by day"," his Ḥajj has been completed and he has fulfilled his remaining rites.'\"" Sufyān said: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind added: \""I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the dawn broke","\"" and he mentioned the ḥadīth. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Bushrān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1960"," Ibn Mājah 3016]"""
"9820","(9815) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us: Sūrah ibn al-Ḥakam, the rationalist, informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever departs from ʿArafāt before dawn"," his Ḥajj has been completed. And whoever misses it"," the Ḥajj has eluded him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"9821","(9816) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, who said: \The Ḥajj is not missed until the dawn breaks from the night of Jamʿ.\"" He said: \""I said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'Did you receive this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' ʿAṭāʾ said: 'Yes.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"9822","(9817) Through this chain of narration: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, that he said the same.\n\n[Likewise]"
"9823","(9818) Through this chain of narration: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad informed me: Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to him that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāẓ, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever reaches the night of Naḥr before the rising of the dawn has attained the Ḥajj. And whoever does not stand until morning has"," the Ḥajj has eluded him.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9824","(9819) Through this chain of narration: Ibn Wahb informed me: Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and others informed me: Nāfiʿ narrated to them, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, something similar.\n\n[Likewise]"
"9825","(9820) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ informed me: My uncle, Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ, narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh used to say—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: \Whoever among the pilgrims reaches the night of Naḥr and stands at the mountains of ʿArafah before the rising of the dawn has attained the Ḥajj. And whoever does not reach ʿArafah before the rising of the dawn"," the Ḥajj has eluded him. Let him come to the House and perform ṭawāf around it seven times"," and perform saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah seven times"," then let him shave or shorten his hair"," if he wishes. If he has his sacrificial animal with him"," let him slaughter it before he shaves. When he has completed his ṭawāf and saʿī"," let him shave or shorten his hair"," then let him return to his family. If the Ḥajj comes upon him the following year"," let him perform Ḥajj if he is able"," and let him offer a sacrifice during his Ḥajj. If he does not find a sacrificial animal"," let him fast three days during the Ḥajj and seven days when he returns to his family.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 581]"""
"9826","(9821) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed me that Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, may Allah be pleased with him, set out for Ḥajj until, when he was at al-Nāziyyah on the road to Makkah, he lost his mounts. He then came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāẓ, may Allah be pleased with him, on the day of Naḥr and mentioned that to him. ʿUmar said to him: \Do as the one performing ʿUmrah does"," then you have exited the state of iḥrām. If the Ḥajj comes upon you the following year"," perform Ḥajj and offer whatever sacrificial animal is easy for you.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik 856]"""
"9827","Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both reported: Abu al-Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakim informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Malik ibn Anas, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, and others informed me that Nafi' narrated to them from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Hibar ibn al-Aswad came on the Day of Sacrifice while 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was offering the sacrifice. He said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," we have made a mistake; we thought that this day was the Day of 'Arafah.\"" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Go to Makkah and perform Tawaf around the House seven times"," and perform Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah — you and those with you. Then sacrifice a hady (offering) if you have one with you. Then shave or shorten your hair and return. When the next Hajj comes"," perform Hajj and offer a sacrifice. And whoever cannot find a sacrifice"," let him fast three days during Hajj and seven days upon returning.\""\n\nJuwayriyah ibn Asma' also narrated this from Nafi'. [Da'if. Reported by Malik"," 857]"""
"9828","Abu Muhammad — 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi reported: Sa'dan ibn Nasr reported: Abu Mu'awiya reported: from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: \I asked 'Umar about a man who missed the Hajj.\"" He said: \""Let him enter ihram for 'Umrah"," and upon him is Hajj the following year.\"" Then I went out the following year and met Zayd ibn Thabit"," so I asked him about a man who missed the Hajj. He said: \""Let him enter ihram for 'Umrah"," and upon him is Hajj the following year.\"" This is how Abu Mu'awiya narrated it.\n\nIt was also narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from him"," and it was narrated from Idris al-Awdi from him"," who added: \""And he should shed blood (offer a sacrifice).\"" Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from al-A'mash with his chain and said: \""He exits ihram with 'Umrah and performs Hajj the following year"," and there is no hady upon him.\""\n\nHe (al-Aswad) said: \""Then I met Zayd ibn Thabit after twenty years"," and he said the same as 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" Sufyan also narrated it from al-Mughirah from Ibrahim"," and Shu'bah narrated it as well. [Sahih]"""
"9829","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar reported: Yahya ibn Muhammad reported: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh reported: my father reported: Shu'bah reported from al-Mughirah al-Dabbi from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i from al-Aswad, who said: \A man came to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) who had missed the Hajj.\"" 'Umar said: \""Make it an 'Umrah"," and upon you is Hajj the following year.\"" Al-Aswad said: \""I remained (in that state) for twenty years"," then I asked Zayd ibn Thabit about that"," and he said the same as 'Umar.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"9830","Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan reported: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi reported: 'Affan reported: Wuhaib reported: Ayyub reported from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from al-Harith ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, who said: \I heard 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) when a man came to him in the middle of the Days of Tashriq who had missed the Hajj. 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: 'Perform Tawaf around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah"," and upon you is Hajj the following year.'\"" He did not mention a hady.\n\nThis narration and the one before it from al-Aswad from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) are both connected (musnad)"," while the narration of Sulayman ibn Yasar from him is disconnected (munqati').\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The connected hadith from 'Umar agrees with our hadith from 'Umar"," and our hadith adds the hady upon it. And the one who adds something to the hadith is more deserving of being considered as having memorized it than the one who does not mention the addition.\""\n\nWe have narrated from Ibn 'Umar as we have stated"," in a connected form.\n\nIn the narration of Idris al-Awdi"," if it is authentic"," it states: \""And he should shed blood (offer a sacrifice)","\"" and this testifies to the authenticity of the narration of Sulayman ibn Yasar.\n\nIbrahim ibn Tahman narrated from Musa ibn 'Uqba from Nafi' from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Hibar ibn al-Aswad that he narrated to him that he had missed the Hajj"," and he mentioned it in a connected form. We have narrated in the story of Huzabah from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr that which indicates the obligation of the hady. We have narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that he said: \""Whoever forgets something of his rites or omits it"," let him shed blood (offer a sacrifice).\"" [Hasan. Reported by Ibn al-Ja'd"," 2340]"""
"9831","Abu Nasr — 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah al-Bashiri, from the children of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, informed us: Abu 'Ali — Hamid ibn Muhammad al-Raffa' al-Harawi informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz reported: Abu al-Nu'man reported: Hammad ibn Zayd reported from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Abu Hurayrah, who attributed it to the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \Your fast-breaking is the day you break your fast"," and your sacrifice is the day you offer sacrifice. Every part of 'Arafah is a place of standing"," and every part of al-Muzdalifah is a place of standing"," and every part of Mina is a place of sacrifice"," and every path of Makkah is a place of sacrifice.\""\n\nRuh ibn al-Qasim also narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Abu Hurayrah"," in a marfu' form. Ibn 'Ulayyah and 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated it from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Abu Hurayrah in a mawquf form. Part of it was narrated through another route from al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah in a marfu' form. It was also narrated from al-Thawri from Ibn al-Munkadir from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Reported by Abu Dawud"," 2324]"""
"9832","'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi reported: 'Abdan ibn Ahmad reported: Yahya ibn Hatim al-'Askari reported: Muhammad ibn Isma'il — Abu Isma'il — reported: Sufyan reported from Ibn al-Munkadir from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \'Arafah is the day when the Imam stands (in 'Arafah)"," and the Sacrifice is the day when the Imam offers sacrifice"," and the Fast-breaking is the day when the Imam breaks the fast.\""\n\nThis Muhammad is known as al-Farisi"," and he is a Kufi"," the judge of Fars"," who is the only one to narrate it from Sufyan. [Munkar]"""
"9833","Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz reported: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd reported: al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah reported: Hushaym reported from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab from al-Saffah ibn Matar from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Usayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The Day of 'Arafah is the day on which the people stand (in 'Arafah).\""\n\nThis is a good mursal hadith. Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Marasil. [Da'if. Reported by Abu Dawud in al-Marasil"," 138]"""
"9834","Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr reported: Abu al-Abbas al-Asamm reported: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman reported: al-Shafi'i reported: Muslim ibn Khalid reported from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \I said to 'Ata': A man performed Hajj for the first time"," and the people erred regarding the Day of Sacrifice — will it suffice him?\"" He said: \""Yes"," by my life"," it will indeed suffice him.\"" He said: \""And I think he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Your fast-breaking is the day you break your fast"," and your sacrifice is the day you offer sacrifice.'\"" And I think he said: \""And 'Arafah is the day you stand (in 'Arafah).'\"" [Da'if. Reported by al-Shafi'i in al-Umm"," 1/382]"""
"9835","Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saqqa' informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Battah al-Isbahani reported: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Zakariyya reported: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi reported: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji reported from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid ibn Jabr — Abu al-Hajjaj — regarding the words of the Most High: \And [mention] when We made the House a place of return for the people and [a place of] security\"" (al-Baqarah: 125). He said: \""They return to it and go and come back"," but they never fulfill their worldly desire from it.\"" [Sahih. Reported by Ibn Jarir in his Tafsir"," 1/580]"""
"9836","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi reported: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn reported: Adam ibn Abi Iyas reported: Warqa' reported from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid regarding His words: \A place of return for the people\"" — he said: \""They never fulfill their worldly desire from it"," ever.\"" And \""and [a place of] security\"" — he said: \""Whoever enters it has no fear.\"" [Sahih]"""
"9837","(9832) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Warqāʾ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His (Exalted is He) words, \And proclaim to the people the Hajj\"" (al-Ḥajj: 27). He said: When Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," commanded Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) to proclaim the Hajj to the people"," he said: \""O people"," your Lord has taken a House and commanded you that you perform its Hajj.\"" So everything that heard his call — stone"," tree"," hillock"," earth"," or anything else — responded. They said: \""Labbayka Allāhumma labbayka\"" (Here we are"," O Allah"," here we are). [Ḥasan in virtue of corroborating chains. Ibn ʿAsākir in his Tārīkh"," 6/206]"""
"9838","(9833) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Jarīr narrated from Qābūs, meaning Ibn Abī Ẓabyān, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: When Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) finished building the House, he said: \My Lord"," I have finished.\"" He said: \""Proclaim the Hajj to the people.\"" He said: \""My Lord"," how far will my voice reach?\"" He said: \""Proclaim"," and upon Me is the conveyance.\"" He said: \""My Lord"," what shall I say?\"" He said: \""O people"," the Hajj of the Ancient House has been prescribed upon you.\"" So those between the heavens and the earth heard it. Do you not see that they come from the farthest ends of the earth"," saying the Talbiyah? [Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating chains. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 2/421]"""
"9839","(9834) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Muʿādh and Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Ibn ʿAwn from Mujāhid, who said: We were with Ibn ʿAbbās and they mentioned the Dajjāl. They said: \Between his eyes is written K-F-R (kāfir).\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I did not hear him say that. Rather"," he said: 'As for Ibrāhīm"," look at your companion (i.e."," the Prophet ﷺ); and as for Mūsā"," he is a man of wheat-coloured complexion"," with curly hair"," riding a red camel"," muzzled with a rope of palm-fibre — as though I am looking at him now"," descending into the valley"," saying the Talbiyah.'\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Mūsā from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAdī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 5596]"""
"9840","(9835) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Saʿīd ibn Mayasarah al-Bakrī, who narrated to me: Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The site of the House in the time of Ādam was a span or more"," as a marker. The angels used to perform its Hajj before Ādam. Then Ādam performed its Hajj"," and the angels received him and said: 'O Ādam"," from where have you come?' He said: 'I have performed the Hajj of the House.' They said: 'The angels performed its Hajj before you.'\"" [Munkar. The author narrated it in al-Shuʿab"," 3986]"""
"9841","(9836) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Labīd from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Quraẓī, or someone else, who said: Ādam (peace be upon him) performed the Hajj, and the angels met him and said: \May your rite be blessed"," O Ādam! We performed its Hajj two thousand years before you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it"," 532]"""
"9842","(9837) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Seventy prophets passed through the Fajj al-Rawḥāʾ as pilgrims"," wearing garments of wool. And seventy prophets prayed in the Mosque of al-Khayf.\"" And through this chain of narration"," as a reading upon him"," from Ibn Isḥāq: a trustworthy person from the people of Madīnah narrated to me from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," who said: \""There is no prophet except that he performed the Hajj of the House"," except for Hūd and Ṣāliḥ. And Nūḥ performed its Hajj. When what occurred on earth of the Flood befell"," the House was afflicted with what afflicted the earth"," and the House was a reddish mound. Then Allah sent Hūd (peace be upon him)"," and he became occupied with the affair of his people until Allah took his soul"," and he did not perform its Hajj until he died. Then when Allah established Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) in the place"," he performed its Hajj. After him"," no prophet remained except that he performed its Hajj.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 2/653]"""
"9843","(9838) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Aws Abū Zayd al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Mūsā ibn ʿImrān (peace be upon him) performed the Hajj with fifty thousand of the Children of Israel"," wearing two woollen cloaks"," and he was saying the Talbiyah: 'Labbayka Allāhumma labbayka"," labbayka taʿabbudan wa riqqan"," labbayka anā ʿabduka"," anā ladayka"," ladayka yā kāshif al-kurb' (Here we are"," O Allah"," here we are; here we are in worship and servitude; here we are"," I am Your servant"," I am at Your disposal; at Your disposal"," O Remover of distresses).' And the mountains responded to him.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It has not been reported to us from any of the prophets or past nations that anyone ever came to the House except in the state of iḥrām. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not enter Makkah"," to our knowledge"," except in the state of iḥrām"," except during the Conquest (Fatḥ).\"" [Very weak]"""
"9844","(9839) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \No one enters Makkah — neither its inhabitants nor anyone else — except in the state of iḥrām.\"" And Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās: \""By Allah"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not enter it except as a ḥājj (pilgrim) or a muʿtamir (performing ʿUmrah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9845","(9840) Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Muḥammadābādhi informed us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhi narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us in Harāt in the year 279 AH: al-Qaʿnabī narrated, reciting from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest wearing a helmet (mighfar) on his head. When he removed it, a man came and said: \Ibn Khaṭal is clinging to the curtains of the Kaʿbah.\"" He said: \""Kill him.\"" Mālik said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was not in the state of iḥrām that day.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others"," and Muslim narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī"," Yaḥyā"," and others"," all from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 1749]"""
"9846","(9841) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmmār al-Duhnī narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest wearing a black turban, without being in the state of iḥrām. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1358]"
"9847","(9842) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original source: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Yaḥyī ibn Ḥassān informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir that the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of Conquest wearing a black turban upon his head. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Mājah 2822]"
"9848","(9843) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Sūsī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us: my father informed me: al-Awzāʿī informed us: Yaḥyī ibn Abī Kathīr informed us: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me: Abū Hurayrah narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the Conquest of Makkah. He said: He stood and said, \Indeed"," Allah withheld the Elephant from Makkah and granted authority over it to His Messenger and the believers. It was not made lawful for anyone before me"," nor will it be for anyone after me. It was only made lawful to me for a single hour of the day"," and this is my hour.\"" He then mentioned the remainder of the hadith. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2302]"""
"9849","(9844) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar set out from Makkah until, when he reached Qudayd, news came to him from Madīnah, so he turned back and entered Makkah without iḥrām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 9471]"
"9850","(9845) He said: And Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb that he was asked about a man who enters Makkah without iḥrām, and he said, \I see no harm in that.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9851","(9846) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī informed us: Yaḥyī ibn Ḥassān informed us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām informed me: Yaḥyī informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah informed me that his father informed him: He accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. The people entered into iḥrām for ʿUmrah except for me. I hunted a wild donkey and fed my companions while they were in iḥrām. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him that we had surplus meat from it. He said, \Eat it","\"" while they were in iḥrām.\n\nMuslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\nAnd Abū Muḥammad"," the freedman of Abī Qatādah"," narrated from Abī Qatādah"," who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached al-Qāḥah"," and among us were those in iḥrām and those not in iḥrām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1196]"""
"9852","(9847) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz al-Ṭabarānī informed us there: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh informed us: Rūḥ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥafṣah informed us: Ibn Shihāb narrated from Abī Sinān from Ibn ʿAbbās that al-Aqraʿ ibn Ḥābis said, \O Messenger of Allah"," is Hajj every year?\"" He said"," \""No"," rather it is one Hajj. Whoever performs Hajj after that"," it is supererogatory. Had I said yes"," it would have become obligatory"," and had it become obligatory"," you would not have heeded nor obeyed.\"" And the hadith of Suraqah regarding ʿUmrah has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Nasāʾī 2620]"""
"9853","(9848) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī informed us: Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī narrated from Abī al-Safar, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās saying, \Let me hear what you say"," and understand what I tell you. Beware! Do not go out.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Any boy whose family performs Hajj on his behalf and he then reaches the age of maturity"," Hajj is incumbent upon him. If he dies"," he has fulfilled his Hajj. And any slave whose family performs Hajj on his behalf and he is then freed"," Hajj is incumbent upon him. If he dies"," he has fulfilled his Hajj.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 141875]"""
"9854","(9849) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl informed us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash from Abī Ẓabyān from Ibn ʿAbbās, who raised it [to the Prophet ﷺ], saying: \Any child who performs Hajj and then reaches the age of sin [puberty]"," it is incumbent upon him to perform another Hajj. And any Bedouin who performs Hajj and then emigrates [to Madīnah]"," it is incumbent upon him to perform another Hajj. And any slave who performs Hajj and is then freed"," another Hajj is incumbent upon him.\"" Al-Qāḍī said: He narrated it to me as marfūʿ. The Shaykh said: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl is alone in raising it from Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ from Shuʿbah"," while others narrated it from Shuʿbah as mawqūf. Likewise"," Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Aʿmash as mawqūf"," and that is correct. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9855","(9850) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Sharīḥ ibn ʿAqīl informed us: Abū Marwān al-ʿUthmānī informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated from Ḥarām ibn ʿUthmān from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad, the two sons of Jābir, from their father Jābir, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If a young child performs Hajj"," Hajj will be incumbent upon him when he reaches maturity"," if he finds the means.\"" He then mentioned the remainder of the hadith regarding the slave and the Bedouin in the same manner. Ḥarām ibn ʿUthmān is weak [in narration].\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ regarding a slave who entered into iḥrām for Hajj and was then freed: they said"," \""If he was freed at ʿArafah"," it suffices him. If he was freed at Jamʿ [Muzdalifah]"," then he should return to ʿArafah"," and it will suffice him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it in al-Kāmil 2/446]"""
"9856","(9851) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, saying: A recitation was read before Abū al-Yamān that Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed him from al-Zuhrī: Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet ﷢ mounted al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās behind him, and al-Faḍl was a handsome man. The Prophet ﷺ stopped to give fatwā to the people. A woman from Khathʿam, who was beautiful, came seeking a fatwā from the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Faḍl began to look at her, and her beauty impressed him. The Prophet ﷺ turned toward al-Faḍl while he was looking at her, took hold of al-Faḍl's chin, and turned his face away from looking at her. That woman of Khathʿam said, \O Messenger of Allah"," the obligation of Allah regarding Hajj upon His servants has reached my father"," but he is an elderly man who is unable to mount his riding animal. Will it suffice if I perform Hajj on his behalf?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her"," \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim recorded it through other chains from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 4138]"""
"9857","(9852) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʢUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Musaddad and ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī informed us, and the wording is that of ʿAlī: Sufyān informed us: al-Zuhrī informed us, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that a woman from the tribe of Khathʿam asked the Prophet ﷺ on the morning of Jamʿ (Muzdalifah), while al-Faḍl was riding behind him. She said: \The obligation of Allah upon His servants has overtaken my father"," who is an elderly man unable to remain mounted on a riding animal. Do you think I may perform Hajj on his behalf?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: Sufyān said that ʿAmr ibn Dīnar used to add in this narration from al-Zuhrī"," before he saw Ibn Shihāb"," that she said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will that benefit him?\"" He said: \""Yes"," just as if one of you had a debt upon him and you paid it off.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9858","(9853) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: Abū Bishr Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ḥayshayah — and he is Jaʿfar ibn Iyās — said: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: \My sister vowed to perform Hajj"," but she has died.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \""If she had a debt upon her"," would you have paid it?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then discharge the right of Allah"," for He is more deserving of fulfillment.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Buraydah ibn Ḥuṣayb from the Prophet ﷺ"," and its mention has passed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6321]"""
"9859","(9854) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me, from Qatādah ibn Duʿāmah, that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated to him: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās was passed by a man who was making talbiyah, saying: \Labbayka ḥajjatan ʿan Shubrumah (Here I am for a Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah).\"" He said: \""And who is Shubrumah?\"" He said: \""He bequeathed that Hajj be performed on his behalf.\"" He said: \""Have you performed Hajj for yourself?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then begin with yourself and perform Hajj for yourself"," then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.\"" This is how ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated it.\n\nAnd Ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it from Qatādah"," from ʿAzrah"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," except that he did not mention in it the wording of the bequest (waṣiyyah). And we narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," from ʿAṭāʾ: that he saw no harm in a man performing Hajj on behalf of his father even if he did not bequeath it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9860","(9855) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā informed us: Isḥāq, meaning Ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Ṭabāʿ, informed us: Abū Maʿshar informed us, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," will admit three persons into Paradise by virtue of a single Hajj: the deceased"," the one who performs Hajj on his behalf"," and the one who carries that out.\""\n\nThis Abū Maʿshar is Najīḥ al-Sindī al-Madanī"," who is weak. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥārith 355]"""
"9861","(9856) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muqriʾ al-Khastūjirdī informed us, saying: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Khastūjirdī informed us: Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us: Zājir ibn al-Ṣalt al-Ṭāḥī informed us: Ziyād ibn Sufyān informed us, from Abū Salamah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding a man who bequeathed a Hajj: \Four Hajjs are recorded for him: a Hajj for the one who bequeathed it"," a Hajj for the one who carried it out"," a Hajj for the one who wrote it down"," and a Hajj for the one who commanded it.\""\n\nThis Ziyād ibn Sufyān is unknown (majhūl)"," and the chain is weak. Weak narrations have been reported regarding Hajj on behalf of parents with weak chains"," so I have omitted them. In some of what we have narrated there is sufficiency"," and with Allah is the success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"9862","(9857) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Qurayr al-Baṣrī, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn: that a man came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \My companion and I raced our horses to the pass of Thaniyyah"," and we came upon a gazelle while we are both in iḥrām. What do you think about that?\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to a man beside him: \""Come"," so that the two of us may judge.\"" So the two of them judged that he should give a young she-goat"," and he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. He said: And that man was ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik 9322]"""
"9863","(9858) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from Abī ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd: that a person in iḥrām threw a sack and a jerboa fell out of it and was killed. Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled in the matter that a young kid (jafrah) or a young she-kid (jafrah) should be given. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 7/407]"
"9864","(9859) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Sālim, informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ — regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: \And do not kill game while you are in a state of iḥrām"," and whoever kills it intentionally among you\"" — I said to him: \""If one kills it by mistake"," must he pay a penalty?\"" He said: \""Yes"," thereby he magnifies the sanctities of Allah"," and the established sunnahs have passed regarding it.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 629]"""
"9865","(9860) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Muslim and Saʿīd informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnar, who said: \I saw the people paying a penalty for accidental killing.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī that he said: \""Judgment is rendered against him for both accidental and intentional killing.\"" And from Ibrāhīm: \""Judgment is rendered against the one in iḥrām for accidental killing.\"" And from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah: that ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to render judgment against him for both accidental and intentional killing.\n\nAnd we have narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he said regarding His words — \""Allah has pardoned what is past\"" — he said: \""What occurred during the Jāhiliyyah.\"" And \""And whoever repeats"," Allah will take retribution from him\"" — he said: \""And whoever repeats it in Islam"," Allah will take retribution from him"," and upon him in that is the expiation (kaffārah).\"" And from al-Ḥasan and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī: \""Judgment is rendered against him whenever he strikes (game).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 630]"""
"9866","(9861) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Adīb al-Bisṭāmī informed us — it being read to him in Khastūjird — Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ghiṭrīf informed us: Hārūn ibn Yūsuf informed us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar informed us: Sufyān informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik, meaning Ibn ʿUmayr, informed us: he heard Qabīṣah ibn Jābir al-Asadī say: \We went out as pilgrims"," and our disputing increased while we were in iḥrām — which was faster in running"," the gazelle or the horse? While we were thus"," a gazelle appeared before us — and al-sunūḥ means it passed by us from the left.\"" Hārūn said it with tashdīd. \""A man among us threw a stone at it and did not miss its vital organs. It fell on its side and he rode upon it and killed it. It was dropped before us. When we arrived in Makkah"," we went to ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in Minā. I and the companion of the gazelle entered upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh"," may Allah the Most High be pleased with him"," and he mentioned to him the matter of the gazelle that was killed. And perhaps he said: I and the companion of the gazelle went forward and narrated the story to him. ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'Did you hit it intentionally or by mistake?' And perhaps he said: ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," asked him: 'How did you kill it — intentionally or by mistake?' He said: 'I certainly aimed my arrow intentionally"," but I did not intend to kill it.' A man added"," so ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'Intent and mistake have both come together.' Then he turned toward a man — by Allah"," his face was as though it were a piece of silver — and perhaps he said: Then he turned to a man beside him and spoke with him for a while. Then he turned to my companion and said to him: 'Take a sheep from the flock"," slaughter it"," and give its meat as food.' And perhaps he said: 'Give its meat in charity"," and make its skin into a water-skin for watering.' When we left his presence"," I turned to the man and said to him: 'O you who asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh for a fatwā — the fatwā of Ibn al-Khaṭṭāh will not avail you anything before Allah! By Allah"," ʿUmar did not know until he asked the one beside him. So sacrifice your riding animal"," give it in charity"," and magnify the rites of Allah.'\"" He said: \""So the one with the two springs (dhū al-ʿUwaynatayn) went to him.\"" And perhaps he said: \""The one with the two springs went to ʿUmar and informed him.\"" And perhaps he said: \""I did not know of anything — by Allah"," I was not aware except of him striking me with the whip.\"" And perhaps he said: \""Then he said to my companion"," striking him repeatedly"," then he said: 'May Allah fight you! You transgressed in giving fatwā and killed the haram"," and you say: By Allah"," ʿUmar did not know until he asked the one beside him! Have you not read the Book of Allah? For Allah says: \""The penalty is judged by two just men among you.\""' Then he turned to me and grabbed the gathered part of my cloak — and perhaps he said: my garment — and I said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," I will not permit you from myself anything that Allah has made unlawful for you.' So he released me. Then he turned to me and said: 'I consider you to be a young man of eloquent speech and expansive chest. A man may have ten character traits — nine of them good — and perhaps he said: righteous — and one corrupt. The corrupt trait ruins the nine righteous ones. So beware of the calamities of youth.'\""\n\nIbn Abī ʿUmar said: Sufyān said: \""And ʿAbd al-Malik"," when he narrated this ḥadīth"," said: 'I have not omitted from it a single alif or wāw.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 8240]"""
"9867","(9862) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-San'ani in Makkah informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, who said: I was in the state of ihram when I saw a gazelle and shot it, striking its horn base — meaning the root of its horn — and it died. That weighed upon my heart, so I came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, to ask him. I found beside him a man of fair complexion and delicate countenance, and it was 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf. I asked 'Umar, and 'Abd al-Rahman turned to me and said: \Do you consider a sheep sufficient?\"" He said: Yes. So 'Umar commanded me to slaughter a sheep. When we rose from his presence"," a companion of mine said: \""Indeed"," the Commander of the Faithful does not give a proper fatwa until he asks the man.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," heard some of his words and struck him with a whip. Then he turned toward me to strike me"," so I said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I said nothing — it was he who said it.\"" He said: So he left me"," then said: \""You intended to kill what is haram and to transgress in giving fatwa.\"" Then the Commander of the Faithful said: \""Indeed"," in a person there are ten character traits — nine good and one bad — and that bad one corrupts them all.\"" Then he said: \""Beware of the stumbles of youth.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 8239]"""
"9868","(9863) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us; Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, who said: Abu Hariz narrated to me, saying: I killed a gazelle while I was in the state of ihram, so I came to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him. He said: \Go to two men from your brothers and let them judge for you.\"" So I went to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf and Sa'd"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," and they judged against me a yearling kid. Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid added in it"," from Mansur: \""And I had forgotten my state of ihram.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Sa'd in al-Tabaqat"," 6/154]"""
"9869","(9864) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us; al-Rabi' informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us; Makhariq informed us, from Tariq ibn Shahab, who said: We went out as pilgrims, and a man among us called Arbad trampled a lizard and split its back. We came to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Arbad asked him. 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Judge"," O Arbad.\"" He said: \""You are better than me"," O Commander of the Faithful"," and more knowledgeable.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I only commanded you to judge in the matter"," not to praise me.\"" Arbad said: \""I see in it a young goat that has gathered water and trees.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Then that is what is required of it.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 8221]"""
"9870","(9865) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Whoever kills an ostrich"," upon him is a badanah (a full camel) from the camels.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"9871","(9866) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us; 'Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated, from 'Abd al-Malik, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the pigeons of the Haram: \For one sheep"," a sheep; for two eggs"," a dirham; for an ostrich"," a jazur (a full camel); for a wild cow"," a cow; and for a wild donkey"," a cow.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by al-Daraqutni"," 2/247]"""
"9872","(9867) Al-Shafi'i narrated, from Sa'id, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: \For a wild cow"," a cow; and for a camel"," a cow.\"" This is in what Abu 'Abd Allah permitted me to narrate from him"," from Abu al-'Abbas"," from al-Rabi'"," from al-Shafi'i. [Da'if. Narrated by al-Shafi'i in al-Umm"," 2/295]"""
"9873","(9868) With this chain of narration from al-Shafi'i: Sa'id ibn Salim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata' al-Khurasani, that 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, Zayd ibn Thabit, Ibn 'Abbas, and Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with them all, said regarding the ostrich killed by one in ihram: \Upon him is a badanah (a full camel) from the camels.\"" Al-Shafi'i said: \""This is not established among the scholars of hadith"," and it is the saying of the majority of those I met"," so according to their saying: in the ostrich there is a badanah. And by analogy we said: in the ostrach there is a badanah — but not because of this.\"" The Shaykh said: \""The basis of its weakness is that it is mursal"," for 'Ata' al-Khurasani was born in the year fifty and did not meet 'Umar"," nor 'Uthman"," nor 'Ali"," nor Zayd"," and in the time of Mu'awiyah he was a young boy"," and no hearing from Ibn 'Abbas is established for him"," although it is possible that he heard from him"," for Ibn 'Abbas died in the year sixty-eight. However"," 'Ata' al-Khurasani"," along with the discontinuity of his hadith from those we named"," is among those whom the scholars of hadith have spoken about. And Allah knows best.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by al-Shafi'i in al-Umm"," 2/293]"""
"9874","(9869) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Khalil al-Burjilani narrated to us; Abu al-Nadr Hisham ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; al-Mas'udi narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, that he wrote to Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud asking about the one in ihram who kills a wild donkey, or an ostrich, or the egg of an ostrich, and about the locust killed by one in ihram. He wrote back to him: \As for the one in ihram who kills a wild donkey"," upon him is a badanah; and for the ostrich"," a badanah; and for the egg of an ostrich"," fasting a day or feeding a poor person. As for the locust"," a man from the people of Hims killed a locust while in ihram and came to 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and asked him. 'Umar said to him: 'What did you give for it?' He said: 'I gave a dirham for it.' He said: 'You people of Hims — your dirhams are many"," and a date is more beloved to me than a locust.'\"" This is in the narration of al-Mas'udi. It was also narrated from Ibn Abi 'Arubah"," from Qatadah"," in this hadith"," that he said: He wrote to him that Ibn Mas'ud says regarding it — meaning the ostrich — a badanah. [Da'if]"""
"9875","(9870) 'Abd al-Khaliq ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Mu'adhdhin informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Khanb informed us; Abu Isma'il al-Tirmidhi narrated to us; Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to me; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shahab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \For the ostrich"," a badanah; for the wild cow"," a cow; for the urwiyyah (mountain goat)"," a cow; for the gazelle"," a sheep; for the pigeons of Makkah"," a sheep; for the hare"," a sheep; and for the locust"," a handful of food.\"" [Da'if]"""
"9876","(9871) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, that his father used to say: \For the wild cow"," a cow; and for the sheep of the gazelles"," a sheep.\"" Malik"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""I have always heard that when one in ihram kills an ostrich"," upon him is a badanah.\"" [Sahih]"""
"9877","(9872) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Tājir narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr informed me, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī ʿAmmār, who said: I met Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh and asked him about the hyena — may I eat it? He said: Yes. I said: Is it game (ṣayd)? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī, 2836]"
"9878","(9873) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ḥajjāj, meaning Ibn Minhāl, and Sulaymān, meaning Ibn Ḥarb, and ʿĀṣim, meaning Ibn ʿAlī, all said: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us. He said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmmār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the hyena, and he said: \It is game (ṣayd).\"" And he stipulated therein a ram (kabsh) if the muḥrim (one in the state of iḥrām) hunts it.\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ḥajjāj. Some of them said: \""If he hunts it (aṣābahā)","\"" and some of them said: \""If he kills it (aṣābahā).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9879","(9874) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Abū Khalīfah narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāh al-Ḥajabī narrated to us: Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibrāhīm al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The hyena is game (ṣayd)"," so eat it"," and therein is a mature ram (kabsh musinn) if the muḥrim kills it.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 2648]"""
"9880","(9875) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us: Aḥmad informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm al-Harwī informed us: Hushaym narrated to us: Manṣūr narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: He (the Prophet ﷺ) decreed regarding the hyena a ram (kabsh). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharh al-Maʿānī, 2/165]"
"9881","(9876) Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿIkrimah, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ classified the hyena as game (ṣayd) and decreed therein a ram (kabsh).\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in a narration other than that of Abī Bakr: \And this is a ḥadīth whose like cannot be established if it stands alone.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: He said this because of its discontinuity (inqiṭāʿ)"," and then he corroborated it with the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿAmmār from Jābir. And the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿAmmār is a sound ḥadīth by which the proof is established.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: I asked al-Bukhārī about it and he said: \""It is a ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: And the ḥadīth of ʿIkrimah has also been narrated in a connected (mawṣūl) form. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 989]"""
"9882","(9877) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qirmīsīnī narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Ḥammād al-Ramlī narrated to us: Ibn Abī al-Sarī narrated to us: al-Walīd narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The hyena is game (ṣayd)"," and therein is a ram (kabsh).\"" [Munkar in its isnād. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/245]"""
"9883","(9878) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated, from Abī al-Zubayr al-Makkī. And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others besides them, all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us that Abā al-Zubayr narrated to him, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed regarding the hyena a ram (kabsh), regarding the gazelle a ewe (shāh), regarding the rabbit a young she-goat (ʿanāq), and regarding the jerboa a young kid (jafrah).\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, Sufyān al-Thawrī, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, al-Layth ibn Saʿd, and others, from Abī al-Zubayr. And it was narrated by al-Ajlal al-Kindī in a marfūʿ (elevated) form, and there was disagreement regarding it. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Mālik, 931]"
"9884","(9879) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Tamtām narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Ziyād ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, from al-Ajlal, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from the Prophet ﷺ: \Regarding the hyena"," a ram (kabsh); regarding the gazelle"," a ewe (shāh); regarding the rabbit"," a young she-goat (ʿanāq); and regarding the jerboa"," a young kid (jafrah).\"" He (the narrator) said: I said — meaning to Abī al-Zubayr — \""What is a jafrah?\"" He said: \""A large one","\"" meaning a large young lamb or kid.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Fuḍayl and others corroborated it from al-Ajlal in the same manner."""
"9885","(9880) It was narrated from al-Ajlal, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I do not think he narrated it except in a raised (marfūʿ) form"," that he (the Prophet ﷺ) judged and mentioned it.\"" Abū Saʿid al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Abū ʿUbaydah ibn Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to us: Mālik ibn Suʿayr narrated to us"," from al-Ajlal.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: And this is closer to being correct"," and the correct view is that it is mawqūf (stopped) at ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," from Jābir"," from ʿUmar"," as his own statement."""
"9886","(9881) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī al-Kūfī informed us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed regarding the hyena a ram (kabsh), regarding the gazelle a ewe (shāh), regarding the rabbit a young kid (jafrah), and regarding the jerboa a young she-goat (ʿanāq). Thus it is in my book: a young kid (jafrah) for the rabbit and a young she-goat (ʿanāq) for the jerboa. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"9887","(9882) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sa'id narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Aṭa', that he heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: Regarding the hyena (al-ḍabu'), the expiation is a ram (kabsh).\n\n(T) Mujahid and 'Ikrimah narrated it from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). [Hasan. Al-Shafi'i cited it in al-Umm, 2/296.]"
"9888","(9883) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik and Sufyan narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah: that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭab (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding the gazelle (al-ghazal) that the expiation is a she-goat ('anz), and regarding the rabbit (al-arnab) a young she-goat one year old ('anāq), and regarding the jerboa (al-yarbū') a young she-goat (jafrah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"
"9889","(9884) Abu Ṣalih ibn Abi Ṭahir al-'Anbari informed us — my grandfather, Yaḥya ibn Manṣur al-Qaḍi, informed us — Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Isma'ili informed us — 'Isa ibn Ḥammad informed us — al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me — Abu al-Zubayr narrated from Jabir, from 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭab (may Allah be pleased with him): that he ruled regarding the hyena (al-ḍabu') killed by one in iḥram — the expiation is a ram (kabsh); and regarding the gazelle (al-ẓaby) a sheep (shāh); and regarding the rabbit (al-arnab) a young she-goat ('anāq); and regarding the jerboa (al-yarbū') a young she-goat (jafrah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"9890","(9885) Abu al-Qasim — Zayd ibn Abi Hashim al-'Alawi and 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Najjar in Kufah — they both said: Abu Ja'far — Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duḥaym informed us — Ahmad ibn Ḥazim informed us — 'Amr ibn Ḥammad narrated from Asbaṭ, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, who said: A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: \I have killed a rabbit (arnab) while I am in iḥram. What is your opinion?\"" He (Ibn 'Abbas) replied: \""It walks on four legs"," and the young she-goat ('anāq) walks on four legs. It eats trees"," and the young she-goat eats trees. It chews the cud"," and the young she-goat chews the cud. Offer in its place a young she-goat ('anāq).\""\n\n[Ḍa'īf.]"""
"9891","(9886) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Ḥasan — Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Karizi informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Abu 'Ubayd — Ibn Mahdi narrated from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Ḥarb, from al-Nu'man ibn Ḥumayd, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): that he ruled regarding the rabbit (al-arnab) that the expiation for one killed by a person in iḥram is a young she-goat (ḥullān).\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: Al-Aṣma'i and others stated: His word \al-ḥullān\"" means \""al-jady\"" (a young male goat).\n\n[Ḍa'īf.]"""
"9892","(9887) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Ḥasan al-Karizi informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Abu 'Ubayd — Ibn 'Ulayyat narrated from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): that he ruled regarding the hyena (al-ḍabu') the expiation is a ram (kabsh); and regarding the gazelle (al-ẓaby) a sheep (shāh); and regarding the jerboa (al-yarbū') a young she-goat (jaf' or jafrah).\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: Abu Zayd stated: \Al-jaf' is a kid of the goat species that has reached four months of age and has been weaned from its mother.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"9893","(9888) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan narrated from 'Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, from his father Ibn Mas'ud: that he ruled regarding the jerboa (al-yarbū') the expiation is a young she-goat (jaf' or jafrah).\n\nAnd with his chain of narration, al-Shafi'i informed us — Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Ibn Mas'ud ruled regarding the jerboa (al-yarbū') with a young she-goat (jaf' or jafrah).\n\nThe Shaykh (al-Hafiz) said: Both of these narrations from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) are mursal (disconnected), and one of them corroborates the other.\n\n[Hasan li-ghayrihi. Al-Shafi'i cited it, no. 1683.]"
"9894","(9889) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayḥ, that he said: \If I had the authority to rule"," I would rule regarding the fox (al-tha'lab) that the expiation is a young male goat (jady).\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from Aṭa' that he said: \""Regarding the fox (al-tha'lab)"," the expiation is a sheep (shāh).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. 'Abd al-Razzaq cited it"," no. 8227.]"""
"9895","(9890) Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Faḍl informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan narrated from Mukhariq, from Ṭariq, that Arbad hunted a hyena (ḍabb) and split its back. He then came to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him. 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \What is you opinion?\"" He replied: \""A young male goat (jady) that has gathered water and trees.\"" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Then that is its expiation.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 9764.]"""
"9896","(9891) Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan narrated from Muṭarrif, from Abu al-Safar, that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding the um ḥubayn (a small lizard-like creature) that the expiation is a young sheep (ḥullān) from the flock.\n\n[Ḍa'īf. Al-Shafi'i cited it, no. 1684.]"
"9897","(9892) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Muslim ibn Khālid and Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ that he said: \If one in iḥrām kills a game animal that is one-eyed or defective"," then its expiation (fidya) with a similar one-eyed or defective animal is more beloved to me. And if one kills the young of game animals"," then its expiation is with the young of sheep.\""\n[Hasan. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 7/407]"""
"9898","(9893) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us that Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to me from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent as a gift to Abū Jahl a camel with a silver ring in its nose"," in order to enrage the polytheists therewith.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of corroborating narrations. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1749"," Aḥmad 1/261]"""
"9899","(9894) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {So an expiation [consisting of] fasting, or charity, or a sacrifice} — he said: \He may choose whichever of them he wishes.\""\nAnd from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār who said: \""Everything in the Quran that contains 'or... or' (aw... aw) means that one has the choice of whichever one wishes.\""\nIbn Jurayj said: \""Except the words of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger} — for one is not given a choice in that.\""\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""As Ibn Jurayj and others have said regarding the one who wages war (muḥārib) and others — this is my position on this matter.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 633]"""
"9900","(9895) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth informed us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \If you wish"," offer a sacrifice (nusuk); if you wish"," fast three days; and if you wish"," feed three ṣāʿ measures to six poor persons.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9901","(9896) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Hilāl al-Būzanjardī informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū al-Walīd Ḥassān ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā informed us that ʿAbd Allāh informed us that al-Awzāʿī informed us that al-Zuhrī narrated from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man came and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am ruined!\"" He said: \""Woe to you! What is the matter?\"" He said: \""I had intercourse with my wife during a day of Ramaḍān.\"" He said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not have one.\"" He said: \""Then fast two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able.\"" He said: \""Then feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I do not have the means.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a basket (ʿaraq) containing fifteen ṣāʿ of dates. He said: \""Take it and give it in charity.\"" He said: \""To someone poorer than my family? By Allah"," there is no one between the two lava tracts of Madīnah more in need than my family.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laughed until his teeth became visible"," and said: \""Take it"," seek forgiveness from Allah"," and feed your family.\""\nAl-Walīd ibn Muslim"," Hiql ibn Ziyād"," and Masrūr ibn Ṣadaqah also narrated it from al-Awzāʿī.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5812]"""
"9902","(9897) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed it to us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā informed us; ʿAbd Allāh, that is Ibn al-Mubārak, informed us; al-Awzāʿī informed me; Ibn Shihāb informed me.\nThe Shaykh Abū Bakr said: And Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ḥāsib informed me; al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā informed us; Hiql narrated from al-Awzāʿī. He said: And Ibn Abī Ḥassān informed us; Duḥaym informed us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us; al-Awzāʿī informed me; al-Zuhrī informed me. And this is the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Mubārak from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am ruined!\"" He said: \""Woe to you! What have you done?\"" He said: \""I had intercourse with my wife during Ramaḍān.\"" He said: \""Free a slave.\"" He said: \""I do not have one.\"" He said: \""Fast two consecutive months.\"" He said: \""I am not able.\"" He said: \""Then feed sixty poor persons.\"" He said: \""I do not have the means.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a basket (ʿaraq)"," and he said: \""Take it and give it in charity.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," upon other than my family? By Him in whose Hand is my soul"," there is no one between the two tent-ropes of Madīnah\"" — and ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb said: \""between the two lava tracts of Madīnah\"" — \""more in need than I.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laughed until his teeth became visible"," then said: \""Take it and seek forgiveness from your Lord.\""\nAnd ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb said: \""He was brought a large basket (miktal) containing fifteen ṣāʿ.\""\nAl-Ismāʿīlī said: \""None of them mentioned ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayj other than Ibn al-Mubārak.\""\nAnd Hiql said: \""A basket (ʿaraq) containing fifteen ṣāʿ.\""\nDuḥaym said: \""Woe to you! What is that?\"" He said: \""I had intercourse with my wife during a day of Ramaḍān.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a basket (ʿaraq) containing fifteen ṣāʿ.\nThe Shaykh said: Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Adab from Ibn Muqātil from Ibn al-Mubārak from al-Awzāʿī up to his words \""between the two tent-ropes of Madīnah","\"" and he did not mention what comes after that.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5812]"""
"9903","(9898) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl ibn Zakariyyā al-Dabbī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr from al-Ḥakam from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His words (the Exalted): {So the penalty is an equivalent of what he killed of livestock} — he said: \When a person in iḥrām kills game"," its expiation is judged against him. If he has its equivalent"," he slaughters it and gives its meat in charity. If he does not have its equivalent"," its expiation is valued in dirhams"," then the dirhams are valued in food"," and he fasts one day for every half ṣāʿ. The food is intended to mean fasting"," because when one finds the food"," one has found the expiation.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 13360]"""
"9904","(9899) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us that Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam who said: I heard Miqsam regarding the one who kills game and does not have its expiation — he said: \The game is valued in dirhams"," and the dirhams are valued in food"," and he fasts one day for every half ṣāʿ.\""\nShuʿbah said: And Abān and Abū Maryam told me that it was from Ibn ʿAbbās — meaning Abān ibn Taghlib. Thus in the narration of Shuʿbah is the valuation of the game animal"," while in the narration of Manṣūr is the valuation of the expiation (jazāʾ). And Manṣūr has the better narration of the two in terms of context.\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he equated in the expiation: if it was a sheep"," one day of fasting equaled feeding two poor persons; and if it was a badanaḥ (camel) or a cow"," one day of fasting equaled feeding one poor person. And he said: \""A mudd"," a mudd.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd 155]"""
"9905","(9900) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdūs informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: \When a person in iḥrām kills something of the game"," judgment is passed against him regarding it. If he kills a gazelle or the like"," then upon him is a sheep to be slaughtered in Makkah. If he does not find one"," then feeding six poor persons. If he does not find the means"," then fasting three days. If he kills an ibex or the like"," then upon him is a cow. If he does not find one"," he feeds twenty poor persons. If he does not find the means"," he fasts twenty days. If he kills an ostrich or a wild donkey or the like"," then upon him is a badanah (camel). If he does not find one"," he feeds thirty poor persons. If he does not find the means"," he fasts thirty days. The food is a mudd"," a mudd — their satiation.\"" This narration and the one before it indicate that"," according to him"," this is in order (tartīb). And Allah knows best.\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr 5/41]"""
"9906","(9901) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn al-Muthannā al-ʿAnbarī informed us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ismāʿīl al-Mukattib informed us that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn al-Muthannā al-ʿAnbarī informed us that Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us that Shibl ibn ʿAbbād narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ who said: And Mujāhid narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a louse that had fallen on his face and said: \Do your vermin harm you?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he commanded him to shave his head"," and they were at al-Ḥudaybiyyah. It was not made clear to them that they would exit iḥrām there"," while they were still hopeful of entering Makkah. So Allah revealed: {So an expiation [consisting of] fasting"," or charity} — a measure (faraq) distributed among six poor persons — or a sacrifice (nusuk)"," a sheep. And the sacrifice is to be offered in Makkah.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shibl"," without his words: \""And the sacrifice is to be offered in Makkah.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1722]"""
"9907","(9902) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abu Naṣr al-'Irāqī informed us — Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — 'Abd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to me — Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from 'Ikrimah, who said: Marwān asked Ibn 'Abbās while we were in Wādī al-Azraq: \What do you say about game we have hunted and find no substitute for it among livestock?\"" He replied: \""Determine its price and give it in charity to the poor of Makkah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9908","(9903) Abu Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabī' informed us — al-Shāfi'ī informed us — Sa'īd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Aṭā' regarding the verse {And the penalty is the equivalent of what he killed of livestock} (Q 5:95) up to {an offering reaching the Ka'bah, or an expiation by feeding the poor}: He said: \Because he killed it within the Ḥaram"," intending the House"," its expiation is to be offered at the House.\"" [Ḥasan. Al-Shāfi'ī reported it"," no. 632]"""
"9909","(9904) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Ākhirīn — they said: Abu al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfi'ī informed us — Mālik narrated from Abu al-Naḍr, the freedman of 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd Allāh al-Taymī — from Nāfi', the freedman of Abū Qatādah — from Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī, who said: He was with the Prophet ﷺ until, when they were on one of the roads to Makkah, he lagged behind with companions who were in iḥrām while he was not in iḥrām. He saw a wild donkey, mounted his horse, and asked his companions to hand him his whip, but they refused. He asked them for his spear, but they refused. So he took his spear, pursued the donkey, and killed it. Some of the Prophet's ﷺ companions ate from it, but some refused. When they caught up with the Prophet ﷺ, they asked him about that. He said: \It is merely food that Allah has provided for you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"," no. 5172]"""
"9910","(9905) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abu al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū Mūsā Hārūn ibn Mūsā al-Zāhid narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read it back to Mālik, and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhārī reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways and others from Mālik, and Muslim reported it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Qutaybah."
"9911","(9906) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Ākhirīn — they said: Abu al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Rabī' informed us — al-Shāfi'ī informed us — Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam — from 'Aṭā' ibn Yasār — from Abū Qatādah, regarding the wild donkey, similar to the ḥadīth of Abu al-Naḍr, except that in Zayd's ḥadīth it is stated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do you have any of its meat with you?\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim reported it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"9912","(9907) Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān said: I heard Abū Muḥammad say: I heard Abū Qatādah say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached al-Qāḥah. Among us were those in iḥrām and those not in iḥrām. I noticed my companions looking at something, so I looked and saw a wild donkey. I saddled my horse, mounted, and took my spear. My whip fell, so I said to my companions: \Hand it to me","\"" while they were in iḥrām. They said: \""By Allah"," we will not help you with anything.\"" So I retrieved my whip"," then approached the donkey from behind — it was behind a hill — and I struck it with my spear and hamstrung it. I brought it to my companions. Some of them said: \""Eat it","\"" and some said: \""Do not eat it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ahead of us. I urged my horse"," caught up with him"," and asked him. He said: \""It is ḥalāl"," so eat it.\"" Al-Bukhārī reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Alī ibn 'Abd Allāh"," and Muslim reported it from Qutaybah from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"," no. 1727]"""
"9913","(9908) Abu Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Hishām narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — from 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah — from his father, who said: He set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. His companions entered iḥrām, but he did not. The Prophet ﷺ went on, and I was with my companions. Some of them began laughing at one another. I looked and saw a wild donkey. I attacked it and struck it down. I sought their help, but they refused to assist me. We ate from it, and we feared we might be cut off — meaning, separated from the Prophet ﷺ. I went at the gallop of my horse seeking the Prophet ﷺ. I met a man from Ghifār in the depths of the night and asked: \Where did you leave the Prophet ﷺ?\"" He said: \""At al-Suqyā.\"" So I caught up with him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," your companions convey their salām and the mercy of Allah to you"," and they fear they may be cut off from you. Wait for them"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" And I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have caught a wild donkey"," and I still have some of it left.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to the people: \""Eat","\"" while they were in iḥrām. Al-Bukhārī reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mu'ādh ibn Faḍālah from Hishām"," and Muslim reported it from another direction from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"," no. 1725]"""
"9914","(9909) Abu Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh, from the original of his hearing, informed us — Abū 'Uthmān 'Amr ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us — Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb informed us — Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Abū Ḥāzim ibn Dīnār narrated from 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah — from his father, who said: One day I was sitting with a group of the Prophet's ﷺ companions in a house on the road to Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was camped ahead of us. The people were in iḥrām, while I was not in iḥrām. The people spotted a wild donkey. I was busy repairing my sandal and they did not inform me of it. I turned and saw it. I went to my horse, saddled it, and mounted, having forgotten the whip and the spear. I said to them: \Hand me the whip and the spear.\"" They said: \""We will not help you with anything.\"" So I dismounted"," took them"," mounted"," pursued it"," and killed it. Then I brought it"," dragging it by its legs"," and it had died. They fell upon it and began eating it. Then they began to doubt their eating of it"," as they were in iḥrām. We set out"," and I hid the foreleg with me. We caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: \""Do you have any of it with you?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" I handed him the foreleg"," and he ate it while he was in iḥrām"," until he stripped it to the bone. Al-Bukhārī reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abd al-'Azīz ibn 'Abd Allāh from Muḥammad ibn Ja'far"," and Muslim reported it from another direction from Abū Ḥāzim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"," no. 2431]"""
"9915","(9910) Abu Aḥmad 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī al-'Adl and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī both said: Abu 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allāh and 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan — 'Alī said: He narrated to us, and Ibrāhīm said: He informed us — Abū 'Āṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me from Mu'ādh ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn 'Uthmān al-Taymī, from his father, who said: We were with Ṭalḥah ibn 'Ubayd Allāh — may Allah be pleased with him — on the road to Makkah, and we were in iḥrām. They presented us with the meat of game, and Ṭalḥah was asleep. Some of us ate, and some of us abstained and did not eat. When he awoke, he said to those who had eaten: \You have done rightly","\"" and to those who had not eaten: \""You have erred"," for we ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were in iḥrām.\"" Muslim reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," no. 197]"""
"9916","(9911) Abu al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ al-Bazzār narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — from 'Īsā ibn Ṭalḥah — from 'Umayr ibn Salamah — from a man of Bahz, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out intending Makkah. When he was in one of Wādī al-Rawḥā', the people found a wounded wild donkey. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \Leave it until its owner comes.\"" The man from Bahz — who was its owner — came and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is your command regarding this donkey?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — and he divided it among the companions while they were in iḥrām. He said: Then we continued until we reached al-Abwā'"," and there was a gazelle crouching in the shade of a tree with an arrow in it. The Prophet ﷺ ordered a man to stand by it until the people had passed by it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Nasā'ī reported it"," no. 4344; Aḥmad"," 3/418]"""
"9917","(9912) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Susi narrated to us: Abu 'Ali Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi narrated to us: Hafs ibn 'Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Hisham, the companion of al-Dastawa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man from the people of Sham asked me about game meat that had been hunted for others — could he eat it while he was in a state of ihram? I gave him a verdict that he could eat it. Then I came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. He said: \What verdict did you give?\"" I said: \""I permitted him to eat it.\"" He said: \""Had you given him any other verdict"," I would have struck your head with the whip.\"" Then 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""You have only been forbidden to hunt it.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq (8344)]"""
"9918","(9913) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu al-Sha'tha' say: I asked Ibn 'Umar about game meat that a person in a state of halal gives as a gift to one in a state of ihram. He said: \'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to eat it.\"" I said: \""I am asking you about yourself — would you eat it?\"" He said: \""'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was better than me.\"" [Sahih]"""
"9919","(9914) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar that a group of people in a state of ihram passed by him at al-Rabadhah and asked him for a verdict regarding game meat that some people in a state of halal had found — could they eat it? He gave them a verdict permitting them to eat it. He said: Then I came to 'Umar ibn al-Khatrap (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him about that. He said: \What verdict did you give them?\"" I said: \""I gave them a verdict to eat it.\"" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Had you given them any other verdict"," I would have caused you pain.\""\n\nAnd with his chain"," Malik narrated to us"," from Zayd ibn Aslam"," from 'Ata' ibn Yasar"," that Ka'b al-Ahbar came from Sham in a caravan of people in a state of ihram. When they were somewhere along the road"," they found game meat"," and Ka'b gave them a verdict permitting them to eat it. When they came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)"," they mentioned that to him. He said: \""Who gave you this verdict?\"" They said: \""Ka'b.\"" He said: \""Then I have appointed him as your leader until you return.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik (783)]"""
"9920","(9916) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Julabadhi narrated to us: Sahl ibn 'Ammar al-'Ataki narrated to us: al-Jarud ibn Yazid al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abu Hanifah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from his grandfather al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, who said: We used to eat game meat, carry it as provisions, and eat it while we were in a state of ihram, in the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\n\nAnd similarly, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Abu Hanifah with the same meaning. [Batil. See al-Lisan 3/121]"
"9921","(9917) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn 'Abdillah ibn Mawhab, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) set out performing Hajj or 'Umrah, and we set out with him. He dispatched a group of them, and I was among them. He said: \Take the coast of the sea until you meet me.\"" So we took the coast of the sea. When we turned back toward the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," they had all entered into a state of ihram except Abu Qatadah. While we were traveling"," we saw wild donkeys. I assailed one of the female donkeys and killed it. They dismounted and ate from its meat. They said: \""Are we eating game meat while we are in a state of ihram?\"" They carried what remained of its meat until they came to the Prophet (peace be upon him). They said: \""We had entered into a state of ihram"," while Abu Qatadah had not entered into ihram. We saw wild donkeys"," and he assailed a female donkey and killed it. We dismounted and ate from its meat"," then we carried what remained of its meat.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Is there anyone among you who commanded him to carry it or pointed it out to him?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then eat what remains of its meat.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Abu 'Abdillah. In the hadith of al-Muqri' there is no mention of \""or 'Umrah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il from Abu 'Awanah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Kamil. [Sahih. Bukhari (1728)]"""
"9922","(9918) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, who said: Abu Qatadah was among a group of people in a state of ihram, while Abu Qatadah was in a state of halal. The people saw a wild donkey but did not alert him until Abu Qatadah himself saw it. He snatched a whip from one of them, then charged at the donkey and felled it. He brought it to them, and they ate and carried some of it. They met the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him. He said: \Did any one of you point it out to him or command him to do anything?\"" They said: \""No"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then eat.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Sahih. Muslim (1196)]"""
"9923","(9919) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani al-Faqih both said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah. My companions entered into a state of ihram, and I did not enter into ihram. I saw a donkey, so I charged at it and hunted it. I mentioned its matter to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and mentioned that I had not entered into ihram and that I had hunted it for him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded his companions, and they ate, but he did not eat from it when I informed him that I had hunted it for him. 'Ali said: Abu Bakr said to us: His statement \I hunted it for you\"" and his statement \""he did not eat from it\"" — I do not know anyone who mentioned these in this hadith from Ma'mar"," and it is in accordance with what was narrated from 'Uthman. [Shadhdh. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq (8337)]"""
"9924","(9920) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Abu al-Shaykh al-Isbahani narrated to us: 'Abdan narrated to us: Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nThe Sheikh said: This is an unusual wording that we have not recorded except from this chain.\n\nAnd we have narrated from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, in this hadith: that the Prophet (peace be upon him) ate from it. That narration was included by the authors of the two Sahihs in their two books, to the exclusion of the narration of Ma'mar, even though both chains are sound. And Allah knows best. [Shadhdh. See the one before it]"
"9925","(9921) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Asamm narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: 'Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yahya ibn 'Abdillah ibn Salim and Ya'qub ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to me that 'Amr, the freed slave of al-Muttalib, informed them both, from al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdillah ibn Hantab, from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), that he said: \The game of the land is lawful for you"," while you are in a state of ihram"," so long as you do not hunt it or it is not hunted for you.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud (11351)]"""
"9926","(9922) Abu 'Abdillah narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: My grandfather narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn 'Ufayr narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdillah ibn Hantab, from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The game of the land is lawful for you"," so long as you do not hunt it or it is not hunted for you.\""\n\nSo these are three reliable narrators who established its chain from 'Amr.\n\nAnd similarly"," al-Shafi'i narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad from 'Amr"," and from the trustworthy narrator according to him from Sulayman ibn Bilal from 'Amr. And similarly"," Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated it from Malik ibn Anas from 'Amr. [Da'if. See the one before it]"""
"9927","(9923) It was narrated by ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr from a man from Banī Salamah from Jābir from the Prophet ﷺ. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported it among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn Abī Yaḥyā is more precise than al-Dārawardī, and Sulaymān alongside Ibn Abī Yaḥyā — the Shaykh said: likewise Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim, and both of them alongside Sulaymān are among the reliable narrators (al-athbāt)."
"9928","(9924) Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah, who said: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) at al-ʿArj on a summer day, and he was in iḥrām. He had covered his face with a velvet cloth of deep red colour. Then the meat of game was brought to him, and he said to his companions: \Eat.\"" They said: \""Will you not eat?\"" He said: \""I am not in the same state as you; this game was hunted on my account.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 786]"""
"9929","(9925) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; they said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib, from his father, that he performed ʿUmrah with ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) in a caravan, and a bird was gifted to him. He ordered them to eat it, but he himself refused to eat. ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ said to him: \Shall I eat from that which you are not eating?\"" He said: \""I am not in this matter like you; it was hunted on my behalf and killed for my sake.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 8345]"""
"9930","(9926) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Muḥammad al-Dhuhlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās from al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah, that he presented a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what was on my face, he said: \We only returned it to you because we are in iḥrām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 2434]"""
"9931","(9927) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān narrated to us, Shuʿayb narrated to us from al-Zuhrī. ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās informed him: he heard al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah al-Laythī — who was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — narrating that he presented a wild ass to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in iḥrām, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it. Al-Ṣaʿb said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perceived the signs of displeasure on my face regarding the rejection of my gift, he said: \We have not rejected it out of any aversion toward you"," but we are in iḥrām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""
"9932","(9928) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he informed him that al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah informed him: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān, and he presented a wild donkey to him, and he returned it to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the displeasure on his face, he said: \It is not out of any rejection of you"," but I am in iḥrām.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. He also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān and Maʿmir ibn Rāshid from al-Zuhrī with the same meaning. And Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqamah"," and others narrated it from al-Zuhrī.\n\nIbn ʿUaynah contradicted them and narrated it as follows: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us"," Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad narrated to us"," ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us"," Sufyān narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās; al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah informed him: he presented the meat of a wild ass to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he returned it. He saw the displeasure on his face and said: \""We have not rejected it out of any aversion toward you"," but we are in iḥrām.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and ʿAmr al-Nāqid from Sufyān"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""I presented to him some of the meat of a wild ass.\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī narrated it from Sufyān with the correct wording"," as the rest of the people narrated from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1194]"""
"9933","(9929) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us; he said: We heard it from al-Zuhrī, both from the beginning and the end, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās. He said: Al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Abwāʾ or Waddān, and I presented a wild ass to him, and he returned it to me. When he saw the displeasure on my face, he said: \It is not out of any rejection of you"," but we are in iḥrām.\"" Thus I found it in my book"," and it is the hearing of al-Ḥumaydī from Sufyān in what has preceded"," though he became confused in it afterwards.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1193]"""
"9934","(9930) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; he said: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī said: Sufyān used to say in the ḥadīth: \I presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the meat of a wild ass.\"" And sometimes Sufyān said: \""It was dripping with blood","\"" and sometimes he did not say it. And Sufyān"," in what had preceded"," sometimes said: \""A wild ass","\"" then he shifted to \""meat\"" until he died.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥumaydī"," 783]"""
"9935","(9931) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Mūsā narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah presented a wild ass to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in iḥrām, and he returned it to him and said: \Were we not in iḥrām"," we would have accepted it from you.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Abū Kurayb. Thus al-Aʿmash narrated it from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1194]"""
"9936","(9932) Shuʿbah contradicted him and narrated it as follows: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥinnāʾī narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us from Ḥabīb; he heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A side of a wild ass was presented to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in iḥrām, and he returned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh. Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī contradicted him and narrated it from Shuʿbah from Ḥabīb, as al-Aʿmash narrated from Ḥabīb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1194]"
"9937","(9933) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Fadl informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah presented a wild ass to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the state of ihram, and he (the Prophet ﷺ) returned it."
"9938","(9934) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from al-Hakam from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah presented (a gift) to the Prophet ﷺ at Qudayd while he was in the state of ihram — the haunch of a wild ass — and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it, while it was dripping blood.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Ghandar from Shu'bah, and perhaps the correct hadith of Shu'bah from al-Hakam is: \the haunch of an ass","\"" and his hadith from Habib is \""a wild ass","\"" as Abu Dawud narrated it.\n\nAl-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated it from Abu al-Walid and Sulayman ibn Harb"," who both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam and Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," presented (a gift) to the Prophet ﷺ. One of them said: \""at Qudayd"," the haunch of an ass","\"" and the other said: \""a wild ass","\"" and he (the Prophet ﷺ) returned it. Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us of it.\n\nAhmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: al-Asfati narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nIf the narration is thus"," then the narration of Shu'bah from Habib agrees with the narration of al-A'mash from Habib"," and the narration of Shu'bah from al-Hakam agrees with the narration of Mansur from al-Hakam. Thus al-Hakam is alone in mentioning the meat or what carries its meaning"," and Allah knows best.\n\n[Sahih. Muslim 1194]"""
"9939","(9935) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated from al-Hakam ibn 'Utbah from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah presented a leg of a wild ass to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Qudayd, and he returned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman. [Sahih. Muslim 1194]"
"9940","(9936) Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas informed us: al-Rabi' said: al-Shafi'i said: If al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah presented the ass alive to the Prophet ﷺ, then it is not permissible for a person in ihram to slaughter a live wild ass. And if he presented it as meat, then it may be interpreted that he (the Prophet ﷺ) knew that it had been hunted for him, and so he returned it to him. Its clarification is found in the hadith of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: The hadith of Malik that al-Sa'b presented an ass to the Prophet ﷺ is more established (athbat) than the hadith of the one who narrated that he presented some meat of an ass to him, and Allah knows best.\n\nThe Sheikh said: It has also been narrated in the hadith of al-Sa'b that he (the Prophet ﷺ) ate from it. [Sahih]"
"9941","(9937) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Sa'id — Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi — narrated to me: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Ja'far ibn 'Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri from his father, that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah presented the haunch of a wild ass to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Juhfah, and he (the Prophet ﷺ) ate from it, and the people ate from it. This is a sound (sahih) chain of narration. If it is preserved (mahfuz), then it is as though he (the Prophet ﷺ) returned the live animal and accepted the meat, and Allah knows best. [Hasan. Ibn Wahb narrated it as in al-Fath 4/32]"
"9942","(9938) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n(And in another chain:) Abu 'Abdullah informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Ibn Jurayj: al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas asked him, reminding him: \How did you narrate to me about the meat of game that was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the state of ihram?\"" He said: \""A limb of game meat was presented to him"," and he returned it. He said: 'We do not eat it"," for we are in the state of ihram.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Yahya.\n\nIn the narration of Abu 'Asim: Zayd ibn Arqam came"," and Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with him"," came to him and asked him for a legal ruling regarding game meat. He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought game meat while he was in the state of ihram"," and he returned it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Yahya al-Qattan. [Sahih. Muslim 1195]"""
"9943","(9939) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated from Humayd al-Tawil from Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith from his father, who said: Al-Harith was the deputy of 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, over Ta'if. He prepared a meal for 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and included in it partridges, francolins, and wild game meat. He sent it to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. The messenger came to him while he was beating (branches) for his camels. He came to him while he was shaking off the leaves from his hand. They said to him: \Eat.\"" He said: \""Feed it to lawful (halal) people"," for we are in the state of ihram.\"" Then 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I adjure by Allah whoever is present here from (the tribe of) Ashja': Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was presented with a leg of a wild ass while he was in the state of ihram"," and he refused to eat from it?\"" They said: \""Yes.\""\n\nThe interpretation of these two musnads is what al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," mentioned regarding the interpretation of the hadith of the one who narrated in the story of al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah that he presented some ass meat to him. As for 'Ali and Ibn 'Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," they held the view that eating it is prohibited for the person in ihram absolutely. However"," 'Umar"," 'Uthman"," Talhah"," al-Zubayr"," may Allah be pleased with them"," and others opposed them"," and with them is the hadith of Abu Qatadah and Jabir"," and Allah knows best. [Da'if. Abu Dawud narrated it"," 1849]"""
"9944","(9940) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said to him: \O son of my sister"," it is only ten nights. If anything occurs to your mind regarding it"," then leave it\"" — meaning the eating of game meat.\n\n[Sahih. Malik narrated it"," 787]"""
"9945","(9941) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Imran from 'Abdullah ibn Shumas, who said: I came to 'A'ishah and asked her about game meat that a lawful person (halal) presents to a person in ihram. She said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ differed concerning it. Some of them disliked it"," and some of them saw no harm in it"," and there is no harm in it.\"" [Da'if. Ibn Asakir narrated it in his Tarikh"," 41/379]"""
"9946","(9942) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated from Mufaddal from Yazid from Mujahid from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \When a man enters the state of ihram and he has game with him"," he should leave it.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Hasan that he said: \""He should release it"," and if he slaughters it"," then upon him is the penalty (jaza').\"""""
"9947","(9943) Abū Saʿīd informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that al-Ḥasan narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd, who said: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār was asked about a muḥrim (one in the state of iḥrām) who slaughters game. He said: \He may eat it"," and upon him is the penalty (jazāʾ). Discarding it is corruption.\"" Ḥammād said: \""And Ayyūb used to admire this statement of ʿAmr.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī that he said: \""It is carrion (maytah); he may not eat it.\"" And from ʿAṭāʾ: \""The ḥalāl (non-muḥrim) may not eat it.\""\n\nAnd from ʿAṭāʾ: \""If he catches game"," then upon him is a fidyah (ransom); and if he eats it"," then upon him is the value of what he ate.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Ibn Abī Laylā from ʿAṭāʾ"," that ʿĀʾishah"," al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them) said regarding game slaughtered in Makkah: \""It may not be eaten.\"" It was said: \""What should be done with it?\"" He said: \""It should be discarded in the manner of a dead animal.\"" And in the narration of al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿUmar"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them): \""They disapproved of slaughtering game that was hunted in the ḥill (non-sacred territory) while in the state of iḥrām within the Ḥaram.\""\n\nAnd in another narration from al-Ḥajjaj from ʿAṭāʾ: \""That ʿĀʾishah"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn disapproved of slaughtering game in Makkah"," but they saw no harm in bringing it in already slaughtered.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ that he said: \""When a ḥalāl person catches game in the Ḥaram"," the same ruling is applied to him as is applied to the muḥrim.\"" He said: \""And the muḥrim"," if he catches game in the Ḥaram"," then upon him is one kaffārah (expiation).\"""""
"9948","(9944) Abū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Jarīr narrated. And Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — and the wording is his — that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī informed us that Jarīr informed us from Manṣūr from Mujāhid from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said on the day of the Conquest, the Conquest of Makkah: \There is no hijrah (emigration) after this"," but rather jihād and intention. So when you are called to mobilise"," then mobilise.\"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest"," the Conquest of Makkah: \""Indeed"," this land was sanctified by Allah on the day He created the heavens and the earth; thus it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Resurrection. Its thorns may not be cut"," its trees may not be felled"," its game may not be driven away"," and its lost property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\"" Al-ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," except al-idhkhar (a type of fragrant grass)"," for it is for their blacksmiths and their homes.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Except al-idhkhar.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1737]"""
"9949","(9945) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," sanctified Makkah. It was not made lawful for anyone before me"," nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful to me for an hour of a day. Its grass may not be cut"," its trees may not be felled"," its game may not be driven away"," and its lost property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\"" Al-ʿAbbās said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," except al-idhkhar"," for our blacksmiths and our homes.\"" He said: \""Except al-idhkhar.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1736]"""
"9950","(9946) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī and al-Busrī both said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us. He mentioned it with its chain, except that he said: \It was only made lawful","\"" and he said: \""For our blacksmiths and the roofs of our homes.\"" And he added: ʿIkrimah said: \""Do you know what 'its game may not be driven away' means? It means moving it from its shade and taking its place.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," except that he said: \""For our blacksmiths and our graves.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous]"""
"9951","(9947) Abū Shurayḥ al-Khuzāʿī narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said in the hadith: \It is not permissible for any person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood therein or to cut a tree therein.\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān"," who said: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us that Yaḥyā narrated to us that al-Layth narrated from Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abī Shurayḥ. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1735]"""
"9952","(9948) Abū Hurayrah narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said in the hadith: \It is sacred; its trees may not be felled"," its thorns may not be cut"," and its fallen property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ"," Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī"," and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Sūsī"," who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-ʿAbbāb ibn al-Walīd informed us that my father informed us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us that Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that Abū Hurayrah narrated to me. He mentioned it and said: Al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," except al-idhkhar"," for we use it in our homes and our graves.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Except al-idhkhar"," except al-idhkhar.\"" Thus said al-Walīd ibn Yazīd from al-Awzāʿī.\n\nAnd al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from al-Awzāʿī"," and he said in the hadith: \""Its game may not be driven away"," its thorns may not be cut"," and its fallen property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\"" And in another narration from him: \""Its trees may not be felled"," its game may not be driven away"," and its lost property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\""\n\nAnd Shaybān narrated from Yaḥyā"," and he said in the hadith: \""Its thorns may not be struck down"," its trees may not be felled"," and its fallen property may not be picked up except by one who announces it.\"" All of this is recorded in its appropriate places in the Book"," if Allah wills. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 112]"""
"9953","(9949) Abū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Saʿīd narrated from Maṭar from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was addressing the people at Minā when he saw a man on a mountain cutting trees. He called him and said: \Did you not know that in Makkah its trees may not be cut and its grass may not be harvested?\"" He said: \""Yes"," but a weak camel of mine compelled me.\"" So he placed him upon a camel and said to him: \""Do not repeat it","\"" and he did not impose any penalty upon him. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿArūbah in al-Manāsik 26]"""
"9954","(9950) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Whoever cuts anything from the trees of the Ḥaram — whether he is ḥalāl or muḥrim — for a small tree"," the penalty is a sheep"," and for a large tree"," a cow.\""\n\nThis is narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr and ʿAṭāʾ.\n\nAnd with this chain"," he said in the dictation and the fidyah regarding what was mentioned earlier from Ibn al-Zubayr and ʿAṭāʾ"," that they agreed: for a dūḥah (a large tree) the penalty is a cow. The dūḥah is a great tree.\n\nAnd ʿAṭāʾ said: \""For a tree smaller than that"," the penalty is a sheep.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""The qiyās (analogical reasoning)"," were it not for what I have described"," would be that the one who cuts it should ransom it with its value.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: It has been narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ regarding a man who cuts from the trees of the Ḥaram: he said: \""For a small branch (qaḍīb)"," the penalty is one dirham"," and for a dūḥah"," a cow.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9955","(9951) Abū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ narrated to me that Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-Qāriʾ narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us that Sufyān informed us from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī from his father from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \We did not write from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) except the Qurʾān and what is in this ṣaḥīfah.\"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Al-Madīnah is sacred"," between ʿAyr and Thawr. Whoever introduces therein an innovation or gives refuge to an innovator"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind. Allah will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory act. The covenant of the Muslims is one; the lowest among them may act on its behalf. Whoever betrays a Muslim"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind. No obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him. And whoever allies himself with a people without the permission of his masters"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind. No obligatory or supererogatory act will be accepted from him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Mahdī from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1771]"""
"9956","(9952) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say: \If I were to see the gazelles grazing in al-Madīnah"," I would not startle them.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""What is between its two lava fields is sacred.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. And Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Ibn al-Musayyab that Abū Hurayrah said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sanctified what is between the two lava fields of al-Madīnah.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""If I were to find the gazelles between its two lava fields"," I would not startle them.\"" And he designated twelve miles around al-Madīnah as a protected pasture (ḥimā).\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh the ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us"," who said: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated from ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Maʿmar. And Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1774]"""
"9957","Abu 'Abd Allah — al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Ghadairi — informed us in Baghdad; he said: Abu 'Amr — 'Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sammak — narrated to us; he said: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-'Utaridi narrated to us; he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-Madinah is a sacred sanctuary (haram) between 'Ayr and Thawr. Whoever introduces therein an innovation (hadath) or gives refuge to an innovator"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind.\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 6870]"""
"9958","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; he said: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; he mentioned it with its chain of narration similar to the foregoing, and he added: \No obligatory act (sarf) nor supererogatory act ('adl) will be accepted from him.\"" Al-Bukhari and Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from the hadith of Zaidah and others"," from al-A'mash. [Sahih. See the preceding.]"""
"9959","Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; he said: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; he said: Tamtam narrated to us; he said: Musa narrated to us; he said: Wuhaib narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from 'Abbad ibn Tamim al-Ansari, from 'Abd Allah ibn Zayd, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he said: \Indeed"," Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah sacred and supplicated for it"," and I have declared al-Madinah sacred just as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred"," and I have supplicated for it in its mudd and sa' twice as Ibrahim supplicated for Makkah.\"" Al-Bukhari recorded it in the Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il"," and Muslim recorded it through another route from Wuhaib. [Sahih. Bukhari 2022]"""
"9960","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī informed us; he said: Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; he said: Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn al-Sindi narrated to us; he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us; he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from 'Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Indeed"," Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah sacred"," and I have declared al-Madinah sacred just as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred"," and I have supplicated for it in its mudd and sa' just as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) supplicated for Makkah.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari. [Sahih. Muslim 1360]"""
"9961","Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Nazif al-Farra' al-Misri — informed us in Makkah; he said: Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Mawt al-Makki — narrated to us by dictation; he said: 'Ali — meaning Ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz — narrated to us; he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik.\n\n(And) Abu al-Khayr — Jami' ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Muhammadabadi — informed us; he said: Abu Tahir — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muhammadabadi — narrated to us; he said: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from what he read to Malik ibn Anas, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, the freed slave of al-Muttalib, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (ﷺ) caught sight of Uhud and said: \This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. O Allah"," indeed Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred"," and I declare sacred what lies between its two mountains (labatayha).\"" Al-Bukhari recorded it in the Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi. [Sahih. Bukhari 3187]"""
"9962","Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; he said: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; he said: Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us; he said: Sa'id narrated to us; he said: Ya'qub ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned the hadith in its entirety within the story of Khaybar — he said: \When Uhud became visible to us"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'A mountain that loves us and we love it.' And when he overlooked al-Madinah"," he said: 'O Allah"," I declare sacred what lies between its two mountains (labatayha)"," just as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred. O Allah"," bless them in their sa' and their mudd.'\"" Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Sa'id ibn Mansur. [Sahih. Muslim 1365]"""
"9963","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; he said: Abu al-'Abbas — 'Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi — narrated to us; he said: al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us; he said: 'Arim narrated to us; he said: Thabit ibn Yazid — Abu Zayd — narrated to us; he said: 'Asim ibn Sulayman — Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ahwal — narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," al-Madinah is a sacred sanctuary (haram)"," a place of security"," from such-and-such to such-and-such. Its trees shall not be cut"," and no innovation (hadath) shall be introduced therein. Whoever introduces an innovation therein"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind. No obligatory act (sarf) nor supererogatory act ('adl) will be accepted from him.\"" Al-Bukhari recorded it in the Sahih from 'Arim. [Sahih. Bukhari 1768]"""
"9964","Abu al-Husayn — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran — informed us in Baghdad; he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us; he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; he informed us: 'Asim said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: \Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) declare al-Madinah sacred?\"" He said: \""Yes"," it is inviolable (haram). Allah and His Messenger declared it sacred. Its vegetation shall not be cut. Whoever does that"," upon him is the curse of Allah"," the angels"," and all of mankind.\"" The wording is that of Muhammad's hadith"," and in the narration of Ibrahim it is: \""Whoever does that","\"" and the remainder is the same. Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb"," from Yazid ibn Harun. [Sahih. Muslim 1366]"""
"9965","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; he said: Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed me; he said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Hakim, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I declare sacred what lies between the two mountains (labatay) of al-Madinah — that its thorny trees not be cut and its game not be hunted.\"" And he said: \""Al-Madinah is better for them"," if they only knew. No one departs from it out of aversion except that Allah will replace in it one who is better than him"," and no one endures its hardships and difficulties except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. [Sahih. Muslim 1363]"""
"9966","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us; he said: Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; he said: Muhammad ibn Shadhan and Ahmad ibn Salamah both said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Hadi, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred"," and I declare sacred what lies between its two mountains\"" — meaning al-Madinah. Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Muslim 1361]"""
"9967","(9963) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād informed us — and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us that Abū Aḥmad Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us — both saying: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from ʿUtbah ibn Muslim from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr that Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam addressed the people and mentioned Makkah, its people, and its sanctity. Thereupon Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj called out to him and said: \What is the matter with me that I hear you mentioning Makkah"," its people"," and its sanctity"," yet you have not mentioned al-Madīnah"," its people"," and its sanctity"," when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has indeed sanctified what lies between its two lava tracts"," and that is in our possession written on a Khawlānī parchment — if you wish"," I can read it to you.\"" Marwān fell silent"," then said: \""I have heard some of that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1351]"""
"9968","(9964) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī informed us that Abū Usāmah narrated to us from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr who informed me that Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to him from his father Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \I have indeed sanctified what lies between the two lava tracts of al-Madīnah"," just as Ibrāhīm sanctified Makkah.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: And Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī used to find a bird in the hand of one of us"," so he would take it"," release it from his hand"," and set it free.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Abī Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1353]"""
"9969","(9965) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī in Baghdād informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us that Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib ibn Ḥayyān al-Mukharramī informed us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us that Sulaymān al-Shaybānī informed me that Usayr ibn ʿAmr informed me that he heard Sahl ibn Ḥunayf say: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say, gesturing with his hand toward al-Madīnah: \It is a sanctuary"," a place of security.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1375]"""
"9970","(9966) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhārī informed me that Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated to us from al-Shaybānī from Yusr ibn ʿAmr from Sahl ibn Ḥunayf who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gestured with his hand toward al-Madīnah and said: \It is a sanctuary"," a place of security.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""
"9971","(9967) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī informed us that Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar informed us that Qabīṣah informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) sanctified Makkah"," and I have sanctified al-Madīnah — what lies between its two lava tracts. Its thorny trees shall not be cut"," and its game shall not be hunted.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1362]"""
"9972","(9968) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī informed us that Abū Ḍamrah Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ al-Laythī informed me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah narrated to me from Yaʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmaz that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbādah al-Zuraqī informed him that he used to hunt birds at Biʾr Ihāb, and they (the birds) were there. ʿUbādah saw me when I had taken a sparrow, so he snatched it from me, released it, and said: \Indeed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sanctified what lies between its two lava tracts"," just as Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him) sanctified Makkah.\"" And ʿUbādah was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ in meaning. Aḥmad 317]"""
"9973","(9969) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us that Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Yaʿqūb ibn Muḥammad informed us that ʿImrān ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf informed us — and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī informed us that Abū Muṣʿab al-Zuhrī informed us that Abū Thābit ʿImrān ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd, the freedman of al-Munbaʿith, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf from his father who said: I hunted a bird at al-Qunbulah and went out with it in my hand. My father, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, met me and said: \What is this in your hand?\"" I said: \""A bird I hunted at al-Qunbulah.\"" He twisted my ear severely"," snatched it from my hand"," released it"," and said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has sanctified the game of what lies between its two lava tracts.\"" Abū Muṣʿab said"," meaning the two lava tracts of al-Madīnah. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān. In the narration of al-Muʾammalī"," he said: from his father"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sanctified what lies between its two lava tracts"," meaning al-Madīnah"," and he did not mention the story. [Ṣaḥīḥ in meaning. al-Bazzār 3. No. 1008]"""
"9974","(9970) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik narrated to us from Yūnus ibn Yūsuf from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī that he found some boys who had driven a fox into a corner, so he drove them away from it. Mālik said: \I do not know except that he said: 'Is this done in the sanctuary of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?'\"" He (the narrator) said: And Mālik narrated to us from a man who said: \""Zayd ibn Thābit came to me while I was at al-Aswāf"," and I had hunted a nuhs (a small bird)"," so Zayd took it from my hand and released it.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Būshanjī said: \""The nuhs is a small bird"," larger than a sparrow"," resembling a quail.\"" The man whom Mālik ibn Anas (may Allah have mercy on him and on us) did not name is said to be Sharḥabīl Abū Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it 1578]"""
"9975","(9971) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī informed us that Abū Usāmah narrated to us from al-Walīd who informed me that Sharḥabīl Abū Saʿd informed me that he entered al-Aswāf, a place in al-Madīnah, and hunted a nuhs there, i.e., a bird. Zayd ibn Thābit came upon him while the bird was with him. He twisted my ear and said: \Let it go! May you have no mother! Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has sanctified the game of what lies between its two lava tracts?\"" It has also been narrated in this regard from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," raised to the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ in meaning. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it 36225]"""
"9976","(9972) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAttāb al-ʿAbdī in Baghdād informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq Abū ʿAwf al-Buzūrī informed us that Khālid ibn Makhlad al-Qaṭawānī informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Mukharramī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd that Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) rode to his palace at al-ʿAqīq and found a slave cutting trees. He stripped him (of what he had cut). When he returned, the slave's people came to him asking him to return to them what he had taken from their slave. He said: \I seek refuge in Allah that I should return anything that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has granted me as spoils.\"" So he returned nothing to them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1364]"""
"9977","(9973) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, from Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar — from the progeny of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah — narrated it in a similar manner, except that he said: \He found a boy cutting trees or stripping them"," so he seized his belongings.\"" And at the end of it he said: \""And he refused to return them to them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others."""
"9978","(9974) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Ṣāliḥ, the freed slave of al-Tawʾamah, one of the sons of Saʿd narrated to me, from Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever you find cutting anything from the trees — meaning the trees of the Ḥaram of al-Madīnah — his belongings are yours. Its trees shall not be cut nor lopped.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: \""So Saʿd saw some boys cutting"," and he took their belongings. They went to their masters and informed them that Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) had done such and such. So they came to him and said: 'O Abū Isḥāq"," your boys — or your freed slaves — have taken the belongings of our boys.' He said: 'Rather"," I took it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""Whoever you find cutting from the trees of the Ḥaram"," his belongings are yours.\"" But ask me from my wealth whatever you wish.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Al-Ṭayālī narrated it (218); Abū Dāwūd (2038).]"""
"9979","(9975) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Abī ʿAlī al-Saqqāʾ both informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated from his father, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father, that he used to go out from al-Madīnah and would find a woodcutter with fresh wood that he had cut from some of the trees of al-Madīnah, so he would seize his belongings. He would be spoken to about it, and he would say: \I shall not leave a bounty that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has granted me","\"" and he was among the wealthiest of people.\n\nHis father was Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qurashī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"9980","(9976) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Abū Salamah Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to me, Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm narrated, from Sulaymān ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I saw Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ seize a man who was hunting in the Ḥaram of al-Madīnah"," which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had sanctified"," and he stripped him of his garments. His masters came and spoke to him about it. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sanctified this Ḥaram and said: \""Whoever catches anyone hunting in it"," let him strip him.\"" I will not return to you a provision that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has provided me. But if you wish"," I will pay you its price.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (2037).]"""
"9981","(9977) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Maymūn al-Raqqī narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Makhzūmī narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Insān — al-Ḥumaydī said: \A tribe from the Arabs\"" — narrated from his father"," from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," from his father al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""We came with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Layyah"," intending Makkah"," until when we were at the Sidrah"," at the edge of al-Qarn al-Aswad"," opposite it"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) directed his gaze toward Nakhb"," then he stopped until the people stopped"," then he said: 'Verily"," the hunting of Wajj and its trees — meaning its trees — are sacred and forbidden.' And that was before his descent upon al-Ṭāʾif and the siege of Thaqīf.\""\n\nAḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith"," and he said in it: \""He directed his gaze toward Nakhb\"" — meaning a valley.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (2032).]"""
"9982","(9978) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥafṣ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Khālid — or he said Makhlad — narrated to me, Khārijah ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pasture of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) shall not be lopped nor cut"," but it may be stripped gently.\"" Thus he said.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (2039).]"""
"9983","(9979) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣibghī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād al-Surrī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways said: Khārijah ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me, from his father al-Ḥārith ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Makīth al-Juhnī, then al-Rabʿī, that he asked Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sulamī, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: \We have sheep and boys"," and they strip the fruit of al-Ḥablah for their sheep.\""\n\nKhārijah said: \""It is the fruit of the samurah (acacia) tree.\"" Jābir said: \""No! Then no! The pasture of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) shall not be lopped nor cut. But strip gently.\"" Jābir said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — I think he said — forbade the cutting of al-Masad.\""\n\nJābir said: \""Al-Masad is a stick used for a young she-camel.\"" Ibn Abī Uways said: \""The Ḥimā is around al-Madīnah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"9984","(9980) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḥuddānī narrated, from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, who said: \My grandfather was a freed slave of ʿUthmān ibn Maẓʿūn"," and he tended a piece of land belonging to ʿUthmān in which there were vegetables and cucumbers. He said: \""Sometimes ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) would come to me at midday"," placing his garment over his head"," inspecting the Ḥimā"," ensuring that its trees were neither cut nor lopped. He would sit with me and talk to me"," and I would feed him from the cucumbers and vegetables. One day he said to me: 'I see that you will not leave this place.' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I am appointing you over this place. So whoever you see cutting a tree or lopping"," take his axe and his rope.' I said: 'Shall I take his cloak?' He said: 'No.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ibn al-Jaʿd narrated it (1/48).]"""
"9985","(9981) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation. Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah. Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Khālid al-Khayyāṭ narrated from al-ʿUmarī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) designated al-Naqīʿ as a pasture for the horses.\n\nWe have also narrated that from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it (2/155).]"
"9986","(9982) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us. Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, reciting to him. al-Maʿmarī — meaning al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb — narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm, Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated to us. My father narrated from Wahb, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, that he narrated from Abū Saʿīd, the freed slave of al-Mahrī, that hardship and severity befell them in al-Madīnah. He came to Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and said to him: \I have many dependents"," and hardship has befallen us. I intend to move my family to some of the rural areas.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""Do not do so. Stay in al-Madīnah. We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — I think he said — until we arrived at ʿUsfān.\"" He said: \""He stayed there for some nights. The people said: 'By Allah"," we are not here for anything. Our families are behind us"," and we do not feel safe for them.' This reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'What is this that reaches me of your talk?' I do not know how he said it. He said: 'By Him in Whose Hand is my soul — or by Him in Whose Hand is my soul' — Ḥammād was uncertain which of the two words he said — 'I had intended — or I was about to intend' — I do not know which of the two he said — 'I would command my she-camel to be saddled"," then I would not untie any of its knots until I arrive at al-Madīnah.' And he said: 'O Allah"," Ibrāhīm sanctified Makkah and made it sacred. O Allah"," I sanctify al-Madīnah as sacred"," between its two mountain passes"," that no blood be shed in it"," no weapon be carried in it for fighting"," and no tree be lopped in it except for fodder. O Allah"," bless our city for us. O Allah"," bless our ṣāʿ for us. O Allah"," bless our mudd for us' — three times. 'O Allah"," make with the blessing two blessings.' By Him in Whose Hand is my soul"," there is no ravine or pass of al-Madīnah except that upon it are two angels guarding it until you arrive at it.\""\n\nThen he said to the people: \""Set out.\"" So we set out and headed toward al-Madīnah. By Him by whom oaths are sworn — or by Him by whom oaths are sworn — Ḥammād was uncertain in this word alone — \""We had not set down our saddles when we entered al-Madīnah before Banū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ghaṭfān raided it"," and nothing had incited them to that before.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥammād ibn Ismāʿīl.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim (1374).]"""
"9987","(9983) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Tamtām narrated to us — Hudbah narrated to us — Hammām narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us — Hammām narrated to us — Qatādah narrated from Abū Ḥassān, from ʿAlī, regarding the matter of the Ḥaram of al-Madīnah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Its vegetation shall not be cut"," its game shall not be driven away"," and its lost property shall not be picked up except by one who publicly announces it. It is not permissible for a man to carry weapons in it for the purpose of fighting"," nor is it permissible for a man to cut a tree from it"," except a man who fodder his camel.\"" In the narration of Hudbah: \""a camel.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ by other than him. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (2035).]"""
"9988","(9984) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to me — Abū ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar witnessed the Fatḥ (conquest) when he was twenty years old"," and he had with him a refractory horse and a heavy spear.\"" He said: \""ʿAbd Allāh went to cut grass for his horse"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O ʿAbd Allāh! O ʿAbd Allāh!'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it (2/12).]"""
"9989","(9985) In what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from al-ʿAbbās, from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Shāfiʿī, as a report from Ibn Abī Laylā, that he narrated from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both: \They both disapproved of removing any soil or stones of the Ḥaram to the Ḥill (the non-sacred area).\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Qāsim al-Azrāqī informed us from his father"," from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir"," who said: 'I came to Makkah with my mother' — or he said"," 'my grandmother' — 'and Ṣafīyah bint Shaybah came to her and honored her and did something for her. Ṣafīyah said: \""I do not know how to reward her for it.\"" So she sent her a piece of the Rukn (corner of the Kaʿbah). We left with it and stopped at the first campsite"," and he mentioned their illness and ailment altogether.' He said: 'My mother — or my grandmother — said: \""It seems to us that nothing has afflicted us except that we removed this piece from the Ḥaram.\"" She said to me"," and I was the most like them: \""Take this piece to Ṣafīyah and return it to her"," and say to her: 'Allah has placed something in His Ḥaram"," and it is not befitting that it be removed from it.'\"" ʿAbd al-Aʿlā said: \""They said to me: 'It was only a short time before we were waiting for you to enter the Ḥaram"," as if we had been released from our tethers.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"9990","(9986) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us — Muṭayyin narrated to us — Sufyān ibn Bishr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Muʾammal al-Makhzūmī, from Ibn Muḥayṣin, from ʬāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted Suhayl ibn ʿAmr as a gift from the water of Zamzam.\""\n\nAnd it was also reported in that regard from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās.\n\n[Ḥasan. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Awsaṭ (5796).]"""
"9991","(9987) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — they both said: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Shaybān al-Baghdādī in Harāt informed us — Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us — Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us — Abū al-Zubayr said: \We were with Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," conversing"," when the time for the ʿAṣr prayer arrived. He stood and prayed with us"," wearing a single garment wrapped around him"," while his cloak was placed aside. Then water from Zamzam was brought to him"," and he drank"," and drank again. They said: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is the water of Zamzam","' regarding which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The water of Zamzam is for whatever purpose it is drunk.'\"" He said: \""Then the Prophet ﷺ"," while he was in al-Madīnah before the conquest of Makkah"," sent word to Suhayl ibn ʿAmr: 'Send us some water of Zamzam"," and do not leave any behind.' So he sent two water-skins.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Al-Ḥāfiẓ said in al-Talkhīṣ (2/268).]"""
"9992","(9988) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī narrated to us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to me — Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ Abū Kurayb narrated to me, and I asked him — Khallād ibn Yazīd al-Juʿfī narrated to me — Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Juʿfī narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that ʿĀʾishah used to carry the water of Zamzam and would narrate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do so. And another narrator narrated it from Abū Kurayb and added: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried it in water-skins and leather containers"," and he would pour it upon the sick and give them to drink.\"" Al-Bukhārī said: \""Khallād ibn Yazīd was not followed up in this.\""\n\n[Ḥasan by other than him. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (963). Abū Yaʿlā (4683).]"""
"9993","(9989) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us — Ādam narrated to us — Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding the Most High's words {that which may be reached by your hands and your lances} (al-Māʾidah: 94): \He means arrows"," and 'that which may be reached by your hands' also means small game — young birds and eggs. 'And your lances' means large game.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī. Al-Ṭabarī narrated it in his Tafsīr (5/37).]"""
"9994","(9990) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — they both narrated: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb said — I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd saying — I heard my father saying — ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to me, who said: \I asked al-Awzāʿī about a man who set his dog upon game in the Ḥill"," and the game entered the Ḥaram"," and the dog sought it and brought it out into the Ḥill and killed it. He said: 'I have nothing to say regarding it"," but I dislike burdening oneself.' I said: 'O Abā ʿAmr"," give a ruling on it.' He said: 'I would not like to eat it"," nor do I see any sin in one who does so.'\""\n\nʿAbd al-Salām said: \""The Ḥajj became easy for me that year"," so I met Ibn Jurayj and asked him about it. He said: 'I heard ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās"," that he was asked about it"," and he said: \""I would not like to eat it"," nor do I see any sin in one who does so.\""\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And this is what al-Shāfiʿī said regarding the one who sends his dog after game from the Ḥill into the Ḥill"," and the game takes refuge and enters the Ḥaram"," and the dog kills it therein — it does not suffice as a penalty"," nor may it be eaten. And he distinguished between the dog and the arrow: if it strikes it or other than it in the Ḥaram"," it is permissible.\""\n\n[Ḥasan.]"""
"9995","(9991) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to us — Abū al-Tayyāḥ said: \I heard Anas ibn Mālik saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mingle with us to the point that he would say to my young brother: \""O Abā ʿUmayr"," what has the little bird done?\""' — meaning his bird.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī (5778).]"""
"9996","(9992) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated from Abū al-Tayyāḥ, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the finest of all people in character. I had a brother who was called Abū ʿUmayr — I think he was an infant. When he would come"," he would say: 'O Abā ʿUmayr"," what has the little bird done?' He used to play with it. And sometimes the prayer would come while he was in our house"," and he would order the carpet beneath it to be swept and sprinkled with water"," then he would stand"," and we would stand behind him"," and he would pray with us.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ and others from ʿAbd al-Wārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī (5850).]"""
"9997","(9993) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, reported to us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to me from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: There was a son of Umm Sulaym whose name was Abū ʿUmayr. The Prophet ﷺ used to jest with him when he visited Umm Sulaym. One day he came and found him grieving, so he said: \Why is Abū ʿUmayr sad?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," his little finch that he used to play with has died.\"" The Prophet ﷺ began to say: \""O Abū ʿUmayr"," what did the little finch do?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""
"9998","(9994) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān reported to us in Baghdad, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr; both said: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us. He said: I heard Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrating in the house of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from ʿAṭāʾ, that ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, was given a bird or a gazelle as a gift within the Ḥaram, so she set it free. Hishām said that day: \Ibn Abī Rabbāḥ does not know that the Commander of the Faithful"," meaning ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr"," remained in Makkah for nine years"," and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come and see quails and partridges in cages.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"9999","(9995) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik reported to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Quraish from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, that a man came to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: \My companion and I raced our horses to the pass of al-Thaniyyah"," and we caught a gazelle while we were both in the state of iḥrām. What do you think?\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to a man beside him: \""Come"," let us both judge.\"" So they judged that he owed a she-goat. And he mentioned in the hadith that ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""That was ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Previously cited under no. 9857.]"""
"10000","(9996) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, Abū Bishr, narrated to us: Abū Shaybah Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zubaydī narrated to us: Mujāhid narrated, saying: A group of people from Iraq came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: \We drove a hyena and chased it among ourselves until we caught it"," and among us were those who were in the state of iḥrām and those who were not.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""If it was a male hyena"," then a fat ram; and if it was a female hyena"," then a fat ewe.\"" They said: \""O Abū al-ʿAbbās"," upon each one of us?\"" He said: \""No"," but share it among yourselves.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"10001","(9997) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from ʿAmmār, the mawlā of Banī Hāshim, that the mawlās of Ibn al-Zubayr entered the state of iḥrām when a hyena passed by them. They struck it with their staffs and caught it. Doubt arose in their hearts, so they came to Ibn ʿUmar and mentioned that to him. He said: \Upon you is a ram.\"" They said: \""Upon each one of us a ram?\"" He said: \""You have made it severe upon yourselves; upon every one of you is a ram.\"" ʿAlī said: The linguists said: \""La-muʿazzaz bikum\"" means \""la-mushaddad bikum\"" (i.e."," made severe upon you). It was also narrated by ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Ḥammād from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār from Rabbāḥ from Ibn ʿUmar"," as a connected narration. [Ḍaʿīf. Cited by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/250.]"""
"10002","(9998) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik ibn Anas and others informed me that Nāfiʿ narrated to them from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people at ʿArafah, teaching them the matters of the Ḥajj. Among what he said to them was: \When you come to Minā"," whoever has stoned the jamrah"," that which was forbidden to him has become permissible"," except women and perfume. No one should touch women or perfume until he has performed ṭawāf of the House.\"" Mālik said: And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to me from Ibn ʿUmar"," who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Whoever has stoned the jamrah"," then shaved or shortened his hair"," and sacrificed a hady if he had one with him"," that which was forbidden to him has become permissible"," except women and perfume"," until he performs ṭawāf of the House.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Cited by Mālik"," 922.]"""
"10003","(9999) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammādābādhī narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dawrī narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ḥafarī narrated to us from Sufyān from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from al-Ḥasan, meaning al-ʿUranī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When you have stoned the jamrah"," everything has become permissible for you except women"," until you perform ṭawāf of the House.\"" A man said to him: \""May he apply perfume?\"" He said: \""As for me"," I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ anointing his head with musk—or he said"," with sukk. Is that perfume or not?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Previously cited under no. 9596.]"""
"10004","(10000) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Ḥibbān ibn Hilāl narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us: Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \If one has slaughtered"," shaved"," and then caught game before visiting the House"," then upon him is its penalty"," so long as anything of his iḥrām remains upon him.\"" Allah"," the Most High"," said: {And when you have exited iḥrām"," then you may hunt.} [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10005","(10001) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from his father, from the fuqahāʾ of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \Whoever catches game after having stoned the jamrah but before performing the ṭawāf of ifāḍah"," upon him is its penalty.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10006","(10002) Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Ḥusayn from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kathīr al-Dārī from Ṭalḥah ibn Abī Ḥafṣah from Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥārith, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, came to Makkah and entered the Dār al-Nadwah on a Friday, intending to stay near it so as to be close to the mosque. He threw his cloak over a pillar in the House, and a bird from among the pigeons alighted upon it. He drove it away, and it landed upon another pillar. A snake struck it and killed it. After he had prayed Jumuʿah, I and ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān entered upon him, and he said: \Judge between me concerning something I did today. I entered this house intending to stay near it to be close to the mosque. I threw my cloak upon this pillar"," and a pigeon alighted upon it. I feared it would soil it with its droppings"," so I drove it away. It landed upon this other pillar"," and a snake struck it and killed it. I felt in my soul that I had driven it from a place of safety to a place where its death awaited it.\"" I said to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him: \""What do you think? Shall we judge against the Commander of the Faithful with a two-year-old she-goat of ʿAfraʾ?\"" He said: \""I think so.\"" And ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," ordered it to be done. [Ḍaʿīf. Cited by al-Shāfiʿī"," 644.]"""
"10007","(10003) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us in the book *Mukhtaṣar al-Ḥajj*: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he ruled regarding a pigeon from the pigeons of Makkah with a sheep. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10008","(10004) And Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī al-Kūfī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he assigned for the pigeons of the Ḥaram, upon the muḥrim and the ḥalāl alike, a sheep for every pigeon. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10009","(10005) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ: that ʿUthmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ḥumayd's son killed a pigeon, so he came to Ibn ʿAbbās and mentioned that to him. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Slaughter a sheep and give it in charity.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: \""Was it from the pigeons of Makkah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ibn Jurayj"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said regarding a pigeon: \""A sheep"," from which nothing is to be eaten; it is to be given in charity.\""\n\nAnd from Ibn Abī Laylā"," from ʿAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," regarding the *khuḍrī*"," the *dubsī*"," the *qumrī*"," the *qaṭāṭ*"," and the *ḥajal*: a sheep"," a sheep (i.e."," each carries the expiation of one sheep). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 645]"""
"10010","(10006) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn Mahdī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Shuʿbah, from a man—I think it was Abū Bishr—from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, from Ibn ʿUmar, regarding a man who closed his door upon a pigeon and its two chicks—meaning he returned and they had died. Ibn ʿUmar imposed upon him three sheep from the flock. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 8273]"
"10011","(10007) And in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh permitted me to narrate from him, from Abī al-Walīd al-Faqīh: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Abī Bishr, from ʿAṭāʾ, Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, and Manṣūr, from ʿAṭāʾ: that a man closed his door upon a pigeon and its two chicks, then departed for ʿArafāt and Minā. When he returned, they had died. He came to Ibn ʿUmar and mentioned that to him, so he imposed upon him three sheep, and a man ruled alongside him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10012","(10008) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say regarding the pigeons of Makkah when one is killed: \A sheep.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10013","(10009) The Shaykh, Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī, informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Sharīk narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm, from ʿAṭāʾ, regarding large birds: \A sheep—the *kurkī*"," the *ḥubārī*"," the *wazz*"," and the like.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 2257]"""
"10014","(10010) And Abū al-Ḥasan, Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh, informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyinī informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah informed me: ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Whatever is other than the pigeons of the Ḥaram"," then for it is its price"," if the muḥrim kills it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10015","(10011) Abū Bakr, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī ʿAmmār informed him: that he arrived with Muʿādh ibn Jabal and Kaʿb al-Aḥbār along with a group of muḥrim people from Bayt al-Maqdis for ʿUmrah. When we were along part of the road, and Kaʿb was by a fire warming himself, a swarm of locusts passed by him. He took two locusts, killed them, and forgot his iḥrām. Then he remembered his iḥrām and cast them away. When we arrived in al-Madīnah, the people entered upon ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), and I entered with them. Kaʿb recounted the story of the two locusts to ʿUmar. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Who was that with? Perhaps it was you"," O Kaʿb?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the people of Ḥimyar love locusts. What did you assess for yourself?\"" He said: \""Two dirhams.\"" He said: \""Well done! Two dirhams are better than a hundred locusts. Do what you have assessed for yourself.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 646]"""
"10016","(10012) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me. He said: I heard al-Qāsim, meaning Ibn Muḥammad, say: \I was sitting with Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) when a man asked him about a locust he had killed while in iḥrām. Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'For it is a handful of food. And you shall certainly take a handful of locusts—but no (i.e."," do not do that).'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: His statement \""you shall certainly take a handful of locusts\"" means that only the monetary value is due. And his statement \""but no\"" means: \""You should exercise caution and pay more than what is incumbent upon you"," after I have informed you that it is more than what is incumbent upon you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 649]"""
"10017","(10013) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard ʿAṭāʾ say: Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about hunting locusts within the Ḥaram, and he said: \No","\"" and he prohibited it. He (the narrator) said: \""Either I said to him"," or a man from the people said: 'Your people take them while they are sitting huddled in the mosque.'\"" He replied: \""They do not know.\""\n[Sound. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 647]"""
"10018","(10014) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, the same (hadith), except that he said: \Munḥanūn\"" (bent over). Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""And Muslim is more correct of the two; the ḥuffāẓ narrated from Ibn Jurayj: 'Munḥanūn.'\"""""
"10019","(10015) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated to us from Maymūn ibn Jābir from Abū Rāfiʿ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The locust is from the game of the sea.\""\n[Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1853]"""
"10020","(10016) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us from Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim, from Abū al-Muhazzim, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \We came upon a swarm of locusts"," and a man was striking them with his whip while he was in iḥrām. It was said to him: 'This is not permissible.' That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he said: 'It is only from the game of the sea.'\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it from Musaddad. And with its meaning"," Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Abū al-Muhazzim.\nAbū al-Muhazzim is Yazīd ibn Sufyān"," who is weak (ḍaʿīf)"," and Maymūn ibn Jābir is not well known (ghayr maʿrūf). And Allah knows best.\nAnd it has been said that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Maymūn"," from Abū Rāfiʿ"," from Kaʿb"," as his (Kaʿb's) own statement. [Very weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1854]"""
"10021","(10017) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dimashqī narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: \The best I heard concerning the eggs of the ostrich is the ḥadīth of Abū al-Zinād"," from al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'For every egg (broken by one in iḥrām)"," there is (the expiation of) fasting a day or feeding a poor person.'\""\nAnd similarly"," Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ"," and others narrated it from al-Walīd ibn Muslim"," from Ibn Jurayj"," from Abū al-Zinād"," from al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/249]"""
"10022","(10018) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Abū Qurrah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj; Ziyād ibn Saʿd informed me, from Abū al-Zinād, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding the eggs of an ostrich broken by a man in iḥrām: fasting a day for every egg.\nThe Shaykh said: This is how Abū Qurrah — Mūsā ibn Ṭāriq — narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. And Abū ʿĀṣim, Hishām ibn Sulaymān, and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rāwād narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyād ibn Saʿd, from Abū al-Zinād, from a man, from ʿĀʾishah, and this is the correct version, as stated by Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī and other ḥuffāẓ. And it has been narrated through another chain as well. [Weak. See the preceding]"
"10023","(10019) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl al-Ṣayrafī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah; Maṭar al-Warrāq narrated to them that Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to them from a man among the Anṣār: that a man in iḥrām caused his mount to trample upon ostrich eggs. The man went to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him about that. ʿAlī said: \Upon you"," for every egg"," is a young she-camel or the foetus of a she-camel.\"" The man went to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what ʿAlī had said. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \""ʿAlī has said what you heard. But come to the concession: for every egg"," fasting a day or feeding a poor person.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 5/58]"""
"10024","(10020) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, saying: Saʿīd was asked about the eggs of an ostrich obtained by one in iḥrām, and he informed us from Maṭar, who mentioned it with its meaning. This is the preserved (version).\nAnd it has been narrated in this regard from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī, and it has been narrated through another chain. [Weak. See the preceding]"
"10025","(10021) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī — and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh — informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjarah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding ostrich eggs obtained by one in iḥrām: (the expiation is) according to their price.\nAnd Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated it from Ibrāhīm, and he said: \According to their value (qīmatihā).\""\nAnd that was narrated from Abū al-Muhazzim"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. And it has been narrated in this regard from a group of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them all). [Denounced (munkar). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/247]"""
"10026","(10022) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī — informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr, from Qatādah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said regarding the egg of an ostrich obtained by one in iḥrām: \Fasting a day or feeding a poor person.\""\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 636]"""
"10027","(10023) And with its isnad, he said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr, from Qatādah, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, a similar narration."
"10028","(10024) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, Abū Khaythamah narrated to us, Khuṣayf narrated, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh, regarding the egg of the ostrich that a muḥrim obtains: he said, its compensation is its price, or he said, its value. [Weak]"
"10029","(10025) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us, Abū Usāmah narrated, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he assigned for every two eggs of the pigeons of the Ḥaram one dirham.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from Saʿīd, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, as his own statement. Then he said: I think ʿAṭāʾ intended by his statement this value at the time he said it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10030","(10026) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, he said: al-Shāfiʿī said, on the authority of Hushaym, from Manṣūr, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿAlī, regarding one who obtains the egg of an ostrich: he said, he should slaughter camels equivalent in number to them. It was said to him: What if one of the camels escapes? He said: For some eggs may be cracked.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Neither we nor them—meaning the Iraqis—nor anyone we know of holds this view. He says: he must pay its price. Al-Shāfiʿī said in the Kitāb al-Manāsik: they narrated this from ʿAlī via a chain that the scholars of ḥadīth do not consider reliable, and for that reason we abandoned it, because when something becomes obligatory upon a person, it is not discharged by something uncertain—it may or may not exist—rather it is discharged only by something definite and established.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: In what he cited, there is no evidence that al-Ḥasan heard directly from ʿAlī, and the ḥadīth of Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). It has also been narrated therein that this occurred during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and that the Prophet ﷺ referred his questioner to fasting one day or feeding a poor person. [Weak. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm, 7/25]"
"10031","(10027) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan the Qāḍī informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb narrated, from al-Taymī, from Abī Mijlaz, from Ibn ʿAbbās (regarding \the game of the sea and its food\""): he said: its food is what the sea casts out. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10032","(10028) Abū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Bakr informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Rūḥ narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: What is your opinion regarding the game of rivers and the pools of floodwater—is it the game of the sea? He said: Yes. Then he recited to me: \This is fresh"," sweet"," pleasant to drink"," and this is salty"," bitter; and from each you eat tender meat\"" [Sūrat Fāṭir: 12]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 8422]"""
"10033","(10029) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf the Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: ʿAṭāʾ was asked about the pond of al-Qasr. He said: It is a great pond within the Ḥaram—may game be hunted from it? He said: Yes, and I wish we had some of it with us now. [Weak]"
"10034","(10030) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Muʿādh narrated to us, al-Ashʿath narrated, from al-Ḥasan: that he saw no harm in a muḥrim slaughtering that which, if left alone, would not fly, such as the duck and the hen, and he disliked that he slaughter that which, if left alone, would fly, such as the pigeon and the like. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10035","(10031) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Abū Ṭāhir Sahl ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Farrukhān al-Zāhid narrated to us, Ḥarmalah narrated, Ibn Wahb informed us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, he said: I heard ʿUbaydullāh ibn Miqsam say: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad say: I heard ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, say: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: There are four creatures, all of them vermin, that may be killed in the Ḥill and the Ḥaram: the kite, the crow, the mouse, and the rabid dog.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd and others, from Ibn Wahb, and he added: I said to al-Qāsim: What about the snake? He said: It should be killed even when small. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1198]"
"10036","(10032) The Qāḍī Abū al-Haytham ʿUtbah ibn Khaythamah and Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five creatures are all vermin and may be killed within the Ḥaram: the crow, the kite, the rabid dog, the scorpion, and the mouse.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān, and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah, all of them from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 1732]"
"10037","(10033) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak, may Allah have mercy upon him — informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Five are the harmful creatures that may be killed in the Ḥill and the Ḥaram: the mouse"," the scorpion"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," the rabid dog"," and the piebald crow (al-ghurāb al-abqaʿ).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar"," from Shuʿbah"," and he said: \""The snake (al-ḥayyah) instead of the scorpion","\"" as though Shuʿbah was doubtful about that.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1198]"""
"10038","(10034) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: Abū ʿĀmir informed us: Shuʿbah narrated it with his chain, except that he said: \Five that may be killed in the Ḥill and the Ḥaram: the snake or the scorpion.\"" Then he mentioned the rest. It is as though the narration of Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī is more authentic"," due to its agreement with the other narrations from ʿĀʾishah and Ibn al-Musayyab. The ḥadīth regarding the snake and the wolf was narrated as a mursal (disconnected narration)"," and that will be addressed"," if Allah wills.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"10039","(10035) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us among the last [narrators], they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, he said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Five creatures — there is no sin upon the one in iḥrām for killing them: the crow"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," the scorpion"," the mouse"," and the rabid dog.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1730]"""
"10040","(10036) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \What creatures may the one in iḥrām kill?\"" He said: \""The mouse"," the scorpion"," the crow"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," and the rabid dog.\"" I said to Nāfiʿ: \""The snake?\"" He said: \""The snake — there is no disagreement about it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kāmil"," from Ḥammād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1198]"""
"10041","(10037) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us: Abū Saʿīd — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād — informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Five creatures — there is no sin upon the one who kills them in the Ḥill and the Ḥaram: the crow"," the mouse"," the rabid dog"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," and the scorpion.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and Ibn Abī ʿUmar"," from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1199]"""
"10042","(10038) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Aṣbaḥ ibn al-Faraj informed me: Ibn Wahb informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shaybānī informed us: Tamīm ibn Muḥammad informed us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus informed me from al-Zuhrī: Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: Ḥafṣah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Five creatures — all of them are harmful (fawāsiq) — there is no sin upon the one who kills them: the scorpion"," the crow"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," the mouse"," and the rabid dog.\"" The wording is that of Ḥarmalah's narration. And in the narration of Aṣbaḥ"," he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Five creatures — there is no harm upon the one who kills them.\"" Then he mentioned them.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aṣbaḥ"," and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1731]"""
"10043","(10039) Abū al-Ḥusayn — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān — informed us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — informed us: Hāshim ibn Yūnus informed us: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿAlī ibn Baḥr informed us: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl informed me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abī Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Five — killing them is permissible in the Ḥaram: the snake"," the scorpion"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," the mouse"," and the rabid dog.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Without his statement"," and the wolf.]"""
"10044","(10040) Abū Naṣr — ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — and Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī — both of them informed us, reading over them in Khusrawjird: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿm, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one in iḥrām may kill the snake and the scorpion"," and he may pelt the crow but not kill it"," and he may kill the rabid dog"," the mouse (al-fuwaysiqah)"," the kite (ḥidāʾah)"," and the predatory beast (al-sabuʿ al-ʿādī).\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in Kitāb al-Sīrah from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," from Hushaym"," who said: Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1848]"""
"10045","(10041) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — informed us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyādah informed us, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Empty]"
"10046","(10042) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — informed us: Mālik ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Wabarah, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of the wolf"," the mouse"," and the kite (ḥidāʾah).\"" It was said to him: \""And the snake and the scorpion?\"" He said: \""That used to be said.\"" Yazīd ibn Hārūn said"," meaning the one in iḥrām. Al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a ḥujjah (as a basis for evidence).\n\nAnd we have narrated it as a good mursal ḥadīth from Ibn al-Musayyab.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad 2/22]"""
"10047","(10043) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Yahya ibn Ayyub, Yazid ibn Iyyad, and Hafs ibn Mayasara informed me — that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah al-Aslami informed them from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The muhrim (one in the state of ihram) may kill the snake and the wolf.\"" [Da'if. Reported by 'Abd al-Razzaq (8384)]"""
"10048","(10044) He said, and Ibn Wahb informed me — Ibn Jurayj informed me — from Abu al-Zubayr — from Mujahid — from Abu 'Ubaydah — from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the like of it regarding the snake."
"10049","(10045) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Ahmad ibn Sahl informed us — Dawud ibn Rushayd informed us — Hafs ibn Ghayyath informed us — al-A'mash informed us — from Ibrahim — from al-Aswad — from 'Abd Allah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina when a snake leapt upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Kill it.\"" We rushed toward it"," but it outran us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: \""It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in their Sahihs from 'Umar ibn Hafs from his father. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari (1733)]"""
"10050","(10046) Abu Kurayb narrated from Hafs ibn Ghayyath with this isnad, in abridged form: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a muhrim to kill a snake at Mina.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed him — Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — Abu Kurayb informed us.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb. [Sahih. Muslim (2235)]"
"10051","(10047) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq informed us — Ibn Abi Uways informed us — from Malik — from Ibn Shihab — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from 'A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The gecko (wazagh) is a fawasiq (harmful creature).\"" And I did not hear him command that it be killed.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways"," and Muslim reported it from the hadith of Yunus from Ibn Shihab"," though others besides him heard him commanding its killing. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari (1734)]"""
"10052","(10048) Hilal ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us — al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn 'Ayyash al-Qattan informed us — Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — (h) and Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us — Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar informed us — from al-Zuhri — from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas — from his father who said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of the gecko and named it a fawasiq. The wording of both is the same.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih. Muslim (2238)]"
"10053","(10049) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Tusi informed us — Abu Hatim al-Razi informed us — 'Ubayd Allah, he being the son of Musa, informed us — Ibn Jurayj informed us — from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr ibn Shaybah — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib — from Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of geckos (awzagh).\n\nAl-Bukhari extracted it from the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah, and Muslim reported it from various routes from Ibn Jurayj. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari (3180)]"
"10054","(10050) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh informed us — Bishr ibn Musa informed us — al-Humaydi informed us — Sufyan said: I heard Zayd ibn Aslam saying, \And what dog is more biting (a'qar) than the snake?\"" Al-Humaydi said: \""Everything that bites you is al-'aqur (the biting creature).\"" [Sahih]"""
"10055","(10051) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us — Ibn Bukayr said: Malik said: \The dog that is al-'aqur (vicious biter)"," which the muhrim is commanded to kill"," is everything that bites people"," attacks them"," and frightens them — such as the lion"," the leopard"," the cheetah"," and the wolf — that is the 'vicious dog' (al-kalb al-'aqur).\"" [Hasan]"""
"10056","(10052) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us — Abu 'Ubayd said regarding His statement, \and the vicious dog (al-kalb al-'aqur)\"": I was informed from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah that he said: \""Its meaning is every predatory animal that bites (ya'qir)"," and it is not restricted specifically to the dog.\""\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: \""It is permissible in speech to refer to a predatory beast as a 'dog' (kalb). Do you not see that they narrate in the military campaigns (maghazi) that 'Utaybah ibn Abi Lahb was severely harmful to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he said: 'O Allah"," set against him one of your dogs.' So 'Utaybah went out to the Sham with his companions and stopped at a lodging"," and a lion came upon them and singled him out from among his companions and killed him. Thus"," the lion here has been designated by the name 'dog.' This is also the meaning of the Most High's statement: {And those of the hunting animals which you have trained as taught by Allah} [Al-Ma'idah: 4] — for this is a name derived from 'dog' (kalb)"," and then the hunting of the cheetah"," the falcon"," and the hawk entered into it. Therefore"," every predatory animal that wounds or bites is called a 'vicious dog' (kalb 'aqur).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: \""We were commanded by 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," to kill the snake"," the scorpion"," the mouse"," and the hornet while we were in the state of ihram.\"" [Sahih]"""
"10057","(10053) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān said: \The first time I saw al-Zuhrī"," I came to him while he was narrating to the people. I heard him saying: Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me from his father"," that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was asked about the snake (al-ḥayyah) that the muḥrim kills. He said: 'It is an enemy"," so kill it wherever you find it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Fasawī narrated it in al-Maʿrifah 1/355.]"""
"10058","(10054) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burhān informed us in Baghdad — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, and they mentioned to him the statement of Ibrāhīm regarding the snake: \There is a penalty (jazāʾ) when the muḥrim kills it.\"" Ḥammād said: \""There was no man in Kūfah more audacious in rejecting the āthār than Ibrāhīm"," and that was due to the paucity of what he had heard from the ḥadīth of the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him. And there was no man in Kūfah more excellent in following and emulating than al-Shaʿbī"," and that was due to the abundance of what he had heard.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"10059","(10055) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Mālik al-Mālinī informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb, meaning al-Dīnawarī, narrated to us — ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Hārūn al-Firyābī said: \I heard al-Shāfiʿī"," Muḥammad ibn Idrīs"," in Makkah saying: 'Ask me whatever you wish"," and I shall answer you from the Book of Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," and from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him.'\"" He said: \""So I said to him: 'May Allah set you right — what do you say regarding a muḥrim who kills a hornet (zunbūr)?' He said: 'Yes"," in the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful.' Allah"," the Most High"," says: *'Whatever the Messenger gives you"," take it; and whatever he forbids you"," abstain from it'* (al-Ḥashr 7).\"" [Ḥasan. Ibn ʿAsākir narrated it in his Tārīkh 51/272.]"""
"10060","(10056) Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from Ribʿī, from Ḥudhayfah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'Follow the two after me: Abū Bakr and ʿUmar.'\"" [Ḥasan. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (3662).]"""
"10061","(10057) And Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Misʿar, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him: \That he commanded the muḥrim to kill the hornet (al-zunbūr).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"10062","(10058) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us from Mālik, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Hudayr: \That he saw ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," removing ticks (qirād) from his camel in mud at al-Suqyā"," while he was in iḥrām.\"" Thus he narrated it in the dictation (imlāʾ) and in the abridged version of al-Ḥajj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it (1680).]"""
"10063","(10059) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us in the book *Ikhtilāf Mālik wa al-Shāfiʿī* — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī, from Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbdullāh: \That he saw ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," removing ticks from his camel in mud at al-Suqyā.\"" And thus Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr and others narrated it from Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ"," adding: \""While he was in iḥrām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it (793).]"""
"10064","(10060) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed him — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī, from Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Hudayr: \That he saw ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," removing ticks from his camel in the mud at al-Suqyā"," while he was in iḥrām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"10065","(10061) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abī ʿUbayd — Hushaym narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās: \He said to ʿIkrimah: 'Stand and remove the ticks from this camel.' He said: 'I am in iḥrām.' He said: 'Stand and slaughter it.' So he slaughtered it. Then Ibn ʿAbbās said to him: 'How many ticks (qurād)"," lice (ḥalamah)"," and large lice (ḥamnānah) do you think you have killed now?'\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""Al-Aṣmaʿī said: The smallest of ticks is called qumqāmah; when it grows larger"," it is called ḥamnānah; and when it becomes very large"," it is called ḥalamah.\""\n\nHe said: \""What is intended by this is that Ibn ʿAbbās saw no harm in the muḥrim removing ticks from his camel. And al-taqrīd is the removal of ticks from the camel with mud or by hand.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it (8406).]"""
"10066","(10062) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \The muḥrim does not offer expiation (fidāʾ) for game except for that whose flesh is eaten.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Umm 2/320.]"""
"10067","(10063) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, who said: I was sitting with Ibn ʿAbbās when a man came to him whose hair I had never seen longer on anyone. He said: \I have entered iḥrām and this hair is upon me.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Cover up that which is below the ears of it.\"" He said: \""I kissed a woman who is not my wife.\"" He said: \""That is the zinā of your mouth.\"" He said: \""I saw a louse and I threw it away.\"" He said: \""That is the lost thing which is not to be sought.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 13691]"""
"10068","(10064) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: ʿUyaynah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jawshan narrated from his father, who said: A man said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \May I scratch my head while I am in iḥrām?\"" He said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās put his hand into his own hair while he was in iḥrām and scratched his head vigorously"," and said: 'As for me"," I do this.'\"" He said: \""What if I kill a louse?\"" He said: \""That is far removed! The louse does not relieve the itching of your head"," and it is not what I intended. You have only been forbidden from killing game.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 14950]"""
"10069","(10065) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ḥassān ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, that a man came to him and said: \I killed a louse while I was in iḥrām.\"" Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""That is the lightest of killings.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10070","(10066) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ, the mawlā of Ibn ʿUmar, from his father, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he would use the siwāk while fasting and would look in the mirror while in iḥrām. He said: \The muḥrim may scratch his head so long as he does not kill a creature or scratch the skin of his head so that it bleeds.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10071","(10067) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥurr ibn al-Ṣayyāḥ, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say regarding the louse that the muḥrim kills: \He should give in charity a morsel or a handful of food.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 570]"""
"10072","(10068) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that an ant bit one of the Prophets, so he ordered the village of the ants to be burned. Allah then revealed to him: \Was it not enough that a single ant bit you"," that you destroyed a nation among the nations that glorify Allah?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb. Al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Yūnus"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 2856]"""
"10073","(10069) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A Prophet from among the Prophets rested beneath a tree"," and an ant stung him. He ordered his belongings to be removed from beneath it"," and then ordered it to be burned in the fire. Allah then revealed to him: 'Why not a single ant?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 2241]"""
"10074","(10070) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the killing of four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 5267]"
"10075","(10071) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Miṣrī, narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Mālik narrated — and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated — from Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman was punished regarding a cat which she confined until it died of hunger"," and she entered the Fire.\"" He said — and Allah knows best — \""She neither fed it nor gave it water when she confined it"," nor did she set it free so that it could eat from the vermin of the earth.\""\n\nIn the narration of Ibn Wahb: \""She entered the Fire.\"" And it was said to her — and Allah knows best — \""You neither fed it nor gave it water when you confined it"," nor did you set it free so that it could eat from the vermin of the earth until it died of hunger.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 2236]"""
"10076","(10072) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī in Ahwāz narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Thābit narrated from Misʿar, from Ziyād ibn ʿAlāqah, from his uncle Quṭbah, and from Ziyād ibn Fiyāḍ, from Abū ʿIyāḍ, that both of them said: It was disliked for a man to kill that which does not harm him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10077","(10073) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us — Muṭayyin narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Ḥasan ibn Thābit and his father narrated to us — from Misʿar — from Ziyād ibn ʿIlāqah — from his paternal uncle, who said: It was disliked that a man should kill that which does not harm him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10078","(10074) And Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us — Warqāʾ narrated to us — from Ibn Abī Najīḥ — from Mujāhid — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylá narrated to us — from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him with lice falling upon his face and said to him: \Do your vermin harm you?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he ﷺ ordered him to shave his head. He (the narrator) said: They were at al-Ḥudaybiyah"," and it had not been made clear to them that they would exit iḥrām thereby"," and they still harboured hope of entering Makkah. So Allah revealed the expiation (fidyah)"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to give a ṣāʿ (or a farq) of food to six poor persons"," or to fast three days"," or to slaughter a sheep.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf"," from Warqāʾ"," and Muslim recorded it through another chain from Ibn Abī Najīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1720]"""
"10079","(10075) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik — from Nāfiʿ — that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar went out during the trial (fitnah) intending ʿumrah, and he said: \If I am prevented from the House"," we shall do as we did with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" So he went out"," entered iḥrām for ʿumrah"," and proceeded until"," when he appeared atop al-Baydāʾ"," he turned to his companions and said: \""The matter of the two (ḥajj and ʿumrah) is but one. I bear witness to you that I have made ḥajj obligatory along with my ʿumrah.\"" Then he continued until"," when he came to the House"," he performed ṭawāf around it seven times"," and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah seven times"," and did not add anything upon that"," considering it sufficient for him"," and he offered a sacrifice.\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá. In the narration of Ibn Bukayr"," he entered iḥrām for ʿumrah because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had entered iḥrām for ʿumrah in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyah"," and the remainder carries the same meaning.\n\nImām al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""If I am prevented from the House"," we shall do as we did with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ\"" — meaning: We shall exit iḥrām as we exited iḥrām with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it through various chains from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1712]"""
"10080","(10076) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me — my father narrated to me — ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated — from Maʿmar — al-Zuhrī said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me — from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam, each one's ḥadīth corroborating that of his companion, who both said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out at the time of al-Ḥudaybiyah with some one hundred and forty of his companions, until when they were at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded his sacrificial animal, marked it, and entered iḥrām for ʿumrah. He mentioned the ḥadīth in full regarding his descent at the farthest part of al-Ḥudaybiyah, and then regarding the coming of Suhayl ibn ʿAmr and what he settled with him when they were turned away from the House. He said: When he had finished the drafting of the treaty, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \Rise"," offer your sacrifices"," and then shave your heads.\"" He said: By Allah"," not a single man among them stood up"," even after he said that three times. When none of them stood up"," he rose and went to Umm Salamah and mentioned to her the difficulty he had experienced with the people. Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," would you like that? Go out and do not speak a word to any of them until you have sacrificed your animal and called your barber to shave your head.\"" So he rose and went out and did not speak to any of them until he had done that — he sacrificed his animal and called his barber"," who shaved his head. When they saw that"," they rose and began to sacrifice"," and some began shaving the heads of others"," and they nearly killed one another out of grief.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3945]"""
"10081","(10077) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us — from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Al-Zuhrī narrated to me — from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr — from Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, and he mentioned the ḥadīth in full. He added regarding his descent at al-Ḥudaybiyah that they were distressed in the ḥill (state of non-iḥrām) and that they used to pray within the Ḥaram. And he added in the statement of Umm Salamah, that she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," do not rebuke them"," for a great matter has befallen them — what they saw of you having accepted the settlement and your return"," and that victory was not granted to you. Go out"," O Messenger of Allah"," and do not speak to anyone among the people until you come to your sacrificial animal"," sacrifice it"," and exit your iḥrām. For when the people see you have done that"," they will do as you have done.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from her and did not speak to anyone until he came to his sacrificial animal"," sacrificed it"," and shaved his head. When the people saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done that"," they rose and did likewise — they sacrificed"," and some shaved their heads while others shortened their hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," forgive those who shave their heads\"" — three times. It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and those who shorten their hair?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O Allah"," forgive those who shave their heads\"" — three times. It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and those who shorten their hair?\"" He said: \""And those who shorten their hair.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned back"," returning.\n\nAnd from Ibn Isḥāq"," who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to me — from Mujāhid — from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: It was said to him: \""Why did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ express preference for those who shave their heads three times"," and for those who shorten their hair only once?\"" He said: \""Because they did not doubt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See above]"""
"10082","(10078) And Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyá ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Yaḥyá ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām al-Warrāq narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Mālik narrated — from Abī al-Zubayr — from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyah — one camel on behalf of seven persons, and one cow on behalf of seven persons.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá and Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1318]"
"10083","(10079) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd ibn Tawbah narrated to us — Abū Badr narrated to us, he said: I heard ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad narrating — from Nāfiʿ — that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh and Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh both spoke to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar during the nights when al-Ḥajjāj came against Ibn al-Zubayr, and they said: \It will not harm you if you do not perform ḥajj this year"," for we fear that a barrier may be placed between you and the House.\"" He said: \""We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending ʿumrah"," and the disbelievers of Quraysh stood between us and the House"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed his animal"," shaved his head"," and then returned.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm"," from Abī Badr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1717]"""
"10084","(10080) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Muʿādh ibn al-Muthanná narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad, the brother of Juwayriyyah, narrated to us — Juwayriyyah narrated to us — from Nāfiʿ — that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh and Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh both informed him that they had spoken to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar on the nights when the army came against Ibn al-Zubayr, before he was killed, and they said: \It will not harm you if you do not perform ḥajj this year"," for we fear that a barrier may be placed between you and the House.\"" He said: \""We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the disbelievers of Quraysh stood between us and the House"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed his animal and shaved his head. I bear witness to you that I have made ʿumrah obligatory upon myself. If Allah wills"," I shall set out. If I am left unhindered between myself and the House"," I shall perform ṭawāf"," and if a barrier is placed between me and it"," I shall do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did when I was with him.\"" So he entered iḥrām for ʿumrah at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah"," then travelled for a while and said: \""The matter of the two is but one. I bear witness to you that I have made ḥajj obligatory along with my ʿumrah.\"" He did not exit from either of them until he exited on the Day of Sacrifice"," and he offered a sacrifice. And he used to say: \""Whoever combines ḥajj and ʿumrah and enters iḥrām for both of them together"," he shall not exit iḥrām until he exits from both of them on the Day of Sacrifice"," and he shall perform a single ṭawāf for both of them"," and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," on the day he enters Makkah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ. His statement \""on the day he enters Makkah\"" refers to returning to al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," that a single ṭawāf will suffice for both when he enters Makkah after the ṭawāf of arrival for both of them together. Then the second release will not occur except by ṭawāf of the House on the Day of Sacrifice"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAl-Bukhārī also narrated it from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"," from Juwayriyyah"," from Nāfiʿ"," that some of the sons of ʿAbdullāh said: \""If only you would stay...\"" — and he mentioned it with that meaning"," because in the narration of Juwayriyyah's brother"," ʿUbaydullāh and Sālim informed him that they had spoken"," whereas in the other narrations from Nāfiʿ"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh and Sālim spoke"," and ʿAbdullāh is more correct. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1713]"""
"10085","(10081) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Tamtām, i.e., Muḥammad ibn Ghālib, narrated to us — Saʿd, i.e., Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-ʿAwfī, narrated to us — Fulayḥ narrated — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ went out intending ʿumrah, and the disbelievers of Quraysh stood between him and the House, so he sacrificed his animal and shaved his head at al-Ḥudaybiyah, and he settled with them that he would perform ʿumrah the following year, and that he would not bring weapons upon them, nor remain there except for the duration they desired. So he performed ʿumrah the following year as he had agreed with them, and when he had stayed for three days, they ordered him to leave, and he left. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2554]"
"10086","(10082) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me — Abū Yaʿlá Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Abū Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated — from Fulayḥ, and he mentioned it with a similar narration, except that he said: \and that he would not bring weapons upon them except swords.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," from Surayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See above]"""
"10087","(10083) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī — informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Muslim — narrated to us; Abū Ḥātim — informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ — narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah, meaning Ibn Ṣāliḥ — informed us; Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Abī Kathīr — from ʿIkrimah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was prevented (from performing ʿUmrah)"," so he shaved his head"," was intimate with his wives"," and sacrificed his hady (offering) until he performed ʿUmrah the following year.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad from Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Wuḥāẓī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1714]"""
"10088","(10084) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb and Abū Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq — and the wording is that of Abū Aḥmad — both said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm — informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mukharramī — narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad — narrated to us; Shaybān — from Qatādah, regarding His (Allah's) words: {\That Allah may forgive you your sins of the past and the future"," and complete His favour upon you"," and guide you to a straight path\""} — he said: Anas ibn Mālik informed us that it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) upon his return from al-Ḥudaybiyyah"," while his Companions were overcome with grief and sorrow"," having been prevented from their rites"," and they had slaughtered the hady at al-Ḥudaybiyyah. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""A verse has been revealed to me that is more beloved to me than the entire world.\"" He then recited it to his Companions"," and they said: \""Congratulations to the Prophet of Allah! Allah has made clear what He will do for you"," but what will He do for us?\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed in that regard: {\""That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow.\""}\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1786]"""
"10089","(10085) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib and ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm — narrated to us; al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbd al-Malik — from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When we returned from al-Ḥudaybiyyah"," the Companions of Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) were overcome with grief and sorrow"," as they had slaughtered their hady in their places. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'A verse has been revealed to me that is more beloved to me than the entire world.'\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding narration.]"""
"10090","(10086) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār — narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr — from ʿUmar ibn Dharr — from Mujāhid, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed three ʿUmrahs"," all of them in Dhū al-Qaʿdah"," including the ʿUmrah in which the hady was prevented (from reaching its place). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent word to the people of Makkah"," and they agreed that he should turn back from them that year. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slaughtered the hady at al-Ḥudaybiyyah"," where he had encamped at the tree"," and then departed.\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"10091","(10087) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb — informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn — informed us; Abū ʿUmays — said: I heard ʿAṭāʾ say: \The encampment of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at al-Ḥudaybiyyah was in the Ḥarra"," and there he slaughtered the hady.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""We hold that he slaughtered in the Ḥill (the area outside the Ḥaram) because Allah"," the Most High"," says: {'They are the ones who disbelieved and barred you from the Sacred Mosque"," and the hady was prevented from reaching its place'} — and the entire Ḥaram is its place according to the people of knowledge.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Al-Ḥudaybiyyah is a place on earth"," part of which is in the Ḥill and part of which is in the Ḥaram. So he slaughtered the hady"," according to us"," in the Ḥill"," and there is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) where the pledge of allegiance was taken beneath the tree"," regarding which Allah"," the Most High"," revealed: {'Allah was certainly pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you beneath the tree.'} And regarding His words: {'And do not shave your heads until the hady reaches its place'} — its place"," and Allah knows best"," here (in the case of being prevented) seems to be that when one is prevented (iḥṣār)"," he slaughters where he is prevented"," and in the absence of iḥṣār"," the place is the Ḥaram. And slaughtering is a broad Arabic expression.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Something has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that supports the correctness of this.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10092","(10088) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Mālik — from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — from Yaʿqūb ibn Khālid al-Makhzūmī — from Abū Asmāʾ, the freedman of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar — that he informed him that he was with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, and he set out with him from Madinah. They passed by Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was ill at al-Suqyā. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar stayed with him until he feared he would miss (the journey), so he departed and sent word to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays (may Allah be pleased with them both), who were in Madinah, and they came to him. Then Ḥusayn gestured toward his head, so ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered his head to be shaved, and then he offered a sacrifice on his behalf at al-Suqyā, slaughtering a camel on his behalf. Yaḥyā said: \Ḥusayn had set out with ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) on that journey.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Mālik 768]"""
"10093","(10089) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Mālik — that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Companions exited the state of iḥrām at al-Ḥudaybiyyah. They slaughtered the hady and shaved their heads, and exited the state of iḥrām from everything before performing ṭawāf of the House and before the hady reached its place. Then we do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered any of his Companions, or anyone who was with him, to make up anything or to repeat anything.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ 800]"
"10094","(10090) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn al-Jahm — narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faraj — narrated to us; al-Wāqidī — narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ — from his father — from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \This ʿUmrah was not a makeup (qaḍāʾ)"," but rather it was a condition upon the Muslims that they would perform ʿUmrah the following year in the month in which the polytheists had prevented them.\""\n\n[Bāṭil]"""
"10095","(10091) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm — informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah — from Ibn Ṭāwūs — from his father — from Ibn ʿAbbās; and from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \There is no ḥaṣr (prevention) except the prevention of the enemy.\"" One of them added: \""The ḥaṣr has now gone away.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 1692]"""
"10096","(10092) Abū Zakariyyā — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — informed us; al-Rabīʿ — informed us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Mālik —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Mālik — from Ibn Shihāb — from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh — from his father, who said: \Whoever is prevented from reaching the House due to illness does not exit the state of iḥrām until he performs ṭawāf of the House and the saʿy between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 805]"""
"10097","And with this isnad, from his father, that he said: The *muhsar* (one prevented from completing the rites) does not exit the state of ihram until he performs Tawaf of the House (the Ka'bah) and the Sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. If he is compelled to wear some garments that are indispensable for him, he may do so but must offer a fidya (expiation).\n\nAl-Shafi'i said in the *Kitab al-Manasik*: The *muhsar* is the one prevented by illness. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"
"10098","Abu Nasr — 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qatadah — informed us; Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from a man among the people of Basra who was of an old generation, that he said: I set out for Makkah, and while I was on the road, my thigh was broken. I sent word to Makkah, where 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, and other people were present, but no one granted me permission to exit the state of ihram. So I remained at that water (place) for seven months, and then I exited the ihram by performing an 'Umrah. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik, 804]"
"10099","Abu al-Husayn — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad — informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; Ayyub narrated from Abu al-'Ala', who said: I set out to perform 'Umrah, and when I was at al-Dathiniyyah, I fell from my mount and was injured. I sent word to Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas, and they were asked. They said: He has no fixed time as the one performing Hajj has; he must remain in his ihram until he reaches the House. He said: So I moved through those waters for six or seven months until I reached the House. He is Abu al-'Ala': Yazid ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, one of the trustworthy narrators among the Basrans. [Sahih]"
"10100","Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm — informed us; al-Rabi' — informed us; al-Shafi'i — informed us; Malik — informed us.\n\n(And) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajaniyy — informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Ibn 'Umar, Marwan, and Ibn al-Zubayr issued a verdict for Ibn Huzabah al-Makhzumi — who had been thrown from his mount on one of the roads to Makkah while he was in a state of ihram — that he should treat himself with what is necessary and offer a fidya. When he recovers, he should perform an 'Umrah and exit the state of his ihram, and it will be incumbent upon him to perform Hajj the following year and offer a sacrifice (hadya). [Sahih. Narrated by Malik, 80]"
"10101","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, that she said: We do not know of any state of being forbidden (haram) that renders one permissible except the Tawaf of the House. And we mention it, if Allah wills, as evidence in the matter of the exception (al-istithna') in Hajj. And with Allah lies success. [Sahih]"
"10102","Abu Nasr — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Tabarani therein — informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'igh narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh narrated to us; Hisham ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Abu al-Nu'man — 'Arim — narrated to us; 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to me; al-Hajjaj ibn Abi 'Uthman narrated to me; he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me that 'Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, narrated to him; he said: al-Hajjaj ibn 'Amr al-Ansari narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever suffers a broken bone or becomes lame has exited the state of ihram"," and upon him is another Hajj.\"" He said: So I narrated it to Ibn 'Abbas and Abu Hurayrah"," and they both said: \""He spoke the truth.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of 'Abd al-Warith. And in the narration of Rawh from al-Hajjaj ibn 'Amr al-Ansari"," it says: \""He has exited the state of ihram"," and upon him is another Hajj.\"" And the rest carries the same meaning.\n\nAnd thus narrated it Yahya al-Qattan"," Abu 'Asim"," and others from al-Hajjaj ibn Abi 'Uthman al-Sawwaf from Yahya; they mentioned in it the hearing of 'Ikrimah from al-Hajjaj ibn 'Amr al-Ansari. However"," Ma'mar contradicted him"," from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir"," inserting a man between them. [Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 1862]"""
"10103","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us of it; Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from 'Ikrimah from 'Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, who said: I asked al-Hajjaj ibn 'Amr al-Ansari about the prevention of a Muslim, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever suffers a broken bone or becomes lame has exited the state of ihram"," and upon him is the Hajj the following year.\"" 'Ikrimah said: So I narrated it to Ibn 'Abbas and Abu Hurayrah"," and they both said: \""Al-Hajjaj spoke the truth.\""\n\nAnd with the same meaning narrated Mu'awiyah ibn Salam from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir"," and narrated Yazid ibn Abi Habib from 'Ikrimah from 'Abdullah ibn Rafi'.\n\n'Ali ibn al-Madini said: Al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir is more established (athbat). [Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 186]"""
"10104","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us of that; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara' narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Some of the people of knowledge, if it is authentic, have interpreted it to mean that he exits the state of ihram after the Hajj has lapsed, by the same means by which one whose Hajj has lapsed without illness exits. And it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas, authentically from him, that he said: There is no *hasr* (prevention) except the prevention of an enemy. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"
"10105","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Karzi informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us from Abu 'Ubayd; 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us from Aban ibn Taghlib from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father from 'Abdullah — that is, Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) — regarding the man who was bitten while in a state of ihram for 'Umrah and was prevented (from continuing). 'Abdullah said: Send the sacrificial animal (hadya) and appoint between yourselves and him a designated day (*yawm amarin*). When the hadya is slaughtered in Makkah, this one exits the state of ihram.\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: Al-Kisa'i said: *Al-amar* is the sign (*'alamah*) by which something is recognized. He said: Appoint a day that you know, so that you do not differ. [Sahih]"
"10106","Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Hisham from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and said: \Do you not wish to perform Hajj?\"" She said: \""I am unwell.\"" He said to her: \""Perform Hajj and stipulate the condition: 'My place of exiting ihram is where You have prevented me.'\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i said in the *Kitab al-Manasik*: If the hadith of 'Urwah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the exception (al-istithna') were established"," I would not go beyond it"," because in my view it is not permissible to contradict what is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Shaykh said: This hadith has been established through various routes from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). As for the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah from Hisham"," it has been narrated in a connected (*mawsul*) form. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Shafi'i"," 575]"""
"10107","(10103) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us — Ibn Sa'id narrated to us — 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-A'la narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that the Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, passed by Duba'ah while she was ailing, and he said: \Do you wish to perform Hajj?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then perform Hajj"," and stipulate"," saying: O Allah"," my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\""\n\n'Abd al-Jabbar connected it"," and he is trustworthy"," from Sufyan"," and others transmitted it as mursal. Abu Usamah — Hammad ibn Usamah and Ma'mar ibn Rashid — also connected it from Hisham"," from his father"," from 'A'ishah"," and Ma'mar from al-Zuhri"," from 'Urwah"," from 'A'ishah.\n\n[Sahih. Al-Daraqutni recorded it (2/219).]"""
"10108","(10104) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Darimi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Abu Kurayb narrated to us — Abu Usamah narrated from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and said to her: \Do you wish to perform Hajj?\"" She said: \""By Allah"," I find myself only in pain.\"" He said to her: \""Perform Hajj"," and stipulate"," saying: O Allah"," my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\"" And she was under the marriage of al-Miqdad.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayr"," and al-Bukhari recorded it from 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il"," from Abu Usamah.\n\n[Sahih. Al-Bukhari recorded it (4801).]"""
"10109","(10105) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to me — my father narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, and she said: \I wish to perform Hajj"," but I am ailing.\"" The Prophet"," peace be blessings be upon him"," said: \""Perform Hajj"," and stipulate that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\""\n\n[Sahih. See the preceding narration.]"""
"10110","(10106) He said: and 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us — Ma'mar narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah — a similar narration.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from 'Abd ibn Humayd, from 'Abd al-Razzaq."
"10111","(10107) Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Azraqi narrated to us — Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from Ibn Jurayj — Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Tawus and 'Ikrimah, the mawla of Ibn 'Abbas, narrating from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a heavy woman and I wish to perform Hajj — how do you command me to enter ihram?\"" He said: \""Enter ihram and stipulate that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\""\n\n[Sahih. Muslim recorded it (1208).]"""
"10112","(10108) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us — Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Tawus and 'Ikrimah, the mawla of Ibn 'Abbas, narrating from Ibn 'Abbas: that Duba'ah came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, and said: \I am a heavy woman and I wish to perform Hajj — what do you command me?\"" He said: \""Enter ihram for Hajj and stipulate that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\"" And she reached her destination.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. He also recorded it additionally from the hadith of 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid and Abu 'Asim"," from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Sahih. See the preceding narration.]"""
"10113","(10109) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us — Habib ibn Yazid narrated from 'Amr ibn Harim — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, commanded Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr to stipulate during Hajj, and she did that by the command of the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him.\n\nMuslim recorded it in his Sahih from Harun ibn 'Abd Allah, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi. [Sahih. Muslim (1208).]"
"10114","(10110) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran in Baghdad informed us — 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Riyahi narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun informed us — Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated from Abu Bishr, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr while she wished to perform Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be blessings be upon him, said to her: \Stipulate upon entering ihram that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me"," for that is for you.\""\n\n[Sahih.]"""
"10115","(10111) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us — Yahyay al-Himmani narrated to us — 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us — Hilal ibn Khabab narrated from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I wish to perform Hajj — shall I stipulate?\"" He said: \""Yes"," stipulate.\"" She said: \""What shall I say?\"" He said: 'Say: Here I am"," O Allah"," here I am. My place of exiting ihram from the earth is wherever You restrain me.'\""\n\nHe said: and 'Abbad narrated from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf"," from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir"," from 'Ikrimah"," from Ibn 'Abbas"," from the Prophet"," peace be blessings be upon him — something similar.\n\nAbu Dawud recorded it in Kitab al-Sunan from Ahmad ibn Hanbal"," from 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam"," with the first isnad"," without the second.\n\n[Sahih. Abu Dawud recorded it (1776).]"""
"10116","(10112) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me — Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Tabari narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us — al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwarrudhi narrated to us — Isra'il narrated from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet, peace be blessings be upon him, said to Duba'ah: \Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You restrain me.\""\n\nAbu 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Sarraj narrated it to us from Ahmad ibn Mani'.\n\n[Sahih.]"""
"10117","(10113) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib both said: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us; Rabāḥ ibn Abī Maʿrūf al-Makkī narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Ḍubāʿah: \Perform Ḥajj and stipulate: 'My place of exiting iḥrām is wherever You restrain me.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1208]"""
"10118","(10114) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī informed us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ḍubāʿah: \Perform Ḥajj and stipulate: 'My place of exiting iḥrām is wherever you restrain me.'\"" — thus he narrated it from Jābir. [Munkar]"""
"10119","(10115) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū Muslim narrated to us; Muslim narrated to us; Hishām narrated to us; Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir that the Prophet ﷺ said to Ḍubāʿah bint al-Zubayr: \Perform Ḥajj and stipulate: 'My place of exiting iḥrām is wherever you restrain me.'\"" [Munkar]"""
"10120","(10116) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated to us from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl from Zaynab bint Nabīṭ, the wife of Anas ibn Mālik, from Ḍubāʿah bint al-Zubayr that the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \Perform Ḥajj and stipulate.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bayhaqī narrated it in al-Kabīr 840]"""
"10121","(10117) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-ʿAṭṭār al-Ḥīrī informed us, and he wrote it for me in his own hand; the Imam Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; ʿIṣām ibn Riwād ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Ḍubāʿah bint al-Zubayr, who said: She said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I intend to perform Ḥajj"," so how should I enter iḥrām for Ḥajj?\"" He said"," \""Say: 'O Allah"," I enter iḥrām for Ḥajj if You permit me"," assist me in it"," and make it easy for me. And if You restrain me"," then it is an ʿUmrah. And if You restrain me from both of them"," then my place of exiting iḥrām is wherever You restrain me.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10122","(10118) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī reported it as a narration from Ibn Mahdī from Sufyān from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā from Suwayd ibn Ghaflah, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me, \O Abā Umayyah"," perform Ḥajj and stipulate"," for you have what you stipulated"," and upon you is what Allah has stipulated for you.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Umm 7/407]"""
"10123","(10119) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿUmayrah ibn Ziyād from ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Perform Ḥajj and stipulate"," and say: 'O Allah"," I intended Ḥajj and resolved upon it; if it is made easy"," then it is Ḥajj"," otherwise it is an ʿUmrah.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Al-Bayhaqī narrated it in al-Kabīr 6917]"""
"10124","(10120) And Abū Ṭāhir and Abū Saʿīd both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Muḥammad narrated to us; Surayj informed us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād informed us; ʿAlqamah ibn Abī ʿAlqamah narrated from his mother from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she used to say: \Make a stipulation (istithnāʾ) in Ḥajj: 'O Allah"," I intended Ḥajj and resolved upon it; if You complete it"," then it is Ḥajj"," otherwise it is an ʿUmrah.'\"" And she herself used to make the stipulation and would command those who were with her to make the stipulation.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"10125","(10121) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father, who said: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said to me, \Do you make a stipulation (istithnāʾ) when you perform Ḥajj?\"" I said to her"," \""What should I say?\"" She said"," \""Say: 'O Allah"," I intended Ḥajj and resolved upon it; if You make it easy"," then it is Ḥajj"," and if a restrainer restrains me"," then it is an ʿUmrah.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it 576]"""
"10126","(10122) And it has been narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, who said: Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, used to command us, when we performed Ḥajj, to make a stipulation (istithrāṭ).\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Abū Isḥāq al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to me; ʿUbayd ibn Yaʿīsh narrated to us; Yūnus informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah from his father, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Tārīkh 1/176]"
"10127","(10123) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to disapprove of stipulating conditions (al-ishtirāṭ) during Ḥajj and would say: \Is not the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sufficient for you? If any of you is prevented from performing Ḥajj"," let him perform Ṭawāf of the Bayt and Saʿī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," then exit the state of Iḥrām entirely"," and perform Ḥajj the following year"," offering a sacrifice; and if he cannot find one"," he should fast.\"" Yūnus said: Rabīʿah said: \""We do not know of any stipulation that is permissible in Iḥrām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1715]"""
"10128","(10124) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yūnus, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to disapprove of stipulating conditions during Ḥajj and would say: \Is not the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sufficient for you?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding narration.]"""
"10129","(10125) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Ibn Nājiyah narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah, and ʿAlī ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, and he mentioned it similarly. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad, from Ibn al-Mubārak, through both chains of narration, thus in abridged form. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Maʿmar and added: \And if any of you is prevented by an impediment"," then when he reaches it (the House)"," let him perform Ṭawāf of it and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah"," then shave or shorten (his hair)"," and upon him is Ḥajj the following year.\"" Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Ibn Nājiyah narrated to us: Ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it. And I hold that Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," had the ḥadīth of Ḍubāʿah bint al-Zubayr reached him"," would have adopted it and would not have disapproved of stipulating conditions"," just as his father did not disapprove of it. And with Allah lies success."""
"10130","(10126) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah narrated to us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masrrah narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Azraqī narrated to us: Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated, regarding a woman who had wealth and sought her husband's permission for Ḥajj, but he did not grant it. He said: Ibrāhīm al-Ṣāʾigh said: Nāfiʿ said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \It is not permissible for her to set out except with her husband's permission"," and it is not permissible for a woman to travel for three nights except with a maḥram whom marriage to her is prohibited.\"" Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaʿqūb also narrated it from Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm. [Munkar]"""
"10131","(10127) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhawayh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us. Abū al-Muthannā said: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: al-Zuhrī narrated from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If the wife of any of you seeks permission to go to the mosque"," do not prevent her.\"" The wording of both their narrations is the same. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others from Sufyān. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10132","(10128) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: My father narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 858]"""
"10133","(10129) That is from what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād al-Makhzūmī, from Ibn ʿUmar, who heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding the verse: {Whoever is able to find a way to it} (Āl ʿImrān:97), he said: \The provision and the mount.\"" And we have narrated it through authentic chains from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) as a mursal narration"," and it strengthens this musnad narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10134","(10130) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: al-Ḍaḥḥākh ibn Makhlad, Abū ʿĀṣim, narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abū Mujāhid al-Ṭāʾī narrated to us: Muḥill ibn Khalīfah narrated from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when two men came to him; one complained of poverty and the other complained of the highway being cut off (i.e., bandits). He said: \It will not be long before a woman departs from al-Ḥīrah to Makkah without any escort"," and the Hour will not be established until one of you goes around with his charity and finds no one to accept it. Then wealth will overflow"," and one of you will stand before Allah"," with no veil between him and Allah"," and no interpreter to translate for him. He will say: 'Did I not give you wealth?' He will say: 'Indeed.' He will say: 'Did I not send a messenger to you?' He will say: 'Indeed.' He will look to his right and see nothing but the Fire"," and he will look to his left and see nothing but the Fire. So let each of you protect himself from the Fire"," even with half a date; and if he cannot find that"," then with a good word.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"," from Abī ʿĀṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1347]"""
"10135","(10131) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us. And Abū Bakr informed me: al-Qāsim narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr Zāj said: al-Naḍr informed us: Isrāʾīl informed us: Saʿd al-Ṭāʾī informed us: Muḥill ibn Khalīfah narrated from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), a man came to him and complained of poverty, and another came and complained of the highway being cut off. He said: \O ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim"," have you seen al-Ḥīrah?\"" I said: \""I have not seen it"," but I have been told about it.\"" He said: \""If your life is prolonged"," you will surely see the woman traveler depart from al-Ḥīrah until she performs Ṭawāf of the Kaʿbah"," fearing none but Allah.\"" I said to myself: \""Where then will the brigands of Ṭayyʾ who have set the land ablaze?\"" He said: \""If your life is prolonged"," the treasures of Kisrā will be conquered.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Kisrā ibn Hurmuz?\"" He said: \""Kisrā ibn Hurmuz. And if your life is prolonged"," you will see a man bring forth a handful of gold or silver"," seeking someone to accept it from him"," and he will find no one to accept it from him. And one of you will surely meet Allah on the Day he meets Him"," with no interpreter between him and Him to translate for him. He will say: 'Did I not send a messenger to you to convey to you?' He will say: 'Indeed.' He will look to his right and see nothing but Jahannam"," and he will look to his left and see nothing but Jahannam.\"" ʿAdī said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Protect yourselves from the Fire"," even with half a date; and if you cannot find half a date"," then with a good word.'\"" ʿAdī said: \""I have seen the woman traveler depart from al-Kūfah until she performed Ṭawāf of the Bayt"," fearing none but Allah. And I was among those who conquered the treasures of Kisrā ibn Hurmuz. And if your lives are prolonged"," you will see what Abū al-Qāsim (peace and blessings be upon him) said: a man will bring forth a handful of gold or silver and find no one to accept it from him.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥakam"," from al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl. Al-Shāfiʿī said in the old opinion: \""And it has reached us that Ibn ʿUmar traveled with a female slave of his"," who was not his maḥram"," and she had no maḥram with her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3400]"""
"10136","(10132) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿd al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿUqbah ibn Khālid narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Naṣr ibn ʿAlī informed us: Abū Aḥmad narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to have a female slave of his called Ṣafiyyah ride behind him, and she would travel with him to Makkah. And in the narration of ʿUqbah: that Ibn ʿUmar performed Ḥajj with a female slave of his called Ṣāfiyyah, on the hind part of a camel. Al-Shāfiʿī said in the new opinion: \And it has reached us from ʿĀʾishah"," Ibn ʿUmar"," and ʿUrwah the same as our opinion"," that a woman may travel for Ḥajj even if she has no maḥram with her. He also mentioned it from ʿAṭāʾ"," and in the old opinion from Mālik ibn Anas.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1728]"""
"10137","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-'Abbas al-Duri narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, that 'A'ishah was informed that Abu Sa'id used to issue a fatwa that a woman should not travel except with a mahram. She said: \Not all of them have a mahram.\"" [Sahih]"""
"10138","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and others informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Sufyan narrated — (H) — and 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon and said: \Let no man be alone in private with a woman"," and let no woman travel except with a mahram.\"" A man stood up and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," my wife has gone out for Hajj"," and I have been enlisted in such-and-such military expedition.\"" He said: \""Then go and perform Hajj with your wife.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of 'Ali.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn 'Abdillah"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others"," from Sufyan. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 4935]"""
"10139","Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us; Abu Nu'aym narrated — (H) — and Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Birti informed us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \I have been enlisted in such-and-such military expedition"," and my wife wishes to perform Hajj.\"" He said: \""Return and perform Hajj with your wife.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Nu'aym. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 2896]"""
"10140","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, i.e. al-Shaybani, narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Musaddad narrated — and Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us; Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna said: Yahya narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah informed me; Nafi' narrated from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let not a woman travel for three days except with a mahram.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 1037]"""
"10141","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let not a woman travel a journey of three days and more except with her father"," her brother"," her son"," or a mahram of hers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others"," from Abu Mu'awiyah.\n\nQaza'ah ibn Yahya narrated it from Abu Sa'id"," and in one of the two narrations from him he said: \""More than three.\"" And in the other narration he said: \""Two days.\"" And Abu Hurayrah narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Sahih. Muslim"," 1340]"""
"10142","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Malik narrated — (H) — and Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam al-Warraq narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated; I read to Malik — (H) — and Abu 'Abdillah informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; al-Qa'na'i narrated, having read to Malik, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of one day and one night except with a mahram of hers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated it from Malik"," from Sa'id"," from his father"," from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih. Muslim"," 1339]"""
"10143","Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us; Malik narrated it.\n\nAnd thus did Layth ibn Sa'd and Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrate it, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and it has already been mentioned in the Book of Salah."
"10144","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdillah al-Shaybani narrated to us orally; Husayn ibn al-Hasan and Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not permissible for a Muslim woman to travel a distance of one night except with a man who is a mahram of hers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah. [Sahih. Muslim"," 1339]"""
"10145","Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of one day except with a mahram.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb"," from Yahya ibn Sa'id"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from Adam"," from Ibn Abi Dhi'b. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari"," 1038]"""
"10146","'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Isa ibn Abi Qummash narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us; al-Darawardi narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Waqid ibn Abi Waqid al-Laythi, from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to his wives during his Hajj: \This (is your Hajj); then (after this) it is (a matter of) remaining confined (in your homes).\"" [Hasan for other than it. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 1722]"""
"10147","(10143) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak — informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from Salih, the freed slave of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \This is only this (pilgrimage)"," then (there will be) staying at home in seclusion.\"" He said: So all of them used to travel except Zaynab and Sawdah"," for they both said: \""No mount shall move us after what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nSalih ibn Kaysan followed him in narrating from Salih ibn Nabhan"," and we reported it at the beginning of the book from the hadith of Abu Waqid al-Laythi.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab prevented the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) from performing Hajj due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \""This is only this Hajj"," then (there will be) staying at home in seclusion.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: We reported at the beginning of the Book of Hajj"," in the chapter on the Hajj of women"," from 'Umar that he permitted them to perform Hajj in the last Hajj he performed"," and sent with them 'Uthan ibn 'Affan and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf. In this"," and in the Hajj of all other women"," there is evidence that the"""
"10148","(10144) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us — Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Marwazī in Baghdad narrated to us — Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us from his father, from his grandfather: that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave permission to the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) to perform ḥajj, and sent ʿUthmān and Ibn ʿAwf with them. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to the people: \No one shall approach them or look at them"," except from a distance.\"" They were in the hawāʾidj upon the camels. He set them down at the beginning of the valley"," while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both) dismounted at its rear"," and no one ascended toward them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1761]"""
"10149","(10145) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us — ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Abū Bishr narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated to us — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The 'well-known days' (al-ayyām al-maʿlūmāt) are the ten days"," and the 'numbered days' (al-ayyām al-maʿdūdāt) are the days of al-Tashrīq.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10150","(10146) Abū ʿAbdullāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us — saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: \I saw Ibn ʿAbbās pronouncing the takbīr on the day of al-Nafr in Makkah"," reciting: {And remember Allah during the numbered days}.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10151","(10147) Abū ʿAbdullāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us — saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to us — from Mujāhid, who said: \The 'well-known days' are the ten days"," and the 'numbered days' are the days of al-Tashrīq.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10152","(10148) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdad narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukarram narrated to us — Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to us — Abū Jamrah narrated to us — from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the story of al-Tamattuʿ, who said — and he said: {Whatever is easy of the hady} — a camel, or a cow, or a sheep, or a share in a sacrifice. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Shuʿbah, and likewise Muslim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1603]"
"10153","(10149) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — he said: I heard Mujāhid narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Of the eight pairs (al-azwāj al-thamāniyah) — meaning the hady.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10154","(10150) He said — and Saʿīd narrated to us — Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us — Abū Isḥāq narrated to us — from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The eight pairs are from the camels"," the cattle"," the sheep"," and the goats — according to one's means. The greater it is"," the more virtuous.\"""""
"10155","(10151) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī said — Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — Abū Zurʿah narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — from Abī Jaʿfar: that a man asked ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the hady — from what does it consist? He replied: \From the eight pairs.\"" As though the man was uncertain"," so ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Do you recite the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Have you then heard Allah"," the Most High"," say: {O you who believe"," fulfill the contracts. The livestock animals have been made lawful to you}?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Have you heard Him say: {And mention the name of Allah upon what He has provided for them of livestock}?\"" And He said: {And of the livestock are carriers and those too small. Eat of what Allah has provided for you.} He said: \""Have you heard Allah say: {Of the sheep two"," and of the goats two"," and of the cattle two"," and of the camels two}?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Have you heard Allah say: {O you who believe"," do not kill game while you are in iḥrām} — until His words — {as a hady reaching the Kaʿbah}?\"" The man said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then I killed a gazelle — what is upon me?\"" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: {A hady reaching the Kaʿbah.} ʿAlī said: \""Allah has named a hady reaching the Kaʿbah"," as you hear.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10156","(10152) By way of inference from what Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and others informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb — Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you — from Ibn Shihāb — who said: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Agharr informed me that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \When Friday comes"," there are angels at every door of the mosque"," recording the first one and the first one [to arrive]. When the imam sits [on the pulpit]"," they roll up the scrolls and come to listen to the remembrance. The likeness of the one who comes early is like one who offers a camel"," then like one who offers a cow"," then like one who offers a ram"," then like one who offers a chicken"," then like one who offers an egg.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and others from Ibn Wahb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another direction from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 887]"""
"10157","(10153) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not slaughter except a musinnah (a mature animal)"," unless it is difficult for you"," in which case you may slaughter a jadhaʿah (a young animal) from the sheep.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1963]"""
"10158","(10154) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to say regarding the sacrificial animals (aḍ-ḥāyā) and the sacrificial camels (al-budun): \A thaniyyah (a two-year-old) or above.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10159","(10155) Abū Saʿid ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Barṭī al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraīʿ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, Abū Salamah narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered the camel of Abū Jahl as hadī in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah"," and on its head was a ring (burrah) of silver. Abū Jahl had been seized on the day of Badr.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā. In the narration of Yazīd ibn Zuraīʿ"," it states: \""In its nose was a ring (burrah) of gold","\"" and the remainder carries the same meaning. Abū Dāwūd also narrated it in the book of Sunan from Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl. And Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," and he said: \""In its nose was a ring (burrah) of silver"," to enrage the polytheists thereby.\"" There was a discrepancy regarding it from Muḥammad ibn Salamah"," from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq; it was said: \""A ring (burrah) of silver","\"" and it was said: \""of gold.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/261]"""
"10160","(10156) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Hāshimī narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Mustaʿīnī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAlī al-Madanī narrated to us, my father said: \I used to think that this was from the authentic ḥadīths of Ibn Isḥāq"," but he has practised tadlīs (concealed the chain). Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us"," from his father"," from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," who said: 'Someone I do not suspect narrated to me"," from Ibn Abī Najīḥ"," from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿAbbās.'\"" ʿAlī said: \""Thus the ḥadīth is muḍṭarib (discrepant).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim"," from Ibn Abī Najīḥ."""
"10161","(10157) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Marwarrūdhī narrated to us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet ﷺ offered among his sacrificial camels (badanah) a camel that belonged to Abū Jahl, in whose nose was a ring (burrah) of silver.\n\nThis is a ṣaḥīḥ chain, except that they hold that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim took it from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq and then practised tadlīs regarding it. If Jarīr explicitly stated that he heard it from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, the ḥadīth would become ṣaḥīḥ. And Allah knows best.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Manṣūr, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, without mention of the ring (burrah). [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/273]"
"10162","(10158) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī and al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār both narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drove forward one hundred sacrificial camels (badanah)"," among which was the camel of Abū Jahl.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from al-Ḥakam"," from Miqsam"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and there is a discrepancy regarding its text. What we have mentioned suffices. [Munkar]"""
"10163","(10159) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī both informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Seventy sacrificial camels (badanah) were slaughtered—or were caused to be slaughtered—on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah"," among which was the camel of Abū Jahl. When they were turned away from the House (the Kaʿbah)"," they moaned as a she-camel moans for her young.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 3076]"""
"10164","(10160) And Hushaym narrated it from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered as hadī during his Ḥajj one hundred sacrificial camels (badanah), among which was a camel that belonged to Abū Jahl, on whose head was a ring (burrah) of silver. Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Hushaym narrated it. And Ibn Abī Laylā narrated it on another occasion. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"
"10165","(10161) Such as was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād, Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Adamī narrated to us, Abū Qilābah informed us, Abū ʿĀṣim and Abū Nuʿaym both narrated to us, saying: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās; and from al-Ḥakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered as hadī one hundred sacrificial camels (badanah), among which was the camel of Abū Jahl, in whose nose was a ring (burrah) of silver.\n\nIt was also narrated by Mālik ibn Anas in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ in a mursal form, and it carries strength due to what has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"
"10166","(10162) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm: that the Messenger of Allah ￺ offered as hadī a camel that belonged to Abū Jahl ibn Hishām during a Ḥajj or an ʿUmrah.\n\nIt was also narrated by Suwayd ibn Saʿīd, from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Mālik 841]"
"10167","(10163) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Akhrām in Naysābūr informed us: Suwayd ibn Saʿīd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khasrūjirdī both said: Abū Bakr al-Imām Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Ṣūfī informed us from his original book: Suwayd ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, from Anas ibn Mālik, from Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) sacrificed a camel on behalf of Abū Jahl.\n\nAbū Ḥāzim said: No one other than Suwayd al-Ḥaddānī narrated it, and no reliable narrator other than Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf ibn al-Akhrām and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated it from Suwayd, and no trustworthy narrator narrated it from Aḥmad other than the Imām Abū Bakr (may Allah have mercy on him).\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for others. Al-Khaṭīb narrated it in his Tārīkh, 4/84.]"
"10168","(10164) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: Abū al-Naḍr informed us: Abū Khaythamah informed us: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not slaughter except a musinnah (a mature animal)"," unless it is difficult for you"," in which case slaughter a jadhaʿah (a young animal) from the sheep.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ as previously mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced under number 10153.]"""
"10169","(10165) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Bāghandī informed us: Qabīṣah informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb, from his father, who said: \We were in a military expedition"," and among us or leading us was Mujāshiʿ ibn Masʿūd"," a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The sheep became scarce"," and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""The jadhaʿah suffices as the thanī suffices from it.\""'\"" [Daʿīf]"""
"10170","(10166) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \Whoever vows a badanah (sacrificial camel)"," let it be garlanded with two sandals and let it be marked (mashʿūrah)"," then let it be driven until it is slaughtered at al-Bayt al-ʿAtīq (the Kaʿbah) or at Minā on the Day of Sacrifice — it has no other place of slaughter besides that. And whoever vows a camel or a cow as a sacrifice"," let it be slaughtered wherever one wishes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 8804.]"""
"10171","(10167) And with this chain of narration, Mālik narrated from ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Anṣārī that he asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab about a badanah that a woman had made obligatory upon herself. Saʿīd said: \Al-budn (sacrificial camels) are from camels"," and the place of slaughter of al-budn is al-Bayt al-ʿAtīq"," unless she has designated a specific place on the earth"," in which case she should slaughter it there. If she cannot find a badanah"," then a cow. If she cannot find a cow"," then ten sheep.\""\n\nHe said: \""Then I came to Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and he said the same as Saʿīd"," except that he said: 'If there is no cow"," then seven sheep.'\""\n\nHe said: \""Then I came to Khārijah ibn Zayd"," and he said the same as Sālim.\""\n\nHe said: \""Then I came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he said the same as Sālim.\"" [Ḥasan. Mālik narrated it"," 409.]"""
"10172","(10168) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us verbally: Abū Saʿīd Aḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out in the year of al-Ḥudaybiyyah with over one hundred of his Companions. When he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he garlanded the sacrificial animals, marked them (ashʿarahā), and entered into iḥrām from there.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 3926.]"
"10173","(10169) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us by recitation, and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us verbally; both said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, from Abū Ḥassān, from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed Ẓuhr at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah. Then his sacrificial camel was brought to him, and he marked the right side of its hump, then wiped the blood over it, then garlanded it with two sandals. Then his mount was brought, and when it stood upright on al-Baydāʾ, he pronounced the talbiyyah for Ḥajj.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿAdī from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1243.]"
"10174","(10170) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Musaddad informed us: Yaḥyā narrated from Shuʿbah with this ḥadīth, and he said: \Then he wiped the blood with his hands.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: Hammām narrated it"," meaning from Qatādah"," and he said: \""He wiped the blood from it with his finger.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd"," 1752.]"""
"10175","(10171) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that when he sent sacrificial animals from Madīnah, he would garland them and mark them at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah. He would garland them before marking them, and that would be in one place, while he was facing the qiblah. He would garland them with two sandals and mark them from the left side. Then they would be driven with him until they were stopped with the people at ʿArafah, and then he would depart with them when they departed. When he arrived at Minā on the morning of the Day of Sacrifice, he would slaughter them before shaving or trimming (the hair). He would slaughter his sacrificial animals with his own hand, standing them in rows and facing them toward the qiblah. Then he would eat from them and feed others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10176","(10172) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Mālik ibn Anas and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar both narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to mark his sacrificial camels from the left side, unless they were difficult to handle (ṣiʿāban muqarranah), in which case, if he could not get between them, he would mark from the right side. When he intended to mark them, he would face them toward the qiblah. When he marked them, he would say: \Bismillāh"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" He would mark them with his own hand and slaughter them with his own hand"," standing. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10177","(10173) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, they said: al-Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that he used not to care on which side he placed the *ish'ar* (marking incision) — on the left or on the right. Al-Shafi'i said in another narration besides this one: The *ish'ar* is to be made on the right side, and thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked his sacrifice, and he mentioned the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas. [Authenticated by others. Al-Shafi'i cited it (1716)]"
"10178","(10174) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us: al-Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Malik ibn Anas and 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar and others informed me that Nafi' narrated to them that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The *hady* (sacrificial animal) is that which is garlanded (*quddila*), marked with the *ish'ar*, and halted with at 'Arafah. [Authentic. Malik cited it (849)]"
"10179","(10175) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: There is no *hady* except that which is garlanded, marked with the *ish'ar*, and halted with at 'Arafah. [Authentic]"
"10180","(10176) He said, and Sulayman also narrated from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of it."
"10181","(10177) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us: Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: The *badanah* (sacrificial camel) is marked with the *ish'ar* only so that it may be known that it is a *badanah*. [Authentic. Ibn Abi Shaybah cited it (13206)]"
"10182","(10178) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Matar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: al-Aswad sent a young slave of his to 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and he asked her about sacrificial animals that he had sent along with him — should he halt with them at 'Arafat? She said: Whatever you wish — if you wish, then do so, and if you wish, then do not. [Authentic]"
"10183","(10179) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Aṣbahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once offered a sheep as a sacrifice and garlanded it. [Authentic. Muslim (1321)]"
"10184","(10180) Abu 'Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hajjaj al-Warraq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it with its like, except that he said: \Once to the House — a sheep — and he garlanded it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Authentic. See the preceding]"""
"10185","(10181) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I used to fashion the garlands of the sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send them off, then remain in a state of *iḥrām* (permissible, i.e., not in consecration). Al-Bukhari narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Muhammad ibn Kathir. And it was also narrated by Wahayb ibn Khalid and Hammad ibn Zayd from Mansur, with the mention of the sheep in it. [Authentic. Al-Bukhari (1616)]"
"10186","(10182) Al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah also narrated from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, she said: We used to garland the sheep and send them off, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of permissibility — nothing was forbidden for him thereby. Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us of it: Abu 'Abd Allah al-Shaybani narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Muhajiri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated from al-Hakam, and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from 'Abd al-Ṣamad. [Authentic. Muslim (1321)]"
"10187","(10183) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed me; Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us; Ibn 'Awn narrated from al-Qasim from Umm al-Mu'minin, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I used to make its garlands from wool that was in our possession.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari in the Sahih from 'Amr ibn 'Ali from Mu'adh"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Ibn 'Awn.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1618]"""
"10188","(10184) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabarani narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim both said: Ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said; and Sulayman narrated to us: Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us; Qabisah narrated to us; they both said: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from 'Abd Rahman ibn Abi Layla from 'Ali, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to give in charity the coverings of the sacrificial camels that I had slaughtered and their skins.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari in the Sahih from Qabisah and Muhammad ibn Kathir"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah from Ibn Abi Najih.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1621]"""
"10189","(10185) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajanī informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Nafi' from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar: \He used to adorn his sacrificial camels with Egyptian cloth"," saddle-cloths"," and garments"," then he would send them to the Ka'bah and it would be clothed with them.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Malik 849]"""
"10190","(10186) He said: And Malik narrated to us that he asked 'Abdullah ibn Dinar: \What would 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar do with the coverings of his sacrificial camels when the Ka'bah was clothed with this covering?\"" He said: \""'Abdullah would give them in charity.\""\n\n[Sahih. See the preceding]"""
"10191","(10187) He said: And Malik narrated from Nafi': \Abdullah ibn 'Umar would not tear the coverings of his sacrificial camels"," nor would he adorn them until he departed with them from Mina to 'Arafah.\"" Others added in it"," except the place of the hump. \""When he slaughtered them"," he would remove their coverings for fear that the blood might spoil them"," then he would give them in charity.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Malik 850]"""
"10192","(10188) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Nadr al-Harashi narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Baluwayh narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; they both said: 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Aflah ibn Humayd narrated from al-Qasim from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own hands"," then he would mark them and garland them"," then he would send them to the House while he remained in Madinah. Nothing that was permissible for him became forbidden for him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim in the Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Bukhari 1612]"""
"10193","(10189) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Anas ibn 'Iyad narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah, who said: \I used to twist the garlings of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," then he would send them while he was residing"," and he would not avoid anything that the one in ihram avoids. It reached her that Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan had sent a sacrificial animal and had not entered ihram.\"" She said: \""Does he have a Ka'bah to perform Tawaf around? For we do not know of anyone for whom garments become forbidden that become permissible for him until he performs Tawaf of the Ka'bah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd from Hisham"," in abridged form.\n\n[Sahih. Muslim 1321]"""
"10194","(10190) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated from what he recited to Malik.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah informed us; Abu Zakariyya ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya said: I recited to Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, who informed him that Ziyad wrote to 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: \Ibn 'Abbas said: Whoever sends a sacrificial animal becomes forbidden for him what is forbidden for the pilgrim until the sacrificial animal is slaughtered. I have sent my sacrificial animal"," so write to me with your command"," or instruct the one in charge of the sacrificial animal.\"" 'A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""It is not as Ibn 'Abbas said. I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own hands"," then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would garland them with his own hands"," then he would send them with my father"," and nothing that Allah had made permissible for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became forbidden for him until the sacrificial animal was slaughtered.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari in the Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf and others from Malik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1611]"""
"10195","(10191) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us; Abu Yahya 'Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman informed us; Shu'ayb narrated; he said: al-Zuhri said: \The first to remove the blindness from the people and clarify the Sunnah for them in this matter was 'A'ishah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ.\"" Al-Zuhri said: \""Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rah"""
"10196","(10192) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Sadiq — Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris and Abu Nasr — Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Fami — all of them said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas and 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah, one camel on behalf of seven persons, and one cow on behalf of seven persons. [Sahih. Muslim 1318]"
"10197","(10193) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Ma'rūf al-Faqīh informed us — Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us — Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'īd narrated to us — Mālik mentioned it, narrating similarly to the foregoing, except that he said: \at al-Ḥudaybiyyah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Qutaybah"," from Mālik."""
"10198","(10194) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Farrā' and Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Ja'far ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Salām said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Abū Khaythamah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Zuhayr narrated to us — Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said: \We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," entering iḥrām for the Ḥajj"," and with us were women and children. When we arrived at Makkah"," we performed ṭawāf of the House and sa'ī between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded us to share in the camels and cattle — every seven of us contributing to one badanah.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn 'Abdān.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1213]"""
"10199","(10195) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — 'Abd al-Malik narrated from 'Aṭā', from Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh, who said: \We used to perform tamattu' in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) by slaughtering a cow"," with seven of us sharing in it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Hushaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1318]"""
"10200","(10196) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us — 'Affān narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us — Qays ibn Sa'd narrated from 'Aṭā', from Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \A cow is for seven"," and a badanah is for seven.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1318]"""
"10201","(10197) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — al-Zuhrī informed me — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, both of whom narrated to him together, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) set out intending to visit the House, not desiring war, and with him he drove the hady — seventy badanahs for seven hundred men, each badanah on behalf of ten men. Thus did Ibn Isḥāq narrate it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 4/323]"
"10202","(10198) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad — 'Abdullāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to"
"10203","(10199) Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Tahir in Baghdad narrated to us: 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Khuraqi narrated to us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' Abu Zayd al-Harawi narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us — and Abu 'Amr al-Adib narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Qurrah narrated from Qatadah, who said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, \How many were they in the Pledge of al-Ridwan?\"" He said"," \""One thousand five hundred.\"" I said"," \""It has reached us that Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah said"," 'They were one thousand four hundred.'\"" He said"," \""May Allah have mercy upon him"," he has made an error. He narrated to me that they were one thousand five hundred.\"" The wording is that of Abu Dawud"," and the hadith of al-Harawi is to the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in al-Sahih from the hadith of Yazid ibn Zurya' from Ibn Abi 'Arubah from Qatadah"," and he cited the narration of Abu Dawud from Qurrah as corroborating evidence.\n\nAnd Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated from Ibn Abi 'Arubah the opposite of what Yazid ibn Zurya' said"," and Allah knows best. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 3922]"""
"10204","(10200) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan al-'Amiri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, who said: We said to Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, \How many were you on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah?\"" He said"," \""Fifteen hundred.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from 'Abd Allah ibn Idris"," and al-Bukhari recorded it through various chains from Husayn.\n\nAnd al-A'mash narrated from Salim from Jabir"," who said"," \""We were one thousand four hundred.\"" And 'Amr ibn Murrah similarly reported from Salim in one of the two narrations from him. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 5310]"""
"10205","(10201) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani — dictation — narrated to us: Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri in Makkah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'faran narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, who said: 'Amr heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying, \We were on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah one thousand four hundred"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us"," 'You are the best of the people of the earth.' Had I been able to see today"," I would have shown you the location of the tree.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in al-Sahih from 'Ali and Qutaybah"," and Muslim recorded it from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh and others"," all from Ibn 'Uyaynah from 'Amr ibn Dinar. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 3923]"""
"10206","(10202) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak — may Allah have mercy on him — narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to me: 'Amr heard Ibn Abi Awfa, a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who had witnessed the Pledge of al-Ridwan, saying, \We were on that day one thousand three hundred"," and on that day the Muhajirun constituted one-eighth.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi"," and al-Bukhari also pointed to the narration of Abu Dawud"," and this 'Amr is Ibn Murrah"," and the closest narration is that of 'Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir.\n\nAnd Maqil ibn Yasar al-Muzani"," Salmah ibn al-Akwa'"," and al-Bara' ibn 'Azib — all of them — witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah"," except that in one narration from al-Bara' it is stated that they were on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah one thousand four hundred or more"," as though they were in doubt about the excess"," or some of the narrators transmitted it on the authority of al-Bara'"," and Allah knows best. And Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah clarified in the narration of Abu al-Zubayr from him that they slaughtered one camel on behalf of seven and one cow on behalf of seven"," as though they had slaughtered the seventy on behalf of some of them and the cattle on behalf of the remainder"," one cow for every seven"," and Allah knows best. [Sahih. Muslim 1857]"""
"10207","(10202) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Bakr al-Ḥayrīyy informed us, saying: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us: al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to us, from ʿIlbāʾ ibn Aḥmar, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey of ours when the day of sacrifice arrived. We shared in the camel sacrifice, ten persons per camel, and in the cow sacrifice, seven persons per cow.\n\nIt was narrated with this chain, and the hadith of Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir is more authentic than that, for he witnessed al-Ḥudaybiyyah and witnessed the Ḥajj and the ʿUmrah, and he reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to share seven persons in one sacrificial camel (badanah). Thus, it is more deserving of acceptance. And success is from Allah.\n\nIt was narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: We sacrificed on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah seventy sacrificial camels, one camel being shared by ten persons. I do not think this was anything but an error, for al-Firyābī narrated it from al-Thawrī and said: one camel was shared by seven persons.\n\nAnd likewise Mālik ibn Anas, Ibn Jurayj, Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah, and others narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, saying: one camel was shared by seven persons.\n\nAnd likewise ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated from Jābir. Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj gave precedence to their narration when he extracted it over the narration of others.\n\nAs for the hadith of al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsār was alone in mentioning the camel being shared by ten persons in it.\n\nThe hadith of ʿIkrimah is narrated uniquely by Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid from ʿIlbāʾ ibn Aḥmar.\n\nAnd the hadith of Jābir is more authentic than all of that, for he reported their sharing in it during the Ḥajj and the ʿUmrah and at al-Ḥudaybiyyah by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Thus, it is more deserving of acceptance. And success is from Allah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī, 905.]"
"10208","(10204) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: \Ride it.\"" The man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," it is a sacrificial camel.\"" He said: \""Ride it"," woe to you!\"" — on the second or third occasion.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 1604.]"""
"10209","(10205) Abū Ṭāhir al-Imām informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated to us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: While a man was driving a sacrificial camel that had been garlanded, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Ride it.\"" He said: \""It is a sacrificial camel"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Woe to you"," ride it! Woe to you"," ride it!\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1322.]"""
"10210","(10206) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muslim narrated to us: Hishām and Shuʿbah narrated to us, saying: Qatādah narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said to him: \Ride it.\"" He said: \""It is a sacrificial camel.\"" He said: \""Ride it.\"" He said: \""It is a sacrificial camel.\"" He said: \""Ride it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 1605.]"""
"10211","(10207) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Thābit al-Bunānī, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: \Ride it.\"" He said: \""It is a sacrificial camel.\"" He said: \""Ride it\"" — two or three times.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1323.]"""
"10212","(10208) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, who said: Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about riding the sacrificial animal, and he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \Ride it in a kindly manner"," if you are compelled to do so"," until you find another mount.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1324.]"""
"10213","(10209) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī informed us: Salamah ibn Shabīb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan informed us: Maʿqil narrated to us, from Abū al-Zubayr, who said: I asked Jābir about riding the sacrificial animal, and he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \Ride it in a kindly manner"," until you find another mount.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb.\n\nAnd it was narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," that he said: \""If you are compelled to ride your sacrificial camel"," ride it without causing it hardship.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"," 1324.]"""
"10214","(10210) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us: My father narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Zuhayr — meaning Ibn Abī Thābit — who said: I heard al-Mughīrah — meaning Ibn Ḥadaf al-ʿAbsī — heard a man from Hamdān ask ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, about a man who purchased a cow to sacrifice with it, and it gave birth. He said: \Do not drink its milk except what is surplus. And when the day of sacrifice arrives"," slaughter it and its calf on behalf of seven persons.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"10215","(10211) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \When a sacrificial camel gives birth"," its young should be carried along until it is sacrificed with it. And if no mount is found for it"," it should be carried upon its mother until it is sacrificed with her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 84.]"""
"10216","(10212) And with his chain: Mālik narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, that his father said: \If you are compelled to ride your sacrificial camel"," ride it without causing it hardship. And if you are compelled to drink its milk"," drink what remains after its young has been satisfied. And when you sacrifice it"," sacrifice its young along with it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 847.]"""
"10217","(10213) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī — informed us; Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī — in Kūfah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us; al-Tabūdhakī — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl — narrated to us; Wahb ibn Khālid narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed Ẓuhr in Madīnah — four rakʿahs — while we were with him, and he prayed ʿAṣr at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah — two rakʿahs. He then spent the night there until, when morning came, he mounted his riding camel. When it ascended with him upon the elevated ground, he pronounced takbīr, tasbīḥ, and taḥmīd, then he entered into iḥrām for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah together. The people then likewise entered into iḥrām for both. When we arrived, he commanded them, so they converted it into an ʿUmrah, and then they entered into iḥrām for Ḥajj on the day of Tarwiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sacrificed seven camels with his own hand, standing, and he slaughtered in Madīnah two horned, black-and-white rams.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1476]"
"10218","(10214) Abū Naṣr — ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū ʿAmr — Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī — informed us; Abū Muslim narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Thawr, from Rāshid ibn Saʿd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Luḥayy, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qurṭ, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The most excellent of days before Allah is the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)"," then the Day of Qarr (Yawm al-Qarr) — the day on which the people settle down.\"" It is the day that follows the Day of Sacrifice. Five or six sacrificial camels were brought before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and they began approaching him one by one"," whichever he would begin with. When their sides fell (i.e."," they collapsed upon being slaughtered)"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said something softly which I did not understand. I said to the one beside me"," \""What did he say?\"" He said: \""Whoever wishes may cut off (a portion).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1765]"""
"10219","(10215) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us, dictating; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, from Ziyād ibn Jubayr, that:\n\nIbn ʿUmar came upon a man who was slaughtering his sacrificial camel while it was sitting down. He said: \Set it up standing"," shackled — it is the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1627]"""
"10220","(10216) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym said: Abū Bishr narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said:\n\nI saw Ibn ʿUmar slaughtering his sacrificial camel while it was standing, with one of its legs hobbled, resting on three legs. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10221","(10217) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim — Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAlawī — in Kūfah informed us; Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī informed us; Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ẓabyān, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that:\n\nHe used to recite this verse: {fa-dhkurū ism Allāhi ʿalayhā ṣawāff} — meaning, hobbled, standing on three legs. He would say: \Bismillāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhumma minka wa laka.\"" He was asked about their hides"," and he said: \""Give them in charity"," or benefit from them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr 9/152]"""
"10222","(10218) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, who said:\n\nWhoever recites it as ṣawāfin, he says it means hobbled; and whoever recites it as ṣawāff, he says it means standing in rows before him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr 9/152]"
"10223","(10219) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir.\n\nHe said: And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sābit informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Companions used to slaughter the sacrificial camel with its left foreleg hobbled, standing on the remainder of its legs.\n\nThe ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir is connected (mawṣūl), and his ḥadīth from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sābit is disconnected (mursal). [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1767]"
"10224","(10220) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Baṣrī —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, from Ḥarmalah ibn ʿImrān, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Azdī, who said: I heard Ghurfah ibn al-Ḥārith al-Kindī say:\n\nI was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage. The sacrificial camels were brought, and he said: \Call Abū al-Ḥasan for me.\"" So ʿAlī was called. He said to him: \""Take hold of the lower end of the spear.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of the upper end. Then they both thrust it into the camels. When he had finished"," he mounted his mule and seated ʿAlī behind him. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 1766]"""
"10225","(10221) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simarrī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; Qatādah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sacrificed two horned, black-and-white rams. I saw him placing his foot upon their flanks, pronouncing the name of Allah and saying Allāhu Akbar, then he slaughtered them with his own hand.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam, and Muslim narrated it through two other chains from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5233]"
"10226","(10222) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ — narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slaughtered a cow on behalf of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) on the Day of Sacrifice.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1319]"
"10227","(10223) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū al-Qāsim Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mūsawī in Makkah narrated to us — Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Wuhaib ibn Khālid narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, regarding the description of the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \When the Day of Naḥr arrived"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered sixty-three camels"," and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) slaughtered the remainder. There had been one hundred camels with him. Then a piece of meat was taken from each camel and all of it was cooked together. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) ate from it and drank from its broth.\"" Muslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the Ḥadīth of Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl from Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"10228","(10224) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us — Muḥammad and Yaʿlā, the two sons of ʿUbayd, said — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his camel"," he slaughtered thirty with his own hands and commanded me"," so I slaughtered the rest.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār related it thus"," and the narration of Jaʿfar is more authentic"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd extracted it"," 1764]"""
"10229","(10225) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ushtah al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us — al-Naḍr ibn Ismāʿīl, Imām of the Mosque of al-Kūfah, narrated to us — (ḥ) and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh, Abū Muslim, narrated to us — Maʿqil ibn Mālik narrated to us — al-Naḍr ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Abū Ḥamzah al-Thumālī, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O Fāṭimah"," stand by your udḥiyyah and witness it"," for indeed every sin you have committed shall be forgiven with the first drop of its blood that falls"," and say: 'Verily"," my ṣalāh"," my sacrifice"," my life"," and my death are for Allah"," Lord of the worlds; He has no partner"," and by that I am commanded"," and I am of the Muslims.'\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," is this exclusively for you and your Ahl al-Bayt"," or for the Muslims in general?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Nay"," for the Muslims in general.\"" The wording is that of the Ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān. We did not record it from the Ḥadīth of ʿImrān except through this chain"," and it is not strong. And it has been related from ʿAmr ibn Khālid through his chain from ʿAlī"," and ʿAmr ibn Khālid is abandoned (matrūk). And it has been related from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""Let not a Jew or a Christian slaughter the Muslim's sacrifice.\"" And from Ibn ʿAbbās: \""He disliked that a Jew or a Christian should slaughter the Muslim's sacrifice.\"" And we consider reprehensible what they considered reprehensible"," and if one does so"," there is no repetition required upon its owner"," because of the statement of Allah"," the Exalted: {And the food of those who have been given the Book is lawful for you} [al-Māʾidah: 5] — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," their slaughtered animals — and we shall mention it in its entirety"," if Allah wills"," in the Book of Sacrifices. [Munkar. Al-Ḥākim extracted it: 4/247]"""
"10230","(10226) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us — Abū al-Azhar narrated to us — Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to me — Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated to us from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \Every part of Minā is a place of slaughter"," and every day of al-Tashrīq is a day of slaughter.\"" [Munkar. Aḥmad extracted it"," 4/82]"""
"10231","(10227) He said, and Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bukayr al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us — Suwayd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The days of al-Tashrīq are all days of slaughter.\"" The first is mursal"," and this is not strong"," because its narrator is Suwayd"," and Abū Muʿayd related it from Sulaymān from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jubayr"," and this is the position of Aṭāʾ and al-Ḥasan. We shall mention it in its entirety"," if Allah wills"," in the Book of Uḍāḥī. [Munkar. See the preceding]"""
"10232","(10228) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, meaning al-Shaybānī, narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \I stood here at ʿArafah"," and all of ʿArafah is a place of standing; and I stood here at Jamʿ"," and all of Jamʿ is a place of standing; and I slaughtered here"," and all of Minā is a place of slaughter. So slaughter in your encampments.\"" Muslim related it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"10233","(10229) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us — Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Aṭāʾ, from Jābir, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \All of ʿArafah is a place of standing"," and all of al-Muzdalifah is a place of standing"," and all of Minā is a place of slaughter"," and all the paths of Makkah are a road and a place of slaughter.\"" Yaʿqūb said: \""Usāmah ibn Zayd is considered trustworthy and reliable by the people of his city"," al-Madīnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd extracted it"," 937]"""
"10234","(10230) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us — Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Aṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: \The places of slaughter for the camels are in Makkah"," but it has been purified from bloodshed"," and Minā is part of Makkah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih]"""
"10235","(10231) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Mihrajānī therein informed us — Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, Abū al-Ḥasan, narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us — Aṭāʾ narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: \The place of slaughter is in Makkah"," but it has been purified from bloodshed.\"" He said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās"," the speaker"," said: 'And Makkah is part of Minā.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10236","(10232) He said, and Ibn Jurayj said — Aṭāʾ narrated to me: \Ibn ʿAbbās used to slaughter in Makkah"," and Ibn ʿUmar did not use to slaughter in Makkah; he used to slaughter in Minā.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10237","Nāfiʿ reported that Ibn ʿUmar used to perform the sacrifice at the Manḥar (place of sacrifice). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10238","ʿUbayd Allāh reported, meaning the Manḥar of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. And it has been narrated previously from ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿUmarī from Nāfiʿ that Ibn ʿUmar used to sacrifice in Makkah near al-Marwah and to sacrifice in Minā near the Manḥar. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10239","Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father from Jābir, describing the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Then he went to the Manḥar and sacrificed sixty-three camels with his own hand"," and he gave the remainder to ʿAlī"," who sacrificed what was left"," and he included him in his hady. Then he commanded that a piece be taken from each camel"," and they were placed in a pot and cooked"," and he ate from its meat and drank from its broth. Then he proceeded to the House (the Kaʿbah).\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""
"10240","Miqsam narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed one hundred camels during the Ḥajj. He sacrificed sixty of them with his own hand and commanded that the remainder be sacrificed"," so they were sacrificed. Then a piece was taken from each camel and gathered in a pot"," and he ate from it and drank from its broth.\"" It was said to Muḥammad: \""So that he would have eaten from all of them?\"" Muḥammad said: \""Yes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than him. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/314]"""
"10241","ʿAmrah narrated from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you forbade us from eating the meat of the sacrificial animals after three days.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I only forbade you on account of the group of people who had come at the time of the sacrifice. Eat"," give in charity"," and store.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1971]"""
"10242","ʿAlqamah said: \ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd sent me with a voluntary hady and said to me: 'You and your companions eat one-third"," give one-third in charity"," and send one-third to the family of my brother ʿUtbah.'\"" Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī narrated it; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ḥabīb from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr: 9702]"""
"10243","Here is the translated text in English:

It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him- said: ""Indeed, the greatest of days with Allah is Yawm al-Nahar, then Yawm al-Qar', and it is the one that will be followed. He said: 'We were given five or six dates, and we would eat them and then they would be taken away from us, and we would not know what to do with them. Then, when their time had come, they would be taken away, and I would not know what to do with them. I said to the one who would be followed, ""Whoever wants to take them, let him take them."""," the greatest of days before Allah is the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)"," then the Day of al-Qarr"," which is the one that follows it.\"" He said: \""Five or six camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and they began to draw near to him"," whichever one he would begin with. When their sides fell"," he spoke a word softly that I did not understand. I said to the one sitting next to me: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say?' He said: 'He said: \""Whoever wishes may cut off (a piece).\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated under no. 10214]"""
"10244","Muslim al-Muṣabbiḥ reported that he saw Ibn ʿUmar depart (after the sacrifice) and he did not eat anything from the meat of his sacrifice. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10245","Ḥuṣayn said: \Mujāhid was asked: 'Does a man eat from his sacrifice?' He said: 'It does not harm him if he does not eat from it. His statement"," the Most High"," {So eat from it} is like His statement"," {And when you have exited iḥram"," then hunt}. So whoever wishes may hunt.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10246","ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to stand over his camels (of sacrifice) and to distribute all of them—their meat, their skins, and their coverings—to the poor, and not to give the butcher anything from them as his fee. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1630]"
"10247","(10243) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu 'Uthman — Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan — informed us that Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, dictating: Yahya ibn Muhammad and Ja'far ibn Muhammad, known as al-Turk, and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab — Yahya said: \Yahya ibn Yahya informed us","\"" and the other two said: \""Abu Khaythamah informed us"," from 'Abd al-Karim"," from Mujahid"," from 'Abd Rahman ibn Abi Layla"," from 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to stand by his sacrificial animals"," to give in charity their meat"," their skins"," and their covering"," and that the slaughterer should not be given anything from them.\"" Then he said: \""We shall give him from our own.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1317]"""
"10248","(332) Chapter: That which has been designated as a sacrificial offering should not be replaced, whether for better or for worse from it."
"10249","(10244) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — Muhammad ibn Bakr — Abu Dawud — al-Nufayli — Muhammad ibn Salamah — Abu 'Abd al-Rahim — Jahm ibn al-Jarud — Salim ibn 'Abd Allah — from his father, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, offered a noble she-camel as a sacrifice and was given three hundred dinars for it. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I offered a noble she-camel as a sacrifice and was given three hundred dinars for it. Should I sell it and buy sacrificial camels with its price?\"" — or he said \""a sacrificial camel\"" — \""I am uncertain.\"" He ﷺ said: \""No"," sacrifice it.\"" Abu Dawud said: \""Abu 'Abd al-Rahim is Khalid ibn Yazid"," the maternal uncle of Muhammad ibn Salamah"," from whom Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated.\"" [Da'if. Abu Dawud 1756]"""
"10250","(10245) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub — Sulayman ibn Harb and Musaddad — Hammad ibn Zayd — and Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab — Abu al-Rabi' — Hammad ibn Zayd — Ayyub — and Abu 'Abd Allah — Abu al-Walid — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar — 'Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri — Hammad — from Ayyub, who said: \I heard Mujahid narrating from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla"," from Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah"," who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me during the time of al-Hudaybiyyah while I was kindling a fire beneath a cooking pot"," and lice were falling upon my face. He said: 'Do the vermin of your head harm you?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Shave your head and fast three days"," or feed six poor persons"," or offer a sacrifice.'\"" Ayyub said: \""I do not know with which of these he began.\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 3954]"""
"10251","(10246) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — Harun ibn Sulayman al-Isfahani — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi — Shu'bah — I heard Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard 'Ubayd ibn Fayruz saying: I said to al-Bara': \Narrate to me regarding what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked or prohibited concerning sacrificial animals.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said\"" — with his hand"," and my hand was shorter than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — \""Four defects are not permissible in sacrificial animals: a one-eyed animal whose blindness is manifest"," a sick animal whose illness is manifest"," a lame animal whose lameness is manifest"," and a broken bone whose marrow is not contained.\"" He said: \""I dislike that there should be a defect in the ear or the horn.\"" He said: \""Whatever you dislike"," leave it"," but do not prohibit it upon others.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 2802]"""
"10252","(10247) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq — Abu 'Abd Allah al-Shaybani — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab — Ja'far ibn 'Awn — Mis'ar — from Abu Husayn: that Ibn al-Zubayr saw his sacrificial animals and among them was a one-eyed she-camel. He said: \If the defect occurred after you purchased them"," then proceed with them; but if the defect was present before you purchased them"," then replace them.\"" [Sahih]"""
"10253","(10248) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah — Yahya ibn Yahya — 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id — Abu al-Tayyah al-Duba'i — Musa ibn Salamah al-Hudhali, who said: I set out with Sinan ibn Salamah performing 'Umrah. Sinan had with him a sacrificial camel which he was driving. It became exhausted on the road, and he was preoccupied with concern for it — how could he bring it if it became incapacitated? He said: \When I reach the city"," I will seek clarification about that.\"" I awoke"," and when we descended upon al-Bat-ha'"," he said: \""Go to Ibn 'Abbas so that we may speak with him.\"" He mentioned the matter of his sacrificial camel to him. He said: \""You have asked one who is knowledgeable. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent sixteen sacrificial camels with a man and commanded him regarding them. He went"," then returned and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what should I do if any of them becomes incapacitated?' He said: 'Slaughter it"," then dip its sandals in its blood"," and place it upon its side. Neither you nor any member of your party should eat from it.'\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1325]"""
"10254","(10249) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah — Yahya ibn Yahya — Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah — Abu al-Tayyah — Musa ibn Salamah — from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent eighteen sacrificial camels with a man. He mentioned it with a narration similar to that of 'Abd al-Warith, but he did not mention the story, and he said \azhafa\"" instead of \""ubdi'a.\"" [Sahih]"""
"10255","(10250) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari in Baghdad — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar — Ahmad ibn Mansur — 'Abd al-Razzaq — Ma'mar — Qatadah — Sinan ibn Salamah — from Ibn 'Abbas: that Dhu'ayb informed him that the Prophet ﷺ sent two sacrificial camels with him and commanded him: if any affliction befell them, he should slaughter them, then dip their sandals in their blood, and strike the side of each with its sandal, and leave them for the people, neither commanding anything regarding them nor eating from them himself, nor any of his companions. [Sahih. Muslim 1326]"
"10256","(10251) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — Abu al-'Abbas, that is al-Asamm — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi — Muhammad ibn al-Minhal — Yazid ibn Zurai' — Sa'id — Qatadah — Sinan ibn Salamah — from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that Dhu'ayb al-Khuza'i narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the sacrificial camels with him and commanded him: if any affliction befell any of them, he should slaughter it, dip its sandal in its blood, and strike its side with it. He commanded him not to eat anything from it, nor any member of his party, and to distribute it. [Sahih. Previously referenced]"
"10257","Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn reported to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from a man from the tribe of Aslam, who said: He said, \O Messenger of Allah"," what should I do with a sacrificial animal (hadī) that becomes injured?\"" He (ﷺ) commanded him to slaughter it"," then to place its sandal (i.e."," the garland around its neck) in its blood"," and to leave it between itself and the people so that they may eat from it.\""\n\n[Sound. Reported by Mālik (851)]"""
"10258","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us; Sufyān reported to us, from Hishām, from his father, from Nājiyah al-Aslamī: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a sacrificial animal (hadī) with him and said, \If it becomes injured"," then slaughter it"," then dip its sandal (i.e."," the garland) in its blood"," then leave it between itself and the people.\""\n\n[Sound. Reported by al-Tirmidhī (910)]"""
"10259","Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik reported to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: Whoever leads a camel as a voluntary offering and it becomes injured, then he slaughters it and leaves it between it and the people so that they may eat from it, then there is nothing upon him. But if he eats from it or commands that it be eaten, then he must bear its cost.\n\n[Sound. Reported by Mālik (852)]"
"10260","He said: And Mālik narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dīlī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, the same as that."
"10261","Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik reported to us, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: Whoever offers a sacrificial camel (badanah) and it goes astray or dies, if it was a vow (nadhr), then he must replace it, and if it was voluntary (tatawwuʿ), then if he wishes he may replace it, and if he wishes he may leave it.\n\nThis is the sound version, as a mawqūf narration. Likewise, Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated it from Nāfiʿ. [Reported by Mālik (853)]"
"10262","And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Bishr informed us; al-Muʿāfā ibn ʿImrān reported to us, from al-Awzāʿī, from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever offers a voluntary sacrificial camel (badanah) and it becomes injured"," then there is no replacement upon him. But if it was a vow (nadhr)"," then a replacement is upon him.\""\n\nIt was narrated with this chain from al-Awzāʿī"," and I think it is an error (wahm). For others narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir al-Aslamī. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir is one through whom mawqūf narrations may be elevated (to the Prophet ﷺ). And Allah knows best.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"10263","Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed us; my father informed me; al-Awzāʿī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; Bishr ibn Bakr reported to us, from al-Awzāʿī; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir informed me; Nāfiʿ, the freed slave of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever offers a voluntary sacrifice and it goes astray"," then if he wishes he may replace it"," and if he wishes he may leave it. And if it was a vow (nadhr)"," then let him replace it.\""\n\nAnd al-Qarqasānī narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"," but he contradicted the group (jamāʿah) in its text (matn).\n\n[Munkar. Reported by Ibn Khuzaymah (2579)]"""
"10264","Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed it to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz and Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us; Muḥammad ibn Muṣʿab al-Qarqasānī reported to us, from al-Awzāʿī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever offers a voluntary sacrificial animal (hadī) and it becomes injured"," then if he wishes he may eat from it"," and if he wishes he may leave it. And if it was a vow (nadhr)"," then let him replace it.\""\n\nAnd the correct version is the narration of the group (jamāʿah) from al-Awzāʿī"," and the sound version is the narration of Mālik from Nāfiʿ. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Munkar — the narration of al-Qarqasānī"," as reported by al-Dāraquṭnī (2/242)]"""
"10265","And the first wording was narrated from Ibn Abī al-Zinād, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, as a marfūʿ narration, except that its chain is weak.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed it to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us; the Qāḍī al-Maḥāmilī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shabīb informed us; ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Saʿīd informed us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, and he mentioned in it: \If it goes astray…\""\n\n[Munkar. Reported by al-Dāraquṭnī (2/242)]"""
"10266","Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Isfārayīnī informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; my grandfather informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bazīʿ informed us; Ziyād, meaning Ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bakkāʾī, informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who is Ibn Abī Laylā, reported to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Abī al-Khayl, from Abī Qatādah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever leads a voluntary sacrificial animal (hadī) and it becomes injured"," then let him not eat from it"," for if he eats from it"," then he must bear its cost. Rather"," let him slaughter it"," then let him dip its sandal (i.e."," the garland) in its blood"," then let him strike its side with it. And if it was an obligatory sacrificial animal (hadī wājib)"," then let him eat from him if he wishes"," for it must necessarily be fulfilled.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Khuzaymah said: This hadith is mursal (disconnected) between Abī al-Khayl and Abī Qatādah — there is a man (missing) between them.\n\n[Munkar. Reported by Ibn Khuzaymah (2580)]"""
"10267","Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, that two of her sacrificial camels went missing. She sent ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr with two other camels, and she slaughtered them. Then, after that, she found the two that had gone missing, and she slaughtered them as well."
"10268","Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Journeying is undertaken to only three mosques: al-Masjid al-Ḥarām"," al-Masjid al-Aqṣā"," and my mosque.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah."""
"10269","Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me that ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas narrated to them that Salmān al-Agharr narrated to him that he heard Abū Hurayrah reporting that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Journeying is undertaken to only three mosques: the Mosque of the Kaʿbah"," my mosque"," and the Mosque of Ilyās (i.e."," al-Aqṣā). And prayer in my mosque is more beloved to me than a thousand prayers in any other"," except the Mosque of the Kaʿbah.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī"," and it is also established from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and others from the Prophet (ﷺ)."""
"10270","Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) halted his mount at al-Baṭḥāʾ which is at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, and he prayed there. Nāfiʿ said: And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to do that. Al-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim recorded it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā."
"10271","Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Abū Ḍamrah — Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ — narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that whenever he returned from Ḥajj or ʿUmrah, he would halt his mount at al-Baṭḥāʾ which is at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah — the place where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to halt his mount. Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Musayyibī from Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ."
"10272","Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Abū Saʿīd al-Sukkārī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl — that is, Ibn Masʿūd al-Jaḥdarī — narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṣarrām — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Masʿūd al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us: al-Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān al-Numayrī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us: Sālim narrated to me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was shown in his place of overnight stay at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, in the bottom of the valley, and it was said to him: \You are in a blessed al-Baṭḥāʾ.\"" Mūsā said: And Sālim halted his mount at the same halting place where ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to halt"," seeking to locate the place where the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had stayed overnight. It was lower down than the mosque which is at the bottom of the valley"," between it and the road"," in the middle of that area. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. Al-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr from al-Fuḍayl"," and Muslim recorded it from the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar from Mūsā."""
"10273","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us. He said: Abū Dāwūd said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Madanī say: \The place of overnight stay (al-Muʿarras) is at six miles from Madīnah.\"""""
"10274","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Adamī al-Qāriʾ — in Baghdad, in his mosque, narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, the companion of al-Narsī, narrated to us: Shabābah ibn Sawwār al-Fazārī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to follow the traces of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and pray in those places, to the extent that when the Prophet (ﷺ) dismounted beneath a tree, Ibn ʿUmar would pour water under it so that it would not dry out."
"10275","Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Sukkārī — in Baghdad, informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿAbbās al-Tarqafī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd — Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ — narrated to us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ narrated to us, from Abī Ṣakhr, from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no one who sends salām upon me except that Allah returns my spirit to me so that I may return the salām to him.\"""""
"10276","Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Mihrajānī, the son of Abū ʿAlī al-Saqqāʾ — in Naysābūr, and Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ al-Mihrajānī — there, both informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, that when Ibn ʿUmar returned from a journey, he would enter the mosque and then come to the grave and say: \Al-salāmu ʿalayka yā Rasūl Allāh. Al-salāmu ʿalayka yā Abā Bakr. Al-salāmu ʿalayka yā abāh.\"""""
"10277","(10272) And Abū Aḥmad al-'Adl informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from 'Abd Allāh ibn Dīnār that he said: I saw 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar standing at the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, then offering salāms upon the Prophet ﷺ and supplicating, and then supplicating for Abū Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Mālik, 397]"
"10278","(10273) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Sawwār ibn Maymūn, Abū al-Jarrāh al-'Abdī, said: A man from the family of 'Umar narrated to me from 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Whoever visits my grave — or he said: Whoever visits me — I shall be an intercessor or a witness for him. And whoever dies in one of the two Ḥarams, Allah shall raise him among the secure ones on the Day of Resurrection. This is an unknown (majhūl) isnād. [Munkar. Reported by al-Ṭayālisī, 65]"
"10279","(10274) Abū Muḥammad 'Abd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Nāfi' ibn Isḥāq al-Khuzā'ī in Makkah narrated to us — al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Muḥammad al-Janadī narrated to us — Salama ibn Shabīb narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzāq narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn Sulaymān, Abū 'Umar, narrated from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym from Mujāhid from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever performs Ḥajj and then visits my grave after my death is as if he visited me during my lifetime. [Bāṭil. Reported by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr, 1397]"
"10280","(10275) Abū Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn 'Adī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — 'Alī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — and Abū Aḥmad informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Baghawī narrated to us — Abū al-Rabī' al-Zahrānī narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us, and he mentioned it. Ḥafṣ alone transmitted it, and he is weak (ḍa'īf). [Bāṭil]"
"10281","(10276) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us — 'Abd Allāh, that is, al-Qa'nabī, from Mālik from Zayd ibn Rabāḥ from Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Agharr, and from Mālik from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Salmān from his father al-Agharr, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, save al-Masjid al-Ḥarām. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim reported it from the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Musayyib and others from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī, 1133]"
"10282","(10277) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū 'Uthmān Sa'īd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdān and Abū Muḥammad 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqri' said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn 'Affān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Umar from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is superior to a thousand prayers in other mosques, save al-Masjid al-Ḥarām. Muslim reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from 'Ubayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 395]"
"10283","(10278) Abū Muḥammad 'Abd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū Muḥammad 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuhrī al-Qāḍī in Makkah narrated to us — Abū Yaḥyā 'Abd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ḥabīb al-Mu'allim from 'Aṭā' ibn Abī Rabāḥ from 'Abd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, save al-Masjid al-Ḥarām, and a prayer in al-Masjid al-Ḥarām is better than a hundred prayers in my mosque. [Qawī. Reported by Aḥmad, 4/3]"
"10284","(10279) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-'Adl informed us — Abū Aḥmad Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-'Abbās narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd al-Raḥīm ibn Danūqā informed us — Zakariyyā ibn 'Adī narrated to us — Ḥātim narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Ṣakhr from Abū Salamah from Abū Sa'īd al-Khudrī, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the mosque that was founded upon taqwā, and he said: It is this mosque of mine. Muslim reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Ḥātim ibn Ismā'īl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1398]"
"10285","(10280) And Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū Sa'īd ibn al-A'rābī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Kūfī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān al-Ḍabbī narrated from 'Abd al-Malik from 'Aṭā' from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is equivalent to a thousand prayers in other mosques, save al-Masjid al-Ḥarām, for it is superior. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Ibn al-A'rābī in his Mu'jam, 1/no. 472]"
"10286","(10281) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqri' and Abū 'Uthmān Sa'īd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdān said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn 'Affān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated from 'Ubayd Allāh — (ḥ) and Abū 'Abd Allāh informed us — Abū al-'Abbās narrated to us — al-'Abbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us — Abū 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Burshān al-'Abdī informed us — 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Umar narrated from Khubayb ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān from Ḥafṣ ibn 'Āṣim from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: That which is between my grave and my minbar — and in the narration of Ibn 'Ubayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed, that which is between my minbar and my house is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my ḥawḍ. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim reported it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of 'Ubayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī, 1138]"
"10287","(10282) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us in Ṭūs: Abū Muḥammad ibn Shawdhab al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us: Sufyān and Mālik ibn Anas narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm from his paternal uncle ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd al-Māzinī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from Mālik.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1137]"""
"10288","(10283) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah narrated to us: Abū Mūsā narrated to us: Makkī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: Salama, meaning Ibn al-Akwʿ, would seek to pray at the pillar near the muṣḥaf. I said: \O Abū Muslim"," I see you seeking to pray at this pillar.\"" He said: \""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) seeking to pray at it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 480]"""
"10289","(10284) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz informed us in Baghdad: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Fākihī informed us in Makkah: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarra narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Jārī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from ʿĪsā ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed iʿtikāf, his bed or couch was placed at the Pillar of Repentance (Ustuwānat al-Tawbah), towards the qibla, and he would lean against it, according to what ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz stated.\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 1774]"
"10290","(10285) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣabghī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: my brother narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān from Nāfiʿ: that Ibn ʿUmar used to say regarding the pillar to which Abū Lubābah had tied himself: \It is the third from the grave"," and it is the third from the courtyard.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"10291","(10286) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl narrated from Hishām ibn Saʿd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad informed us: Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated from Abī Ḥāzim from Sahl ibn Saʿd that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \My pulpit is upon a gateway from the gateways of Paradise.\"" In the narration of al-Ṣaghānī"," he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said"," and he mentioned it"," raising it (as a marfūʿ narration). Hishām raised it"," but ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim did not raise it"," in the more authentic of the two narrations from him.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 5/335]"""
"10292","(10287) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāyinī informed us there: Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated from his father from Sahl, who said: \We used to say that the pulpit is upon a gateway from the gateways of Paradise.\"" Sahl said: \""Do you know what al-turʿah is?\"" We said: \""Yes"," it is the gate.\"" He said: \""Yes"," it is the gate.\"" It has also been narrated from him as a marfūʿ narration with different wording.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"10293","(10288) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us, saying: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bukayr al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated from Abī Ḥāzim from Sahl ibn Saʿd from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise"," and the legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.\""\n\nIt was differed upon regarding Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: it was said from him from Abū Hurayrah"," and it was said from him from Umm Salamah. And it was differed upon regarding its text (matn).\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous hadith]"""
"10294","(10289) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaʿqūb al-Iyādī informed us in Baghdad: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf ibn Khallād narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, meaning Ibn ʿAlqamah, narrated from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \This pulpit of mine is upon a gateway from the gateways of Paradise.\"" Saʿīd added in his narration: It was said to Muḥammad: \""What is al-turʿah?\"" He said: \""That which is elevated.\"" ʿAmmār al-Duhnī contradicted him regarding Abū Salamah"," in both its chain (isnād) and its text (matn).\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 31729]"""
"10295","(10290) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī narrated to us in Baghdad: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb al-Dabbī narrated to us: Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmmār al-Duhnī from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Umm Salamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.\"" In the narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said.\n\nAnd similarly"," Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated it from ʿAmmār al-Duhnī. And it was narrated from Zāʾidah from ʿAmmār from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah with the wording of the hadith of Umm Salamah.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī 696]"""
"10296","(10291) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Ḥārithī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Fāmī, and Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muʿāwiyah informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to come to Qubāʾ, walking and riding. And in the hadith of Yaḥyā: riding and walking.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Yaḥyā, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Mūsā from Yaḥyā.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Bukhārī 1136]"
"10297","(10292) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us — my father narrated to us — 'Ubayd Allah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to the Mosque of Quba' riding and on foot. Ibn Numayr added in his narration: And he would pray two rak'ahs therein.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr. Al-Bukhari said: 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr added it and mentioned it, and he [al-Bukhari] extracted it from the hadith of Yahya al-Qattan. [Sahih; previously referenced.]"
"10298","(10293) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duham narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hazim informed us — 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Abu Nu'aym and Qabisah narrated to us — from Sufyan — from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to the Mosque of Quba' riding and on foot.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym, and Muslim extracted it from another route from al-Thawri. [Sahih; previously referenced.]"
"10299","(10294) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bashran in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us — from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn 'Umar would not pray the Duha prayer except that he would come to the Mosque of Quba' and pray therein, because the Prophet ﷺ used to visit it every Saturday.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Sufyan, without mentioning the Duha prayer. [Sahih; Muslim 1399.]"
"10300","(10295) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan al-'Amiri narrated to us — Abu Usamah narrated to us — 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to me — Abu al-Abrad Musa ibn Sulaym, a mawla of Banu Khatmah, narrated to me — that he heard Usayd ibn Zahir al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, narrating from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: A prayer performed in the Mosque of Quba' is equal to an 'Umrah.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Tarikh from 'Abd Allah ibn Abu Shaybah from Abu Usamah, except that he said in its matn: \Whoever comes to the Mosque of Quba' and prays therein"," it shall be equal to an 'Ummah.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi; Ibn Majah (1411) extracted it.]"""
"10301","(10296) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me — Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-'Anzi informed me — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah al-Madini narrated to us — Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us — Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Amir ibn Sa'd and 'A'ishah bint Sa'd both saying: We heard Sa'd saying: That I should pray in the Mosque of Quba' is more beloved to me than that I should pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. [Sahih; al-Hakim (3/13) extracted it.]"
"10302","(10297) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ja'far al-Madani narrated to us — from Sharik ibn Abi Namir — from 'Ata' ibn Yasar — from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would go out in the latter part of the night to al-Baqi' and say: \Peace be upon you"," O abode of a believing people. What has been promised to you shall come to you tomorrow"," deferred. And we"," if Allah wills"," shall join you. O Allah"," forgive the people of Baqi' al-Gharqad.\"""""
"10303","(10298) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu al-Walid narrated to us — Hamid ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us — Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ja'far (h). And Abu al-Walid informed me — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Isma'il — and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya, Yahya ibn Ayyub, and Qutaybah."
"10304","(10299) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from his original copy informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ma'n narrated to us — Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar narrated to us — that he and a man called Ibn Yusuf from Banu Tamim passed by Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Yusuf said: We find with other people narrations that we do not find with you. He [Rabi'ah] said: I have many narrations, but Rabi'ah ibn al-Hudayr used to keep the company of Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah, and he claimed that he never heard Talhah narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ anything except a single hadith. Rabi'ah said: I asked him, \What is it?\"" He said: Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah said to me: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and when we overlooked the Harrah of Waqim"," we descended from it"," and lo"," there were graves in a curved area. We said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," these are the graves of our brothers.\"" He said: \""These are the graves of our companions.\"" Then we went out"," and when we came to the graves of the martyrs"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \""These are the graves of our brothers.\"" [Hasan; Abu Dawud (2043) extracted it.]"""
"10305","(10300) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Jabir al-Saqati narrated to us — Hamid, meaning Ibn Yahya, narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ma'n al-Madani al-Khuza'i narrated to us — Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar narrated to us — from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman — from Rabi'ah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hudayr, who said: I never heard Talhah ibn 'Ubayd Allah narrate any hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one single hadith, and he mentioned it with a similar meaning."
"10306","(10301) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir al-Sa'igh narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us — 'Isa ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me — from Abu Mawdud — from Nafi', who said: I saw Ibn 'Umar when he went to the graves of the martyrs on his she-camel, turning it this way and that. He was asked about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on this road on his she-camel, and I said: Perhaps my camel's hoof will fall upon the hoof of his camel. [Hasan.]"
"10307","(10302) Abū Isḥāq — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, the Imām, may Allah have mercy upon him — informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Jawsqānī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ibn Abī al-Mawāli narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach us the prayer of Istikhārah for all matters just as he would teach us a Sūrah from the Qurʾān. He would say: \When one of you intends to do something"," let him perform two rakʿahs of voluntary prayer"," then let him say: 'O Allah"," I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge"," and I seek ability through Your power"," and I ask You from Your immense bounty. For You have power and I have none"," and You know and I do not know"," and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah"," if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion"," my livelihood"," and the outcome of my affairs' — or he said"," 'in my immediate and my ultimate affairs' — 'then decree it for me"," make it easy for me"," and bless me in it. And if You know that this matter is harmful for me in my religion"," my livelihood"," and the outcome of my affairs' — or he said"," 'in my immediate and my ultimate affairs' — 'then turn it away from me and turn me away from it"," and decree for me the good wherever it may be"," then make me content with it.'\"" He said: \""And he should name his need.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1109]"""
"10308","(10303) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar al-Bakrāwī and Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād from ʢāṣim al-Aḥwal from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sarjis, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) would travel, he would say: \O Allah"," You are the Companion in travel and the Deputy over the family. O Allah"," accompany us in our journey and deputize for us over our family. O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel"," from the grief of a sorrowful return"," from loss after prosperity"," from the supplication of the oppressed"," and from an evil sight regarding family and wealth.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1343]"""
"10309","(10304) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar both said: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Simāk narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) intended to set out on a journey — Ziyād did not say \on a journey\"" — he would say: \""O Allah"," You are the Companion in travel and the Deputy over the family. O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from distress in travel and from sorrow upon return. O Allah"," contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us.\"" And when he intended to return"," he would say: \""We are returning"," repentant to our Lord"," praising Him.\"" And when he entered his family"," he would say: \""Repentance"," repentance to our Lord"," turning back"," leaving no sin upon us.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/255]"""
"10310","(10305) And ʿAlī informed us: Aḥmad narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Simāk, and he mentioned it with its chain, similar to the ḥadīth of ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar."
"10311","(10306) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī al-Rāzī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥātim narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Isḥāq al-Hamdānī narrated to us: al-Muḥāribī narrated from ʿUmar ibn Musāwir al-ʿIjlī from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would never intend a journey except that when he rose from his sitting place, he would say: \O Allah"," by You I set out"," to You I turn"," and in You I seek protection. You are my trust and my hope. O Allah"," suffice me against what concerns me and what I do not concern myself with"," and what You know better than I. O Allah"," grant me piety"," forgive my sin"," and direct me to goodness wherever I turn.\"" Then he would depart. And this is what the common people say: \""By You I set out.\""\n\nAnd Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," used to say: The correct form is \""ibtasartu","\"" meaning \""I began my journey.\"""""
"10312","(10307) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed me: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated to me from his father, who used to say: Rarely would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out on a journey for jihād or otherwise except on a Thursday.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ within the ḥadīth of the repentance of Kaʿb ibn Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2789]"
"10313","(10308) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Dīnawarī Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yūnus ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik from Kaʿb ibn Mālik, who said: Rarely would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out on a journey except on a Thursday.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad from Ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"10314","(10309) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Khalīl al-Rāzī narrated to us: Abū Ghassān Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr and ʿAṭāʾ from al-Shaʿbī from Umm Salamah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would leave his house, he would say: \In the name of Allah. O Allah"," I seek refuge in You lest I should slip or be led astray"," or wrong or be wronged"," or act ignorantly or be treated with ignorance.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 5094]"""
"10315","(10310) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says: 'In the name of Allah"," I place my trust in Allah; there is no power and no strength except with Allah","' it will be said to him: 'You have been protected and you have been sufficed.'\""\n\nAnd Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated it from Ibn Jurayj and added in it: \""When he leaves his house.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 5095"," al-Tirmidhī 3427]"""
"10316","(10311) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ, the judge in Kūfah, informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Jarīr from Qazaʿah, who said: Ibn ʿUmar sent me on an errand, and he took my hand and said: \I bid you farewell just as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bade me farewell when he sent me on an errand.\"" He said: \""I entrust to Allah your religion"," your trust"," and the seals of your deeds.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 2600]"""
"10317","(10312) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb in Hamadhān informed us; Isḥāq ibn Aḥmad al-Khazzāz narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān narrated to us that he heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad say: I was with Ibn ʿUmar when a man came to him and said, \I intend to travel.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said"," \""Wait"," so that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to bid us farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion"," your trust"," and the seals of your deeds.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2531)]"""
"10318","(10313) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī informed me from Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was intending to travel, and he greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, \I enjoin you to observe taqwā of Allah and to say 'Allāhu Akbar' upon every elevation.\"" When the man departed"," he said"," \""O Allah"," fold up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3445)"," Ibn Mājah (2771)]"""
"10319","(10314) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; and Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-Raqqī narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; they both said: Sufyān narrated to us from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from Sālim from his father: ʿUmar sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for ʿUmrah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, \Include us in your righteous supplications and do not forget us.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1198)"," al-Tirmidhī (3562)]"""
"10320","(10315) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuhrī al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, ʿAmr ibn Marzūq, and Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah informed us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh informed us from Sālim from his father from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): He sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for ʿUmrah, and he granted him permission and said, \Do not forget us"," O my brother"," in your supplications.\"" He (ʿUmar) said"," \""He said to me a word for which I would not love to have the world in exchange.\"" Shuʿbah said"," \""I later met ʿĀṣim in al-Madīnah and he narrated it to me"," and in it [the Prophet said]"," 'Include us"," O my brother"," in your supplications.'\"" In the narration of Ibn Yūsuf"," he said in his isnād: \""I heard Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrate from his father from ʿUmar","\"" and in its matn: \""He said to me a word I would not love to have the world in exchange","\"" with the word \""ukhiyya\"" (my brother) appearing at both the beginning and the end from his perspective. [Ḍaʿīf. See the preceding]"""
"10321","(10316) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me that Abū al-Zubayr informed him. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that ʿAlī al-Azdī informed him that Ibn ʿUmar taught him that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted his camel heading out for a journey, he would say \Allāhu Akbar\"" three times"," then say: \""Glory be to the One who has subjected this to us"," for we could not have done so [by ourselves]"," and indeed to our Lord we shall return.\"" [Sūrat al-Zukhruf: 13–14] \""O Allah"," we ask You in this journey of ours for righteousness and taqwā"," and for deeds which You love and are pleased with. O Allah"," make this journey easy for us and fold away its distance from us. O Allah"," You are the Companion in travel and the Deputy over the family. O Allah"," we seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel"," the grief of a wretched return"," and the evil of the sight regarding family and wealth.\"" He said: And when he returned"," he would say these words and add to them: \""Returning"," repenting"," praising our Lord.\"" The wording is that of Ḥajjāj. In the narration of Ibn Wahb: \""O Allah"," we ask You in this journey of ours\"" — and he did not say \""which You love\"" — and he said: \""O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel"," the grief of the sight"," and the evil of the return.\"" And he added: \""Worshippers of our Lord"," praising Him.\"" The rest is the same. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim (1342)]"""
"10322","(10317) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq. He said: ʿAlī ibn Rabīʿah informed me that he witnessed ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) when he mounted. When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said, \Bismillāh\"" (In the name of Allah). When he was seated upon the mount"," he said"," \""Al-ḥamdu lillāh\"" (All praise is due to Allah)"," then he said: \""Glory be to the One who has subjected this to us"," for we could not have done so [by ourselves]"," and indeed to our Lord we shall return.\"" [Sūrat al-Zukhruf: 13–14] Then he praised Allah three times and said \""Allāhu Akbar\"" three times"," then he said"," \""There is no god but You; I have wronged myself"," so forgive me"," for none forgives sins but You.\"" Then he laughed"," and it was said"," \""What makes you laugh"," O Commander of the Faithful?\"" He said"," \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) do as I did and say as I said"," then he laughed"," and we said"," 'What makes you laugh"," O Prophet of Allah?' He said"," 'The servant' — or he said"," 'I am astonished at the servant — when he says: There is no god but You; I have wronged myself"," so forgive me"," for none forgives sins but You"," while he knows that none forgives sins but He.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2603)"," al-Tirmidhī (3446)]"""
"10323","(10318) Ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated to us from Manṣūr from Mujāhid from Abū Maʿmar from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: When a man mounts a beast and does not mention the name of Allah, Satan rides behind him and says to him, \Sing!\"" If he cannot sing well"," he says to him"," \""Wish for things.\"" Mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (8781)]"""
"10324","(10319) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī in al-Kūfah narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Zuhrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī from ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥakm ibn Thawbān from Abū Lās al-Khuzāʿī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted us on camels from the camels of ṣadaqah, weak ones, for the Ḥajj. We said, \O Messenger of Allah"," we do not see that these can carry us!\"" He said"," \""There is no camel except that upon its hump there is a devil. So mention the name of Allah when you mount them"," as He has commanded you"," then make use of them for yourselves"," for it is Allah who carries.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad (4/221)"," Ibn Khuzaymah (2377)]"""
"10325","(10320) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Ḥafṣ ibn Mayṣarah informed me from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Marwān from his father: Kaʿb informed him that Ṣuhayb, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), informed him that whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a village he intended to enter, upon seeing it he would say: \O Allah"," Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow"," Lord of the seven earths and what they bear"," Lord of the devils and what they lead astray"," Lord of the winds and what they scatter — we ask You for the good of this village and the good of its people"," and we seek refuge in You from its evil"," the evil of its people"," and the evil of what is in it.\"" The mention of his father is missing from the narration of Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr"," but it is present in the narration of Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ"," and it is in his narration. Indeed"," Ibn Abī Uways narrated it from Ibn Wahb likewise. And Saʿd ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd said from Ibn Abī al-Zinād from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Marwān from his father from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mughīth from Kaʿb from Ṣuhayb. And that was narrated from a weak perspective from Abū Marwān al-Aslamī from his father from his grandfather"," who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to Khaybar"," and he mentioned something similar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim (1/614)]"""
"10326","(10321) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us; Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us; Ṣafwān narrated to us; Sharīḥ ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us that he heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Walīd narrate from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went on a campaign or travelled and night overtook him, he would say: \O earth"," my Lord and your Lord is Allah. I seek refuge in Allah from your evil"," the evil of what is in you"," the evil of what has been created in you"," and the evil of what creeps upon you. I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of every lion and serpent"," every snake and scorpion"," from the inhabitant of the town"," and from the evil of the father and what he begot.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad (2/132)]"""
"10327","(10322) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā, that is, Ibn Bukayr, narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Ibn Abī Ḥabīb — from al-Ḥārith ibn Yaʿqūb — that Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to him — that he heard Busr ibn Saʿīd — that he heard Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard Khawla bint Ḥakīm al-Aslamiyya saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: Whoever arrives at a lodging and then says, \I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created","\"" nothing shall harm him until he departs from that lodging.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba and Ibn al-Rumḥ from al-Layth ibn Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2708]"""
"10328","(10323) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq, son of al-Bayāḍ, in Baghdad, informed us — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Khiraqī narrated to us — Abū Qilāba narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Kathīr narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd narrated from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) alighted at a place, he would not depart until he had prayed two rakʿahs therein.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — Ibn Khuzayma narrated it: 1260]"
"10329","(10324) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās al-Asfāṭī narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us — both saying: ʿImrān narrated from Qatāda — from Abū Burda — from Abū Mūsā, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say when he feared a people: \O Allah"," I place You before them and I seek refuge in You from their evil.\"" In the narration of Abū Dāwūd from his father"," he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to say that when he supplicated against a people.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — Abū Dāwūd narrated it: 1537]"""
"10330","(10325) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to me — my father narrated from Qatāda — from Abū Burda ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays, that his father narrated to him, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say when he feared a people: \O Allah"," we place You before them and we seek refuge in You from their evil.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — See the preceding hadith]"""
"10331","(10326) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me — al-ʿAlāʾ narrated — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī narrated to me — my father narrated to me — Qutayba ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — al-ʿAlāʾ narrated from his father — from Abū Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \The bell is the flute of the devil.\"" In the narration of Sulaymān: \""The flute of the devils.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba ibn Saʿīd and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2114]"""
"10332","(10327) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salama informed us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Jarīr narrated from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ — from his father — from Abū Hurayra — from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: \The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell or a dog.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr"," and it was also narrated regarding the bell from Umm Ḥabība (may Allah be pleased with her) from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2113]"""
"10333","(10328) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān in Baghdad informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — my father and Isḥāq ibn Bakr both narrated to us — Bakr ibn Muḍar narrated — Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿa narrated — ʿIrāk ibn Mālik narrated — Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated — from Abū al-Jarrāḥ, the freedman of Umm Ḥabība — from Umm Ḥabība, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: \The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain — Abū Dāwūd narrated it: 2554]"""
"10334","(10329) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr — from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm — that Abū Bashīr al-Anṣārī informed him that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) during some of his journeys. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent a messenger — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr said, I think he said, while the people were in their place of overnight stay — saying: \Let no string or any other kind of necklace remain around the neck of any camel"," except that it be cut off.\"" Mālik said: I think that was on account of the evil eye.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 2843]"""
"10335","(10330) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated — from Ayyūb — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: Riding the animal that feeds on filth was prohibited.\n\nAnd ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays narrated from Ayyūb, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prohibited it. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Abū Dāwūd narrated it: 2557]"
